        "crawl_text": "Carl Zeiss AG Publicly traded company Global Carl-Zeiss-Stra\u00dfe 22, 73447 Oberkochen, Germany Germany Global ZEISS generated total annual revenue of nearly 12 billion euros in the fiscal year 2024/25. The company employs around 46,600 employees globally in approximately 50 countries. Investing 15 percent of revenue in science and R&D to drive innovation. Leading technology enterprise in optics and optoelectronics. Skip to main content\n\n][1]\nZEISS Group Global\nOpens in another tab [ ][2] [ back ][3]\nGlobal\n* [ About us ][4]\n* [ Products and solutions ][5]\n* [ Careers ][6]\n* [ Contact ][7]\n* [ Contact ][8]\n* ### Related ZEISS Websites\n* [ Annual Report of the ZEISS Group ][9]\n* [ ZEISS Forum ][10]\n[ ][11]\n[ ][12]\n* [Home][13]\n* About us\nWhat drives us\n][14]\n\n### Scroll animation items\n\n# What drives us\n\nAs the pioneer of science in optics, we continue to challenge the limits of human imagination.\n\n## Shaping the future\n\nZEISS is an internationally leading technology enterprise operating in the optics and\noptoelectronics industries. As a company wholly owned by a foundation, ZEISS is rooted in and\ncommitted to responsibility in all its activities. As the pioneer of scientific optics, we continue\nto challenge the limits of human imagination. With our passion for excellence we create value for\nour customers and inspire the world to see in new ways.\n\n## Innovative solutions\n\nThe semiconductor industry, e-mobility providers, Nobel Prize winners, medical clinics and\nophthalmologists, film makers and eye care practitioners \u2013 to name but a few \u2013 rely on ZEISS.\nIts optics are needed to manufacture microchips, research infectious diseases, manage the quality of\nelectric cars and windmills, provide the best possible treatment for brain and eye surgery or create\naward-winning films.\n* [ Products & Solutions ][15]\n\n## A strong foundation\n\nThe company was founded in 1846 by Carl Zeiss, who anchored precision, a commitment to innovation\nand the creation of real value for customers and society. In 1889, Ernst Abbe established the Carl\nZeiss Foundation in memory of his partner as the sole owner of ZEISS, until today the foundation is\nexclusively committed to promoting science and progress. As a pioneer of corporate responsibility\nZEISS is following a clear path: To enable customers to achieve their goals with value-added\nsolutions developed and manufactured in a responsible manner.\n* [ Carl Zeiss Foundation ][16]\n\n## Committed to sustainability\n\nThe foundation as owner is expecting sustainable contributions from ZEISS. The company's dividends\nare used by the foundation to fund scientific and research programs in areas essential to the future\nof humanity, from the aging society to the circular economy. ZEISS works toward clear goals: By\nfiscal year 2024/25, the company aims to reduce scope 1 and 2 emissions as much as possible and to\noffset the remaining unavoidable emissions. Specific programs for MINT education, public health\ncare, nature and climate protection and social commitment are part of the global ZEISS\nsustainability strategy.\n* [ Sustainability at ZEISS ][17]\n\n## A future-oriented portfolio\n\nToday, around 46,600 employees globally in around 50 countries work hard to fulfill and exceed\ncustomer expectations. They generated total annual revenue of nearly 12 billion euros (fiscal year\n2024/25) in the four ZEISS segments Semiconductor Manufacturing Technology, Industrial Quality &\nResearch, Medical Technology and Consumer Markets. Currently, 15 percent of revenue is invested in\nscience and R&D. ZEISS believes that innovation and technology are the key to a sustainable future\nand solutions for global challenges.\n* [ Innovation at ZEISS ][18]\n\n## Find out more about ZEISS\n\nCheck out our innovative solutions, our company by the numbers and dive into the world of ZEISS.\n\n[ Products & Solutions ][19]\n[ Facts & Figures ][20]\n[ Back to top ][21]\nRelated ZEISS Websites\n[ Annual Report of the ZEISS Group ][22] [ ZEISS Forum ][23]\n* Frequently Used\n\n[Sustainability at ZEISS][24] [Innovation at ZEISS][25] [History at a glance][26] [Carl Zeiss\nFoundation][27]\n* About ZEISS\n\n[About][28] [Career][29] [Newsroom][30] [Compliance][31] [Accessibility statement][32]\n* Social Media\n\n[Facebook][33] [Instagram][34] [LinkedIn][35] [YouTube][36] [X][37]\nSelect ZEISS Area\nZEISS Group\n* [Cinematography][38]\n* [Hunting][39]\n* [Nature Observation][40]\n* [Planetariums][41]\n* [Simulation Projection Solutions][42]\n* [Vision Care][43]\n* [Digital Solutions & Software Development][44]\n* [Industrial Quality Solutions][45]\n* [OEM Solutions][46]\n* [Research Microscopy Solutions][47]\n* [Spectroscopy][48]\n* [ZEISS Group][49]\n* [Extended Reality][50]\n* [Medical Technology][51]\n* [Photography][52]\n* [Semiconductor Manufacturing Technology][53]\n* [Sunlens][54]\nSelect website\nGlobal website (English)\n* Select language\n* [ Global website (English) ][55]\n* Select location\nThe content of this page was created with help of Generative AI\n* Legal\n\n[Contact ][56] [Publisher][57] [Legal Notice][58] [Privacy Notice][59] [Cookie Notice][60] [Cookie\nPreferences][61]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/home.html\n[3]: #\n[4]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss.html\n[5]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/products-and-solutions.html\n[6]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/career.html\n[7]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/contact.html\n[8]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/contact.html\n[9]: https://www.zeiss.com/annualreport\n[10]: https://www.zeiss.com/zeissforum\n[11]: #search\n[12]: #\n[13]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/home.html\n[14]: #\n[15]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/products-and-solutions.html\n[16]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss/present/facts-figures/carl-zeiss-foundation.htm\n[17]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss/present/sustainability.html\n[18]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss/future/innovation.html\n[19]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/products-and-solutions.html\n[20]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss/present/facts-figures.html\n[21]: #to-top\n[22]: https://www.zeiss.com/annualreport\n[23]: https://www.zeiss.com/zeissforum\n[24]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss/present/sustainability.html\n[25]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss/future/innovation.html\n[26]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss/past/history.html\n[27]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss/present/facts-figures/carl-zeiss-foundation.htm\n[28]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss.html\n[29]: https://www.zeiss.com/career\n[30]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss/present/newsroom.html\n[31]: https://www.zeiss.com/compliance\n[32]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/legal-information/accessibility-statement.html\n[33]: https://www.facebook.com/zeissgroup\n[34]: https://www.instagram.com/zeissgroup/\n[35]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/zeiss/\n[36]: https://www.youtube.com/user/ZEISSGroup\n[37]: https://x.com/zeiss_group\n[38]: https://www.zeiss.com/photonics-and-optics/en/cinematography.html\n[39]: https://www.zeiss.com/photonics-and-optics/en/hunting.html\n[40]: https://www.zeiss.com/photonics-and-optics/en/nature-observation.html\n[41]: https://www.zeiss.com/planetariums/en/home.html\n[42]: https://www.zeiss.com/simulation-projection-solutions/home.html\n[43]: https://www.zeiss.com/vision-care/en/home.html\n[44]: https://www.zeiss.com/digital-innovation/home.html\n[45]: https://www.zeiss.com/metrology/en/home.html\n[46]: https://www.zeiss.com/oem-solutions/home.html\n[47]: https://www.zeiss.com/microscopy/en/home.html\n[48]: https://www.zeiss.com/spectroscopy/home.html\n[49]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/home.html\n[50]: https://www.zeiss.com/extended-reality/en/home.html\n[51]: https://www.zeiss.com/meditec/en/home.html\n[52]: https://www.zeiss.com/photonics-and-optics/en/photography.html\n[53]: https://www.zeiss.com/semiconductor-manufacturing-technology/home.html\n[54]: https://www.zeiss.com/sunlens/en/home.html\n[55]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/about-zeiss.html\n[56]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/contact.html\n[57]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/legal-information/publisher.html\n[58]: https://www.zeiss.com/corporate/en/legal-information/legal-notice-and-general-terms-and-condit\nions.html\n[59]: https://www.zeiss.com/privacy\n[60]: https://www.zeiss.com/cookies\n[61]: # Skip to main content\n\n][1]\nZEISS Group Global\nOpens in another tab [ ][2] [ back ][3]\nGlobal\n* [ About us ][4]\n* [ Products and solutions ][5]\n* [ Careers ][6]\n* [ Contact ][7]\n* [ Contact ][8]\n* ### Related ZEISS Websites\n* [ Annual Report of the ZEISS Group ][9]\n* [ ZEISS Forum ][10]\n[ ][11]\n[ ][12]\n[ ][13]\n\n## For which product or product area would you like to contact us?\n\nBased on your selection, we will guide you to proper contact\n\nYour product interest\n* [Vision Care][14]\n* [Extended Reality][15]\n* [Medical Technology][16]\n* [Semiconductor Manufacturing Technology][17]\n* [Industrial Quality Solutions][18]\n* [Research Microscopy Solutions][19]\n* [Photography][20]\n* [Cinematography][21]\n* [Hunting][22]\n* [Nature Observation][23]\n* [Simulation Projection Solutions][24]\n* [Planetariums][25]\n* [Spectroscopy][26]\n* [OEM Solutions][27]\n* [Digital Solutions][28]\nConfirm product selection\nCancel\nZEISS Group\n\n# Contact & Support\n\n[ Overview ][29]\n\n## Important contacts at a glance\n* [\n[ZEISS Products & Solutions] [ZEISS Products & Solutions]\n\n### Products & Services\n\nDo you have an inquiry about a product or a service request?\n\n][30]\n* [\n[ZEISS Career] [ZEISS Career]\n\n### Jobs & Careers\n\nAre you interested in a job at ZEISS?\n\n][31]\n* [\n[ZEISS Press & Media] [ZEISS Press & Media]\n\n### Press & Media\n\nAre you looking for the right press contact or have a general press inquiry?\n\n][32]\n* [\n[ZEISS Supplier] [ZEISS Supplier]\n\n### Supplier\n\nDo you need information about our purchasing and supplier portal?\n\n][33]\n* [\n[ZEISS Conference Center] [ZEISS Conference Center]\n\n### Conference Center\n\nAre you looking for a state-of-the-art event location for a business event?\n\n][34]\n* [\n[ZEISS Museum] [ZEISS Museum]\n\n### ZEISS Museum\n\nAre you interested in a guided tour in the ZEISS Museum of optics or would like to handover a\ndevice?\n\n][35]\n* [\n[ZEISS History & Archive] [ZEISS History & Archive]\n\n### History & Archive\n\nWould you like to learn more about the history of ZEISS or the older ZEISS products?\n\n][36]\n* [\n[ZEISS CAD Systems] [ZEISS CAD Systems]\n\n### CAD Systems\n\nDo you need information about the Creo Parametric CAD system used at ZEISS?\n\n][37]\n\n## Your general inquiry for ZEISS\n\nZEISS Headquarters Oberkochen | Germany\n[ZEISS Group] [ZEISS Group]\n\nIf you have general questions or requests, please feel free to contact us via the form or visit us\nonsite\n\n**Carl Zeiss AG**\nCarl-Zeiss-Stra\u00dfe 22\n73447 Oberkochen\nGermany\n\nForm is loading...\n\n### Your form is being submitted...\n\nUploading files...\n* Your file(s) couldn't be submitted. Please abort to return to the form.\nAbort\n\nIf you want to have more information on data processing at ZEISS, please refer to our [data\nprotection notice][38].\n\nSubmit\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n* How to apply for a job at ZEISS?\n\nYou can access our online job portal at our [ZEISS career website][39]. For procedural reasons we\nwould kindly ask you to apply directly via our eRecruiting tool.\n\n[ Job openings and applications ][40]\n* Where to find the Annual Report of Carl Zeiss AG and Carl Zeiss Meditec AG?\n\nYou can find the current Annual Report of Carl Zeiss AG on our website:\n[www.zeiss.com/annualreport][41] .\nWe do not offer a printed version anymore. If you are interested in the Annual Report of Carl\nZeiss Meditec AG, please visit the website [www.zeiss.com/meditec-ag][42]\n* How to set up a sponsoring request?\n\nRequests to ZEISS for donations must be submitted via the Carl Zeiss Sponsorship Fund. Before you\nsubmit your application, we would be grateful if you could take a quick look at our guidelines.\n\n[ Sponsor guidelin"
