        "crawl_text": "Resonon Inc. High-precision data Rugged and reliable systems Superior results in challenging environments 123 Commercial Drive, Bozeman, MT 59715 USA USA Hyperspectral Imaging Systems and Software | Resonon\n\nHyperspectral Imaging Solutions\n\nHyperspectral Imaging Solutions\n\nBack\nHyperspectral Cameras\nPika UV (330-800nm)\nPika L (400-1000nm)\nPika L-F (420-980nm)\nPika XC2 (400-1000nm)\nPika IR (900-1700nm)\nPika IR+ (900-1700nm)\nPika IR-L (925-1700nm)\nPika IR-L+ (925-1700nm)\nPika SWIR (1000-2500nm)\nSee All Cameras\nHyperspectral Systems\nAirborne Remote Sensing\nFully-Integrated Airborne\nOutdoor\nSpectralSight\u2122\nBenchtop - Reflectance\nBenchtop - Reflectance/Transmission\nBenchtop - Large Samples\nBio-LIF\u2122\nSee All Systems\n\nMachine Vision\nSoftware\n\nSpectronon\u2122\n\nRVS Machine Vision\n\nAirborne\n\nSDK\n\nCompatible Software\n\nSee All Software\nProducts\n\nBack Precision Agriculture\nEnvironmental Monitoring\nBiotechnology\nRemote Sensing\nFood Production\nIndustrial Applications\nSee All Applications\nApplications\n\nBack\nBlog\nResearch Publications\nManuals & Tutorials\nTutorial Videos\nData Sheets\nDownloads\nSee More\nLibrary\n\nBack Customer Support\nSales and Support Team\nTraining\nInternational Distributors\nWarranty and Repair\nImager Service Plan\nPolicies, Terms & Conditions\nSee More\nSupport\n\nBack\nAbout Us\nWhat Our Clients Say\nWhy Choose Resonon\nCareers\nSee More\nCompany\n\nBack Contact Resonon\nInternational Distributors\nSee More\nContact Us\n\nSearch Google\n\nHyperspectral Imaging Solutions\nHyperspectral Imaging Applications\nLearn About Hyperspectral Imaging\n\nHyperspectral Imaging Systems\n\nResonon has been designing and building hyperspectral imaging systems for over 20 years.&nbsp; Our hyperspectral imagers are used around the world in factories, laboratories, underwater, on the ground, in the air, and in Low Earth orbit.\n\nOur integrated hardware and software systems produce high-quality data to stimulate new insights and solve challenging problems.&nbsp;\n\nContact us to determine the best system for your application.\nView Complete Systems\nView Hyperspectral Cameras\nRead Our Latest Blog Post\n\nBy combining our AI model with Resonon's hyperspectral imaging system, we can distinguish plastic objects to recognize and classify waste. We are able to detect objects that we were once unable to when using just RGB cameras. I am very satisfied with the purchase of the Resonon camera.\n\nMyeong-hun Lim\nManager\nSuperBin\n&#xE022;\n&#xE023;\n\nAirborne Remote Sensing System\nComplete systems providing georegistered hyperspectral data from drones and piloted aircraft. See More\n\nFully-Integrated Airborne\nFully-integrated, ready-to-fly hyperspectral airborne system. See More\n\nOutdoor\nPortable, tripod-based, hyperspectral system for outdoor measurements. See More\n\nSpectralSight\u2122\n\nSystem for rapid automated hyperspectral data collection and optical sorting. See More\n\nBenchtop - Reflectance\n\nLaboratory system for measuring hyperspectral reflectance data. See More\n\nBenchtop - Reflectance/Transmission\nLaboratory system for measuring both reflectance and transmission hyperspectral data. See More\n\nBenchtop - Large Samples\nLaboratory hyperspectral systems for scanning large objects.\nSee More\n\nBio-LIF\u2122\nLaser-Induced Fluorescence and Hyperspectral Imaging combined to yield unparalleled insight into biological samples emission data. See More\n\nMachine Vision Systems\nHyperspectral machine vision systems for automated optical inspection, sorting, and quality control. See More\n\nSpectronon\u2122 Software\nPowerful analysis and visualization tools make Spectronon popular for all types of hyperspectral data. See More\n\nPika UV (330-800nm) See More\n\nPika L (400-1000nm) See More\n\nPika L-F (420-980nm) See More\n\nPika XC2 (400-1000nm) See More\n\nPika IR (900-1700nm) See More\n\nPika IR+ (900-1700nm) See More\n\nPika IR-L (925-1700nm) See More\n\nPika IR-L+ (925-1700nm) See More\n\nPika SWIR (1000-2500nm) See More\n\nComplete Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions\n\nTechnical Excellence\nHigh-precision data.\n\nRugged and Reliable\nBuilt for harsh environments.\n\nSuperior Results\nProviding the answers you need.\n\nApplication Example: Hyperspectral Imaging at Night Boosts Plant Stress Detection\n\nA Pika L hyperspectral imager was used with a halogen light to image plants inside a dark room at noon and midnight over several days.\n\nNighttime imaging significantly improved detection of spider mite infestations, increasing classification accuracy by 29-31%.\n\nPublished in: C. Nansen et al,. Plant Methods (2024)\n\nMore Information\nView All Applications\nHyperspectral imaging with an active light source inside dark room (a). Soybean plants at 1 \u00d7 1 (b) and 9 \u00d7 9 (c) spatial binning. Coleus plants at 1 \u00d7 1 (d) and 9 \u00d7 9 (e) spatial binning.\n\nHyperspectral imaging with an active light source inside dark room (a). Soybean plants at 1 \u00d7 1 (b) and 9 \u00d7 9 (c) spatial binning. Coleus plants at 1 \u00d7 1 (d) and 9 \u00d7 9 (e) spatial binning.\n\n&#xE017; Prev\nNext &#xE000;\n\nNewsletter Signup\nGet notifications about our latest products, blog posts, videos, and company news.\n\nName\n\nEmail\n\nSubscribe\nBy clicking subscribe, you are consenting to receive emails from Resonon (~6 per year).&nbsp;\nYou can unsubscribe at any time.\n\nContact Us\nClick below and our hyperspectral experts will contact you soon.\nLearn More\nComplete Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions\n\nDiscover\nHome\nHyperspectral Cameras\nSystems\nMachine Vision\nObjective Lenses\nSoftware\nApplications\nResources\nLibrary\nSupport\nResearch Publications\nDistributors\nCompany\nContact Us\nDownloads\nPrivacy Policy\n\nContact Resonon Inc.\n123 Commercial Drive\nBozeman, MT 59715 USA\n\nPhone: +1.406.586.3356 +1.406.586.3356\nEmail: Contact Us\nFollow\n&#xE005; &#xE006;\n\nWebsite design by JTech Communications\n&copy; 2026 Resonon Inc. [[Resonon - Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions]Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions][1]\n[[Resonon - Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions]Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions][2]\nBack\nHyperspectral Cameras\n[Pika UV (330-800nm)][3]\n[Pika L (400-1000nm)][4]\n[Pika L-F (420-980nm)][5]\n[Pika XC2 (400-1000nm)][6]\n[Pika IR (900-1700nm)][7]\n[Pika IR+ (900-1700nm)][8]\n[Pika IR-L (925-1700nm)][9]\n[Pika IR-L+ (925-1700nm)][10]\n[Pika SWIR (1000-2500nm)][11]\n[See All Cameras][12]\nHyperspectral Systems\n[Airborne Remote Sensing][13]\n[Fully-Integrated Airborne][14]\n[Outdoor][15]\n[SpectralSight\u2122][16]\n[Benchtop - Reflectance][17]\n[Benchtop - Reflectance/Transmission ][18]\n[Benchtop - Large Samples][19]\n[Bio-LIF\u2122][20]\n[See All Systems][21]\n[Machine Vision][22]\nSoftware\n[Spectronon\u2122][23]\n[RVS Machine Vision][24]\n[Airborne][25]\n[SDK][26]\n[Compatible Software][27]\n[See All Software][28]\nProducts\nBack\n[Precision Agriculture][29]\n[Environmental Monitoring][30]\n[Biotechnology][31]\n[Remote Sensing][32]\n[Food Production][33]\n[Industrial Applications][34]\n[See All Applications][35]\n[Applications][36]\nBack\n[Blog][37]\n[Research Publications][38]\n[Manuals & Tutorials][39]\n[Tutorial Videos][40]\n[Data Sheets][41]\n[Downloads][42]\n[See More][43]\n[Library][44]\nBack\n[Customer Support][45]\n[Sales and Support Team][46]\n[Training][47]\n[International Distributors][48]\n[Warranty and Repair][49]\n[Imager Service Plan][50]\n[Policies, Terms & Conditions][51]\n[See More][52]\n[Support][53]\nBack\n[About Us][54]\n[What Our Clients Say][55]\n[Why Choose Resonon][56]\n[Careers][57]\n[See More][58]\n[Company][59]\nBack\n[Contact Resonon][60]\n[International Distributors][61]\n[See More][62]\n[Contact Us][63]\nSearch Google\n[Hyperspectral Imaging Systems Manufacture, Resonon, is located in Bozeman Montana USA]\n\n# About Us\n\nAt Resonon, we understand that pushing the boundaries of research and managing production isn't\neasy. When you need next-level imaging, the limits of traditional vision systems can limit\nadvances.\n\nOur hyperspectral imaging cameras break through these limitations, revealing details invisible to\nstandard sensors and the naked eye.\n\nBy unlocking hidden information, our technology empowers researchers, scientists, engineers, and\nmanufacturers to solve complex problems and accelerate progress. We don't just provide equipment\u2014we\ncollaborate with you to evaluate solutions and integrate technology that meets your specific\nchallenges so that you can start gaining new insights.\n\n> Technical Excellence. Superior Results.\n\n[Resonon Hyperspectral Image Processing Software optical lab]\n\n## What Our Clients Say\n\n**By combining our AI model with Resonon's hyperspectral imaging system, we can distinguish plastic\nobjects to recognize and classify waste. ** We are able to detect objects that we were once unable\nto when using just RGB cameras. I am very satisfied with the purchase of the Resonon camera.\nResonon's cameras have **high spectral resolution**, making it easy to find features during\nclassification. They also have **high spatial resolution**, making micro-scale measurements\npossible. Hyperspectral data is useful because it **provides solutions to difficult and complex\nproblems**.\nAs a university scientist,** I have been working with Resonon and using Resonon cameras for more\nthan 20 years.** In 2019, when I founded Spectral Analytix, it was without hesitation that I\npurchased a [**Pika L**][64] as our imaging work horse.\n**Based on quality and robustness of both hardware and software, I strongly recommend Resonon** as\nyour imaging partner. Additionally, Resonon provides unsurpassed service!\nMyeong-hun Lim\nManager\n[SuperBin][65]\nByung-yeop Kim\nResearcher\n[LG Energy Solution][66]\nDr. Christian Nansen\nFounder\n[Spectral Analytix][67]\n[Case Study][68]\n\n## Why Choose Resonon\n\nA Trusted Partner\n* 20+ years of hyperspectral imaging expertise with over 1000 deployed systems.\n* Trusted provider to leading research entities, including [NASA][69], [NOAA][70], and [NIST][71].\n\nRapid Support by Hyperspectral Experts\n* The hyperspectral imaging experts in our Sales Team will help you to get the right system for your\napplication.\n* Free sample scanning answers \u201cWill hyperspectral imaging work?\u201d before you purchase.\n* 13-day average lead time for standard systems.\n* Rapid support response time, usually within one business day, at no cost\u2014some competitors charge\nfor a support package to guarantee a response within 1 to 3 days.\n\nOutstanding Hyperspectral Systems\n* Resonon\u2019s imagers provide excellent [images][72] and spectral data.\n* Seamless hardware and software integration through in-house development.\n* Built to last. Designed, fabricated, and assembled in the USA with a standard 2-year\nwarranty\u2014systems routinely operate in the field for 10+ years.\n* Exceptional Hyperspectral Software\nHigh-quality data is not enough; Resonon software enables the conversion of ***data ***into\n***useful information***.\nNo 3rd-party software is required to operate our systems, simplifying data processing.\n* **Spectronon\u2122**: Rated among the best hyperspectral software packages by academic and research\nusers\u2014unlike our competitor\u2019s software, you can [download Spectronon][73] and sample data for free\nright now.\n* **Airborne software**: We know that airborne hyperspectral can be difficult. To make it easier,\nour airborne software and Spectronon handle all acquisition, geocorrection, reflectance/radiance\nconversion, post-processing, and creation of clear visualizations.\n* **RVS (Real-time Vision System)**: Powerful but easy-to-implement software streamlined for use in\nhigh-throughput lab scanning and industrial applications.\n\n## Careers\n\nResonon designs, manufactures, and deploys hardware and software for hyperspectral imaging in\nlaboratory, industrial, and airborne environments. As a small business, we offer an exciting,\nfriendly work environment with a flexible schedule. Our current projects span a wide range of\napplications, from developing a sensor for a NASA satellite, to implementing custom machine vision\nsolutions for manufacturing challenges, to assisting researchers in deploying our sensors on drones.\nWe prioritize a healthy work-life balance.\n\nBozeman, Montana is our home base. This lively university town offers excellent schools and is just\nminutes away from world-class skiin"
