          {
            "url": "https://surfaceoptics.com/products/spectral-imaging-systems/710-series-hyperspectral-cameras/",
            "text": "* [ 1-858-675-7404][1]\n* [ Email Us][2]\n* [ Support][3]\n[[Surface Optics Corporation]][4]\n* [Products][5]\n* [\nLab Reflectometers\n][6]\n* [SOC-100 HDR][7]\n* [SOC-210 Bidirectional Reflectometer][8]\n* [\n410 Series Reflectometers\n][9]\n* [SOC-410 DHR Reflectometer][10]\n* [410-VIS-IR Reflectometer][11]\n* [410-Solar Reflectometer][12]\n* [410-Solar-i Reflectometer][13]\n* [ET-10 Emissometer][14]\n* [ET-100 Emissometer][15]\n* [410-LIDAR Reflectometer][16]\n* [Custom SOC410 Reflectometers][17]\n* [Accessories & Maintenance][18]\n* [\nSpectral Imaging Systems\n][19]\n* [710 Series Hyperspectral Cameras][20]\n* [LightShift Multispectral Video][21]\n* [DuoChrome-SM][22]\n* [SOC-750 Midwave Infrared][23]\n* [SOC-760 VNIR-SWIR][24]\n* [Spectral Imaging Resources][25]\n* [Services][26]\n* [\nOptical Properties Measurement Services\n][27]\n* [Spectral Reflectance (HDR)][28]\n* [Emissivity][29]\n* [BSDF / Scatter][30]\n* [Transmittance Measurements][31]\n* [ASTM Testing][32]\n* [Solar Reflectance (SRI/TSR)][33]\n* [Absorptance & Thermal Emittance][34]\n* [Optical Properties Measurements Database][35]\n* [\nVacuum Deposition Coatings\n][36]\n* [Low Observable / Stealth][37]\n* [Large Area][38]\n* [Roll-to-Roll][39]\n* [Diamond-Like Carbon][40]\n* [Vacuum Deposited Gold (VDG)][41]\n* [Anti-Reflection (AR)][42]\n* [Vacuum Deposited Aluminum (VDA)][43]\n* [Spaceflight and Thermal Control][44]\n* [High Reflectance][45]\n* [\nElectro-Optics Engineering\n][46]\n* [SBIR / STTR][47]\n* [Applications][48]\n* [\nSpace\n][49]\n* [\nDefense\n][50]\n* [\n[Photovoltaic solar panel in desert]\nSolar Energy\n][51]\n* [\nGreen Building\n][52]\n* [\nAgriculture\n][53]\n* [News][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [Publications][56]\n* [About Us][57]\n* [Our Company][58]\n* [Company History][59]\n* [Facilities][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Our Team][62]\n* [International Distributors][63]\n\n# 710 Series Hyperspectral Cameras\n\n## VNIR to SWIR hyperspectral imaging systems for microscopy, lab, field, and tower-mounted\n## applications\n\nThe 710-HyCore and 710-OmniCore deliver exceptional spectral resolution, giving researchers the\nability to distinguish subtle differences between materials and compounds at a price point that\nmakes high-performance hyperspectral imaging more accessible than ever. Both capture hyperspectral\ndata from 375\u20131025 nm with 1.65 nm spectral resolution and 1500 spatial channels, share the same\nspectrometer and camera design, and include SpectraCore Capture acquisition software and an SDK\nsupporting C#, C++, and Python. All systems are radiometrically calibrated in our lab to ensure\naccurate, traceable spectral measurements.\n\n[GET A QUOTE][64]\n\n## VNIR to SWIR hyperspectral imaging systems for microscopy, lab, field, and tower-mounted\n## applications\n\nThe 710-HyCore and 710-OmniCore deliver exceptional spectral resolution, giving researchers the\nability to distinguish subtle differences between materials and compounds at a price point that\nmakes high-performance hyperspectral imaging more accessible than ever. Both capture hyperspectral\ndata from 375\u20131025 nm with 1.65 nm spectral resolution and 1500 spatial channels, share the same\nspectrometer and camera design, and include SpectraCore Capture acquisition software and an SDK\nsupporting C#, C++, and Python. All systems are radiometrically calibrated in our lab to ensure\naccurate, traceable spectral measurements.\n\n[GET A QUOTE][65]\n\n### Superior Performance\n\nAchieve a spectral resolution of 1.65 nm at native 1\u00d7 binning, delivering the data density demanded\nby the most exacting R&D, academic, and advanced manufacturing applications.\n\n### 375 \u2013 1025 nm\n\nSpectral Range\n\n### 1.65 nm\n\nSpectral Resolution (FWHM)\n\n### 784\n\nSpectral Channels\n\n### 1500\n\nSpatial Channels\n\n### SDK\n\nAPI supporting C#, C++, and Python\n\n### Microscope Compatible\n\nAttach to C-mount microscopes\n\n### 375 \u2013 1025 nm\n\nSpectral Range\n\n### 1.65 nm\n\nSpectral Resolution (FWHM)\n\n### 784\n\nSpectral Channels\n\n### 1500\n\nSpatial Channels\n\n### SDK\n\nAPI supporting C#, C++, and Python\n\n### Microscope Compatible\n\nAttach to C-mount microscopes\n\n**SOC-710 SERIES**\n\n## Next-generation hyperspectral imaging for research & industry\n\nThe 710-HyCore hyperspectral camera and 710-OmniCore hyperspectral imaging system, build on our\nproven SOC-710 platform.\n\n### ****HyCore VNIR Hyperspectral Camera****\n\nBuilt around a proprietary spectrograph design and co-engineered optics and sensor, the\nnext-generation 710 Series delivers strong performance right out of the box. Our default 1x spectral\nbinning reflects this\u2014providing the signal and resolution needed without relying on binning as a\nworkaround. Ideal for integrators or as a complete hyperspectral imaging system when paired with the\n710 Lab Tower with translation stage.\n\n### ****OmniCore VNIR Hyperspectral Imaging System****\n\nThe 710-OmniCore hyperspectral imaging system stands out with its internal scanning design, making\nit the most versatile hyperspectral imaging system available. It can be used as a lab benchtop\nsystem, mounted to a tripod, boom, or tower for field work, or attached to a microscope\u2014without the\nneed for external scanning hardware. For labs focused on long-term value, the SOC710 provides the\nperformance and flexibility to grow with their research.\n\n### ****710 Lab Tower****\n\nPair the 710\u2011HyCore or OmniCore with a 710 Lab Tower to capture consistently high\u2011quality\nhyperspectral data from day one. The rigid tower ensures repeatable alignment and controlled\ngeometry, while the smooth, programmable stage maintains constant scan speed to match integration\ntime, frame rate, and sample motion. With stable, uniform illumination, this integrated setup\nminimizes motion blur, misregistration, and radiometric striping so your algorithms can fully\ncapitalize on clean, reliable material signatures.\n\n### ****HyCore VNIR Hyperspectral Camera****\n\nBuilt around a proprietary spectrograph design and co-engineered optics and sensor, the\nnext-generation 710 Series delivers strong performance right out of the box. Our default 1x spectral\nbinning reflects this\u2014providing the signal and resolution needed without relying on binning as a\nworkaround. Ideal for integrators or as a complete hyperspectral imaging system when paired with the\n710 Lab Tower with translation stage.\n\n### ****OmniCore VNIR Hyperspectral Imaging System****\n\nThe 710-OmniCore hyperspectral imaging system stands out with its internal scanning design, making\nit the most versatile hyperspectral imaging system available. It can be used as a lab benchtop\nsystem, mounted to a tripod, boom, or tower for field work, or attached to a microscope\u2014without the\nneed for external scanning hardware. For labs focused on long-term value, the SOC710 provides the\nperformance and flexibility to grow with their research.\n\n### ****710 Lab Tower****\n\nPair the 710\u2011HyCore or OmniCore with a 710 Lab Tower to capture consistently high\u2011quality\nhyperspectral data from day one. The rigid tower ensures repeatable alignment and controlled\ngeometry, while the smooth, programmable stage maintains constant scan speed to match integration\ntime, frame rate, and sample motion. With stable, uniform illumination, this integrated setup\nminimizes motion blur, misregistration, and radiometric striping so your algorithms can fully\ncapitalize on clean, reliable material signatures.\n\n## Related Content\n\n#### [Hyperspectral Imaging Microscopy: Performance and Application of the SOC-710 OmniCore\n#### VNIR][66]\n\nMay 7, 2026\n\n#### [Surface Optics Releases New Hyperspectral Imaging Systems: 710-HyCore and 710-OmniCore][67]\n\nMarch 26, 2026\n[[Shihezi University logo over tomatoes growing in a field] ][68]\n\n#### [Transforming Food Manufacturing Inspection with Hyperspectral Imaging ][69]\n\nMarch 4, 2026\n\n#### [From Degradation to Discovery: Hyperspectral Camera Reveals Lost Artistic Depth][70]\n\nJuly 21, 2025\n\n## More Information\n* [\nDOWNLOADS\n][71]\n* [\nFULL SPECIFICATIONS\n][72]\n\n[710-OmniCore VNIR Hyperspectral Imaging System (Datasheet)][73]\n\n[710-HyCore VNIR Hyperspectral Camera (Datasheet)][74]\n\n[710 Lab Tower with Translation Stage (Datasheet)][75]\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nParameter \u2502Value\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nOptical & Spectral\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSpectral Range \u2502375 \u2013 1025 nm\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u250