          },
          {
            "url": "https://surfaceoptics.com/products/spectral-imaging-systems/lightshift-multispectral-video-camera/",
            "text": "* [ 1-858-675-7404][1]\n* [ Email Us][2]\n* [ Support][3]\n[[Surface Optics Corporation]][4]\n* [Products][5]\n* [\nLab Reflectometers\n][6]\n* [SOC-100 HDR][7]\n* [SOC-210 Bidirectional Reflectometer][8]\n* [\n410 Series Reflectometers\n][9]\n* [SOC-410 DHR Reflectometer][10]\n* [410-VIS-IR Reflectometer][11]\n* [410-Solar Reflectometer][12]\n* [410-Solar-i Reflectometer][13]\n* [ET-10 Emissometer][14]\n* [ET-100 Emissometer][15]\n* [410-LIDAR Reflectometer][16]\n* [Custom SOC410 Reflectometers][17]\n* [Accessories & Maintenance][18]\n* [\nSpectral Imaging Systems\n][19]\n* [710 Series Hyperspectral Cameras][20]\n* [LightShift Multispectral Video][21]\n* [DuoChrome-SM][22]\n* [SOC-750 Midwave Infrared][23]\n* [SOC-760 VNIR-SWIR][24]\n* [Spectral Imaging Resources][25]\n* [Services][26]\n* [\nOptical Properties Measurement Services\n][27]\n* [Spectral Reflectance (HDR)][28]\n* [Emissivity][29]\n* [BSDF / Scatter][30]\n* [Transmittance Measurements][31]\n* [ASTM Testing][32]\n* [Solar Reflectance (SRI/TSR)][33]\n* [Absorptance & Thermal Emittance][34]\n* [Optical Properties Measurements Database][35]\n* [\nVacuum Deposition Coatings\n][36]\n* [Low Observable / Stealth][37]\n* [Large Area][38]\n* [Roll-to-Roll][39]\n* [Diamond-Like Carbon][40]\n* [Vacuum Deposited Gold (VDG)][41]\n* [Anti-Reflection (AR)][42]\n* [Vacuum Deposited Aluminum (VDA)][43]\n* [Spaceflight and Thermal Control][44]\n* [High Reflectance][45]\n* [\nElectro-Optics Engineering\n][46]\n* [SBIR / STTR][47]\n* [Applications][48]\n* [\nSpace\n][49]\n* [\nDefense\n][50]\n* [\n[Photovoltaic solar panel in desert]\nSolar Energy\n][51]\n* [\nGreen Building\n][52]\n* [\nAgriculture\n][53]\n* [News][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [Publications][56]\n* [About Us][57]\n* [Our Company][58]\n* [Company History][59]\n* [Facilities][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Our Team][62]\n* [International Distributors][63]\n\n# LightShift Multispectral Video\n\n## Live multispectral video acquisition and processing\n\nLightShift\u2122 captures and processes spectral data at video rates and performs live automated\ncalibration and spectral correlation algorithm processing. Employing a novel plenoptic spectral\nimaging design, LightShift cameras offer customizable sixteen-band filter sets to tailor\nmultispectral imaging detection to your application.\n\n[DATASHEET][64]\n[LightShift VNIR multispectral video]\n\n### High Spectral Resolution\n\nHigh precision scientific grade data\n\n### Internal Scanning Stage\n\nNo special accessories limiting deployment in variable experimental setups\n\n### Faster, Easier Focusing\n\nPreview camera provides live video for real-time focusing\n\n### Open Data Formats\n\nSOC data formats are open source and ENVI compatible\n\n### Interchangeable Lenses\n\nC-mount objective lenses allow choice of field-of-view\n\n### Time Lapse Capability\n\nAutomated hyperspectral data acquisition capability\n\n## Applications\n\nReal-time security surveillance\nMining operatins\nAir quality monitoring\nPrecision agriculture\nOil and gas\nMedical diagnostics\nWildlife monitoring\nMarine biology\nIndustrial process monitoring\nFood safety and quality control\n\n**HIGH PERFORMANCE MULTISPECTRAL IMAGING**\n\n### Real Time Processing\n\nSnapshot spectral imagers obtain the entire spectral dataset during a single detector integration\nperiod, which provides a distinct advantage in spectral imaging of fast-changing phenomena.\n\nThe amount of information generated by snapshot systems is still a key challenge since their\napplication to many practical tasks depends on the ability to process substantial volumes of data to\nmake decisions in real time. A snapshot multispectral video system must process at rates keeping\npace with the real-time acquisition of images.\n\nLightShift is unique in its capability to process images spectrally in real time, from initial gain\nand offsets compensation to spectroradiometric calibration through decision-oriented processing,\nincluding spectral correlation using varied algorithms.\n\n### OEM Solutions\n* VNIR, SWIR or MWIR spectral ranges\n* Initial spectral data collection and reduction for modeling imaging system performance\n* Modification of spectral band count to increase spatial resolution\n* Filter array design and manufacturing\n* Camera housing and mechanical design for environmental considerations\n* Industry-specific interface of USB, GigE\n* System assembly, alignment, calibration and testing\n* Software GUI and spectral algorithm development\n\n**SOFTWARE**\n\n## LightShift Pro\n\nThe LightShift PRO Software application operates in two modes: live video imaging mode or playback\nof stored video mode. The user has the option to stream live video from the camera and playback\nstored video simultaneously in two separate windows within the LightShift application window. The\nsoftware also supports multiple playback windows running simultaneously.\n\n## More Information\n* [\nSPECIFICATIONS\n][65]\n* [\nHOW IT WORKS\n][66]\n* [\nDOWNLOADS\n][67]\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n**Spectral Range** \u2502400-1000 nm\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\