            "text": "* [ 1-858-675-7404][1]\n* [ Email Us][2]\n* [ Support][3]\n[[Surface Optics Corporation]][4]\n* [Products][5]\n* [\nLab Reflectometers\n][6]\n* [SOC-100 HDR][7]\n* [SOC-210 Bidirectional Reflectometer][8]\n* [\n410 Series Reflectometers\n][9]\n* [SOC-410 DHR Reflectometer][10]\n* [410-VIS-IR Reflectometer][11]\n* [410-Solar Reflectometer][12]\n* [410-Solar-i Reflectometer][13]\n* [ET-10 Emissometer][14]\n* [ET-100 Emissometer][15]\n* [410-LIDAR Reflectometer][16]\n* [Custom SOC410 Reflectometers][17]\n* [Accessories & Maintenance][18]\n* [\nSpectral Imaging Systems\n][19]\n* [710 Series Hyperspectral Cameras][20]\n* [LightShift Multispectral Video][21]\n* [DuoChrome-SM][22]\n* [SOC-750 Midwave Infrared][23]\n* [SOC-760 VNIR-SWIR][24]\n* [Spectral Imaging Resources][25]\n* [Services][26]\n* [\nOptical Properties Measurement Services\n][27]\n* [Spectral Reflectance (HDR)][28]\n* [Emissivity][29]\n* [BSDF / Scatter][30]\n* [Transmittance Measurements][31]\n* [ASTM Testing][32]\n* [Solar Reflectance (SRI/TSR)][33]\n* [Absorptance & Thermal Emittance][34]\n* [Optical Properties Measurements Database][35]\n* [\nVacuum Deposition Coatings\n][36]\n* [Low Observable / Stealth][37]\n* [Large Area][38]\n* [Roll-to-Roll][39]\n* [Diamond-Like Carbon][40]\n* [Vacuum Deposited Gold (VDG)][41]\n* [Anti-Reflection (AR)][42]\n* [Vacuum Deposited Aluminum (VDA)][43]\n* [Spaceflight and Thermal Control][44]\n* [High Reflectance][45]\n* [\nElectro-Optics Engineering\n][46]\n* [SBIR / STTR][47]\n* [Applications][48]\n* [\nSpace\n][49]\n* [\nDefense\n][50]\n* [\n[Photovoltaic solar panel in desert]\nSolar Energy\n][51]\n* [\nGreen Building\n][52]\n* [\nAgriculture\n][53]\n* [News][54]\n* [Blog][55]\n* [Publications][56]\n* [About Us][57]\n* [Our Company][58]\n* [Company History][59]\n* [Facilities][60]\n* [Careers][61]\n* [Our Team][62]\n* [International Distributors][63]\n\n# Services\n\n## Optical Properties Measurements\n\n### [Hemispherical Directional Reflectance][64]\n\nHemispherical directional reflectance (HDR) measures the fraction of the light incident on a sample\nat a given angle that is reflected back into the hemisphere. Typical HDR measurements are made out\nto 25 \u03bcm. HDR as a function of reflected polar angle, polarization, wavelength, and temperature.\n\n[More Info][65]\n\n### Emissivity\n\nEmissivity measures a surface\u2019s thermal radiation relative to an ideal black body (0 to 1 scale). An\nemissivity of 0 indicates a perfect reflector, while 1 signifies a perfect emitter. Accurate\nemissivity is vital for non-contact temperature measurements and heat transfer calculations,\ninfluenced by material, surface, temperature, wavelength, and angle.\n\n[More INFO][66]\n\n### Scatter / BSDF\n\nBidirectional reflectance measurement capabilities span the range from 0.3 \u03bcm to beyond 14 \u03bcm with a\nfull four degrees of angular freedom (incident polar and azimuthal angle, and reflected polar and\nazimuthal angle). These measurements are typically made broadband or at a series of\ncustomer-specified wavelengths.\n\n[MORE INFO][67]\n\n### ASTM Testing\n\nASTM standards for optical property testing are developed through a collaborative process involving\nindustry and scientific experts. Surface Optics has actively contributed to defining these testing\nmethodologies, leveraging decades of experience as an optical property testing lab and\ninstrumentation manufacturer.\n\n[MORE INFO][68]\n\n### Absorptance & Emittance\n\nSurface Optics provides precise solar absorptance (\u03b1) and thermal emittance (\u03b5) measurements,\nadhering to ASTM standards for optical property testing. With decades of expertise, we deliver\nreliable data to support thermal control and material optimization across industries.\n\n[MORE INFO][69]\n\n### SRI / TSR\n\nSolar reflectance measures a material\u2019s ability to reflect solar energy, expressed as a percentage\nor a value from 0 to 1, where 0 means no reflectance and 1 indicates total reflectance. Backed by\ndecades of expertise, our lab ensures accurate, reliable solar reflectance data to support your\nproject\u2019s success.\n\n[MORE INFO][70]\n\n## Vacuum Deposition Coatings\n\n### Vacuum Deposited Gold (VDG)\n\nOur VDG coating processes have been certified by major aerospace corporations such as Northrup\nGrumman, Lockheed Martin, JPL, and Raytheon. Coatings can be modified to enhance reflection,\ndurability, and wavelength range.\n\n[MORE INFO][71]\n\n### Anti-Reflection (AR)\n\nAnti-reflection coatings are designed to minimize reflection and maximize light transmission across\nspecified wavelength ranges. These coatings can be tailored to improve optical performance,\ndurability, and environmental resistance for a variety of applications.\n\n[More Info][72]\n\n### Spaceflight & Thermal Control\n\nOver 30 years of expertise in precision thermal control and reflectance coatings for critical\nspaceflight hardware. From design to completion, capabilities include specialized fixturing and safe\nprocessing of aerospace components.\n\n[More INFO][73]\n\n### Vacuum Deposited Aluminum (VDA)\n\nWe offer standard, enhanced, or protected aluminum coating on your substrate. Our in-house design\nand measurement capabilities allow for customized VDA coatings for your substrate and application.\n\n[MORE INFO][74]\n\n### Low Observable / Stealth\n\nWe use optical coating expertise to create unique, spectrally tailored paints. Releasable PVD thin\nfilm coatings are processed into spectrally tailored flake pigment. Wavelength-dependent reflectance\nand absorption can be customized to customer requirements using design principles of optical\ninterference coatings.\n\n[MORE INFO][75]\n\n### Large Area\n\nElectron beam (Ebeam) evaporation or physical vapor deposition (PVD) process to coat large area\ncoatings up to 2.5-3m in diameter (depending on geometry) in a batch system, or 60\u201d wide in our Roll\nto Roll system.\n\n[MORE INFO][76]\n\n### Roll-to-Roll\n\nunique roll-to-roll coating process was developed in-house for Electron Beam, Jori Source and Ion\nAssisted Deposition (IAD) of metallic and dielectric films (all processes scalable).\n\n[MORE INFO][77]\n\n### Diamond-Like Carbon\n\nDiamond-like carbon (DLC) coatings have a broad range of industrial applications due to their\nsuperior mechanical properties such as high hardness, low friction, and promising wear resistance.\nOur DLC coatings are low absorption protective coating with little shift. Deposited using a Filtered\nCathodic Arc Instrument.\n\n[MORE INFO][78]\n\n### High Reflectance\n\nCustom coatings developed per customer requirements. Multilayer design engineering and coating\nability allow SOC to create custom designs for your application. Vacuum deposition Electron Beam\ntechnology is used to minimize weight addition to your substrate.\n\n[MORE INFO][79]\n\n## Custom Engineering\n\n### Electro-Optics Engineering\n\nOur electro-optics engineering services cover full product development \u2013 from feasibility studies\nthrough prototyping and production. Surface Optics has over twenty years of R&D program experience,\nspecializing in custom industrial infrared spectroscopy and imaging spectroscopy systems.\n\n[MORE INFO][80]\n\n### SBIR/STTR\n\nAwarded our first SBIR Phase I contract in 1986, since then Surface Optics has consistently turned\nSBIR R&D efforts into market-ready solutions. We welcome potential STTR partners to collaborate with\nus on cutting-edge research.\n\n[MORE INFO][81]\n[[Surface Optics Corporation]][82]\n\nHave questions?\n* [ 1-858-675-7404][83]\n* [ Email Us][84]\n* [ Support][85]\n* [Products][86]\n* [Services][87]\n* [Applications][88]\n* [News][89]\n* [About Us][90]\n\n\u00a9 Surface Optics Corporation | [Privacy Policy][91] | [Terms & Conditions][92]\n\n[1]: tel:+18586757404\n[2]: https://surfaceoptics.com/contact/\n[3]: https://surfaceoptics.com/support/\n[4]: https://surfaceoptics.com\n[5]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/\n[6]: https://surfaceoptics.com/lab-reflectometers/\n[7]: https://surfaceoptics.com/lab-reflectometers/soc-100-hdr/\n[8]: https://surfaceoptics.com/lab-reflectometers/soc-210-bidirectional-reflectometer/\n[9]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/410-series/\n[10]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/410-series/410-dhr-reflectometer/\n[11]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/410-series/410-vis-ir-reflectometer/\n[12]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/410-series/410-solar-reflectometer/\n[13]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/410-series/410-solar-i-reflectometer/\n[14]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/410-series/et-10-emissometer/\n[15]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/410-series/et100-emissometer/\n[16]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/410-series/410-lidar-reflectometer/\n[17]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/410-series/custom-soc410-reflectometers/\n[18]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/410-series/accessories-maintenance/\n[19]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/spectral-imaging-systems/\n[20]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/spectral-imaging-systems/710-series-hyperspectral-cameras/\n[21]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/spectral-imaging-systems/lightshift-multispectral-video-cam\nera/\n[22]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/spectral-imaging-systems/duochrome-sm/\n[23]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/spectral-imaging-systems/soc-750-midwave-infrared-hyperspec\ntral-imager/\n[24]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/spectral-imaging-systems/soc-760/\n[25]: https://surfaceoptics.com/products/spectral-imaging-systems/resources/\n[26]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/\n[27]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/optical-properties-measurements/\n[28]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/optical-properties-measurements/hemispherical-directional-r\neflectance/\n[29]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/optical-properties-measurements/emissivity-measurements/\n[30]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/optical-properties-measurements/brdf-scatter/\n[31]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/optical-properties-measurements/transmittance-measurements/\n[32]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/optical-properties-measurements/astm-testing/\n[33]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/optical-properties-measurements/solar-reflectance-sri-tsr/\n[34]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/optical-properties-measurements/solar-absorptance-thermal-e\nmittance/\n[35]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/optical-properties-measurements/database/\n[36]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/vacuum-deposition-coatings/\n[37]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/vacuum-deposition-coatings/low-observable-stealth-coatings/\n[38]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/vacuum-deposition-coatings/large-area-coatings/\n[39]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/vacuum-deposition-coatings/roll-to-roll-coatings/\n[40]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/vacuum-deposition-coatings/diamond-like-carbon-coating/\n[41]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/vacuum-deposition-coatings/vacuum-deposited-gold-vdg-coatin\ngs/\n[42]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/vacuum-deposition-coatings/antireflection-ar-coatings/\n[43]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/vacuum-deposition-coatings/vacuum-deposited-aluminum-coatin\ngs/\n[44]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/vacuum-deposition-coatings/spaceflight-and-thermal-control-\ncoatings/\n[45]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/vacuum-deposition-coatings/high-reflectance-coatings/\n[46]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/electro-optics-engineering/\n[47]: https://surfaceoptics.com/services/electro-optics-engineering/sbir-sttr/\n[48]: https://surfaceoptics.com/applications/\n[49]: https://surfaceoptics.com/applications/space/\n[50]: https://surfaceoptics.com/applications/defense/\n[51]: https://surfaceoptics.com/applications/solar-energy/\n[52]: https://surfaceoptics.com/applications/green-building/\n[53]: https://surfaceoptics.com/applications/agriculture/\n[54]: https://surfaceoptics.com/news/\n[55]: https://surfaceoptics.com/news/\n[56]: https://surfaceoptics.com/publications/\n[57]: https://surfaceoptics.com/company/\n[58]: https://surfaceoptics.com/company/\n[59]: https://surfaceoptics.com/company/company-history/\n[60]: https://surfaceoptics.com/company/facilities/\n[61]: https://surfaceoptics.com/company/careers/\n[62]: https://surfaceoptics.com/company/meet-our-team/\n[63]: htt"
