72]\n* [ Display backlighting ][73]\n* [ Projection ][74]\n* [ Smart surface ][75]\n* [ Ambient light sensing ][76]\n* [ In-cabin sensing ][77]\n* [ Drivetrain, chassis & body sensing ][78]\n* [ Position & angle sensing ][79]\n* [ Battery management system ][80]\n* [ Automotive aftermarket ][81]\n* [ Industrial ][82]\n* [ Industrial ][83]\n* [ Function block diagrams ][84]\n* [ Robotics ][85]\n* [ Home & building automation ][86]\n* [ Factory automation ][87]\n* [ Material processing ][88]\n* [ Projection & display ][89]\n* [ Industrial & security x-ray ][90]\n* [ Appliances & tools ][91]\n* [ Access control & security ][92]\n* [ UV-C disinfection & treatment ][93]\n* [ Medical & health ][94]\n* [ Medical & health ][95]\n* [ Medical imaging ][96]\n* [ Digital diagnostic devices ][97]\n* [ Medical lighting ][98]\n* [ Mobile & wearables ][99]\n* [ Mobile & wearables ][100]\n* [ Display management ][101]\n* [ Visualization ][102]\n* [ Authentication ][103]\n* [ Camera enhancement ][104]\n* [ 3D sensing ][105]\n* [ Eye, face and hand tracking ][106]\n* [ Vital sign monitoring ][107]\n* [ Lighting ][108]\n* [ Lighting ][109]\n* [ Agriculture & horticulture ][110]\n* [ Outdoor & industrial lighting ][111]\n* [ Indoor lighting ][112]\n* [ Entertainment ][113]\n* [ Computing ][114]\n* [ Innovation ][115]\n* [ Innovation ][116]\n* [ Optical force sensing ][117]\n* [ Photon counting ][118]\n* [ IR LED IR:6 ][119]\n* [ LED on foil technology ][120]\n* [ Open System Protocol ][121]\n* [ Technology ][122]\n* [ Newsroom ][123]\n* [ Newsroom ][124]\n* [ Press lounge ][125]\n* [ Media assets ][126]\n* [ Events ][127]\n* [ Awards ][128]\n* [ Careers ][129]\n* [ Support & Services ][130]\n* [ Support & Services ][131]\n* [ Download center ][132]\n* [ Product support ][133]\n* [ Design support ][134]\n* [ Technical support ][135]\n* [ Partner network ][136]\n* [ About us ][137]\n* [ About us ][138]\n* [ Investor relations ][139]\n* [ Investor relations ][140]\n* [ Financial news ][141]\n* [ Reports and presentations ][142]\n* [ Share trading information ][143]\n* [ Analyst estimates ][144]\n* [ Investor calendar ][145]\n* [ Share capital ][146]\n* [ Fixed income / public debt ][147]\n* [ General meeting ][148]\n* [ Corporate governance ][149]\n* [ Investor relations contacts ][150]\n* [ OSRAM investor relations ][151]\n* [ Executive committee ][152]\n* [ Executive committee ][153]\n* [ Aldo Kamper ][154]\n* [ Rainer Irle ][155]\n* [ Mark Hamersma ][156]\n* [ Jens Milnikel ][157]\n* [ Adam Wu ][158]\n* [ Supervisory board ][159]\n* [ Sustainability ][160]\n* [ Sustainability ][161]\n* [ Environment ][162]\n* [ Society ][163]\n* [ Governance ][164]\n* [ Sustainability documents ][165]\n* [ Product stewardship ][166]\n* [ Public funded r&d ][167]\n* [ Public funded r&d ][168]\n* [ European projects ][169]\n* [ National projects ][170]\n* [ IPCEI ][171]\n* [ Locations & distribution ][172]\n* [ Locations & distribution ][173]\n* [ Headquarters ][174]\n* [ Design, application & test centers ][175]\n* [ Channel partners ][176]\n* [ Sales offices & branches ][177]\n\u2014 [ Login ][178] \u2014\n[english][179] [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e][180] [deutsch][181] [\ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4][182]\n\u2014 [ams-osram.com][183] [ams-osram.cn (\u4e2d\u6587)][184] \u2014\n* [ Products ][185]\n* [ Sensor solutions ][186]\n* Ambient light, color, spectral & proximity sensors\n[ ][187] [ ][188]\n**Choose your language:**\n[english][189] [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e][190] [deutsch][191] [\ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4][192]\n** Choose your site: ** [ams-osram.com][193] [ams-osram.cn (\u4e2d\u6587)][194]\n[ ][195]\n* [ Products ][196]\n* [ Sensor solutions ][197]\n* Ambient light, color, spectral & proximity sensors\n\n# Ambient light, color, spectral & proximity sensors\n\nIndustry's broadest portfolio of high-performance and high-sensitivity digital discrete and\nintegrated module optical sensors including ambient light sensors, RGB and XYZ color sensors, and\nspectral sensors.\n\n## Our ALS, color, spectral & proximity sensors portfolio\n\n[Ambient light sensors][198]\n[Color sensors][199]\n[Ambient light sensors & proximity detection][200]\n[Color sensors & proximity detection][201]\n[Spectral sensing][202]\n[Spectral sensing white paper][203]\n[Proximity sensors][204]\n\n## Ambient light, color & spectral sensors\n\nOur ambient light, color and spectral sensors are the perfect example of how ams OSRAM brings\nintelligence to light and passion to innovation. We develop leading-edge optical technologies that\nenable our customers to create innovative solutions that open new markets. With many successfully\ndeveloped for mobile & wearable devices, our ALS, color and spectral sensors, are ubiquitous across\na growing number of fields as the megatrends of digitalization and energy efficiency drive demand\nfor these products.\n\nThe core competence of ams OSRAM in complex, highest volume optical modules like these is unmatched\nin the industry. The significant level of integration we undertake, for example light sensor\nintegration at package and wafer level, drives an increase in performance among other benefits. Our\nwide and deep technology portfolio from light source, optical path and package to IC and\nsoftware/algorithms, enables differentiated products and integrated solutions across the value\nchain.\n\n[Select product][205]\n[A hand holding a smartphone with colorful blurred lights in the background.]\n\n## Ambient light sensors\n\nThe ambient light sensor (ALS) products provide measurements of ambient light intensity which\nmatches the human eye response to light under a variety of lighting conditions. Each device has a\nspecific operating range of performance, lux measurement, from extremely low light up to bright\nsunlight.\n\nHigh sensitivity coupled with wide dynamic range make these ALS products ideal for operation behind\ndark inked glass. They enable consumer electronics device manufacturers to implement display dimming\nand brightness control functions, helping to reduce power consumption and extend battery run-time,\nand improving the overall user experience.\n\n[Select product][206]\n[A round digital device displaying the date, time, and several icons on its screen.]\n\n## Color sensors\n\nThe color sensors provide both ambient light intensity (lux) as well as light correlated color\ntemperature (CCT). The color sensor product family includes both RGB (Red, Green, Blue) and\nhigh-accuracy XYZ light sensors for precise color measurement, determination, and discrimination.\nXYZ sensors are capable of providing xy chromaticity coordinates in accordance with the CIE 1931\ncolor map.\n\nThe color sensors include filters to block unwanted IR light, enabling highly accurate color\nmeasurement. Their high sensitivity coupled with their wide dynamic range make them well suited to\ncontinuous CCT measurement of ambient light in display management systems, and\nautomatic-white-balance assistance in camera applications. Some products have additional IR channels\nto assist with IR light source identification.\n\n[Select product][207]\n[A person filming a public talk]\n\n## Ambient light sensors & proximity detection\n\nams OSRAM supplies a family of products which combine an ambient light sensor (ALS) and proximity\ndetection in a single device. The ALS provides measurements of ambient light intensity which matches\nthe human eye\u2019s response to light under a variety of lighting conditions.\n\nThe proximity detection feature allows a large dynamic range of operation for use over short\ndistances and behind dark glass. These devices are intended for use in mobile phones, and over\nlonger distances for presence detection in computer displays and monitors.\n\n[Select product][208]\n[A hand interacting with graphical data on a screen, suggesting sensor-based input or analysis.]\n\n## Color sensors & proximity detection\n\nThe ams OSRAM family of color and ambient light sensing (ALS) sensors combined with proximity\ndetection provides red, green, blue, and clear (RGBC) or green and clear (ALS) light sensing and\nproximity detection. These modules also contain an IR LED or VCSEL for the proximity function.\n\nBoth the light and proximity sensing functions feature high sensitivity and a wide dynamic range, so\nthese devices may be placed behind the dark bezels of smartphones, monitors, laptops, tablets and\nTVs.\n\n[Select product][209]\n[Two people interacting, one holding a yellow object, with blurred faces.]\n\n## Spectral sensing\n\nThe multi-spectral sensing family includes a broad array of spectral sensing devices providing\nbetween 6 and 18 channels in the visible and near-infrared spectrum. All products feature\ninterference filters directly deposited on photodiodes to deliver precise spectral characteristics.\nMost include direct LED drivers to synchronize and control light sources for efficient external\nlight source operation.\n\nChip-scale spectral sensing solutions from ams OSRAM enable designers to implement a broad range of\nnew applications such as: advanced color detection, smoke type detection, optimization in\nhorticulture, authentication, and color and spectral analysis of materials and fluids.\n\n[Select product][210]\n[Two people interacting, one holding a yellow object, with blurred faces.]\n\n## Spectral sensing white paper\n\n## Register for our white paper about spectral sensing\n\nForm loading...\n\nEnter your data and register for the white paper. In the white paper, we mention the applications\nUV-C Treatment, Horticulture, Smoke Detection, Fresh Fruitiness measurement, Healthy indoor\nlighting, Environment Awareness in wearable devices, Material detection and surface monitoring.\nI agree to the processing of my data for registration purposes, as described in [privacy\npolicy][211].* I would like ams OSRAM to use my e-mail address for the purposes of personalised and\ngeneralized advertising and marketing communication related to the products of ams OSRAM.\n\nYour data is used only for internal purposes related to the registration process.\n\n*All fields marked with an asterisk(*) must be filled in.*\n\n## Proximity sensors\n\nams OSRAM proximity sensors function by pulsing an IR emitter, which can be either an [Infrared\nLight Emitting Diode (IR-LED)][212] or a [Vertical Cavity Surface Emitting Laser (VCSEL)][213], and\nmeasuring the reflected energy returned from a target. The amount of refle"
          },
