]\n* [ Reports and presentations ][142]\n* [ Share trading information ][143]\n* [ Analyst estimates ][144]\n* [ Investor calendar ][145]\n* [ Share capital ][146]\n* [ Fixed income / public debt ][147]\n* [ General meeting ][148]\n* [ Corporate governance ][149]\n* [ Investor relations contacts ][150]\n* [ OSRAM investor relations ][151]\n* [ Executive committee ][152]\n* [ Executive committee ][153]\n* [ Aldo Kamper ][154]\n* [ Rainer Irle ][155]\n* [ Mark Hamersma ][156]\n* [ Jens Milnikel ][157]\n* [ Adam Wu ][158]\n* [ Supervisory board ][159]\n* [ Sustainability ][160]\n* [ Sustainability ][161]\n* [ Environment ][162]\n* [ Society ][163]\n* [ Governance ][164]\n* [ Sustainability documents ][165]\n* [ Product stewardship ][166]\n* [ Public funded r&d ][167]\n* [ Public funded r&d ][168]\n* [ European projects ][169]\n* [ National projects ][170]\n* [ IPCEI ][171]\n* [ Locations & distribution ][172]\n* [ Locations & distribution ][173]\n* [ Headquarters ][174]\n* [ Design, application & test centers ][175]\n* [ Channel partners ][176]\n* [ Sales offices & branches ][177]\n\u2014 [ Login ][178] \u2014\n[english][179] [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e][180] [deutsch][181] [\ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4][182]\n\u2014 [ams-osram.com][183] [ams-osram.cn (\u4e2d\u6587)][184] \u2014\n* [ Products ][185]\n* [ Sensor solutions ][186]\n* CMOS image sensors\n[ ][187] [ ][188]\n**Choose your language:**\n[english][189] [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e][190] [deutsch][191] [\ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4][192]\n** Choose your site: ** [ams-osram.com][193] [ams-osram.cn (\u4e2d\u6587)][194]\n[ ][195]\n* [ Products ][196]\n* [ Sensor solutions ][197]\n* CMOS image sensors\n\n# CMOS image sensors\n\nInnovative small form factor, high sensitivity and power efficient CMOS image sensors.\n\n[Download white paper][198]\n\n## Our CMOS image sensor solutions\n\n[Mira image sensor][199]\n[Miniature camera modules][200]\n[Area scan sensors][201]\n[Line scan sensors][202]\n[CMOS image sensors white paper][203]\n\n## Mira image sensor\n\nOur compact [global shutter image sensors][204] with back side illuminated stacked pixel technology\nadvance 2D and [3D vision systems][205] with market leading quantum efficiency at visible and NIR\nwavelengths.\n\nLow-power design paired with highest quantum efficiency qualifies the sensor for power critical\napplication as it achieves superior image quality even in dim lighting conditions.\n\nAdvanced on-chip noise reduction enables impressive quality already on raw image which further\nreduces algorithmic correction load on the image signal processor (ISP).\n\nMira image sensors with MONO, RGB or RGB-IR filter options are the ideal solution for a wide range\nof applications: [AR/VR glasses][206]; drones, [robots][207], biometric door locks and diverse\n[factory automation][208] setups.\n\nFor further details check the following Mira product pages\n* [Mira-220, 1600 x 1400 Pixel][209]\n* [Mira-050, 600 x 800 Pixel][210]\n* [Mira-016, 400 x 400 Pixel][211]\n\nAdditional information on Mira image sensor technology can be found at our [CMOS image sensing\ntechnology page][212]. Fully integrated image sensor modules are available on demand or via\nqualified partners [ams OSRAM partner network][213].\n[Select product][214] [Read our blog post about Mira Family image sensors][215]\n\n## NanEye - Miniature camera modules\n\n[NanEye miniature camera modules][216] are ultra small, fully integrated digital camera module\nconfigurations. They are provided as camera head with integrated cable, which is customizable\nlength, or PCB solderable product variant. NanEye digital camera modules are available with various\nlens and filter options and fit ideal in various applications, like [medical endoscopes][217],\ninspection tools, [AR/VR headsets][218], mini-drones or [robotics][219].\n\nWith a footprint of a just 1 mm\u00b2, it features a 320x320 resolution with a high sensitive 2.4-micron\nrolling shutter pixel, with large full well capacitance. The sensor has a high frame rate of about\n58 fps to permit SNR enhancement and a smooth, low delay display over a wide range of standard\ninterfaces. Additionally, the frame rate can be set as low as 1 fps for use of extended exposure\ntime and lower power consumption.\n\nThe Naneye can drive the signal through a cable length of up to 3 m.\n\nFor further details check the following NanEye product pages\n* [NanEyeM][220]: miniature camera with integrated cabling (or watch [NanEyeM video][221])\n* [NanEyeC][222]: miniature camera with 4-pad solder option (or watch [NanEyeC video][223])\n\nAdditional information on NanEye miniature camera technology can be found on our [CMOS image sensing\ntechnology page][224]. Customized miniature camera modules are available on demand. Find also\nready-made system solutions via qualified partners at [ams OSRAM partner network][225].\n\n[Select product][226]\n[Three colored pencils next to two NanEye miniature camera modules with wires, emphasizing their\nextremely small size.]\n\n## Area scan sensors\n\nThe ams OSRAM family of pipelined global shutter sensors features high frame rates for a wide range\nof demanding professional and industrial applications. Their resolutions range from 2Mpixels up to\n20Mpixels. Rolling shutter image sensors feature high 71Mpixel resolution for use in demanding\nindustrial applications.\n\n[Select product][227]\n[Area scan sensors]\n\n## Line scan sensors\n\nThe CMOS line scan image sensor family from ams OSRAM consists of 23 variants, offering a range of\nresolution and pixel size specifications. Resolution options range from 2kpixels up to 16kpixels and\nline rates extend up to 120,000 lines/s with the new 4LS product family.\n\n[Select product][228]\n[Line scan sensors]\n\n## CMOS image sensors product list\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDevice name\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nDescription\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nProduct Area\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nProduct Type\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nResolution\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nShutter type\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nFrame rate max.\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nOptical format\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nPixel pitch/Pixel pitch X\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nPixel pitch/Pixel pitch Y\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nFunction\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nCRA\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nPackage\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nPackage dimension/Package dimension height typ.\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nPackage dimension/Package dimension length typ.\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nPackage dimension/Package dimension width typ.\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nCover glass\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nCFA option\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nADC mode\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nChannels/Output channels output\n////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\nInterface output\n///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////"
