]\n* [ Reports and presentations ][142]\n* [ Share trading information ][143]\n* [ Analyst estimates ][144]\n* [ Investor calendar ][145]\n* [ Share capital ][146]\n* [ Fixed income / public debt ][147]\n* [ General meeting ][148]\n* [ Corporate governance ][149]\n* [ Investor relations contacts ][150]\n* [ OSRAM investor relations ][151]\n* [ Executive committee ][152]\n* [ Executive committee ][153]\n* [ Aldo Kamper ][154]\n* [ Rainer Irle ][155]\n* [ Mark Hamersma ][156]\n* [ Jens Milnikel ][157]\n* [ Adam Wu ][158]\n* [ Supervisory board ][159]\n* [ Sustainability ][160]\n* [ Sustainability ][161]\n* [ Environment ][162]\n* [ Society ][163]\n* [ Governance ][164]\n* [ Sustainability documents ][165]\n* [ Product stewardship ][166]\n* [ Public funded r&d ][167]\n* [ Public funded r&d ][168]\n* [ European projects ][169]\n* [ National projects ][170]\n* [ IPCEI ][171]\n* [ Locations & distribution ][172]\n* [ Locations & distribution ][173]\n* [ Headquarters ][174]\n* [ Design, application & test centers ][175]\n* [ Channel partners ][176]\n* [ Sales offices & branches ][177]\n\u2014 [ Login ][178] \u2014\n[english][179] [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e][180] [deutsch][181] [\ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4][182]\n\u2014 [ams-osram.com][183] [ams-osram.cn (\u4e2d\u6587)][184] \u2014\n* [ Products ][185]\n* [ Sensor solutions ][186]\n* Direct time-of-flight sensors (dToF)\n[ ][187] [ ][188]\n**Choose your language:**\n[english][189] [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e][190] [deutsch][191] [\ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4][192]\n** Choose your site: ** [ams-osram.com][193] [ams-osram.cn (\u4e2d\u6587)][194]\n[ ][195]\n* [ Products ][196]\n* [ Sensor solutions ][197]\n* Direct time-of-flight sensors (dToF)\n\n# direct Time-of-Flight sensors (dToF)\n\nLow-power time-of-flight sensing technology from ams OSRAM enables host systems to measure distances\naccurately and at extreme speed.\n\n[Download dtoF whitepaper][198]\n[Single-zone dToF webinar][199]\n[Multi-zone sensing webinar][200]\n[Time-of-Flight sensors whitepaper][201]\n\n## direct Time-of-Flight (dToF) sensors\n\nams OSRAM direct Time-of-Flight (dToF) sensors offer fast, precise distance measurement up to 11\nmeters, in a compact fully integrated module. Available in both single and multi-zone\nconfigurations, these devices provide solutions for a wide range of distance measurement\napplications including Laser Detect Auto Focus (LDAF) for mobile, human presence detection for\nenhanced security and power saving in computing, electronic locks & authentication systems and\nobstacle detection and collision avoidance for home and industrial robots.\n\nams OSRAM direct Time-of-Flight (dToF) sensors are based on proprietary SPAD (Single Photon\nAvalanche Photodiode) pixel design and time-to-digital converters (TDCs) which have an extremely\nnarrow pulse width. They measure in real time the direct time-of-flight (dToF) of a 940nm VCSEL\nVertical Cavity Surface Emitting Laser) emitter\u2019s infrared ray reflected from an object.\n* Multi-zone dToF sensor [TMF8829][202]\n* Single-zone dToF sensor [TMF8806][203]\n\n[Select product][204]\n\n## High-resolution 3D sensing with the TMF8829 multi-zone dToF sensor\n\nDiscover how precise 3D depth sensing can improve presence detection and spatial awareness in\nreal-world designs, from robotics and logistics to mobile, wearables and other smart appliances.\n\n**What you\u2019ll gain:**\n* A clear introduction to direct Time-of-Flight sensing technology\n* A deep dive into 3D depth sensing with the [TMF8829 multi-zone dToF sensor][205]: up to 48\u00d732\npixels, 11 m range, and 80\u00b0 field of view.\n* Understanding of on-chip processing for distance, confidence, and ambient light data\n* Examples of multi-object detection and AI-ready depth data in practice\n\n**Where it\u2019s used:**\n* Depth-based object detection and scene mapping\n* Gesture control for headphones and wearables\n* Smart appliances such as lawn movers or coffee machines\n* Industrial robotics, logistics, and camera autofocuus\n\nTake your chance to get a deep dive from our expert David Smith, Senior Product Marketing Manager\nfor direct Time-of-Flight products within the Integrated Optical Solutions (IOS).\n\n[Watch webinar on demand][206]\n\n## Seamless integration of single-zone direct Time-of-Flight sensors\n\nDeep-dive in seamless integration of single-zone dToF Sensors for high accuracy in ultra low power\nmode. Join us for this **engineer-to-engineer webinar** where we will explore how the [TMF8806\nsingle-zone dToF sensor][207] revolutionizes single-zone direct Time-of-Flight systems by combining\ncost-effectiveness, accuracy, and power efficiency. Our expert, David Smith, will dive into the\nsensor\u2019s innovative features, including fast start-up times, industry-leading power consumption, and\nbuilt-in firmware for seamless integration.\n\nLearn more about:\n* The simplicity in I2C commands and register-level access and how it provides ease of customization\nand the ability to future-proof your designs\n* To leverage advanced preconfigured distance modes, superior accuracy of \u00b13% beyond 200mm, and\nsimple calibration for improved manufacturability\n* How optimizing VCSEL pulse settings enhances signal quality and system performance tailored to\nyour application needs and operating conditions\n* Industry leading ultra-low power mode in active ranging\n\n[Watch webinar on demand][208]\n\n## Time-of-Flight sensors white paper\n\n## Register for our time-of-flight sensors white paper\n\nForm loading...\n\nLearn how our ranging sensors in small, surface-mount packages are spreading from mobile to\nindustrial and consumer applications.\nI agree to the processing of my data for registration purposes, as described in [privacy\npolicy][209].* I would like ams OSRAM to use my e-mail address for the purposes of personalised and\ngeneralized advertising and marketing communication related to the products of ams OSRAM.\n\nYour data is used only for internal purposes related to the registration process.\n\n*All fields marked with an asterisk(*) must be filled out.*\n\n## Direct time-of-flight sensors (dToF) product list\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\nDevic\u2502Description \u2502Pro\u2502Pro\u2502Sen\u2502Num\u2502Det\u2502Waf\u2502Fie\u2502Ope\u2502Ope\u2502Sup\u2502Sup\u2502Sup\u2502Wav\u2502Pac\u2502Pac\u2502Pac\u2502Pac\u2502Int\u2502Int\ne \u2502 \u2502duc\u2502duc\u2502sor\u2502ber\u2502ect\u2502er \u2502ld \u2502rat\u2502rat\u2502ply\u2502ply\u2502ply\u2502ele\u2502kag\u2502kag\u2502kag\u2502kag\u2502erf\u2502erf\nname \u2502 \u2502t \u2502t \u2502zon\u2502of \u2502ion\u2502lev\u2502of \u2502ing\u2502ing\u2502vol\u2502vol\u2502vol\u2502ngt\u2502e \u2502e \u2502e \u2502e \u2502ace\u2502ace\n\u2502 \u2502Are\u2502Typ\u2502es \u2502det\u2502dis\u2502el \u2502vie\u2502amb\u2502amb\u2502tag\u2502tag\u2502tag\u2502h \u2502 \u2502dim\u2502dim\u2502dim\u2502inp\u2502out\n\u2502 \u2502a \u2502e \u2502 \u2502ect\u2502tan\u2502opt\u2502w \u2502ien\u2502ien\u2502e \u2502e \u2502e \u2502 \u2502 \u2502ens\u2502ens\u2502ens\u2502ut \u2502put\n\u2502 \u2502 \u2502 \u2502 \u2502ion\u2502ce \u2502ica\u2502 \u2502t \u2502t \u2502min\u2502max\u2502typ\u2502 \u2502 \u2502ion\u2502ion\u2502ion\u2502 \u2502\n\u2502 \u2502 \u2502 \u2502 \u2502zon\u2502max\u2502l \u2502 \u2502tem\u2502tem\u2502. \u2502. \u2502. \u2502 \u2502 \u2502/Pa\u2502/Pa\u2502/Pa\u2502 \u2502\n\u2502 \u2502 \u2502 \u2502 