]\n* [ Reports and presentations ][142]\n* [ Share trading information ][143]\n* [ Analyst estimates ][144]\n* [ Investor calendar ][145]\n* [ Share capital ][146]\n* [ Fixed income / public debt ][147]\n* [ General meeting ][148]\n* [ Corporate governance ][149]\n* [ Investor relations contacts ][150]\n* [ OSRAM investor relations ][151]\n* [ Executive committee ][152]\n* [ Executive committee ][153]\n* [ Aldo Kamper ][154]\n* [ Rainer Irle ][155]\n* [ Mark Hamersma ][156]\n* [ Jens Milnikel ][157]\n* [ Adam Wu ][158]\n* [ Supervisory board ][159]\n* [ Sustainability ][160]\n* [ Sustainability ][161]\n* [ Environment ][162]\n* [ Society ][163]\n* [ Governance ][164]\n* [ Sustainability documents ][165]\n* [ Product stewardship ][166]\n* [ Public funded r&d ][167]\n* [ Public funded r&d ][168]\n* [ European projects ][169]\n* [ National projects ][170]\n* [ IPCEI ][171]\n* [ Locations & distribution ][172]\n* [ Locations & distribution ][173]\n* [ Headquarters ][174]\n* [ Design, application & test centers ][175]\n* [ Channel partners ][176]\n* [ Sales offices & branches ][177]\n\u2014 [ Login ][178] \u2014\n[english][179] [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e][180] [deutsch][181] [\ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4][182]\n\u2014 [ams-osram.com][183] [ams-osram.cn (\u4e2d\u6587)][184] \u2014\n* [ Products ][185]\n* [ Sensor solutions ][186]\n* Optical force sensors\n[ ][187] [ ][188]\n**Choose your language:**\n[english][189] [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e][190] [deutsch][191] [\ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4][192]\n** Choose your site: ** [ams-osram.com][193] [ams-osram.cn (\u4e2d\u6587)][194]\n[ ][195]\n* [ Products ][196]\n* [ Sensor solutions ][197]\n* Optical force sensors\n\n# Optical force sensors\n\nHigh performance optical force sensors for reliable force, touch, and proximity sensing in modern\nhuman machine interfaces.\n\n[Explore your solutions][198]\n\n## Optical force sensor portfolio\n\nOptical force sensors from ams OSRAM enable intuitive, reliable, and design flexible human machine\ninterfaces by measuring force induced surface deformation with light. Using an optically isolated\nemitter detector principle, they precisely distinguish soft, medium, and hard presses and can also\nsupport touch and proximity functions on infrared transparent surfaces with a broad usage in\nautomotive, consumer, and home & building automation applications fields.\nThe Integrated Optical Force Sensor combines low noise photodiode readout, a synchronized infrared\nemitter, temperature sensing, and advanced signal processing in an ultra compact package. This\narchitecture ensures accurate force detection with ambient light suppression, crosstalk\ncancellation, and smart communication for stable and reliable operation\u2014even in harsh environments.\n\nWith no mechanical components or electrical contact to the surface, the sensors integrate seamlessly\nbehind metal, glass, or plastic panels. The result is robust, hygienic, and water resistant control\ninterfaces with high design flexibility. These sensors are ideal for multimodal control elements in\nautomotive, industrial, consumer, and smart surface applications requiring durability, precision,\nand compact integration.\n\n[Select products][199]\nJoin our Newsletter [ Subscribe ][200]\nHidden\n[ ][201]\n\nams-OSRAM AG\nTobelbader Stra\u00dfe 30\n8141 Premstaetten\nAustria\n\nPhone: [+43 3136 500-0][202]\n\n[About ams OSRAM][203]\n* [Newsroom][204]\n* [Investor relations][205]\n* [Sustainability][206]\n* [Locations & distribution][207]\n* [Careers][208]\n* [Accessibility][209]\n\n[Support][210]\n* [Product Selector][211]\n* [Download center][212]\n* [Tools][213]\n* [Customer queries][214]\n* [Technical support][215]\n* [Partner network][216]\n* [Whistleblowing][217]\n\n\u00a9 2026 ams-OSRAM AG. All rights reserved.\n* [Privacy policy][218]\n* [Terms of use][219]\n* [Terms of trade][220]\n* [Imprint][221]\n* [Cookie policy][222]\n* [AI Policy][223]\n* [\u7ca4ICP\u590710066670\u53f7][224]\n* [ ][225]\n* [ ][226]\n* [ ][227]\n* [ ][228]\n* [ 