        "crawl_text": "[\n[Spectricity Logo]\n[Spectricity Logo]\n][1]\n* [Home][2]\n* [Products][3]\n* [Technology][4]\n* [Applications][5]\n  * [Automatic White Balance (AWB)][6]\n* [Newsroom][7]\n* [About Us][8]\n  * [Vision & Mission][9]\n  * [Management Team][10]\n  * [Partners][11]\n  * [Careers][12]\n* [Contact][13]\n* [\u7b80\u4f53\u4e2d\u6587][14]\n\n# Sensing beyond what\u2019s visible.\n\n## Spectricity provides multispectral imaging solutions to enhance color accuracy and analysis\n## capabilities in mobile and consumer electronics.\n\n[Spectricity Lo]\n\n## Your smartphoneis color blind.\n\n### Look at these images of the same scene, captured using the world's most popular flagship phone.\n### The camera's white balancing algorithms easily get confused, failing to produce accurate colors.\n\n[AWB fails to produce accurate colors]\n\n## Meet thenext generationof sensing\n\n### Tiny chip-size multispectral image sensors for unimaginable new applications.\n\n[Discover Our Product][15]\n[Meet the next generation of sensing]\n\n### News\n\n[\n][16]\n\n### [Hyperspectral vs Multispectral Imaging: Understanding the Difference and Choosing the Right\n### Technology for Mobile Devices][17]\n\n2026-04-23\n\nExplore how multispectral and hyperspectral imaging capture and analyze light differently, and\nunderstand their roles across a wide range of applications.\n\n[Read More][18]\n\n[\n[MWC 2026]][19]\n\n### [Spectricity at MWC 2026: Elevating Mobile Spectral Vision][20]\n\n2026-02-12\n\nWe are exhibiting at MWC 2026, showcasing mobile-ready multispectral imaging demos. Visit us to\nexplore applications in wound monitoring, skin analysis, and local AWB.\n\n[Read More][21]\n\n[\n[Photonics West 2026 Website Banner]][22]\n\n### [Catch Spectricity at Photonics West 2026!][23]\n\n2026-01-06\n\nWe will showcase cutting-edge demos at Photonics West 2026: wound monitoring, skin analysis demo,\nand local AWB. All demos are powered by Spectricity\u2019s miniaturized, mobile-ready multispectral\nimaging technology.\n\n[Read More][24]\n\n[Product Portfolio]\n\n### Product Offering\n\n#### **S1 Multispectral Image Sensor**\n\nCore Innovation: Miniaturized and Mass-manufacturable\n\n#### **S1-M Camera Module**\n\nSmall Form Factor Integration\n\n#### **S1-A Accessory Device**\n\nPlug-n-Play Mobile Solution\n\n[Learn More][25]\n[Product Portfolio Mobile]\n\n### S1-A Accessory Device\n\nPlug-n-Play Multispectral Imaging on Mobile Platforms\n\n#### [About Us][26]\n\nSpectricity is a fabless company creating multispectral imaging solutions for high-volume and mobile\ndevices, using CMOS technologies.\n\n[Read More][27]\n\n#### [Careers][28]\n\nWe are hiring.\u00a0We\u2019re looking for innovative minds that want to be part of the future of\nsemiconductors and sensing to better the world.\n\n[Read More][29]\n[[Atlantic Bridge]][30]\n[[Capricorn]][31]\n[[Flanders Investment & Trade]][32]\n[[Flanders Semiconductors]][33]\n[[Garlick & Markison]][34]\n[[Imec]][35]\n[[Imec Xpand]][36]\n[[Lululab]][37]\n[[Namuga]][38]\n[[PDSTI]][39]\n[[Qualcomm]][40]\n[[VLAIO]][41]\n[[Xfab]][42]\n[[Sensinnovat]][43]\n[[University of East Anglia]][44]\n[[UCD Dublin]][45]\n[Spectricity Logo]\n[Spectricity Logo]\n\nSpectricity\nStationsstraat 55\nB-2800 Mechelen\nBelgium\n\n[[email\u00a0protected]][46]\n\n[Home][47]\n[Products][48]\n[Technology][49]\n[Applications][50]\n[Newsroom][51]\n\n[About Us][52]\n\u2013[Vision & Mission][53]\n\u2013[Management Team][54]\n\u2013[Partners][55]\n\u2013[Careers][56]\n[Contact][57]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Spectricity NV \u2013 BE 0685.594.317 \u2013 [Privacy Policy][58]\n\nWe are using cookies to give you the best experience on our website.\n\nYou can find out more about which cookies we are using or switch them off in settings.\n\nAccept\nClose GDPR Cookie Settings\n[Spectricity]\n* Privacy Overview\n* Strictly Necessary Cookies\n* Analytics\n[Powered by\u00a0 GDPR Cookie Compliance][59]\nPrivacy Overview\n\nThis website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience possible. Cookie\ninformation is stored in your browser and performs functions such as recognising you when you return\nto our website and helping our team to understand which sections of the website you find most\ninteresting and useful.\n\nStrictly Necessary Cookies\n\nStrictly Necessary Cookie should be enabled at all times so that we can save your preferences for\ncookie settings.\n\nEnable or Disable Cookies Enabled Disabled\nAnalytics\n\nThis website uses Google Analytics to collect anonymous information such as the number of visitors\nto the site, and the most popular pages.\n\nKeeping this cookie enabled helps us to improve our website.\n\nEnable or Disable Cookies Enabled Disabled\nEnable All Save Settings\n\n[1]: https://spectricity.com/\n[2]: https://spectricity.com/\n[3]: https://spectricity.com/products/\n[4]: https://spectricity.com/technology/\n[5]: https://spectricity.com/applications/\n[6]: https://spectricity.com/applications/awb/\n[7]: https://spectricity.com/news/\n[8]: https://spectricity.com/about-us/\n[9]: https://spectricity.com/about-us/mission-vision/\n[10]: https://spectricity.com/about-us/management-team/\n[11]: https://spectricity.com/about-us/partners/\n[12]: https://spectricity.com/about-us/careers/\n[13]: ht [\n[Spectricity Logo]\n[Spectricity Logo]\n][1]\n* [Home][2]\n* [Products][3]\n* [Technology][4]\n* [Applications][5]\n  * [Automatic White Balance (AWB)][6]\n* [Newsroom][7]\n* [About Us][8]\n  * [Vision & Mission][9]\n  * [Management Team][10]\n  * [Partners][11]\n  * [Careers][12]\n* [Contact][13]\n* [\u7b80\u4f53\u4e2d\u6587][14]\n\n# Sensing beyond what\u2019s visible.\n\n## Spectricity provides multispectral imaging solutions to enhance color accuracy and analysis\n## capabilities in mobile and consumer electronics.\n\n[Spectricity Lo]\n\n## Your smartphoneis color blind.\n\n### Look at these images of the same scene, captured using the world's most popular flagship phone.\n### The camera's white balancing algorithms easily get confused, failing to produce accurate colors.\n\n[AWB fails to produce accurate colors]\n\n## Meet thenext generationof sensing\n\n### Tiny chip-size multispectral image sensors for unimaginable new applications.\n\n[Discover Our Product][15]\n[Meet the next generation of sensing]\n\n### News\n\n[\n][16]\n\n### [Hyperspectral vs Multispectral Imaging: Understanding the Difference and Choosing the Right\n### Technology for Mobile Devices][17]\n\n2026-04-23\n\nExplore how multispectral and hyperspectral imaging capture and analyze light differently, and\nunderstand their roles across a wide range of applications.\n\n[Read More][18]\n\n[\n[MWC 2026]][19]\n\n### [Spectricity at MWC 2026: Elevating Mobile Spectral Vision][20]\n\n2026-02-12\n\nWe are exhibiting at MWC 2026, showcasing mobile-ready multispectral imaging demos. Visit us to\nexplore applications in wound monitoring, skin analysis, and local AWB.\n\n[Read More][21]\n\n[\n[Photonics West 2026 Website Banner]][22]\n\n### [Catch Spectricity at Photonics West 2026!][23]\n\n2026-01-06\n\nWe will showcase cutting-edge demos at Photonics West 2026: wound monitoring, skin analysis demo,\nand local AWB. All demos are powered by Spectricity\u2019s miniaturized, mobile-ready multispectral\nimaging technology.\n\n[Read More][24]\n\n[Product Portfolio]\n\n### Product Offering\n\n#### **S1 Multispectral Image Sensor**\n\nCore Innovation: Miniaturized and Mass-manufacturable\n\n#### **S1-M Camera Module**\n\nSmall Form Factor Integration\n\n#### **S1-A Accessory Device**\n\nPlug-n-Play Mobile Solution\n\n[Learn More][25]\n[Product Portfolio Mobile]\n\n### S1-A Accessory Device\n\nPlug-n-Play Multispectral Imaging on Mobile Platforms\n\n#### [About Us][26]\n\nSpectricity is a fabless company creating multispectral imaging solutions for high-volume and mobile\ndevices, using CMOS technologies.\n\n[Read More][27]\n\n#### [Careers][28]\n\nWe are hiring.\u00a0We\u2019re looking for innovative minds that want to be part of the future of\nsemiconductors and sensing to better the world.\n\n[Read More][29]\n[[Atlantic Bridge]][30]\n[[Capricorn]][31]\n[[Flanders Investment & Trade]][32]\n[[Flanders Semiconductors]][33]\n[[Garlick & Markison]][34]\n[[Imec]][35]\n[[Imec Xpand]][36]\n[[Lululab]][37]\n[[Namuga]][38]\n[[PDSTI]][39]\n[[Qualcomm]][40]\n[[VLAIO]][41]\n[[Xfab]][42]\n[[Sensinnovat]][43]\n[[University of East Anglia]][44]\n[[UCD Dublin]][45]\n[Spectricity Logo]\n[Spectricity Logo]\n\nSpectricity\nStationsstraat 55\nB-2800 Mechelen\nBelgium\n\n[[email\u00a0protected]][46]\n\n[Home][47]\n[Products][48]\n[Technology][49]\n[Applications][50]\n[Newsroom][51]\n\n[About Us][52]\n\u2013[Vision & Mission][53]\n\u2013[Management Team][54]\n\u2013[Partners][55]\n\u2013[Careers][56]\n[Contact][57]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Spectricity NV \u2013 BE 0685.594.317 \u2013 [Privacy Policy][58]\n\nWe are using cookies to give you the best experience on our website.\n\nYou can find out more about which cookies we are using or switch them off in settings.\n\nAccept\nClose GDPR Cookie Settings\n[Spectricity]\n* Privacy Overview\n* Strictly Necessary Cookies\n* Analytics\n[Powered by\u00a0 GDPR Cookie Compliance][59]\nPrivacy Overview\n\nThis website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience possible. Cookie\ninformation is stored in your browser and performs functions such as recognising you when you return\nto our website and helping our team to understand which sections of the website you find most\ninteresting and useful.\n\nStrictly Necessary Cookies\n\nStrictly Necessary Cookie should be enabled at all times so that we can save your preferences for\ncookie settings.\n\nEnable or Disable Cookies Enabled Disabled\nAnalytics\n\nThis website uses Google Analytics to collect anonymous information such as the number of visitors\nto the site, and the most popular pages.\n\nKeeping this cookie enabled helps us to improve our website.\n\nEnabl