            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n[ [PicoQuant] ][2]\n* [Events][3]\n* [Science Hub][4]\n* [Support][5]\n* [Downloads][6]\n* [Careers][7]\n* [About us][8]\n* [Contact][9]\n* [Events][10]\n* [Science Hub][11]\n* [Support][12]\n* [Downloads][13]\n* [Careers][14]\n* [About us][15]\n* [Contact][16]\n[Products][17]\n[Applications & Methods][18]\n[Search][19]\n\n### Products\n* [Microscope Systems][20]\n\n#### Most popular products\n* [\n[Solira upright time-resolved photoluminescence microscope with motorized sample stage for TRPL\nimaging and material characterization.]\n\n##### Solira\n\nSimplify your materials characterization with one flexible TRPL microscope enabling multiple\nmethods for precise and efficient analysis.\n\n][21]\n* [\n[Luminosa single photon counting confocal fluorescence microscope designed for quantitative\ntime-resolved and single-molecule imaging.]\n\n##### Luminosa\n\nComplete confocal fluorescence microscope that empowers researchers to advance quantitative\nfunctional imaging from individual molecules to cells and tissues.\n\n][22]\n* [\n[Compact FLIM and FCS upgrade kit for laser scanning microscopes]\n\n##### LSM Upgrade Kit\n\nCompact FLIM and FCS upgrade kit that adds advanced functional imaging and correlation analysis\nto existing laser scanning microscopes.\n\n][23]\n* [All Microscope Systems][24]\n>220 Z. PicoQuant designs and manufactures spectrometers that range from compact table-top\nspectrometers for teaching or daily routine work to modular high-end systems with exact timing\ndown to a few picoseconds.\n* [Spectrometer Systems][25]\n\n#### Most popular products\n* [\n[FluoTime 300 photoluminescence spectrometer for steady-state and time-resolved measurements]\n\n##### FluoTime 300\n\nDesigned for flexible, sensitive, and precise steady-state and time-resolved spectroscopy across\nthe UV to NIR range and time scales from picoseconds to milliseconds.\n\n][26]\n* [\n[FluoTime 250 compact modular lifetime spectrometer for fluorescence measurements]\n\n##### FluoTime 250\n\nModular lifetime spectrometer designed for flexible fluorescence and photoluminescence\nmeasurements in both materials and life science research.\n\n][27]\n* [\n[Micro-PL upgrade combining a scanning microscope with a spectrometer for spatially resolved,\ntime-resolved photoluminescence analysis.]\n\n##### Micro-Photoluminescence Upgrade\n\nAdd spectral and time-resolved photoluminescence to your setup through flexible\nmicroscope\u2013spectrometer coupling options.\n\n][28]\n* [All Spectrometer Systems][29]\n>220 Z. PicoQuant designs and manufactures spectrometers that range from compact table-top\nspectrometers for teaching or daily routine work to modular high-end systems with exact timing\ndown to a few picoseconds.\n* [Time Tagging and TCSPC Electronics][30]\n\n#### Most popular products\n* [\n[HydraHarp 500 multichannel TCSPC and time tagging unit front view]\n\n##### HydraHarp 500\n\nGet the most out of superconducting nanowire detectors in large-scale quantum communication and\ncomputing experiments requiring precise multichannel timing.\n\n][31]\n* [\n[PicoHarp 330 time tagging and TCSPC unit front view]\n\n##### PicoHarp 330\n\nBoost your time-resolved experiments with a flexible, high-precision time tagging and TCSPC unit\nfor materials science and quantum sensing.\n\n][32]\n* [\n[MultiHarp 160 multichannel time tagging and TCSPC unit with extension modules]\n\n##### MultiHarp 160\n\nScale your photonic quantum computing and detector characterization setups while maintaining\nperformance, flexibility, and high data throughput.\n\n][33]\n* [All Time Tagging and TCSPC Electronics][34]\n>220 Z. PicoQuant designs and manufactures spectrometers that range from compact table-top\nspectrometers for teaching or daily routine work to modular high-end systems with exact timing\ndown to a few picoseconds.\n* [Pulsed Lasers, LEDs, and Drivers][35]\n\n#### Most popular products\n* [\n[Prima 3-color picosecond laser from PicoQuant with trigger, gate, and sync interfaces for\ntime-resolved spectroscopy and microscopy.]\n\n##### Prima\n\nCompact 3-color picosecond laser delivering flexible ns to ms excitation with cost-effective\nmulticolor performance and straightforward operation.\n\n][36]\n* [\n[LDH-I Series smart picosecond diode laser head with integrated cooling, compatible with the\nTaiko PDL M1 driver for calibrated excitation in time-resolved spectroscopy.]\n\n##### LDH-I Series\n\nSmart picosecond laser diode heads covering UV-A to NIR, providing the right combination of\npower, pulse width, and diode type for any time-resolved technique.\n\n][37]\n* [\n[VisUV high-power UV\u2013visible picosecond laser module for spectroscopy and microscopy\nexperiments.]\n\n##### VisUV\n\nVisUV provides clean short pulses and stable timing across key UV and visible wavelengths,\nincluding deep UV lines as well as 488 nm and 532 nm.\n\n][38]\n* [All Pulsed Lasers, LEDs, and Drivers][39]\nPulsed lasers and LED sources engineered for picosecond precision, stable output, and flexible\nuse across life science, materials science, quantum optics and metrology.\n* [Photon Counting Detectors][40]\n\n#### Most popular products\n* [\n[PMA Hybrid Series hybrid photomultiplier detector assembly for single-photon counting and TCSPC\nmeasurements.]\n\n##### PMA Hybrid Series\n\nEnhance your single-photon counting experiments with wide dynamic range and excellent timing\nprecision in the UV and visible even at the highest count rates.\n\n][41]\n* [\n[PMA Series photomultiplier detector assemblies for single-photon counting and time-resolved\nmeasurements.]\n\n##### PMA Series\n\nCapture even the weakest signals over large areas with maximum dynamic range and enhanced\nlow-light sensitivity in a compact detector design.\n\n][42]\n* [\n[PDA-23 cooled 23-pixel SPAD detector array with breakout adapter]\n\n##### PDA-23\n\nUnlock spatially resolved single-photon detection with a 23-pixel SPAD array, combining low dark\ncounts and precise time tagging for advanced experiments.\n\n][43]\n* [All Photon Counting Detectors][44]\n>220 Z. PicoQuant designs and manufactures spectrometers that range from compact table-top\nspectrometers for teaching or daily routine work to modular high-end systems with exact timing\ndown to a few picoseconds.\n* [Software][45]\n\n#### Most popular products\n* [\n[NovaFLIM software interface for fluorescence lifetime imaging analysis]\n\n##### NovaFLIM\n\nAdvanced FLIM analysis software for fast, accurate interpretation of lifetime imaging data.\n\n][46]\n* [\n[UniHarp software interface displaying time resolved histogram measurement data]\n\n##### UniHarp\n\nIntuitive, free software solution for real-time, high-precision photon data acquisition,\nvisualization, and initial data analysis.\n\n][47]\n* [\n[EasyTau 2 interface for fluorescence lifetime data analysis]\n\n##### EasyTau 2\n\nAdvanced software for time-resolved fluorescence acquisition and analysis.\n\n][48]\n* [All Software][49]\n>220 Z. PicoQuant designs and manufactures spectrometers that range from compact table-top\nspectrometers for teaching or daily routine work to modular high-end systems with exact timing\ndown to a few picoseconds.\n* [Product Overview][50]\n\n### Application & Methods\n* [Life Science][51]\n\n#### Most popular applications & methods\n* [All Life Science][52]\n* [\n[FLIM image of sigmoid colon cancer tissue with hematoxylin and eosin staining. The color scale\nrepresents the average fluorescence lifetime within a single spectral channel. Sample courtesy\nof Desiree Ridder, Bundeswehr Hospital Berlin.]\n\n##### Fluorescence Lifetime Imaging Microscopy (FLIM)\n\nAn imaging technique that uses fluorescence lifetimes to generate image contrast.\n\n][53]\n* [\n[Illustration of protein conformational dynamics]\n\n##### Dynamic Structural Biology\n\nInvestigating how proteins dynamically explore multiple conformational states that control\nbiological function.\n\n][54]\n* [\n[Schematic representation of liquid\u2013liquid phase separation showing the formation of dynamic\nbiomolecular condensates within a dilute cellular environment. Created with Biorender.]\n\n##### Liquid-Liquid Phase Separation (LLPS)\n\nInvestigating how biomolecules separate into dynamic liquid phases to organize cellular space\nand regulate biological function.\n\n][55]\n* [Materials Science][56]\n\n#### Most popular applications & methods\n* [All Materials Science][57]\n* [\n[TRPL decay curves illustrating time-dependent photoluminescence and varying carrier lifetimes\nin advanced materials.]\n\n##### Time-Resolved Photoluminescence (TRPL)\n\nA time-resolved technique that measures photoluminescence lifetimes to reveal excited-state\ndynamics in materials.\n\n][58]\n* [\n[illustration of a van der Waals heterostructure emitting quantum light]\n\n##### 2D Materials Research\n\nStudying exciton dynamics, charge carrier processes, and structural properties through optical\nand time-resolved characterization methods.\n\n][59]\n* [\n[Representative surface structure of a solar cell used for optical characterization studies.]\n\n##### Solar Cell Characterization\n\nInvestigating charge-carrier lifetimes and recombination dynamics to enable precise optical\ncharacterization of material quality and device performance.\n\n][60]\n* [Quantum Optics][61]\n\n#### Most popular applications & methods\n* [All Quantum Optics][62]\n* [\n[Schematic comparison of antibunched, bunched and coherent photon emission statistics]\n\n##### Antibunching\n\nA quantum optical signature revealed by time-resolved photon correlation analysis to identify\nsingle-photon emission in materials and nanostructures.\n\n][63]\n* [\n[Schematic illustration of quantum key distribution showing single photons exchanged between\nAlice and Bob while eavesdropping by Eve introduces detectable disturbances.]\n\n##### Quantum Communication\n\nThe transmission of information using individual photons, using quantum effects to ensure\nabsolute security.\n\n][64]\n* [\n[Detector response signals for one two and three photon events]\n\n##### Photon Number Resolution (PNR)\n\nQuantifying photons per detection event enables direct access to photon-number statistics,\nproviding insight into quantum and statistical properties of light.\n\n][65]\n* [Metrology][66]\n\n#### Most popular applications & methods\n* [All Metrology][67]\n* [\n[Satellite Laser Ranging facility at NASA\u2019s Goddard Space Flight Center demonstrating\nhigh-precision time-of-flight distance measurements. Image courtesy of NASA.]\n\n##### LiDAR, Ranging, and Satellite Laser Ranging (SLR)\n\nAn optical technique that analyzes light emission under electrical excitation to reveal\nelectronic properties of electroluminescent materials.\n\n][68]\n* [\n[Resolving dynamic environmental changes through time-resolved fluorescence lifetime detection.]\n\n##### Environmental Sensing\n\nMonitoring environmental signals and trace compounds to understand dynamic changes in natural\nand engineered environments.\n\n][69]\n* [\n[TCSPC start-stop timing scheme showing photon arrival time differences relative to excitation\npulses]\n\n##### Time-Correlated Single Photon Counting (TCSPC)\n\nA photon timing technique that measures single-photon arrival times to resolve ultrafast\ndynamics in fluorescence, materials research, and quantum optics.\n\n][70]\n* [All Applications & Methods][71]\n\nProducts\n* [Microscope Systems][72]\n* [Solira][73]\n* [Luminosa][74]\n* [LSM Upgrade Kit][75]\n* [All Microscope Systems][76]\n* [Spectrometer Systems][77]\n* [FluoTime 300][78]\n* [FluoTime 250][79]\n* [Micro-Photoluminescence Upgrade][80]\n* [All Spectrometer Systems][81]\n* [Time Tagging and TCSPC Electronics][82]\n* [HydraHarp 500][83]\n* [PicoHarp 330][84]\n* [MultiHarp 160][85]\n* [All Time Tagging and TCSPC Electronics][86]\n* [Pulsed Lasers, LEDs, and Drivers][87]\n* [Prima][88]\n* [LDH-I Series][89]\n* [VisUV][90]\n* [All Pulsed Lasers, LEDs, and Drivers][91]\n* [Photon Counting Detectors][92]\n* [PMA Hybrid Series][93]\n* [PMA Series][94]\n* [PDA-23][95]\n* [All Photon Counting Detectors][96]\n* [Software][97]\n* [NovaFLIM][98]\n* [UniHarp][99]\n* [EasyTau 2][100]\n* [All Software][101]\n* [Product Overview][102]\n* [Microscope Systems][103]\n* [Solira][104]\n* [Luminosa][105]\n* [LSM Upgrade Kit][106]\n* [All Microscope Systems][107]\n* [Spectrometer Sy"
          },
