            "url": "https://www.si-ware.com/company/news",
            "text": "Products\nOEM Sensor\nIntegration-Ready Sensors\nDeployable Device\nField-Ready Analyzers\nInnovation Kit\nEmerging Tech Exploration\nOther\nInnovative solutions & software\nSi-NIR Mini\nThe smallest FT-NIR sensor built for integration\n][1][\nSi-NIR Matrix\nCompact OEM sensor delivering consistent readings from inconsistent materials\n][2][\nSi-NIR Mini DVK\nEasiest & fastest way to assess the world\u2019s smallest FT-NIR\n][3][\nSi-NIR Matrix DVK\nPlug-and-play toolkit for quick evaluation and prototyping of heterogeneous material analysis\n][4][\nSi-NIR FiberSense\nRemote FT-NIR spectral sensing through robust fiber connectivity\n][5]\nStart Comparing\n][6][\nAll Products\n][7]\nSi-NIR StreamLine\nAdaptable Process-deployable FT-NIR for in-line, on-line use in factories and fields\n][8][\nSi-NIR OverLine\nRugged FT-NIR for contactless continuous analysis of materials in motion\n][9]\nStart Comparing\n][10][\nAll Products\n][11]\nSi-NIR Flex\nDevelopment platform for NIR analysis with configurable setup\n][12][\nSi-MIR Core\nCompact MIR sensor enabling accurate transmission-based analysis\n][13][\nSi-MIR WideRange\nMulti-purpose MIR spectral sensing platform covering key fingerprint regions\n][14]\nStart Comparing\n][15][\nAll Products\n][16]\nSensing Software Platform\nAgriLIMS\nTech with ag labs in mind\n][17]\nTurnkey Sensing Solutions\nCropScout\nCrop Care on Autopilot\n][18]\n[Technology][19]\nInsights\nBlogs\n][20][[Orange icon of a notepad with three horizontal lines representing text.]\nApplication Notes\n][21]\nCompany\nAbout Us\n][22][\nTeam\n][23][[Orange and gray stylized speech bubble icon with horizontal lines representing text.]\nNews\n][24][[Orange distribution network icon with interconnected nodes around a central circle containing\na location pin.]\nDistributors\n][25][[Orange rectangular image with two stylized white shapes resembling the letter 'E' rotated and\nstacked.]\nCertifications\n][26][[Orange briefcase icon with a white plus symbol in the center.]\nCareers\n][27]\n[Contact][28][Order Now][29]\n[Cookie settings]\nNews & insights\n\n# our latest news\n\nOctober 16, 2025\n\n### Si-Ware Systems Launches the Most Adaptable Inline FT-NIR Sensor for Real-Time Process\n### Monitoring\n\nSi-Ware Systems Launches the Most Adaptable Inline FT-NIR Sensor for Real-Time Process Monitoring\n\n][30]\nJune 30, 2025\n\n### Si-Ware Systems Expands to Saudi Arabia with New Office, Supported by NTDP Relocate Grant\n\nSi-Ware Systems Expands to Saudi Arabia with New Office, Supported by NTDP Relocate Grant\n\n][31]\nMay 14, 2025\n\n### BUCHI Acquires Si-Ware Systems\u2019 NeoSpectra Platform to Establish a Fully Integrated Quality\n### Assurance Ecosystem Based on NIR\n\nThe fully integrated solution empowers growers to proactively monitor, detect, and diagnose crop\nhealth issues to maximize yield, optimize resources, and minimize risk of crop loss.\n\n][32]\nJanuary 28, 2025\n\n### Si-Ware Systems Introduces Cost-Effective High-Performance In-line Process Analyzer, in\n### Partnership with USTECH INNOVATIONS LLC\n\nThe ProLine 2550 offers manufacturers a precise, real-time, and cost-effective solution to optimize\nprocesses and reduce costs.\n\n][33]\nNovember 13, 2024\n\n### Si-Ware Systems & Rock River Laboratory Offer Superior Greenhouse Efficiency With CropScout\n\nThe fully integrated solution empowers growers to proactively monitor, detect, and diagnose crop\nhealth issues to maximize yield, optimize resources, and minimize risk of crop loss.\n\n][34]\nNovember 7, 2024\n\n### Si-Ware Systems Launches New Holistic On-Site Analysis Tool for Instant Sample Verification:\n### NeoSpectra Conformity Solution\n\n][35]\nOctober 10, 2024\n\n### Chevron and Si-Ware Systems Announce Multiple R&D Projects for Improved Environmental and\n### Operational Efficiency\n\nR&D aims to use Si-Ware System\u2019s NeoSpectra advanced on-site testing capabilities to improve\nsustainability and efficiency of Chevron\u2019s operations across various functions and sites.\n\n][36]\nSeptember 19, 2024\n\n### NutriLab Joins NeoSpectra LabStore, Expanding Options for Quick On-Site Analysis of Feed and\n### Feed Ingredients\n\nNeoSpectra partners with Nutrilab, adding advanced feed calibration models to LabStore, enabling\nfaster, accurate on-site feed analysis for users.\n\n][37]\nJuly 3, 2024\n\n### BUCHI extends NIR offering with NeoSpectra handhelds\n\n][38]\nJune 3, 2024\n\n### Ametller Origen Partners with NeoSpectra to Implement Innovative On-Site Food Testing Solutions\n\n][39]\nMarch 3, 2024\n\n### Advancing Dairy Nutrition: NeoSpectra & Cargill's Cloud-Based NIR Solution\n\n][40]\nJanuary 15, 2024\n\n### NeoSpectra and Eurofins QTA Collaborate to Advance On-Site Analysis Solutions for the Food\n### Industry\n\n][41]\nSeptember 5, 2023\n\n### Si-Ware Systems and Eigenvector Research Announce the Integration of Solo Software with\n### NeoSpectra Platform for Enhanced NIR Calibration Model Development\n\nThe integration of state-of-art chemometrics capabilities on a Cloud-based platform simplifies the\ndevelopment and deployment of robust new applications to fleets of handheld analyzers\n\n][42]\nJuly 13, 2023\n\n### Si-Ware Systems and Dairyland Laboratories Join Forces to Provide Holistic End-to-End Analytical\n### Solution to Feed Mills\n\nThe solution streamlines testing processes, reduces costs, and enhances quality control for improved\nproduct consistency\n\n][43]\nMarch 13, 2023\n\n### Rock River Laboratory Advances its Feed Analysis Services Using the NeoSpectra Platform\n\nNew services empower nutritionists, farmers, and feed mills to make better feeding and quality\ndecisions.\n\n][44]\nFebruary 16, 2023\n\n### Si-Ware Partners with Cargill to Provide NeoSpectra Feed Analysis Solutions to the Dairy\n### Industry\n\nThe partnership will provide Cargill\u2019s Dairy Teams with an accurate portable solution to analyze a\nvariety of feed materials in the field to deliver better animal nutrition and increase productivity\n\n][45]\nNovember 30, 2022\n\n### Si-Ware Partners with Eurofins Agro to Explore Applications for Feeds and Forages\n\n][46]\nOctober 24, 2022\n\n### Si-Ware\u2019s NeoSpectra Platform Wins Product Showdown Award at the 2022 MEMS and Sensors Executive\n### Congress\n\nSi-Ware\u2019s NeoSpectra platform was recognized as the winner in the competition for the best product\nfor Sensing as a Service.\n\n][47]\nOctober 6, 2022\n\n### Si-Ware Partners with AB Vista to Offer the NeoSpectra Platform to the Animal Feed Industry\n\nThe partnership will offer NeoSpectra Scanners and Cloud Services along with AB Vista INGOT\ncalibrations using the NeoSpectra LabStore.\n\n][48]\nSeptember 30, 2022\n\n### NeoSpectra by Si-Ware Launches the NeoSpectra LabStore\n\nNeoSpectra by Si-Ware Launches the NeoSpectra LabStore, an Online Marketplace Offering the Largest\nCollection of NIR Calibration Models. Users of NeoSpectra devices can evaluate, select, and\nconfigure validated calibration models built by trusted NIR experts for plug-and-play analysis of a\nwide range of agricultural, food, and feed products.\n\n][49]\nJuly 20, 2022\n\n### NeoSpectra by Si-Ware Puts Customers, Technology First with Website Redesign\n\nThe new website showcases the NeoSpectra instruments, software, applications, and company\ntechnologies specialized for material analysis outside the lab environment.\n\n][50]\nMay 12, 2022\n\n### NeoSpectra by Si-Ware Signs New Distribution Agreement with Labnutris Laboratory to Offer\n### Portable Solutions to Farms, Processors, and Food Producers\n\nNeoSpectra partners with Labnutris in Brazil, introducing on-farm feed analysis. The NeoSpectra\nScanner enhances efficiency, aligning with Labnutris' commitment to reliable agriculture.\n\n][51]\nApril 21, 2022\n\n### New Partnership: NeoSpectra by Si-Ware Partners with AB Vista\u2019s Aunir to Offer Customers\n### Affordable NIR Calibration Choices for In-Field Analysis\n\nThe partnership will offer NeoSpectra Scanner users Aunir\u2019s INGOT NIR calibration models for\naccurate in-field analysis across animal and aqua feed, feed ingredients, pet food, forage and other\nproducts.\n\n][52]\nMarch 31, 2022\n\n### New Partnership: NeoSpectra by Si-Ware and NutriControl provides customers with improved\n### solutions for accurate in-field materials analysis\n\nThe new partnership pairs NutriControl\u2019s industry-leading NIR calibration lines with NeoSpectra by\nSi-Ware\u2019s portable NeoSpectra Scanner technology for unparalleled, accurate testing capabilities.\n\n][53]\nSeptember 28, 2021\n\n### New Partnership: Si-Ware Systems and Dairyland Laboratories partner to launch in-field dairy\n### feed analysis solution\n\nThe partnership will utilize the power of Si-Ware's NeoSpectra technology and Dairyland's feed\ntesting expertise, enabling on-demand results, quicker decisions, and improved feed quality\nassurance.\n\n][54]\nOctober 7, 2019\n\n### Si-Ware Systems moves world's smallest spectral sensor into volume production\n\nSi-Ware has launched volume production of the smallest, highly accurate spectral sensor for\nanalyzing samples of almost any material.\n\n][55]\nSeptember 16, 2019\n\n### Si-Ware launches small, lightweight NeoSpectra Scanner for in-field material analysis\n\nSi-Ware introduces NeoSpectra-Scanner, a portable material analysis tool for on-site identification\nin diverse industries. Prototypes available October; commercial release in Q1 2020.\n\n][56]\nJanuary 8, 2019\n\n### Si-Ware's NeoSpectra is the first spectrometer built into beauty product\n\nThe award winning NeoSpectra-Micro spectral sensor has been customized into Henkel Beauty Care's\nSchwarzkopf Professional SalonLab Smart Analyzer to enable data-driven, highly personalized care\nservice and product recommendations based on analysis of inner hair.\n\n][57]\nSeptember 26, 2017\n\n### NeoSpectra Micro wins SEMI's MEMS & Sensor Technology Showcase award in Europe\n\nSEMI European MEMS and Sensor Summit 2017 conference participants voted to award the SEMI's\nTechnology Showcase Award to Si-Ware for the NeoSpectra Micro.\n\n][58]\nApril 18, 2017\n\n### Si-Ware Systems announces NeoSpectra Micro Development Kits\n\nSi-Ware Systems announced a plug-and-play development kit for NeoSpectra Micro, where material\nanalysis is enabled in the real world for consumers and businesses.\n\n][59]\nJanuary 24, 2017\n\n### Si-Ware Systems introduces first fully integrated chip-sized spectral sensor for industrial and\n### consumer markets\n\nNeoSpectra Micro offers unprecedented NIR spectral sensor range and high performance for food, oil &\ngas, agriculture, pharmaceutical, and medical applications.\n\n][60]\nOctober 18, 2016\n\n### Si-Ware Systems launches European distribution of NeoSpectra sensor for handheld and inline\n### material analysis\n\nSi-Ware Systems announces a European distribution network for its award-winning NeoSpectra spectral\nsensor module, an innovative miniaturized spectrometer.\n\n][61]\nMarch 8, 2016\n\n### Si-Ware Systems launches volume production of NeoSpectra Sensor for material analysis\n\nSi-Ware Systems launches volume production of the smallest, lowest-cost infra-red spectrometer\n\"engine\" for developers.\n\n][62]\nFebruary 9, 2015\n\n### NeoSpectra sensors are used to help solve the world's food demand problems\n\nSi-Ware Systems Prism award winning spectral sensors chosen by Dutch Sprouts for use in its Near\nInfraRed (NIR) portable analyzers that farmers can use for soil analysis.\n\n][63]\nFebruary 6, 2015\n\n### Si-Ware Systems' FT-IR spectrometer wins prestigious Prism award in the Test, Measurement,\n### Metrology category\n\nSi-Ware is honored to have FT-IR spectrometer recognized as a leading new product in the industry by\nthe panel of leading industry experts, venture capitalists, luminaries and visionaries.\n\n][64]\nOpen Search Field\nSort By\nDate (Asc)\n][65][\nDate (Desc)\n][66]\nThank you! Your submission has been received!\nOops! Something went wrong while submitting the form.\n\n### Si-Ware Systems Launches the Most Adaptable Inline FT-NIR Sensor for Real-Time Process\n### Monitoring\n\n][67]\nOctober 16, 2025\n\nThe sensor, Si-NIR StreamLine, combines rugged reliability, wide spectral coverage, and flexible\ninterfacing options to deliver continuous material analysis from factory floors to remote field\noperations.\n\nRead more\n["
