ensors\n\nPowerful, ruggedized, and optimized for SWaP, CRFS sensors are multifunctional, allowing them to be\nrepurposed or interchanged across missions and applications.\n[Multi-domain superiority]\n\n###### Multi-domain superiority\n\nCRFS passive RF technology supports collaborative intelligence networks and integration across the\nair, land, sea, spaceport, and cyber domains to overcome modern threats.\n\nAPPLICATIONS OVERVIEW\n\n### Obtain RF intelligence, maintain spectrum awareness, and achieve mission-critical objectives\n\n### Who we help\n\n##### Military & EW operators\n\n**Military & EW operators**\n\nActionable RF intelligence in contested electromagnetic environments to help military forces gain\nspectrum dominance.\n\n[Read more][141]\n\n##### Spectrum regulators\n\n**Spectrum regulators**\n\nITU-compliant solutions for real-time spectrum monitoring, interference hunting, geolocation, major\nevent management, and more.\u00a0\n\n[Read more][142]\n\n##### Security & intelligence agencies\n\n**Security & intelligence agencies**\n\nActionable RF intelligence and counter surveillance solutions to fight crime, cyber, and homeland\nsecurity threats.\u00a0\n\n[Read more][143]\n\n##### Defense & system integrators\n\n**Defense & system integrators**\n\nAdvanced COTS RF sensor technology adds advanced capabilities, allowing military end users to\nunderstand and exploit the EM environment and achieve spectrum dominance.\n\n\n[Read more][144]\n\nTalk to an advisor to discuss how CRFS can enhance your RF capabilities\n\n[Talk to us][145]\n\n##### CRFS special reports\n\n[ [Forewarned is Forearmed Home] ][146]\n\n###### Forewarned is Forearmed\n\nUsing wide area, networked, radio frequency sensing to enhance regional defence and security in the\nMiddle East. This special report by Dr Thomas Withington joins seemingly disparate threats across\nthe region and offers a framework for how militaries and security agencies can augment their\ndefences by adding a layer of RF protection.\n\n[Read the report][147]\n[ [Competition to Conflict Home] ][148]\n\n###### Competition to Conflict\n\nThe Asia-Pacific is the frontline between competition & conflict. Grey-zone tactics, increased\nmilitarization, and border disputes are reshaping the region\u2019s security landscape. Dr Thomas\nWithington\u2019s special report examines how electromagnetic sensing can strengthen deterr"
