ter\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nChamfer \u25020.05-0.5mm \u00d7 45\u00b0\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nCoating \u2502Single MgF2, Multi-layer AR coating\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n## Product Description\n\nAvailable in positive and negative types; used for telescopes, cameras, collimators, and laser\nsystems.\n\n### Related Products in Spherical Lens\n\n[Biconcave Lens][47][Micro Spherical Lens][48][Rectangular Spherical Lens][49][High Laser Power\nSpherical Lens][50][Large Size Spherical Lens][51][Plano-Concave Lens][52][Biconvex\nLens][53][Plano-Convex Lens][54]\n\n### Applications & Industries\n\n[Semiconductor][55][Scientific Research][56][Automotive][57][Medical & Healthcare][58][Optical\nCommunication][59][Aerospace & Defense][60]\n\n### Technical Resources\n\n#### Optical Coating Guide: AR, HR, and Partial Reflection Coatings\n\n5 min read\n][61][\n\n#### Understanding Optical Surface Quality: Scratch-Dig Standards Explained\n\n6 min read\n][62][\n\n#### Dimensional Tolerances in Precision Lens Manufacturing: What Actually Matters\n\n8 min read\n][63][\n\n#### How to Select the Right Lens Type for Your Optical System\n\n7 min read\n][64]\n\n### Guides & Resources\n\n[Infrared Optics for High-Power Laser Systems \u2014 ZnSe, Ge & Silicon Components][65][Hemispherical\nLens \u2014 Precision Optical Hemispherical Lens Manufacturer | Nova Component][66][Optical Filter \u2014\nPrecision Optical Optical Filter Manufacturer | Nova Component][67][Polarization Optics for Optical\nCommunication & Laser Systems][68]\n\n## Related Products\n\n[Hemispherical Lens / Dome Lens]\nSpherical Lens\n\n### Hemispherical Lens / Dome Lens\n\nOptical domes are lenses with two concentric spheres. Concentricity is critical. Widely used for\ndetectors and optical sensors.\n\nPROD0013\n][69] [\n[Biconvex Lens]\nSpherical Lens\n\n### Biconvex Lens\n\nBiconvex lenses have two convex surfaces and are used for magnification, optical, and laser systems.\n\nPROD0011\n][70] [\n[Large Size Spherical Lens]\nSpherical Lens\n\n### Large Size Spherical Lens\n\nCustomizes large-size spherical lenses up to 600mm. Materials include BK7, Fused Silica, and CaF2.\n\nPROD0012\n][71] [\n[High Laser Power Spherical Lens]\nSpherical Lens\n\n### High Laser Power Spherical Lens\n\nLaser coatings can withstand standard 12,000W lasers. Lenses are mainly made of fused silica with\nlaser threshold > 70J/cm\u00b2.\n\nPROD0014\n][72]\n\n## Request Quote\n\nFill out the form below to request a quote\n\n### Inquiry Submitted!\n\nWe w