lect the Right Lens Type for Your Optical System\n\n7 min read\n][59][\n\n#### Optical Coating Guide: AR, HR, and Partial Reflection Coatings\n\n5 min read\n][60][\n\n#### Understanding Optical Surface Quality: Scratch-Dig Standards Explained\n\n6 min read\n][61][\n\n#### Dimensional Tolerances in Precision Lens Manufacturing: What Actually Matters\n\n8 min read\n][62]\n\n### Guides & Resources\n\n[Optical Design \u2014 Precision Optical Optical Design Manufacturer | Nova Component][63][Optical Prism\n\u2014 Precision Optical Optical Prism Manufacturer | Nova Component][64][Frequently Asked Questions\nAbout Precision Optical Components | Nova Component][65][Optical Filters for Telecommunications &\nData Communication Networks][66]\n\n## Related Products\n\n[Achromatic Cylindrical Lens]\nCylindrical Lens\n\n### Achromatic Cylindrical Lens\n\nA doublet consisting of a positive low-index (crown) and a negative high-index (flint) element\ncemented together to reduce spherical and chromatic aberration.\n\nPROD0020\n][67] [\n[Cylindrical Rod Lens]\nCylindrical Lens\n\n### Cylindrical Rod Lens\n\nMainly used for sensors, light guides, endoscopes, and laser systems. Polishing is available for end\nfaces or cylindrical surfaces.\n\nPROD0026\n][68] [\n[Plano-Convex Cylindrical Lens]\nCylindrical Lens\n\n### Plano-Convex Cylindrical Lens\n\nUsed for optical, laser, and scanner systems. Available in various geometries (circular, square,\nrectangular).\n\nPROD0025\n][69] [\n[Meniscus Cylindrical Lens]\nCylindrical Lens\n\n### Meniscus Cylindrical Lens\n\nA cylindrical lens with one convex surface and one concave surface.\n\nPROD0023\n][70]\n\n## Request Quote\n\nFill out the form below to request a quote\n\n### Inquiry Submitted!\n\nWe will contact you within 24 hours with a quote.\n\nName *\nEmail *\nCompany\nPhone\nQuantity Needed *\nAdditional Requirements\n**Product:** Plano-Concave Cylindrical Lens (PROD0024)\nSubmit Inquiry\nNOVA COMPONENT\n\nNova Component is a leading ma