        "ownership_parent": "",
        "company_type": "Private",
        "employee_count": "",
        "revenue": "",
        "key_numbers": "",
        "contact_person": "Chester Berry",
        "contact_role": "Founder",
        "email": "Sales@precisionoptical.com",
        "phone": "949.631.6800",
        "linkedin": "",
        "website": "https://www.precisionoptical.com",
        "industries": "Military & Defense; Aerospace; Biomedical; Semiconductor; Metrology; Laser; Semi-Conductor",
        "products": "Custom Prisms, Optical Assemblies, Optical Coatings, Metrology Services, Optical Fabrication",
        "certifications": "ITAR registered; ROHS compliant; REACH compliant; ISO 9001:2015 certified; ISO 9001:2015",
        "distributors": "",
        "customers": "",
        "partnerships": "",
        "crawl_text": "Precision Optical ITAR registered and ROHS & REACH compliant, ISO 9001:2015 certification ITAR registered ROHS compliant REACH compliant ISO 9001:2015 certified ISO 9001:2015 Founders\u2019 Award E-Beam Ion Beam Sputtering (IBS) Thermal Evaporation Plasma Assist Ion Assist Cutting-edge technology in optical manufacturing Custom-designed manufacturing facility optimized for precision Experienced engineering team with a focus on quality Custom-designed manufacturing facility optimized for optics production Advanced metrology and manufacturing equipment Family-centered company culture ITAR ROHS REACH ISO 9001:2015 320 Kalmus Drive, Costa Mesa, CA 92626, USA USA Costa Mesa, CA [[Precision Optical Logo]][1]\n\nITAR registered and ROHS & REACH compliant\n\nISO 9001:2015 certification\nView or download:\n[ANAB][2] and [RvA][3]\nEmail Us\nSales@precisionoptical.com\n][4]\n[Call Us\n949.631.6800][5]\nMenu\n* [Optics][6]\n* [Custom Prisms][7]\n* [Corner Cube Retroreflectors][8]\n* [Porro Prisms / Right Angle Prisms][9]\n* [Beamsplitters][10]\n* [Penta Prisms][11]\n* [Other Optics][12]\n* [Optical Flats][13]\n* [Large Optical Flats][14]\n* [Optical Flats and Wedges][15]\n* [Optical Windows and Mirrors][16]\n* [Mounted Reference Flats][17]\n* [Alignment Cubes][18]\n* [Catalog Optics][19]\n* [Assembly & Integration][20]\n* [Coatings][21]\n* [Mirrors][22]\n* [Protected / Enhanced Aluminum][23]\n* [Protected / Enhanced Silver][24]\n* [Dielectric Broadband][25]\n* [Cold / Hot][26]\n* [AR Coatings][27]\n* [Single-Layer AR][28]\n* [V-Coat][29]\n* [Double V-Coat][30]\n* [Broadband (UV, VIS, NIR, SWIR, EX)][31]\n* [Beamsplitters][32]\n* [Non-Polarizing Beamsplitter][33]\n* [Polarizing Beamsplitter][34]\n* [Broadband Polarizing Beamsplitter][35]\n* [Filters][36]\n* [Shortwave Pass][37]\n* [Longwave Pass][38]\n* [Band Pass][39]\n* [Neutral Density][40]\n* [Technology][41]\n* [E-Beam][42]\n* [Ion Beam Sputtering (IBS)][43]\n* [Thermal Evaporation][44]\n* [Plasma Assist][45]\n* [Ion Assist][46]\n* [Equipment][47]\n* [Coating Chambers][48]\n* [Counter Rotating Uniformity Masking][49]\n* [Laminar Flow Hood Stations][50]\n* [Nitrogen Generating System][51]\n* [Thermal, Humidity, and Environmental Chambers][52]\n* [Large Optical Lifting System][53]\n* [Spectrophotometers][54]\n* [Design][55]\n* [Thin Film Software][56]\n* [Custom Tooling][57]\n* [Laser Damage & Durability][58]\n* [QA & Metrology][59]\n* [Specifications and Tolerances][60]\n* [Interferometric Testing][61]\n* [Angular Testing][62]\n* [Mechanical Testing][63]\n* [Spectral Testing][64]\n* [Environmental Testing][65]\n* [Services][66]\n* [Engineering][67]\n* [Materials Qualification][68]\n* [Fabrication][69]\n* [Polishing][70]\n* [Coatings][71]\n* [Assembly][72]\n* [Metrology][73]\n* [CNC Machining][74]\n* [Optical Packaging][75]\n* [About Us][76]\n* [About Precision Optical][77]\n* [Our Facilities][78]\n* [Education and Outreach][79]\n* [Industries We Serve][80]\n* [Military & Defense][81]\n* [Astronomy & Aerospace][82]\n* [Laser][83]\n* [Metrology][84]\n* [Biomedical][85]\n* [Semi-Conductor][86]\n* [News][87]\n* [Contact Us][88]\n* [949.631.6800][89]\n[Sales@precisionoptical.com][90]\n[More Options][91]\nName(Required)\nEmail(Required)\nPhone\nCompany\nMessage\nCAPTCHA\n* * Search Search\n\n# Education & Outreach\n\nPrecision Optical offers an education program committed to supporting the optical community by\npromoting educational advancement of future optical engineers and technicians.\n\nWe offer practical optics education for students at many levels, particularly high school and\ncollege. Many students in Mathematics and Physics can get discouraged from not having a \u201creal life\u201d\napplication of their difficult studies. The Ensign-Lambert Optics Education Program (ELOEP) provides\nfield trips to inspire a next generation of problem solvers in applied Physics and Mathematics.\n\n## Academic and Community Involvement\n\nWe promote high school level students to local schools that offer Optics education, such as\n[University of California Irvine][92], [Irvine Valley College ][93], and\n[The University of Arizona][94]. This helps establish a high school pipeline that is fundamental for\ncolleges\n\nWe also offer various types of internships in coordination with our academic and community partners.\nThrough schools, government, professional societies, and non-profit organizations such as [VitalLink\nOC][95], [The City of Santa Ana][96], [Saddleback College][97] and [Bridge |2| Engineering][98], the\n[Optical Society of Southern California (OSSC)][99], [Optical Institute of Southern California\n(OISC)][100], and [Irvine Valley College (IVC)][101], we have a continuous flow of interns that we\nhope will enter the optics ecosystem. Internship, whether paid, un-paid, or for school credit, have\nbeen mutually beneficial for both the intern and for Precision Optical.\n\n> \u201cMy internship at Precision Optical has opened my eyes to the field of optical engineering, which\n> may play a crucial role in my future career path. I am looking forward to getting to know all the\n> departments in the company and further broadening my knowledge of optics.\u201d\n> \u2013 Dror Sapir, 2014-2015 Intern\n\nPractical application of collegiate level studying in a manufacturing environment is extremely\nbeneficial to both student and employer, and in-turn, to the college. We encourage our own employees\nto take part in local courses. We also are actively partnering with local universities to offer\nlectures and laboratory [courses][102] for students at our facility.\n\n## Outreach Philosophy\n\nOptics and Photonics education outreach can easily start before high school with getting young\npeople interested and aware of the field, and outside of the academic realm. Optics and Photonics is\npresent everywhere in our everyday lives, and most people (kids especially) are not aware of how\nsignificant the science of light it is to everyday life. We offer inspirational/educational field\ntrips for students from middle school to graduate level, as well as industry professionals and\ndignitaries. We host professional events at our facility such as advisory board meetings, panel\ndiscussions, and topical events such as the [National Photonics Initiative][103] . Precision Optical\nis a leader in the Southern California optics community, with heavy involvement with OSA, SPIE, and\nthe OSSC, and is a founding member of SCOPE, the Southern California Optics & Photonics Enterprise\n(cluster).\n\nIn creating a re-generative ecosystem of Optics and Photonics technicians, Precision Optical is\ncommitted to supporting the Optics and Photonics community. As the future holds a very high demand\nfor Optics and Photonics, it also holds a very high demand for optical technicians and engineers.\n\nPlease, [contact us][104] to setup your inspirational high school or college field trip or to\ndiscuss your involvement with ELOEP. See our [blog][105] for real field trip testimonials from our\nstudents.\n\n[[Precision Optical Logo White][Precision Optical Logo White]][106]\n[[Precision Optical Logo White][Precision Optical Logo White]][107]\nPrecision Optical\n320 Kalmus Drive\nCosta Mesa, CA 92626\nUSA\n[949.631.6800][108]\n[Sales@precisionoptical.com][109]\n\n#### Who We Are\n\nPrecision Optical is a world-leading manufacturer of custom prisms and optical assemblies. Our\ncutting edge technology allows us to achieve a level of precision that few others in the industry\ncan match.[ Contact us today][110] to learn more.\n\n#### Navigation\n* [> Home][111]\n* [> Optics][112]\n* [> Coatings][113]\n* [> QA & Metrology][114]\n* [> Services][115]\n* [> Industries][116]\n* [> About Us][117]\n* [> News][118]\n* [> Contact Us][119]\n\nDownload or view our [Terms & Conditions.][120]\n\n#### Latest News\n\n[Precision Optical to Exhibit at SPIE Defense & Security in National Harbor 2026][121]\n\nApril 20, 2026\n\n[Precision Optical (The Prism Specialists) to Exhibit at SPIE Photonics West 2026 in San Francisco,\nCA][122]\n\nJanuary 12, 2026\n\n[Precision Optical to Exhibit at SPIE OptiFab 2025 in Rochester, NY][123]\n\nOctober 13, 2025\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/ISO_9001-ENG-101059-2011-AQ-USA-ANA\nB-7-20250730-1.pdf\n[3]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/ISO_9001-ENG-11428-2007-AQ-USA-RvA-\n9-20250730-1.pdf\n[4]: mailto:Sales@precisionoptical.com\n[5]: tel:9496316800\n[6]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/\n[7]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/\n[8]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/corner-cube-retroreflector/\n[9]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/porro-prism-right-angle-prism/\n[10]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/beamsplitter/\n[11]: https://www.precisionop [[Precision Optical Logo]][1]\n\nITAR registered and ROHS & REACH compliant\n\nISO 9001:2015 certification\nView or download:\n[ANAB][2] and [RvA][3]\nEmail Us\nSales@precisionoptical.com\n][4]\n[Call Us\n949.631.6800][5]\nMenu\n* [Optics][6]\n* [Custom Prisms][7]\n* [Corner Cube Retroreflectors][8]\n* [Porro Prisms / Right Angle Prisms][9]\n* [Beamsplitters][10]\n* [Penta Prisms][11]\n* [Other Optics][12]\n* [Optical Flats][13]\n* [Large Optical Flats][14]\n* [Optical Flats and Wedges][15]\n* [Optical Windows and Mirrors][16]\n* [Mounted Reference Flats][17]\n* [Alignment Cubes][18]\n* [Catalog Optics][19]\n* [Assembly & Integration][20]\n* [Coatings][21]\n* [Mirrors][22]\n* [Protected / Enhanced Aluminum][23]\n* [Protected / Enhanced Silver][24]\n* [Dielectric Broadband][25]\n* [Cold / Hot][26]\n* [AR Coatings][27]\n* [Single-Layer AR][28]\n* [V-Coat][29]\n* [Double V-Coat][30]\n* [Broadband (UV, VIS, NIR, SWIR, EX)][31]\n* [Beamsplitters][32]\n* [Non-Polarizing Beamsplitter][33]\n* [Polarizing Beamsplitter][34]\n* [Broadband Polarizing Beamsplitter][35]\n* [Filters][36]\n* [Shortwave Pass][37]\n* [Longwave Pass][38]\n* [Band Pass][39]\n* [Neutral Density][40]\n* [Technology][41]\n* [E-Beam][42]\n* [Ion Beam Sputtering (IBS)][43]\n* [Thermal Evaporation][44]\n* [Plasma Assist][45]\n* [Ion Assist][46]\n* [Equipment][47]\n* [Coating Chambers][48]\n* [Counter Rotating Uniformity Masking][49]\n* [Laminar Flow Hood Stations][50]\n* [Nitrogen Generating System][51]\n* [Thermal, Humidity, and Environmental Chambers][52]\n* [Large Optical Lifting System][53]\n* [Spectrophotometers][54]\n* [Design][55]\n* [Thin Film Software][56]\n* [Custom Tooling][57]\n* [Laser Damage & Durability][58]\n* [QA & Metrology][59]\n* [Specifications and Tolerances][60]\n* [Interferometric Testing][61]\n* [Angular Testing][62]\n* [Mechanical Testing][63]\n* [Spectral Testing][64]\n* [Environmental Testing][65]\n* [Services][66]\n* [Engineering][67]\n* [Materials Qualification][68]\n* [Fabrication][69]\n* [Polishing][70]\n* [Coatings][71]\n* [Assembly][72]\n* [Metrology][73]\n* [CNC Machining][74]\n* [Optical Packaging][75]\n* [About Us][76]\n* [About Precision Optical][77]\n* [Our Facilities][78]\n* [Education and Outreach][79]\n* [Industries We Serve][80]\n* [Military & Defense][81]\n* [Astronomy & Aerospace][82]\n* [Laser][83]\n* [Metrology][84]\n* [Biomedical][85]\n* [Semi-Conductor][86]\n* [News][87]\n* [Contact Us][88]\n* [949.631.6800][89]\n[Sales@precisionoptical.com][90]\n[More Options][91]\nName(Required)\nEmail(Required)\nPhone\nCompany\nMessage\nCAPTCHA\n* * Search Search\n\n# About Precision Optical\n\n# About Precision Optical\n\n# About Precision Optical\n\nPrecision Optical was founded in 1959 by Chester and Ruth Berry. Chester was an early pioneer in the\nworld of optics. He contributed to some notable projects during the 1940\u2019s and 50\u2019s, including the\nmanufacture of large mirrors for the Palomar Observatory in San Diego County, California.\n\nIn 1959, the Berrys went into business for themselves and founded Precision Optical. They opened a\nsmall shop on the west side of Costa Mesa at 643 West 17th Street. They saw a burgeoning demand for\ncorner cube reflectors and solid glass rangefinders. Chester developed innovative manufacturing\nmethods, including the use of molded blanks, optical contacting, and replication coatings. These\nmethods greatly enhanced manufacturing efficiency and qualit"
