          {
            "url": "https://www.precisionoptical.com/about-us/",
            "text": "[[Precision Optical Logo]][1]\n\nITAR registered and ROHS & REACH compliant\n\nISO 9001:2015 certification\nView or download:\n[ANAB][2] and [RvA][3]\nEmail Us\nSales@precisionoptical.com\n][4]\n[Call Us\n949.631.6800][5]\nMenu\n* [Optics][6]\n* [Custom Prisms][7]\n* [Corner Cube Retroreflectors][8]\n* [Porro Prisms / Right Angle Prisms][9]\n* [Beamsplitters][10]\n* [Penta Prisms][11]\n* [Other Optics][12]\n* [Optical Flats][13]\n* [Large Optical Flats][14]\n* [Optical Flats and Wedges][15]\n* [Optical Windows and Mirrors][16]\n* [Mounted Reference Flats][17]\n* [Alignment Cubes][18]\n* [Catalog Optics][19]\n* [Assembly & Integration][20]\n* [Coatings][21]\n* [Mirrors][22]\n* [Protected / Enhanced Aluminum][23]\n* [Protected / Enhanced Silver][24]\n* [Dielectric Broadband][25]\n* [Cold / Hot][26]\n* [AR Coatings][27]\n* [Single-Layer AR][28]\n* [V-Coat][29]\n* [Double V-Coat][30]\n* [Broadband (UV, VIS, NIR, SWIR, EX)][31]\n* [Beamsplitters][32]\n* [Non-Polarizing Beamsplitter][33]\n* [Polarizing Beamsplitter][34]\n* [Broadband Polarizing Beamsplitter][35]\n* [Filters][36]\n* [Shortwave Pass][37]\n* [Longwave Pass][38]\n* [Band Pass][39]\n* [Neutral Density][40]\n* [Technology][41]\n* [E-Beam][42]\n* [Ion Beam Sputtering (IBS)][43]\n* [Thermal Evaporation][44]\n* [Plasma Assist][45]\n* [Ion Assist][46]\n* [Equipment][47]\n* [Coating Chambers][48]\n* [Counter Rotating Uniformity Masking][49]\n* [Laminar Flow Hood Stations][50]\n* [Nitrogen Generating System][51]\n* [Thermal, Humidity, and Environmental Chambers][52]\n* [Large Optical Lifting System][53]\n* [Spectrophotometers][54]\n* [Design][55]\n* [Thin Film Software][56]\n* [Custom Tooling][57]\n* [Laser Damage & Durability][58]\n* [QA & Metrology][59]\n* [Specifications and Tolerances][60]\n* [Interferometric Testing][61]\n* [Angular Testing][62]\n* [Mechanical Testing][63]\n* [Spectral Testing][64]\n* [Environmental Testing][65]\n* [Services][66]\n* [Engineering][67]\n* [Materials Qualification][68]\n* [Fabrication][69]\n* [Polishing][70]\n* [Coatings][71]\n* [Assembly][72]\n* [Metrology][73]\n* [CNC Machining][74]\n* [Optical Packaging][75]\n* [About Us][76]\n* [About Precision Optical][77]\n* [Our Facilities][78]\n* [Education and Outreach][79]\n* [Industries We Serve][80]\n* [Military & Defense][81]\n* [Astronomy & Aerospace][82]\n* [Laser][83]\n* [Metrology][84]\n* [Biomedical][85]\n* [Semi-Conductor][86]\n* [News][87]\n* [Contact Us][88]\n* [949.631.6800][89]\n[Sales@precisionoptical.com][90]\n[More Options][91]\nName(Required)\nEmail(Required)\nPhone\nCompany\nMessage\nCAPTCHA\n* * Search Search\n\n# About Precision Optical\n\n# About Precision Optical\n\n# About Precision Optical\n\nPrecision Optical was founded in 1959 by Chester and Ruth Berry. Chester was an early pioneer in the\nworld of optics. He contributed to some notable projects during the 1940\u2019s and 50\u2019s, including the\nmanufacture of large mirrors for the Palomar Observatory in San Diego County, California.\n\nIn 1959, the Berrys went into business for themselves and founded Precision Optical. They opened a\nsmall shop on the west side of Costa Mesa at 643 West 17th Street. They saw a burgeoning demand for\ncorner cube reflectors and solid glass rangefinders. Chester developed innovative manufacturing\nmethods, including the use of molded blanks, optical contacting, and replication coatings. These\nmethods greatly enhanced manufacturing efficiency and quality.\n\nOver the next decades, Precision Optical enjoyed great success selling solid retro-reflectors to the\nsurveying and space industries. Precision Optical sold reflectors to support the Apollo Program. In\nthe 1980\u2019s and into the 90\u2019s the company shifted its primary focus from the surveying industry to\ndefense and the burgeoning fields of semi-conductor, aircraft, satellite, and bio-medical technology\nand manufacture.\n\nThe Lambert family took over ownership of the company in the early 90\u2019s. Ruth and Chester continued\nto work for the company until their retirement in the 2000\u2019s. Every year, one employee is selected\nby the whole company to receive the \u201cFounders\u2019 Award,\u201d which is named after Ruth and Chester.\nChester passed away in 2008 at 92 years of age. Ruth has retired, but she regularly attends company\nparties and events.\n\nToday, Precision Optical is poised to enter the next era of its long and storied existence. In\nOctober of 2011, the company moved across town into a new and much larger facility. Located at 320\nKalmus Drive in Costa Mesa, the new facility was custom-designed by Precision Optical to be an ideal\noptics manufacturing plant. The company has also acquired new metrology and manufacturing equipment,\nmaking it one of the world\u2019s most well-equipped optical manufacturing companies.\n\nMore than 60 years after Chester and Ruth founded the company, Precision Optical remains\nfamily-centered and committed to providing a fun, friendly, and challenging work environment for its\nemployees.\n\n## Our Facilities\n\nOur state-of-the- art, 41,655 square-foot facility is located less than five minutes from John Wayne\nAirport at 320 Kalmus Drive in Costa Mesa, California. After more than 50 years on the west side of\nCosta Mesa, we relocated to north-east Costa Mesa in October of 2011 almost tripling our\nmanufacturing space in the process.\n\nOur new facility was custom-designed by us, Precision Optical, to be completely optimized for the\nmanufacturing of precision optical components and assemblies. Every aspect of the facility\u2019s design\nwas meticulously considered by our engineers, management and manufacturing personnel. The facility\nfeatures epoxy flooring throughout and state-of-art climate and particulate controlled rooms. Each\nmanufacturing department was carefully positioned to maximize work-flow efficiencies. The end result\nis an optics manufacturing facility that allows us to maximize what matters most: precision and\nquality.\n\nWe also took great pains to design a facility that minimizes our carbon footprint. To that end, the\nfacility includes solar roof panels to reduce our demand on the electrical grid, energy efficient\nlighting and air conditioners, along with drought-tolerant landscaping.\n\nWe are very proud of our new facility. If you are interested in visiting us and learning more about\nPrecision Optical, please contact us and we\u2019ll schedule a personalized tour.\n\n### Contact Us Today\n\nContact Precision Optical today to schedule your tour and learn more about the products and services\nthat we offer.\n\n[Contact Us][92]\n\n[[Precision Optical Logo White][Precision Optical Logo White]][93]\n[[Precision Optical Logo White][Precision Optical Logo White]][94]\nPrecision Optical\n320 Kalmus Drive\nCosta Mesa, CA 92626\nUSA\n[949.631.6800][95]\n[Sales@precisionoptical.com][96]\n\n#### Who We Are\n\nPrecision Optical is a world-leading manufacturer of custom prisms and optical assemblies. Our\ncutting edge technology allows us to achieve a level of precision that few others in the industry\ncan match.[ Contact us today][97] to learn more.\n\n#### Navigation\n* [> Home][98]\n* [> Optics][99]\n* [> Coatings][100]\n* [> QA & Metrology][101]\n* [> Services][102]\n* [> Industries][103]\n* [> About Us][104]\n* [> News][105]\n* [> Contact Us][106]\n\nDownload or view our [Terms & Conditions.][107]\n\n#### Latest News\n\n[Precision Optical to Exhibit at SPIE Defense & Security in National Harbor 2026][108]\n\nApril 20, 2026\n\n[Precision Optical (The Prism Specialists) to Exhibit at SPIE Photonics West 2026 in San Francisco,\nCA][109]\n\nJanuary 12, 2026\n\n[Precision Optical to Exhibit at SPIE OptiFab 2025 in Rochester, NY][110]\n\nOctober 13, 2025\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/ISO_9001-ENG-101059-2011-AQ-USA-ANA\nB-7-20250730-1.pdf\n[3]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/ISO_9001-ENG-11428-2007-AQ-USA-RvA-\n9-20250730-1.pdf\n[4]: mailto:Sales@precisionoptical.com\n[5]: tel:9496316800\n[6]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/\n[7]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/\n[8]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/corner-cube-retroreflector/\n[9]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/porro-prism-right-angle-prism/\n[10]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/beamsplitter/\n[11]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/penta-prism/\n[12]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/other-optics/\n[13]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/optical-flats/\n[14]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/optical-flats/large-optical-flat/\n[15]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/optical-flats/unmounted-reference-flat/\n[16]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/optical-flats/optical-window-and-optical-mir\nror/\n[17]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/optical-flats/mounted-reference-flat/\n[18]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/alignment-cube/\n[19]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/catalog-optics/\n[20]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/assembly-integration/\n[21]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/\n[22]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/mirror/\n[23]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/mirror/protected-enhanced-aluminum/\n[24]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/mirror/protected-enhanced-silver/\n[25]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/mirror/dielectric-broadband/\n[26]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/mirror/cold-hot/\n[27]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/anti-reflection/\n[28]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/anti-reflection/single-layer/\n[29]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/anti-reflection/v-coat/\n[30]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/anti-reflection/double-v-coat/\n[31]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/anti-reflection/broadband-uv-vis-nir-swir/\n[32]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/beamsplitter/\n[33]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/beamsplitter/non-polarizing-beamsplitter/\n[34]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/beamsplitter/polarizing-beamsplitter/\n[35]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/beamsplitter/broadband-polarizing-beamsplitter/\n[36]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/filter-2/\n[37]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/filter-2/shortwave-pass/\n[38]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/filter-2/longwave-pass/\n[39]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/filter-2/band-pass-2/\n[40]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/filter-2/neutral-density/\n[41]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/thin-film-coating-technology/\n[42]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/thin-film-coating-technology/e-beam/\n[43]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/thin-film-coating-technology/ion-beam-sputtering-ibs\n[44]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/thin-film-coating-technology/thermal-evaporation/\n[45]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/thin-film-coating-technology/plasma-assist/\n[46]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/thin-film-coating-technology/ion-assist/\n[47]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/equipment/\n[48]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/equipment/coating-chambers/\n[49]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/equipment/counter-rotating-uniformity-masking/\n[50]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/equipment/laminar-flow-hood-stations/\n[51]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/equipment/nitrogen-generating-system/\n[52]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/equipment/thermal-humidity-and-environmental-chamber\n[53]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/equipment/large-optical-lifting-system/\n[54]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/equipment/spectrophotometers/\n[55]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/design/\n[56]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/design/thin-film-software/\n[57]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/design/custom-tooling/\n[58]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/laser-damage-durabili"
