          {
            "url": "https://www.precisionoptical.com/services/optical-polishing/",
            "text": "[[Precision Optical Logo]][1]\n\nITAR registered and ROHS & REACH compliant\n\nISO 9001:2015 certification\nView or download:\n[ANAB][2] and [RvA][3]\nEmail Us\nSales@precisionoptical.com\n][4]\n[Call Us\n949.631.6800][5]\nMenu\n* [Optics][6]\n* [Custom Prisms][7]\n* [Corner Cube Retroreflectors][8]\n* [Porro Prisms / Right Angle Prisms][9]\n* [Beamsplitters][10]\n* [Penta Prisms][11]\n* [Other Optics][12]\n* [Optical Flats][13]\n* [Large Optical Flats][14]\n* [Optical Flats and Wedges][15]\n* [Optical Windows and Mirrors][16]\n* [Mounted Reference Flats][17]\n* [Alignment Cubes][18]\n* [Catalog Optics][19]\n* [Assembly & Integration][20]\n* [Coatings][21]\n* [Mirrors][22]\n* [Protected / Enhanced Aluminum][23]\n* [Protected / Enhanced Silver][24]\n* [Dielectric Broadband][25]\n* [Cold / Hot][26]\n* [AR Coatings][27]\n* [Single-Layer AR][28]\n* [V-Coat][29]\n* [Double V-Coat][30]\n* [Broadband (UV, VIS, NIR, SWIR, EX)][31]\n* [Beamsplitters][32]\n* [Non-Polarizing Beamsplitter][33]\n* [Polarizing Beamsplitter][34]\n* [Broadband Polarizing Beamsplitter][35]\n* [Filters][36]\n* [Shortwave Pass][37]\n* [Longwave Pass][38]\n* [Band Pass][39]\n* [Neutral Density][40]\n* [Technology][41]\n* [E-Beam][42]\n* [Ion Beam Sputtering (IBS)][43]\n* [Thermal Evaporation][44]\n* [Plasma Assist][45]\n* [Ion Assist][46]\n* [Equipment][47]\n* [Coating Chambers][48]\n* [Counter Rotating Uniformity Masking][49]\n* [Laminar Flow Hood Stations][50]\n* [Nitrogen Generating System][51]\n* [Thermal, Humidity, and Environmental Chambers][52]\n* [Large Optical Lifting System][53]\n* [Spectrophotometers][54]\n* [Design][55]\n* [Thin Film Software][56]\n* [Custom Tooling][57]\n* [Laser Damage & Durability][58]\n* [QA & Metrology][59]\n* [Specifications and Tolerances][60]\n* [Interferometric Testing][61]\n* [Angular Testing][62]\n* [Mechanical Testing][63]\n* [Spectral Testing][64]\n* [Environmental Testing][65]\n* [Services][66]\n* [Engineering][67]\n* [Materials Qualification][68]\n* [Fabrication][69]\n* [Polishing][70]\n* [Coatings][71]\n* [Assembly][72]\n* [Metrology][73]\n* [CNC Machining][74]\n* [Optical Packaging][75]\n* [About Us][76]\n* [About Precision Optical][77]\n* [Our Facilities][78]\n* [Education and Outreach][79]\n* [Industries We Serve][80]\n* [Military & Defense][81]\n* [Astronomy & Aerospace][82]\n* [Laser][83]\n* [Metrology][84]\n* [Biomedical][85]\n* [Semi-Conductor][86]\n* [News][87]\n* [Contact Us][88]\n* [949.631.6800][89]\n[Sales@precisionoptical.com][90]\n[More Options][91]\nName(Required)\nEmail(Required)\nPhone\nCompany\nMessage\nCAPTCHA\n* * Search Search\n\n# Optical Polishing\n\n# Optical Polishing\n* [Engineering Services][92]\n* [Materials Qualification][93]\n* [Optical Fabrication][94]\n* [Optical Polishing][95]\n* [Assembly Services][96]\n* [Metrology Services][97]\n* [CNC Machining Services][98]\n* [Optical Packaging][99]\n\nOptical polishing is the linchpin of optical fabrication. It is the department that without, one\nwouldn\u2019t have fiished optics. Our polishing department is truly one of the most unique and critical\ndepartments within Precision Optical. It balances ancient recipes of optical craftsmanship, with\nmodern technology. Combined with [**autocollimation**][100], [**interferometry**][101] and\n[**surface quality inspection**][102] equipment, this department continuously inspects in-situ.\n\nPrecision Optical currently has 34 continuous single-sided polishing laps. With a host of laps\nranging from 24\u201d to 96\u201d, Precision Optical can accommodate optical polishing of substrates from 3mm\nto 750mm. Each lap can be configured for specific requirements and can currently polish any material\nlisted on our [**materials** **page**][103]. With our new **[facility][104]** , we have the capacity\nto expand our polishing department for the industries demand. This growth can and will include\npolishing equipment dedicated to **[large flats][105]**, **[infrared materials][106]**, diamond\nturning, and lens polishing.\n\nSince our days of polishing **[cornercubes][107]** that are **[still on the moon][108]**, to\npolishing the next great challenge, our confidence in meeting our customers demand is high. Thru\ndecades of trial, experimentation, research, and demand-driven polishing, we have developed\npolishing techniques and recipes that are repeatable and of the highest quality perfectly suitable\nfor laser and **[HEL applications][109]**. We welcome industry challenges as they continuously\nimprove our process control and push the limits of our polishing department.\n\n[[Precision Optical Logo White][Precision Optical Logo White]][110]\n[[Precision Optical Logo White][Precision Optical Logo White]][111]\nPrecision Optical\n320 Kalmus Drive\nCosta Mesa, CA 92626\nUSA\n[949.631.6800][112]\n[Sales@precisionoptical.com][113]\n\n#### Who We Are\n\nPrecision Optical is a world-leading manufacturer of custom prisms and optical assemblies. Our\ncutting edge technology allows us to achieve a level of precision that few others in the industry\ncan match.[ Contact us today][114] to learn more.\n\n#### Navigation\n* [> Home][115]\n* [> Optics][116]\n* [> Coatings][117]\n* [> QA & Metrology][118]\n* [> Services][119]\n* [> Industries][120]\n* [> About Us][121]\n* [> News][122]\n* [> Contact Us][123]\n\nDownload or view our [Terms & Conditions.][124]\n\n#### Latest News\n\n[Precision Optical to Exhibit at SPIE Defense & Security in National Harbor 2026][125]\n\nApril 20, 2026\n\n[Precision Optical (The Prism Specialists) to Exhibit at SPIE Photonics West 2026 in San Francisco,\nCA][126]\n\nJanuary 12, 2026\n\n[Precision Optical to Exhibit at SPIE OptiFab 2025 in Rochester, NY][127]\n\nOctober 13, 2025\n\n[1]: /\n[2]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/ISO_9001-ENG-101059-2011-AQ-USA-ANA\nB-7-20250730-1.pdf\n[3]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/ISO_9001-ENG-11428-2007-AQ-USA-RvA-\n9-20250730-1.pdf\n[4]: mailto:Sales@precisionoptical.com\n[5]: tel:9496316800\n[6]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/\n[7]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/\n[8]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/corner-cube-retroreflector/\n[9]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/porro-prism-right-angle-prism/\n[10]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/beamsplitter/\n[11]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/penta-prism/\n[12]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/custom-prism/other-optics/\n[13]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/optical-flats/\n[14]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/optical-flats/large-optical-flat/\n[15]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/optical-flats/unmounted-reference-flat/\n[16]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/optical-flats/optical-window-and-optical-mir\nror/\n[17]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/optical-flats/mounted-reference-flat/\n[18]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/alignment-cube/\n[19]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/catalog-optics/\n[20]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/precision-optics/assembly-integration/\n[21]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/\n[22]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/mirror/\n[23]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/mirror/protected-enhanced-aluminum/\n[24]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/mirror/protected-enhanced-silver/\n[25]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/mirror/dielectric-broadband/\n[26]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/mirror/cold-hot/\n[27]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/anti-reflection/\n[28]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/anti-reflection/single-layer/\n[29]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/anti-reflection/v-coat/\n[30]: https://www.precisionoptical.com/coatings/an