            "text": "* [ [English] English English en][1]\n* [ [Fran\u00e7ais] Fran\u00e7ais French fr][2]\n* [ [Deutsch] Deutsch German de][3]\n[+86 (0) 21 6248 6110][4] / [+33 (0) 1 75 43 81 08][5]\n[[Sinoptix | Optical components]][6]\n* [Home][7]\n* [Products][8]\n* [Optical components][9]\n* [Lenses][10]\n* [Aspheres][11]\n* [Cylindrical lenses][12]\n* [Prisms][13]\n* [Optical windows][14]\n* [Optical filters & coatings][15]\n* [Optical mirrors][16]\n* [Micro-optics][17]\n* [Wafers][18]\n* [Optical Materials][19]\n* [Sapphire][20]\n* [Fused silica][21]\n* [Silicon][22]\n* [Germanium][23]\n* [ZnSe][24]\n* [ZnS][25]\n* [CaF2][26]\n* [MgF2][27]\n* [BaF2][28]\n* [KBr][29]\n* [Laser optical components][30]\n* [Optical crystals][31]\n* [Laser crystals][32]\n* [Non-linear crystals][33]\n* [Technical glass][34]\n* [Glass tubes][35]\n* [Glass parts][36]\n* [IR optical components][37]\n* [UV optics][38]\n* [Optomechanics][39]\n* [Plastic optics][40]\n* [Plastic injected lens][41]\n* [Resources][42]\n* [Technical guides][43]\n* [Optical mirror][44]\n* [Parabolic mirror : a complete guide][45]\n* [Optical filter][46]\n* [Optical window][47]\n* [Optical prism][48]\n* [RGB prism : buying guide][49]\n* [Optical lens : a complete guide][50]\n* [Spherical lens for optics : a complete guide][51]\n* [Aspherical lens][52]\n* [Doublet lens][53]\n* [Cylindrical lens][54]\n* [Waveplate for optics : a complete guide][55]\n* [IR optics : a complete guide][56]\n* [What is DLC coating in optics ?][57]\n* [UV optics : a complete guide][58]\n* [Laser optics][59]\n* [Micro-optics diamond turning][60]\n* [Glass working : mechanical polishing, fire polishing, which difference?][61]\n* [Articles on materials][62]\n* [Plastic optics][63]\n* [Germanium : a complete guide][64]\n* [ZnSe / Zinc Selenide][65]\n* [ZnS / Zinc Sulfide][66]\n* [IR optics: BaF2 an alternative to germanium ?][67]\n* [Fused silica / quartz][68]\n* [Optical sapphire glass][69]\n* [Silicon optics : a complete guide][70]\n* [H-K9L Explained][71]\n* [Borosilicate glass : a complete guide][72]\n* [TPX optics : buying guide][73]\n* [THz materials : a complete guide][74]\n* [Chalcogenide Glass: a complete guide][75]\n* [Tools][76]\n* [Optical glass price references & details all in 1 table][77]\n* [Optical Materials Transmission Spectrum Chart][78]\n* [Optical wavelength to frequency converter][79]\n* [ISO 10110 optics design norm : a complete guide][80]\n* [Optical materials abbreviations][81]\n* [Scratch and Dig : a detailed explanation][82]\n* [Miscellaneous][83]\n* [Does China ban Germanium exports?][84]\n* [Best Alternatives to Thorlabs and Edmund Optics in 2026][85]\n* [About us][86]\n* [Customer references][87]\n* [News][88]\n* [Faq][89]\n* [Legal notice][90]\n* [Our offer][91]\n* [Glass working parts][92]\n* [Optics][93]\n* [Request for quote][94]\n* [[Click to open the search input field]Search][95]\n* [ **Menu** Menu ][96]\n* [Link to LinkedIn][97]\n* [Link to Youtube][98]\n* [Link to Mail][99]\n[Home][100]1 / About us\n\n# ABOUT** SINOPTIX**\n\nSinoptix responds to the increasing need for companies to have a reliable optics and glass\nmanufacturing partner in China.\n\nFounded during the year 2006 in France, from the start, Sinoptix\u2019s aim was to provide a reliable\nsolution for the purchasing of optical components and processed glass from China.\n\nIts offer soon expanded, including custom optics manufacturing with key suppliers with price and\nlead-time advantages.\n\nIn 2010, Sinoptix merged with the Belgium company AGC Business Consulting, which is operationally\nlocated in Shanghai, China. This strengthened Sinoptix\u2019s ability to handle complex projects and\noffer integration gain for both structures.\n\nIn 2011, Sinoptix developed a new department within its company, named Sinoptix Distribution,\nspecifically concentrating on supporting Western high-technology companies to distribute their\nproducts in China.\n\nSinoptix\u2019s extensive experience within the optics and glass industry and broad portfolio of audited\nsuppliers means our clients have access to manufacturing solutions for standard and custom needs,\nsmall and batch orders, shorter lead times, and better price advantages while carrying out full\nquality control assessments before worldwide dispatch.\n\n## Our Assets\n\n### THE TEAM\n\nUnderstanding clients\u2019 needs is crucial, which is why Sinoptix combines a multicultural and\nmultilingual team of Chinese and foreign engineers and professionals to avoid misunderstanding and\nensure technical expertise, transparency, and reactivity.\n\n[optical coating]\n\n### OUR FACTORIES\n\nOver the years, Sinoptix has accumulated experience and established a solid network of compliant\nfactories that specialize in different processes, allowing your company access to specific\nproduction capabilities, even if your quantities are limited.\n\n[optics maping | optical expertise]\n\n### QUALITY CONTROL\n\nQuality is key for sustainability; it requires experience, organization, and clarity.\nSinoptix-trained technicians and in-house quality control assessments ensure components meet your\nrequirements before they leave China for trouble-free supply chain management.\n\n### **Showroom**\n* [Optical components][101]\n* [Lenses][102]\n* [Aspheres][103]\n* [Cylindrical lenses][104]\n* [Optical windows][105]\n* [Prisms][106]\n* [Optical filters & coatings][107]\n* [Optical mirrors][108]\n* [Micro-optics][109]\n* [Wafers][110]\n* [Optical Materials][111]\n* [Fused silica][112]\n* [Sapphire][113]\n* [Silicon][114]\n* [Germanium][115]\n* [ZnSe][116]\n* [ZnS][117]\n* [CaF2][118]\n* [MgF2][119]\n* [BaF2][120]\n* [Optical crystals][121]\n* [Laser crystals][122]\n* [Non-linear crystals][123]\n* [Plastic optics][124]\n* [Plastic injected lens][125]\n* [Technical glass][126]\n* [Glass tubes][127]\n* [UV optics][128]\n* [IR optical components][129]\n* [Laser optical components][130]\n* [Optomechanics][131]\n\n[Contact-us][132]\n\n### **WHERE **YOU CAN FIND US\n\nSinoptix Shanghai Office\nOffice 11EF, Yujia Mansion\nN\u00b01336 HuaShan Road\nShanghai 200052\nChina\n\n### **HEADQUARTERS**\n\nAv. Des dessus de Lives (LO), 2\n5101 Namur\nBelgium\n\n### **WHERE **YOU CAN WRITE\n\nContact us directly with your request, we will answer\nto all the emails:\n[[email protected]][133]\n\n### **Optical **components & opto mechanical solutions\n* [Optical components][134]\n* [Lenses][135]\n* [Aspheres][136]\n* [Cylindrical lenses][137]\n* [Optical windows][138]\n* [Prisms][139]\n* [Optical filters & coatings][140]\n* [Optical mirrors][141]\n* [Micro-optics][142]\n* [Wafers][143]\n* [Optical Materials][144]\n* [Fused silica][145]\n* [Sapphire][146]\n* [Silicon][147]\n* [Germanium][148]\n* [ZnSe][149]\n* [ZnS][150]\n* [CaF2][151]\n* [MgF2][152]\n* [BaF2][153]\n* [Optical crystals][154]\n* [Laser crystals][155]\n* [Non-linear crystals][156]\n* [Plastic optics][157]\n* [Plastic injected lens][158]\n* [Technical glass][159]\n* [Glass tubes][160]\n* [UV optics][161]\n* [IR optical components][162]\n* [Laser optical components][163]\n* [Optomechanics][164]\n\n### **WHERE **TO CALL US\n\nCall us to discuss your projects.\nEurope (morning only) : [+33 (0) 1 75 43 81 08][165]\nAsia : [+86 (0) 21 6248 6110][166]\n[Contact-us][167]\n\n### **Disclaimers**\n\n[Privacy policy][168]\n\n[Terms of services][169]\n\n\u00a9 Copyright - Sinoptix | Optical components\n* [Link to LinkedIn][170]\n* [Link to Youtube][171]\n* [Link to Mail][172]\n[ [Scroll to top] Scroll to top ][173]\n\nWe use cookies (and similar identifiers) to deliver and measure personalized ads. By clicking\nAccept, you consent. You can adjust or withdraw consent anytime in Settings. Your choices are shared\nwith our ad partners (including Google) to respect your preferences. See our [Privacy policy][174]\nand Google\u2019s Terms for details on clicking below button.\n\n[Accept settings][175][Hide notification only][176][Settings][177][View Google business safety &\nprivacy and terms site][178]\n\n### Cookie and Privacy Settings\n\nHow we use cookies\n\nWe may request cookies to be set on your device. We use cookies to let us know when you visit our\nwebsites, how you interact with us, to enrich your user experience, and to customize your\nrelationship with our website.\n\nClick on the different category headings to find out more. You can also change some of your\npreferences. Note that blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience on our websites and\nthe services we are able to offer.\n\nEssential Website Cookies\n\nThese cookies are strictly necessary to provide you with services available through our website and\nto use some of its features.\n\nBecause these cookies are strictly necessary to deliver the website, refuseing them will have impact\nhow our site functions. You always can block or delete cookies by changing your browser settings and\nforce blocking all cookies on this website. But this will always prompt you to accept/refuse cookies\nwhen revisiting our site.\n\nWe fully respect if you want to refuse cookies but to avoid asking you again and again kindly allow\nus to store a cookie for that. You are free to opt out any time or opt in for other cookies to get a\nbetter experience. If you refuse cookies we will remove all set cookies in our domain.\n\nWe provide you with a list of stored cookies on your computer in our domain so you can check what we\nstored. Due to security reasons we are not able to show or modify cookies from other domains. You\ncan check these in your browser security settings.\n\nCheck to enable permanent hiding of message bar and refuse all cookies if you do not opt in. We need\n2 cookies to store this setting. Otherwise you will be prompted again when opening a new browser\nwindow or new a tab.\nClick to enable/disable essential site cookies.\nGoogle Analytics Cookies\n\nThese cookies collect information that is used either in aggregate form to help us understand how\nour website is being used or how effective our marketing campaigns are, or to help us customize our\nwebsite and application for you in order to enhance your experience.\n\nIf you do not want that we track your visit to our site you can disable tracking in your browser\nhere:\n\nClick to enable/disable Google Analytics tracking.\nOther external services\n\nWe also use different external services like Google Webfonts, Google Maps, and external Video\nproviders. Since these providers may collect personal data like your IP address we allow you to\nblock them here. Please be aware that this might heavily reduce the functionality and appearance of\nour site. Changes will take effect once you reload the page.\n\nGoogle Webfont Settings:\n\nClick to enable/disable Google Webfonts.\n\nGoogle Map Settings:\n\nClick to enable/disable Google Maps.\n\nGoogle reCaptcha Settings:\n\nClick to enable/disable Google reCaptcha.\n\nVimeo and Youtube video embeds:\n\nClick to enable/disable video embeds.\nPrivacy Policy\n\nYou can read about our cookies and privacy settings in detail on our Privacy Policy Page.\n\n[Privacy policy][179]\n[Accept settings][180][Hide notification only][181]\n\n[1]: https://sinoptix.eu/about-us/\n[2]: https://sinoptix.eu/fr/about-us/\n[3]: https://sinoptix.eu/de/uber-uns/\n[4]: tel:+86 (0) 21 6248 6110\n[5]: tel:+33 (0) 1 75 43 81 08\n[6]: https://sinoptix.eu/\n[7]: https://sinoptix.eu/\n[8]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/\n[9]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/\n[10]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/lenses-supplier/\n[11]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/lenses-supplier/aspheres/\n[12]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/lenses-supplier/cylindrical-lenses/\n[13]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/prisms/\n[14]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/optical-windows/\n[15]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/optical-filter/\n[16]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/optical-mirrors/\n[17]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/micro-optics/\n[18]: https://sinoptix.eu/technical-glass/wafers/\n[19]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/\n[20]: https://sinoptix.eu/sapphire-optical-components/\n[21]: https://sinoptix.eu/quartz-parts/\n[22]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/ir-optical-components/silicon-optical-components/\n[23]: https://sinoptix.eu/optical-components/ir-optical-components/germanium-optical-components/\n[24]: https://sinopt"
