          {
            "url": "https://www.spectraldynamics.com/solutions/pind-system/felix/single-multple-crystal-sensors",
            "text": "[ [Spectral Dynamics Inc.] ][1]\n* [Home][2]\n* [About SD][3]\n* [History of Spectral Dynamics][4]\n* [ Shakers ][5]\n\n### Shakers\n* [Overview][6]\n* [Water Cooled][7]\n* [Air Cooled][8]\n* [Vibration Shaker Systems Buyer's Guide][9]\n\n### Options\n* [Slip Tables & Head Expanders][10]\n* [Shock Test Machines][11]\n* [Hydraulic Exciters][12]\n* [ Vibration Controllers ][13]\n\n### Multiple/Single Axis\n* [Jaguar\u2122][14]\n\n### Single Axis\n* [Panther][15]\n* [Puma\u2122][16]\n* [Lynx\u2122][17]\n* [ Advanced Solutions ][18]\n\n### ARPG Products\n* [SIPS\u2122][19]\n* [VIDAS\u2122][20]\n* [IMPAX-SD-LAB\u2122][21]\n\n### P.I.N.D. System\n* [Felix\u2122 Computer Aided Test System][22]\n\n### Advanced Solutions\n* [Shock Test Systems][23]\n* [BalanceTool\u2122][24]\n\n### High Speed Data Acquisition\n* [VIDAS\u2122][25]\n\n### Data Analysis\n* [CATS\u2122][26]\n* [STAR Modal\u2122][27]\n* [STAR Acoustics\u2122][28]\n* [Support][29]\n\n### Service & Information\n* [Vibration Control Buyer\u2019s Guide][30]\n* [Request Product Information][31]\n* [Contact SD][32]\n* [Customer Training][33]\n* [Domestic US Service][34]\n\n### Software Support\n* [Panther Software Tutorials ][35]\n* [Spectral Dynamics Software FAQs][36]\n* [CATS / STAR Modal\u2122 Help][37]\n\n### Additional Support\n* [Related Links][38]\n* [Technical Library][39]\n* [Spectral Dynamics Vibration Calculator][40]\n1. You are here:\n2. [Home][41]\n3. Advanced Solutions\n4. PIND System\n5. [Felix\u2122 Computer Aided Test System][42]\n6. [Single/Multple Crystal Sensors][43]\nSearch\nSearch\n\n# Single and Multiple Crystal Sensors for PIND Testing with the FELIX System\n\nThe sensor is defined in terms of its longitudinal sensitivity in the physical parameter of pressure\nas -77.5dB+/-3dB ref 1V/microbar as described in the absolute calibration method of ANSI S1.2-1988,\nusing a full-field three sensor underwater reciprocity calibration technique to accurately measure\nthe crystal response.\n\nLess accurate methods of sensitivity measurement used include capacitive pickup calibration or\nultrasonic white noise calibration, which can be used to measure the sensor output but are only\nrelative measurement methods and can made accurate only by referencing the absolute underwater\ncalibration method.\n\nAll SD PIND sensors have a complete Faraday shield around each crystal to protect the sensor from\nunwanted stray electrical signals. This protection enhanced by the five-conductor, seven-layer\nflexible circuit that attaches the sensor to the shaker mounted connector eliminates the need for\nTransient Detectors with Spike indicators required on older PIND systems. The sensor peak\nsensitivity can be dampened by a variety of factors but the most common reason for sensors to lose\nsensitivity over time is the bond that holds the crystal to the front surface wear plate will begin\nto micro crack with use and age.\n\n**MULTIPLE CRYSTAL SENSORS**\n[All SD PIND sensors have a complete Faraday shield around each crystal to protect the sensor from\nunwanted stray electrical signals.]As the sensor crystal and the source of the acoustic wave get\nfarther apart the measured energy is reduced. JEDEC Recommended Practice 114 graphically outlines\nthe decay of detection is down to less than 50% at distances over 0.75 in from the impact site. For\nthe PIND test it is then important that the lid of the part to be tested be placed a close to the\ncrystal in the sensor as possible. The Model 100-5S155-4 sensor incorporates five separate impact\ndetection crystals within the single sensor. The most sensitive area of the sensor are those areas\nwhere each detection crystal is located. For testing small parts, it is important to place the part\ndirectly on one of the four target areas.\n\nFelix Features\n\n* #### [Advanced PIND Detection with the FELIX System][44]\n\n[ [PIND sensor diagram and how it works] ][45]\n* #### [Advanced PIND Testing Technology in the FELIX System][46]\n\n[ [For over fifty years the PIND Products Group of SPECTRAL DYNAMICS, INC. has given users simple,\nreliable, and inexpensive tools to perform Particle Impact Noise Detection (PIND) testing to\nincrease the reliability of electronic components.] ][47]\n* #### [FELIX PIND System: Four Independent Data Acquisition Channels][48]\n\n[ [The FELIX\u2122 system uses four unique channels of data collection. All four channels use the same\nclock to digitize the data at 2.5M samples per second.] ][49]\n* #### [Single and Multiple Crystal Sensors for PIND Testing with the FELIX System][50]\n\n[ [All SD PIND sensors have a complete Faraday shield around each crystal to protect the sensor\nfrom unwanted stray electrical signals.] ][51]\n* #### [Unique Features & Programmable Software][52]\n\n[ [The SD FELIX\u2122 system easily exceeds the requirements of all military standards for PIND\ntesting] ][53]\n\n## Ready to Evaluate the FELIX PIND System for Your Testing Needs?\n\nContact Spectral Dynamics to discuss your PIND testing requirements and learn how the FELIX system\ncan improve accuracy, reliability, and workflow efficiency in your laboratory.\n\n[ Request Information ][54]\n\nSpectral Dynamics, Inc. is a leading worldwide supplier of systems and software for vibration\ntesting, structural dynamics, and acoustic analysis. Spectral Dynamics' products are used for design\nverification, product testing and process improvement by manufacturers of all types of electronic\nand mechanical products.\n\n1500 Wyatt Drive Suite 14\nSanta Clara, CA 95054-1522\nTel: (800) 778-8755\n[sales@spectraldynamics.com][55]\n[service@spectraldynamics.com][56]\n\n### Vibration Controllers\n* [Panther ][57]\n* [ Lynx ][58]\n* [Puma ][59]\n* [Jaguar][60]\n\n### Advanced Solutions\n* [Felix - P.I.N.D.][61]\n* [Shock Test Systems][62]\n\n### Support\n* [Contact][63]\n* [Product Information][64]\n* [Domestic U.S. Service][65]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Spectral Dynamics Inc. [Privacy Policy][66]\n\n[Download our ISO 9001:2015 certificate][67] | [Sitemap][68]\n\n[[Link to Spectral Dynamics Facebook Page]][69][[Link to Spectral Dynamics Google\nresults.]][70][[Link to Spectral Dynamics Youtube Page]][71]\n\n[1]: https://www.spectraldynamics.com/\n[2]: /\n[3]: /home/about-sd\n[4]: /pdf/History_of_Spectral_Dynamics.pdf\n[5]: javascript:;\n[6]: /shakers/overview\n[7]: /shakers/water-cooled\n[8]: /shakers/air-cooled\n[9]: /shakers/vibration-shaker-systems-buyers-guide\n[10]: /shakers/slip-tables-head-expanders\n[11]: /shakers/shock-test-machines\n[12]: /shakers/hydraulic-exciters\n[13]: javascript:;\n[14]: /vibration-controllers/multiple-axis/jaguar\n[15]: /panther\n[16]: /vibration-controllers/single-axis/puma\n[17]: /vibration-controllers/single-axis/lynx\n[18]: javascript:;\n[19]: /solutions/arpg-products/sips\n[20]: /solutions/arpg-products/vidas\n[21]: /solutions/arpg-products/impax-sd-lab\n[22]: /solutions/pind-system/felix\n[23]: /solutions/shock-test-systems\n[24]: /solutions/balancetool-home\n[25]: /solutions/arpg-products/vidas\n[26]: /solutions/analyzer/cats\n[27]: /solutions/analyzer/star-modal\n[28]: /solutions/analyzer/star-acoustics\n[29]: /support\n[30]: /support/vibration-control-buyers-guide\n[31]: /support/request-product-information\n[32]: /support/contact-sd\n[33]: /support/customer-training\n[34]: /support/domestic-us-service\n[35]: /support/panther-software-tutorials\n[36]: /support/spectral-dynamics-software/faqs\n[37]: /support/cats-modal-star-modal/faqs\n[38]: /support/related-links\n[39]: /support/technical-library\n[40]: /support/free-vibration-calculator-download\n[41]: /\n[42]: /solutions/pind-system/felix\n[43]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/single-multple-crystal-sensors\n[44]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/pind-detection\n[45]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/pind-detection\n[46]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/advanced-technology\n[47]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/advanced-technology\n[48]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/four-unique-channels-of-data-acquisition\n[49]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/four-unique-channels-of-data-acquisition\n[50]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/single-multple-crystal-sensors\n[51]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/single-multple-crystal-sensors\n[52]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/unique-features-programmable-software\n[53]: /solutions/pind-system/felix/unique-features-programmable-software\n[54]: /support/request-product-information\n[55]: mailto:sales@spectraldynamics.com\n[56]: mailto:service@spectraldynamics.com\n[57]: /panther\n[58]: /vibration-controllers/single-axis/lynx\n[59]: /vibration-controllers/single-axis/puma\n[60]: /vibration-controllers/multiple-axis/jaguar\n[61]: /solutions/p-i-n-d-system/felix-computer-aided-test-system\n[62]: /solutions/shock-test-systems\n[63]: /support/contact-sd\n[64]: /support/request-product-information\n[65]: /support/domestic-us-service\n[66]: /index.php/support/privacy-policy\n[67]: /pdf/Spectral_Dynamics_2023_ISO_9001_2015_Management_System_Certificate.pdf\n[68]: /sitemap\n[69]: https://www.facebook.com/Spectral-Dynamics-116990255000523/\n[70]: https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1CHBF_enUS945US945&q=Spectral+Dynamics&stick=H4sIAAAAAAAAA\nONgecR4iZFb4OWPe8JSJxgnrTl5jfEgIxdXcEZ-uWteSWZJpZALFxuUpcIlKMWrn65vaJhhVllUlWSarMEgxc-FKiQloiXEWdy38\n8n6KS7eglf3CwfragY8V4oxCth1ado5Ni9BBiAoOx_sIGUkeH7ukUU7lgrZawlxsXsW--QnJ-YIJl__a1WQt8JeS5iLIySxIj8vP\n7dS0IuJ4cCD_-_tlTg5gbodbpx8Za_F0LRvxSE2Fg5GAYYgmCPSciuLsjIyingWsQoGF6QmlxQl5ii4VOYl5mYmFwMA_u693-wAA\nAA&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjGldTl57fvAhUOFTQIHSDKAVcQ6RN6BAgOEAE&biw=1296&bih=739\n[71]: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCEPFhx_26dmu19mxRRBhYWg"
