            "url": "https://www.spectraldynamics.com/solutions/analyzer/star-acoustics",
            "text": "[ [Spectral Dynamics Inc.] ][1]\n* [Home][2]\n* [About SD][3]\n* [History of Spectral Dynamics][4]\n* [ Shakers ][5]\n\n### Shakers\n* [Overview][6]\n* [Water Cooled][7]\n* [Air Cooled][8]\n* [Vibration Shaker Systems Buyer's Guide][9]\n\n### Options\n* [Slip Tables & Head Expanders][10]\n* [Shock Test Machines][11]\n* [Hydraulic Exciters][12]\n* [ Vibration Controllers ][13]\n\n### Multiple/Single Axis\n* [Jaguar\u2122][14]\n\n### Single Axis\n* [Panther][15]\n* [Puma\u2122][16]\n* [Lynx\u2122][17]\n* [ Advanced Solutions ][18]\n\n### ARPG Products\n* [SIPS\u2122][19]\n* [VIDAS\u2122][20]\n* [IMPAX-SD-LAB\u2122][21]\n\n### P.I.N.D. System\n* [Felix\u2122 Computer Aided Test System][22]\n\n### Advanced Solutions\n* [Shock Test Systems][23]\n* [BalanceTool\u2122][24]\n\n### High Speed Data Acquisition\n* [VIDAS\u2122][25]\n\n### Data Analysis\n* [CATS\u2122][26]\n* [STAR Modal\u2122][27]\n* [STAR Acoustics\u2122][28]\n* [Support][29]\n\n### Service & Information\n* [Vibration Control Buyer\u2019s Guide][30]\n* [Request Product Information][31]\n* [Contact SD][32]\n* [Customer Training][33]\n* [Domestic US Service][34]\n\n### Software Support\n* [Panther Software Tutorials ][35]\n* [Spectral Dynamics Software FAQs][36]\n* [CATS / STAR Modal\u2122 Help][37]\n\n### Additional Support\n* [Related Links][38]\n* [Technical Library][39]\n* [Spectral Dynamics Vibration Calculator][40]\n1. You are here:\n2. [Home][41]\n3. Advanced Solutions\n4. Analyzer\n5. [STAR Acoustics\u2122][42]\nSearch\nSearch\n\n## STAR Acoustics\n\n### **Acoustic Intensity Testing**\n\n**Improve Productivity, and Accuracy\n**CATSAcoustics is a complete acoustic intensity program for use with Spectral Dynamics Puma/Cougar\ndata acquisitions systems. STARAcoustics is a complete stand alone acoustic intensity program for\nuse with many other multi-channel FFT instruments or real-time octave analyzers and microphone\nprobes.\n\nAcoustic intensity analysis enables you to:\n* Quickly identify noise sources\n* Accurately determine the sound power radiating from noise sources\n* Acquire measurements in acoustically noisy environments (in-situ), eliminating the need for costly\nacoustic chambers.\n* Check for ISO standards compliance in seconds\n\nOptimized for identifying noise sources and quantifying sound power, STAR Acoustics simplifies\ntesting and helps you attain unmatched testing accuracy. It's comprehensive features set enables you\nto import data from your instrument, perform detailed analysis, view results in a variety of\nformats, and produce high-quality reports.\n\n### **Test Setup and Data Analysis**\n\n**Quickly Set Up Standard or Custom Test Configurations**\nSTARAcoustics organizes data by project: All test parameters related to the instrument, microphone,\nand environmental conditions are conveniently located in a single Project Slate. New and occasional\nusers can guide themselves step-by-step through the acoustic intensity process by referring to the\nShow Assistant, a process-oriented task list.\n\n**Analyze Measurements and Data Sets in a Flexible Display**\nThe STARAcoustics program has a state-of-the-art, interactive measurement display designed expressly\nfor narrow band and octave band acoustic measurements, including real, complex, and bi-polar data.\nYou can view individual measurements, or, because the display accommodates an unlimited number of\nmeasurement windows, view entire data sets to spot trends or anomalies. A comprehensive set of\ndisplay features-cursors, zooming, grids, and scaling-enables you to focus on the measurements of\ninterest.\n\n**Comprehensive Measurement Analysis Functions**\nThe STARAcoustics program performs a very wide variety of functions on narrowband and octave-band\nintensity or sound pressure level (SPL) data. Narrowband cross spectra and auto power data is\nautomatically converted to Intensity and Sound Pressure datatypes respectively, synthesize data into\n1/1 octave, 1 /3 octave, or user-defined bands. Weighting (A, B, and C) and correction (amplitude\nand phase) are easily applied. Critical data evaluation functions such as Pressure-Intensity(PI)\nindex, Residual PI, and Dynamic Capability index are automatically computed as part of the Plot tab\nData Types.\n\n**Checking of Measurement Quality**\nTo check overall measurement quality, the STARAcoustics Measurement display can be configured to\noverlay the Dynamic Capability Index of the measurement system and the PI Index of selected\nmeasurements. You can easily scroll through the PI Indexes for each measurement location and to\nvisually inspect measurements to confirm that they are within the acceptable limits of the dynamic\ncapability of the measurement system.\n\n**Noise Source Identification**\n\n**Locate Noise Sources**\nCATSAcoustics/STARAcoustics graphs data in two or three dimensions to help you identify the location\nof noise sources. Contour maps handle both uniform and non-uniform test grids that match the\ngeometry of a planar test surface. 3D vector displays enable you to examine the characteristics of\nsound fields, particularly around non-uniform structures. The vectors provide insight into noise\nsource locations, strength of intensity, and propagation direction.\n\n### **Sound Power Analysis**\n\n**Quantify and Compare Total Acoustic Energy Using Sound Power\n**STARAcoustics uses the areas associated with each measurement location to compute overall sound\npower. You can view computed power levels in either tabular or chart formats, in watts, decibels or\npercent of total power, and computed by point, component, or overall level. You can rank data to\nquickly identify significant sound power contributors or choose a single command to compute the\ncomposite sound power spectrum from a set of measurements.\n\n**Noise Source Ranking Highlights Key Noise Contributors**\nComputing the sound power for points and groups of points, called Templates and Components, is a\npowerful technique for quickly locating major contributors to overall\n\n## Ready to Evaluate Vibration Control Systems?\n\nContact Spectral Dynamics to discuss your specific testing requirements and explore how our advanced\nvibration control solutions can benefit your laboratory.\n\n[ Request Information ][43]\n\nSpectral Dynamics, Inc. is a leading worldwide supplier of systems and software for vibration\ntesting, structural dynamics, and acoustic analysis. Spectral Dynamics' products are used for design\nverification, product testing and process improvement by manufacturers of all types of electronic\nand mechanical products.\n\n1500 Wyatt Drive Suite 14\nSanta Clara, CA 95054-1522\nTel: (800) 778-8755\n[sales@spectraldynamics.com][44]\n[service@spectraldynamics.com][45]\n\n### Vibration Controllers\n* [Panther ][46]\n* [ Lynx ][47]\n* [Puma ][48]\n* [Jaguar][49]\n\n### Advanced Solutions\n* [Felix - P.I.N.D.][50]\n* [Shock Test Systems][51]\n\n### Support\n* [Contact][52]\n* [Product Information][53]\n* [Domestic U.S. Service][54]\n\n\u00a9 2026 Spectral Dynamics Inc. [Privacy Policy][55]\n\n[Download our ISO 9001:2015 certificate][56] | [Sitemap][57]\n\n[[Link to Spectral Dynamics Facebook Page]][58][[Link to Spectral Dynamics Google\nresults.]][59][[Link to Spectral Dynamics Youtube Page]][60]\n\n[1]: https://www.spectraldynamics.com/\n[2]: /\n[3]: /home/about-sd\n[4]: /pdf/History_of_Spectral_Dynamics.pdf\n[5]: javascript:;\n[6]: /shakers/overview\n[7]: /shakers/water-cooled\n[8]: /shakers/air-cooled\n[9]: /shakers/vibration-shaker-systems-buyers-guide\n[10]: /shakers/slip-tables-head-expanders\n[11]: /shakers/shock-test-machines\n[12]: /shakers/hydraulic-exciters\n[13]: javascript:;\n[14]: /vibration-controllers/multiple-axis/jaguar\n[15]: /panther\n[16]: /vibration-controllers/single-axis/puma\n[17]: /vibration-controllers/single-axis/lynx\n[18]: javascript:;\n[19]: /solutions/arpg-products/sips\n[20]: /solutions/arpg-products/vidas\n[21]: /solutions/arpg-products/impax-sd-lab\n[22]: /solutions/pind-system/felix\n[23]: /solutions/shock-test-systems\n[24]: /solutions/balancetool-home\n[25]: /solutions/arpg-products/vidas\n[26]: /solutions/analyzer/cats\n[27]: /solutions/analyzer/star-modal\n[28]: /solutions/analyzer/star-acoustics\n[29]: /support\n[30]: /support/vibration-control-buyers-guide\n[31]: /support/request-product-information\n[32]: /support/contact-sd\n[33]: /support/customer-training\n[34]: /support/domestic-us-service\n[35]: /support/panther-software-tutorials\n[36]: /support/spectral-dynamics-software/faqs\n[37]: /support/cats-modal-star-modal/faqs\n[38]: /support/related-links\n[39]: /support/technical-library\n[40]: /support/free-vibration-calculator-download\n[41]: /\n[42]: /solutions/analyzer/star-acoustics\n[43]: /support/request-product-information\n[44]: mailto:sales@spectraldynamics.com\n[45]: mailto:service@spectraldynamics.com\n[46]: /panther\n[47]: /vibration-controllers/single-axis/lynx\n[48]: /vibration-controllers/single-axis/puma\n[49]: /vibration-controllers/multiple-axis/jaguar\n[50]: /solutions/p-i-n-d-system/felix-computer-aided-test-system\n[51]: /solutions/shock-test-systems\n[52]: /support/contact-sd\n[53]: /support/request-product-information\n[54]: /support/domestic-us-service\n[55]: /index.php/support/privacy-policy\n[56]: /pdf/Spectral_Dynamics_2023_ISO_9001_2015_Management_System_Certificate.pdf\n[57]: /sitemap\n[58]: https://www.facebook.com/Spectral-Dynamics-116990255000523/\n[59]: https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1C1CHBF_enUS945US945&q=Spectral+Dynamics&stick=H4sIAAAAAAAAA\nONgecR4iZFb4OWPe8JSJxgnrTl5jfEgIxdXcEZ-uWteSWZJpZALFxuUpcIlKMWrn65vaJhhVllUlWSarMEgxc-FKiQloiXEWdy38\n8n6KS7eglf3CwfragY8V4oxCth1ado5Ni9BBiAoOx_sIGUkeH7ukUU7lgrZawlxsXsW--QnJ-YIJl__a1WQt8JeS5iLIySxIj8vP\n7dS0IuJ4cCD_-_tlTg5gbodbpx8Za_F0LRvxSE2Fg5GAYYgmCPSciuLsjIyingWsQoGF6QmlxQl5ii4VOYl5mYmFwMA_u693-wAA\nAA&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjGldTl57fvAhUOFTQIHSDKAVcQ6RN6BAgOEAE&biw=1296&bih=739\n[60]: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCEPFhx_26dmu19mxRRBhYWg"
