y Purposes][65]\n  * [Product Temperature Measurement during Granulation][66]\n* [Service][67]\n  * [Downloads][68]\n  * [Service Request][69]\n* [News][70]\n* [Articles][71]\n* [Videos][72]\n* [Events][73]\n* [Company][74]\n  * [Introduction][75]\n  * [Certification][76]\n  * [Career & Job Offers][77]\n  * [Sustainability at Tempris][78]\n  * [Contact][79]\n1. [Tempris][80]\n\n## Tempris for\n## product-centric lyophilization\n\nLyoCONNECT builds the data layer inside the freeze-dryer. LyoINSIGHT turns this data into\nprocess-understanding, endpoint evaluation, transfer support and optimization.\n[Contact us to explore the benefits of Tempris for your lyo process][81]\n\n# Tempris for Lyophilization\n\n## Product-level visibility and product-centric process intelligence\n\nLyoCONNECT links vial-level product temperature data with process and freeze-dryer information,\ncreating a digital twin foundation at the product and equipment levels. LyoINSIGHT \u2013 powered by\nLyoCLC \u2013 turns this connected data foundation into product-centric process intelligence.\n\n## LyoCONNECT\n\nLyoCONNECT captures real product temperature data, sensor identity and positioning, process data and\nvisualization into a digital twin foundation from R&D through engineering and technology transfer.\n\n### LyoCONNECT\n\nReliable, traceable and connected product temperature data. Creates transparency about product and\nequipment behavior from R&D through technology transfer.\n\n## LyoINSIGHT powered by LyoCLC\u00ae\n\nLyoINSIGHT analyzes lyophilization data from LyoCONNECT with LyoCLC\u00ae and turns measurement data into\nactionable process intelligence.\n\n### LyoINSIGHT powered by LyoCLC\u00ae\n\nProduct-based process decisions with LyoCLC\u00ae. Supports endpoint assessment, cycle optimization,\nscale-up, transfer comparison and CPV-oriented process evaluation.\n\nTempris is the innovation leader in wireless in-process product temperature control for\nfreeze-drying \u2013 with **over 15 years of experience in pharmaceutical practice**. Tempris connects\n**lab, tech transfer, and GMP production** through an identical temperature profile \u2013 regardless of\nlocation, b [Skip to content][1]\n* [Phone][2]\n* [Email][3]\n* [Newsletter][4]\n* [Contact][5]\n* [English][6]\n  * [Deutsch][7]\n* [Phone][8]\n* [Email][9]\n* [Newsletter][10]\n* [Contact][11]\n* [English][12]\n  * [Deutsch][13]\n[[Tempris]][14]\nSearch for:\nToggle Navigation\n* [Tempris][15]\n* [LyoCONNECT][16]\n  * [Products][17]\n    * [Robot-Controlled Process Automation][18]\n    * [3D Digital Twin][19]\n    * [Universal Sensor Technology][20]\n    * [Temperature Measurement Technology][21]\n      * [TLM Software][22]\n      * [Tempris Hardware][23]\n      * [Tempris Accessories][24]\n* [LyoINSIGHT][25]\n  * [Tempris LyoCLC][26]\n* [Applications][27]\n  * [Real-time Product Temperature Monitoring][28]\n  * [Hot-and-Cold Spot Recognition in Lyophilization][29]\n  * [Lyophilization Cycle Optimization][30]\n  * [Lyophilization Cycle Scale-Up and Transfer][31]\n  * [Data Preparation for Regulatory Purposes][32]\n  * [Product Temperature Measurement during Granulation][33]\n* [Service][34]\n  * [Downloads][35]\n  * [Service Request][36]\n* [News][37]\n* [Articles][38]\n* [Videos][39]\n* [Events][40]\n* [Company][41]\n  * [Introduction][42]\n  * [Certification][43]\n  * [Career & Job Offers][44]\n  * [Sustainability at Tempris][45]\n  * [Contact][46]\n[[Tempris]][47]\nSearch for:\nToggle Navigation\n* Search for:\nToggle Navigation\n* [Tempris][48]\n* [LyoCONNECT][49]\n  * [Products][50]\n    * [Robot-Controlled Process Automation][51]\n    * [3D Digital Twin][52]\n    * [Universal Sensor Technology][53]\n    * [Temperature Measurement Technology][54]\n      * [TLM Software][55]\n      * [Tempris Hardware][56]\n      * [Tempris Accessories][57]\n* [LyoINSIGHT][58]\n  * [Tempris LyoCLC][59]\n* [Applications][60]\n  * [Real-time Product Temperature Monitoring][61]\n  * [Hot-and-Cold Spot Recognition in Lyophilization][62]\n  * [Lyophilization Cycle Optimization][63]\n  * [Lyophilization Cycle Scale-Up and Transfer][64]\n  * [Data Preparation for Regulatory Purposes][65]\n  * [Product Temperature Measurement during Granulation][66]\n* [Service][67]\n  * [Downloads][68]\n  * [Service Request][69]\n* [News][70]\n* [Articles][71]\n* [Videos][72]\n* [Events][73]\n* [Company][74]\n  * [Introduction][75]\n  * [Certification][76]\n  * [Career & Job Offers][77]\n  * [Sustainability at Tempris][78]\n  * [Contact][79]\n1. [Tempris][80]\n\n## Tempris for\n## product-centric lyophilization\n\nLyoCONNECT builds the data layer inside the freeze-dryer. LyoINSIGHT turns this data into\nprocess-understanding, endpoint evaluation, transfer support and optimization.\n[Contact us to explore the benefits of Tempris for your lyo process][81]\n\n# Tempris for Lyophilization\n\n## Product-level visibility and product-centric process intelligence\n\nLyoCONNECT links vial-level product temperature data with process and freeze-dryer information,\ncreating a digital twin foundation at the product and equipment levels. LyoINSIGHT \u2013 powered by\nLyoCLC \u2013 turns this connected data foundation into product-centric process intelligence.\n\n## LyoCONNECT\n\nLyoCONNECT captures real product temperature data, sensor identity and positioning, process data and\nvisualization into a digital twin foundation from R&D through engineering and technology transfer.\n\n### LyoCONNECT\n\nReliable, traceable and connected product temperature data. Creates transparency about product and\nequipment behavior from R&D through technology transfer.\n\n## LyoINSIGHT powered by LyoCLC\u00ae\n\nLyoINSIGHT analyzes lyophilization data from LyoCONNECT with LyoCLC\u00ae and turns measurement data into\nactionable process intelligence.\n\n### LyoINSIGHT powered by LyoCLC\u00ae\n\nProduct-based process decisions with LyoCLC\u00ae. Supports endpoint assessment, cycle optimization,\nscale-up, transfer comparison and CPV-oriented process evaluation.\n\nTempris is the innovation leader in wireless in-process product temperature control for\nfreeze-drying \u2013 with **over 15 years of experience in pharmaceutical practice**. Tempris connects\n**lab, tech transfer, and GMP production** through an identical temperature profile \u2013 regardless of\nlocation, batch size, or equipment.\n\nPharma and biotech companies use Tempris as a **scalable, PAT-enabled platform** to:\n* **Significantly reduce time-to-market**\n* **Strategically lower manufacturing costs (COGs)**\n* **Standardize, validate, and integrate global processes without technology disruption**\n\nWith real-time data directly from the product, Tempris empowers strategic initiatives such as\n**design for manufacturability**, digital twins, and automated release decisions.\n\n### The result: Less risk. Faster product launches. Higher margins.\n\n### Are you ready to revolutionize your freeze-drying process and take your product development to\n### the next level?\n\n#### Tempris sensor technology can help you streamline your processes and comply with FDA\n#### regulations, allowing you to get your product to market faster.\n\n[Contact Us][82]\n\n## See how Tempris Sensor Technology Works\n\n\n## Fields of Application of the Tempris System\n\n[**Real-time Product Temperature Monitoring**][83]\n\n[[Icon of a temperature curve]][84]\n[Learn more][85]\n\n[**Hot and Cold Spot Monitoring**][86]\n\n[[icon for hold and cold spot monitoring]][87]\n[Learn more][88]\n\n[**Lyo-Cycle**][89]\n[**Optimization**][90]\n\n[[icon for the lyo cycle - a circle with arrows]][91]\n[Learn more][92]\n\n[**Lyo-Cycle Scale-Up and Transfer**][93]\n\n[[icon for scale-up]][94]\n[Learn more][95]\n\n[**Tempris Data for Regulatory Submission**][96]\n\n[[icon regulatory submissions]][97]\n[Learn more][98]\n\n[**Measurement during Granulation**][99]\n\n[[icon for granulation]][100]\n[Learn more][101]\n\n## Tempris Testimonials\n\n> ### Syros\u2019 Experience with Tempris\n> \n> *\u201eTempris has been a wonderful partner to us, and their wireless technology was very helpful\n> during our product development with an atypical process. They took time to understand our specific\n> need and customized sensors and loading mechanisms for our specific application. Having a reliable\n> and repeatable temperature measurement capability across multiple sites proved essential for\n> transfer activities. Customer service was excellent along with support for both technical needs\n> and parts.\u201d *\n\n[Logo Syros Pharmaceuticals]**Syros Pharmaceuticals**\n\n> ### Pfizer\u2019s Experience with Tempris\n> \n> \u201eTempris wireless sensors allow placement of temperature sensors in any location within a\n> freeze-dryer. They are also the sensor of choice if product temperatures of edge vials are\n> monitored. Tempris sensors do not release heat while thermocouples or data loggers can transfer\n> some heat into the product (very notable for edge vials), obscuring the actual product\n> temperature. It is especially important if small fill volumes are used as readings of\n> thermocouples and data loggers from the edge vials produce uncertain temperature profiles.\u201d\n> \n> [Read More][102]\n\n**Pfizer Inc., Pharmaceutical R&D**\n\u00d7\n\n### Pfizer Testimonial\n\n> **Vaccines** becomes an important part of public health. They play an essential role in preventing\n> the spread of infectious diseases and have saved millions of lives worldwide. Most of vaccines,\n> however, are very sensitive to temperature and need to be lyophilized to remain effective. Pfizer\n> is one of the largest vaccine manufacturers of the world.\n> \n> In order to develop a robust manufacturing process significant efforts need to be made to ensure\n> the quality of the product. We typically design lyophilization process in such way that even\n> relatively wide variability of process parameters during manufacturing do not impact vaccine\n> quality. We perform robust experiments at laboratory scale generating a wide product temperature\n> design space (and wide range of process parameters associated with it) which produce product with\n> acceptable quality. We also make sure that product quality attributes remain within specification\n> for a desired shelf life for all samples generated during robustness study.\n> \n> When we transfer lyophilization process we are making sure that product temperature at large scale\n> remains withi"
