            "text": "[Zum Inhalt wechseln][1]\n[ [Logo_V2_HAIP-07_weiss] ][2]\n* [ PRODUCTS ][3] Schlie\u00dfe PRODUCTS \u00d6ffne PRODUCTS\n\n## [Cameras][4]\n\n[ [Camera_Overview_Header] ][5]\n* [ RGB ][6]\n* [ VNIR (500 - 1000 nm) ][7]\n* [ NIR (700 - 1050 nm) ][8]\n* [ SWIR (900 - 1730 nm) ][9]\n\n## [Illumination][10]\n\n[ [HAIP Solutions Illumination Overview] ][11]\n* [ BlackBright VNIR LED Area ][12]\n* [ BlackBright VNIR LED Bar ][13]\n* [ BlackBright FMWIR Bar ][14]\n\n## [Software][15]\n\n[ [Software_Overview_Header] ][16]\n* [ BlackStudio ][17]\n* [ BlackIndustry On-Camera Classifier ][18]\n\n## [Accessories][19]\n\n[ [BlackIndustry_Station_Vorne_Hinten_thumbnail_header] ][20]\n* [ BlackIndustry Station ][21]\n* [ APPLICATIONS ][22] Schlie\u00dfe APPLICATIONS \u00d6ffne APPLICATIONS\n* [ VEGETATION ][23]\n* [ RECYCLING ][24]\n* [ FOOD INDUSTRY ][25]\n* [ GEOLOGY ][26]\n* [ ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING ][27]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Vegetation] ][28]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Recycling] ][29]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Food Industry] ][30]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Geology] ][31]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Environmental Monitoring] ][32]\n* [ LIBRARY ][33] Schlie\u00dfe LIBRARY \u00d6ffne LIBRARY\n* [ KNOWLEDGE BASE ][34]\n* [ APPLICATION NOTES ][35]\n* [ WHITE PAPERS ][36]\n* [ RESEARCH PUBLICATIONS ][37]\n* [ PRESS ][38]\n* [ NEWS ][39]\n* [ SUPPORT ][40]\n* [ COMPANY ][41] Schlie\u00dfe COMPANY \u00d6ffne COMPANY\n* [ TEAM ][42]\n* [ JOBS ][43]\n* [ SALES ][44]\n* [ RESEARCH PROJECTS ][45]\n* [PRODUCTS][46]\n* [CAMERAS][47]\n* [ILLUMINATION][48]\n* [SOFTWARE][49]\n* [ACCESSORIES][50]\n* [APPLICATIONS][51]\n* [VEGETATION][52]\n* [RECYCLING][53]\n* [FOOD INDUSTRY][54]\n* [GEOLOGY][55]\n* [ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING][56]\n* [LIBRARY][57]\n* [KNOWLEDGE][58]\n* [APPLICATION NOTES][59]\n* [WHITE PAPERS][60]\n* [RESEARCH PUBLICATIONS][61]\n* [PRESS][62]\n* [SUPPORT][63]\n* [NEWS][64]\n* [COMPANY][65]\n* [TEAM][66]\n* [JOBS][67]\n* [SALES][68]\n* [RESEARCH PROJECTS][69]\n* [PRODUCTS][70]\n* [CAMERAS][71]\n* [ILLUMINATION][72]\n* [SOFTWARE][73]\n* [ACCESSORIES][74]\n* [APPLICATIONS][75]\n* [VEGETATION][76]\n* [RECYCLING][77]\n* [FOOD INDUSTRY][78]\n* [GEOLOGY][79]\n* [ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING][80]\n* [LIBRARY][81]\n* [KNOWLEDGE][82]\n* [APPLICATION NOTES][83]\n* [WHITE PAPERS][84]\n* [RESEARCH PUBLICATIONS][85]\n* [PRESS][86]\n* [SUPPORT][87]\n* [NEWS][88]\n* [COMPANY][89]\n* [TEAM][90]\n* [JOBS][91]\n* [SALES][92]\n* [RESEARCH PROJECTS][93]\n[ Contact ][94]\n\n# Research Projects\n\nHyperspectral Imaging\n\n## DeteKTiL\n\n## Detektion von Kunststoff-Teilchen in der Lebensmittelproduktion\n\n## Detection of plastic particles in food production\n\nThe aim of the KMU innovation project DeteKTiL is the developement of a detection system that is\nable to recognize transparent plastic parts via their chemical structure in the infrared range. For\nthis purpose, a conveyor belt system is being designed that ensures an optimally illuminated 360\u00b0\nscan of the food in the process and thus simultaneously enables the detection of the\nchemical-physical structure of foreign particles by means of a spectral camera and thus ensures\ntheir automatic ejection.\n\nThe overriding added value of this project is the reduction in the number of product recalls. This\nresults in a lower health risk for consumers (no ingestion of plastic particles), an economic\nadvantage for companies and CO2 savings due to less faulty production, destruction of food with\nforeign bodies and less logistical effort.\n\n## Key Facts\n* **Project duration**: 01/2024 \u2013 12/2025\n* **Funding measure**: KMU innovativ \u2013 Production Research in the program \u201cFuture of Value Creation\u201d\nof the BMBF\n* **Project partners**: CLK GmbH \u2013 Bildverarbeitung & Robotik, Singer & Sohn GmbH \u2013 F\u00f6rderanlagen-\nund Maschinenbau, Technische Hochschule N\u00fcrnberg Georg Simon Ohm (THN), HAIP Solutions GmbH\n\n## Involved HAIP Products\n\n[[Hyperspectral camera called BlackIndustry VNIR V2 manufactured by HAIP Solutions. Hyperspectral\nimaging systems and cameras]][95]\n\n### [BlackIndustry\n### VNIR V2][96]\n\n500-1000 nm wavelength range\n\n[ Read More ][97]\n[[Hyperspectral camera called BlackIndustry SWIR 1.7 manufactured by HAIP Solutions]][98]\n\n### [BlackIndustry SWIR 1.7\n### Max][99]\n\n900-1730 nm wavelength range\n\n[ Read More ][100]\n[[Hyperspectral imaging software called BlackStudio by HAIP Solutions]][101]\n\n### [BlackStudio][102]\n\nHyperspectral imaging software\n\n[ Read More ][103]\n\n## Project Partners\n\n[ [CLK GmbH und HAIP Solutions] ][104]\n[ [Singer und Sohn und HAIP Solutions] ][105]\n[ [ohm technische Universit\u00e4t N\u00fcrnberg und HAIP Solutions] ][106]\n\n## Funded by\n\n[ [BMBF und HAIP Solutions] ][107] Funding number: 02P23K031\n\n## Other Research Projects\n\n### DHYNAmite\n\nIntegrated plant protection through drone-based hyperspectral technology\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][108]\n[HAIP Solutions Research Project Mikroplastikanalyse IKK]\n\n### Mikroplastikanalyse (IKK)\n\nZIM feasibility study: Use of hyperspectral imaging for microplastic analysis\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][109]\n[HAIP Solutions Joint research project SpectralAIge]\n\n### SpectralAlge\n\nAI-supported spectroscopic plastic ageing determination during mechanical recycling\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][110]\n\n## Start with HSI Today!\n\n[ Contact Us ][111]\n\n## News\n\n[storage room]\n\n## 02.05.2024\n\n## Our joint research project \u201cDeteKTiL\"\n\n\u201cDeteKTiL\u201c stands for \u201cDetection of Plastic Particles in Food Production\u201d and is a research and\ndevelopment project within the Bundesministerium f\u00fcr Bildung und \u2026\n\n[ View More ][112]\n\n## Keep up with\n## the latest News.\n\n## Receive early access to new arrivals, sales, exclusive content, events and much more!\n\n## *By signing up, you will receive HAIP Solutions offers, promotions and other commercial messages.\n## You are also agreeing to HAIP Solutions's Privacy Policy. You may unsubscribe at any time.\n\n#### HAIP Solutions GmbH\n* [ +49 511 37352860 ][113]\n* [ info@haip-solutions.com ][114]\n* [ Escherstr. 23, 30159 Hannover ][115]\n\n#### Quicklinks\n* [ Products ][116]\n* [ Applications ][117]\n* [ Library ][118]\n* [ Support ][119]\n* [ Company ][120]\n* [ News ][121]\n\n#### Follow us\n* [ LinkedIn ][122]\n* [ Instagram ][123]\n* [ YouTube ][124]\n* [ Facebook ][125]\n\n[Privacy Policy][126]\n\n[Imprint][127]\n\n[Cookie Settings][128]\n\n## Get in touch with us!\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://www.haip-solutions.com\n[3]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/\n[4]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#cameras\n[5]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#cameras\n[6]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#rgb\n[7]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#vnir\n[8]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#nir\n[9]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#swir\n[10]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#illumination\n[11]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#illumination\n[12]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackbright-area/\n[13]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackbright-bar/\n[14]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackbright-fast-medium-wave-ir/\n[15]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#software\n[16]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#software\n[17]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/hyperspectral-imaging-software/\n[18]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/on-camera-classifier/\n[19]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/#accessories\n[20]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#accessories\n[21]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackindustry-station/\n[22]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/\n[23]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-