            "text": "[Zum Inhalt wechseln][1]\n[ [Logo_V2_HAIP-07_weiss] ][2]\n* [ PRODUCTS ][3] Schlie\u00dfe PRODUCTS \u00d6ffne PRODUCTS\n\n## [Cameras][4]\n\n[ [Camera_Overview_Header] ][5]\n* [ RGB ][6]\n* [ VNIR (500 - 1000 nm) ][7]\n* [ NIR (700 - 1050 nm) ][8]\n* [ SWIR (900 - 1730 nm) ][9]\n\n## [Illumination][10]\n\n[ [HAIP Solutions Illumination Overview] ][11]\n* [ BlackBright VNIR LED Area ][12]\n* [ BlackBright VNIR LED Bar ][13]\n* [ BlackBright FMWIR Bar ][14]\n\n## [Software][15]\n\n[ [Software_Overview_Header] ][16]\n* [ BlackStudio ][17]\n* [ BlackIndustry On-Camera Classifier ][18]\n\n## [Accessories][19]\n\n[ [BlackIndustry_Station_Vorne_Hinten_thumbnail_header] ][20]\n* [ BlackIndustry Station ][21]\n* [ APPLICATIONS ][22] Schlie\u00dfe APPLICATIONS \u00d6ffne APPLICATIONS\n* [ VEGETATION ][23]\n* [ RECYCLING ][24]\n* [ FOOD INDUSTRY ][25]\n* [ GEOLOGY ][26]\n* [ ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING ][27]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Vegetation] ][28]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Recycling] ][29]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Food Industry] ][30]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Geology] ][31]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Environmental Monitoring] ][32]\n* [ LIBRARY ][33] Schlie\u00dfe LIBRARY \u00d6ffne LIBRARY\n* [ KNOWLEDGE BASE ][34]\n* [ APPLICATION NOTES ][35]\n* [ WHITE PAPERS ][36]\n* [ RESEARCH PUBLICATIONS ][37]\n* [ PRESS ][38]\n* [ NEWS ][39]\n* [ SUPPORT ][40]\n* [ COMPANY ][41] Schlie\u00dfe COMPANY \u00d6ffne COMPANY\n* [ TEAM ][42]\n* [ JOBS ][43]\n* [ SALES ][44]\n* [ RESEARCH PROJECTS ][45]\n* [PRODUCTS][46]\n* [CAMERAS][47]\n* [ILLUMINATION][48]\n* [SOFTWARE][49]\n* [ACCESSORIES][50]\n* [APPLICATIONS][51]\n* [VEGETATION][52]\n* [RECYCLING][53]\n* [FOOD INDUSTRY][54]\n* [GEOLOGY][55]\n* [ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING][56]\n* [LIBRARY][57]\n* [KNOWLEDGE][58]\n* [APPLICATION NOTES][59]\n* [WHITE PAPERS][60]\n* [RESEARCH PUBLICATIONS][61]\n* [PRESS][62]\n* [SUPPORT][63]\n* [NEWS][64]\n* [COMPANY][65]\n* [TEAM][66]\n* [JOBS][67]\n* [SALES][68]\n* [RESEARCH PROJECTS][69]\n* [PRODUCTS][70]\n* [CAMERAS][71]\n* [ILLUMINATION][72]\n* [SOFTWARE][73]\n* [ACCESSORIES][74]\n* [APPLICATIONS][75]\n* [VEGETATION][76]\n* [RECYCLING][77]\n* [FOOD INDUSTRY][78]\n* [GEOLOGY][79]\n* [ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING][80]\n* [LIBRARY][81]\n* [KNOWLEDGE][82]\n* [APPLICATION NOTES][83]\n* [WHITE PAPERS][84]\n* [RESEARCH PUBLICATIONS][85]\n* [PRESS][86]\n* [SUPPORT][87]\n* [NEWS][88]\n* [COMPANY][89]\n* [TEAM][90]\n* [JOBS][91]\n* [SALES][92]\n* [RESEARCH PROJECTS][93]\n[ Contact ][94]\n\n# Research Projects\n\nHyperspectral Imaging\n\n## Mikroplastikanalyse (IKK)\n\n## ZIM Durchf\u00fchrbarkeitsstudie: Einsatz hyperspektraler Bildgebung zur Mikroplastikanalyse\n\n## ZIM feasibility study: Use of hyperspectral imaging for microplastic analysis\n\nThe release of plastics into the environment is a major global problem, with microplastics posing a\ngrowing threat to ecosystems. Current analytical methods, such as FTIR and Raman microscopy, are\nexpensive and complex, limiting large-scale monitoring.\n\nThe planned ZIM feasibility study aims to develop a more accessible hyperspectral imaging based\nsystem that will enable a more efficient and widespread analysis of microplastics to support efforts\nto reduce pollution. The main objectives are to ensure low susceptibility to failure and a high\ndegree of automation in the analysis process. A key component of the project is the creation of a\nclassification database capable of identifying a wide range of plastic types. In addition,\nintegrated particle analysis will be developed to determine the size and shape of microplastic\nparticles.\n\nTo achieve a competitive product, the system will be designed to detect microplastic particles as\nsmall as 100 \u03bcm, complete measurements in less than\n\n[HAIP Solutions Research Project Mikroplastikanalyse IKK]\n\n10 minutes and identify at least the following six polymer types: PP, PE, PET, PS, PVC and PU.\nEvaluation capabilities include polymer type identification with spectral matching, particle\ncounting and particle size and shape measurements.\n\nFor the first time, a third-generation hyperspectral camera will be used for the analysis of\nmicroplastics. The system is significantly less expensive and easier to use than established\nmethods, while making it accessible to new user groups and mobile applications.\n\n## Key Facts\n* **Project duration**: 10/2024 \u2013 05/2025\n* **Funding measure**: Funding program of the Federal Ministry of Economics and Climate Protection\n\u201cCentral Innovation Program for SMEs\u201d (ZIM), funding module feasibility studies\n* **Project partners**: Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz Universit\u00e4t, Institut f\u00fcr Kunststoff- und\nKreislauftechnik, HAIP Solutions\n\n## Involved HAIP Products\n\n[[Hyperspectral camera called BlackIndustry SWIR 1.7 manufactured by HAIP Solutions]][95]\n\n### [BlackIndustry SWIR 1.7][96]\n\n900 - 1730 nm wavelength range\n\n[ Read More ][97]\n[[Hyperspectral imaging software called BlackStudio by HAIP Solutions]][98]\n\n### [BlackStudio][99]\n\nHyperspectral imaging software\n\n[ Read More ][100]\n\n## Project Partners\n\n[ [Leibniz Universit\u00e4t und HAIP Solutions] ][101]\n[ [IKK und HAIP Solutions] ][102]\n\n## Funded by\n\n[ [BMWi und HAIP Solutions] ][103] Funding number: DS200575\n\n## Start with HSI Today!\n\n[ Contact Us ][104]\n\n## Other Research Projects\n\n### DeteKTiL\n\nDetection of plastic particles in food production\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][105]\n[Research project Emsig by HAIP Solutions]\n\n### EMSig\n\nDevelopment of a hyperspectral measurement platform for pest symptom detection\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][106]\n[HAIP Solutions Joint research project SpectralAIge]\n\n### SpectralAlge\n\nAI-supported spectroscopic plastic ageing determination during mechanical recycling\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][107]\n\n## Keep up with\n## the latest News.\n\n## Receive early access to new arrivals, sales, exclusive content, events and much more!\n\n## *By signing up, you will receive HAIP Solutions offers, promotions and other commercial messages.\n## You are also agreeing to HAIP Solutions's Privacy Policy. You may unsubscribe at any time.\n\n#### HAIP Solutions GmbH\n* [ +49 511 37352860 ][108]\n* [ info@haip-solutions.com ][109]\n* [ Escherstr. 23, 30159 Hannover ][110]\n\n#### Quicklinks\n* [ Products ][111]\n* [ Applications ][112]\n* [ Library ][113]\n* [ Support ][114]\n* [ Company ][115]\n* [ News ][116]\n\n#### Follow us\n* [ LinkedIn ][117]\n* [ Instagram ][118]\n* [ YouTube ][119]\n* [ Facebook ][120]\n\n[Privacy Policy][121]\n\n[Imprint][122]\n\n[Cookie Settings][123]\n\n## Get in touch with us!\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://www.haip-solutions.com\n[3]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/\n[4]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#cameras\n[5]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#cameras\n[6]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#rgb\n[7]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#vnir\n[8]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#nir\n[9]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#swir\n[10]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#illumination\n[11]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#illumination\n[12]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackbright-area/\n[13]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackbright-bar/\n[14]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackbright-fast-medium-wave-ir/\n[15]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#software\n[16]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#software\n[17]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/hyperspectral-imaging-software/\n[18]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/on-camera-classifier/\n[19]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/#accessories\n[20]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#accessories\n[21]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackindustry-station/\n[22]: https:/