AM][66]\n* [JOBS][67]\n* [SALES][68]\n* [RESEARCH PROJECTS][69]\n* [PRODUCTS][70]\n* [CAMERAS][71]\n* [ILLUMINATION][72]\n* [SOFTWARE][73]\n* [ACCESSORIES][74]\n* [APPLICATIONS][75]\n* [VEGETATION][76]\n* [RECYCLING][77]\n* [FOOD INDUSTRY][78]\n* [GEOLOGY][79]\n* [ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING][80]\n* [LIBRARY][81]\n* [KNOWLEDGE][82]\n* [APPLICATION NOTES][83]\n* [WHITE PAPERS][84]\n* [RESEARCH PUBLICATIONS][85]\n* [PRESS][86]\n* [SUPPORT][87]\n* [NEWS][88]\n* [COMPANY][89]\n* [TEAM][90]\n* [JOBS][91]\n* [SALES][92]\n* [RESEARCH PROJECTS][93]\n[ Contact ][94]\n\n# Research Projects\n\nHyperspectral Imaging\n\n## PWGram\n\n## Experimentelle Forschung zur Entwicklung eines Multisensor-Messsystems mit Marktreife zur\n## ber\u00fchrungslosen Bestimmung des Wasserversorgungszustands mittels Nahbereichsphotogrammetrie\n\n## Experimental research on the development of a multi-sensor measuring system with market maturity\n## for the non-contact determination of water supply status using short-range photogrammetry\n\nThe aim of the joint project is to further develop the PLANTSENS multi-sensor measuring system for\ndetermining the water supply status of plants into a marketable pre-series model. The measuring\nsystem will be tested indoors, outdoors and in combination with various carrier systems (rail,\ndrone, vehicle, watering trolley, stationary) on various crops in order to create documentation for\nuse and application. Furthermore, the design of an optimized housing with a fastening system that is\ncompatible with the various carrier systems is being developed. The innovation lies in the further\ntechnical development of the multi-sensor measuring system in order to record the water supply\nstatus of plants without the need for soil measurements.\n\n## Key Facts\n* **Project duration**: 08/2024 \u2013 07/2027\n* **Funding measure**: Program to promote innovation of the Federal Ministry of Food and Agriculture\nGerman Innovation Partnership Agriculture (DIP)\n* **Project partners**: Berliner Hochschule f\u00fcr Technik, rabo R. Bormann und Sohn, HAIP Solutions\nGmbH\n\n## Involved HAIP Products\n\n[[Hyperspectral camera called BlackIndustry SWIR 1.7 manufactured by HAIP Solutions]][95]\n\n### [BlackIndustry SWIR 1.7][96]\n\n900 - 1730 nm wavelength range\n\n[ Read More ][97]\n[[Hyperspectral imaging software called BlackStudio by HAIP Solutions]][98]\n\n### [BlackStudio][99]\n\nHyperspectral imaging software\n\n[ Read More ][100]\n\n## Project Partners\n\n[ [Berliner Hochschule f\u00fcr Technik und HAIP Solutions] ][101]\n[ [rabo R. Borgmann & Sohn und HAIP Solutions] ][102]\n[ [DIP Agrar und HAIP Solutions] ][103]\n\n## Funded by\n\n[ [BMEL und HAIP Solutions] ][104] Funding number: 281DP31C23\n\n## Start with HSI Today!\n\n[ Contact Us ][105]\n\n## Other Research Projects\n\n### DHYNAmite\n\nIntegrated plant protection through drone-based hyperspectral technology\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][106]\n[HAIP Solutions Research Project Mikroplastikanalyse IKK]\n\n### Mikroplastikanalyse (IKK)\n\nZIM feasibility study: Use of hyperspectral imaging for microplastic analysis\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][107]\n[HAIP Solutions Joint research project SpectralAIge]\n\n### SpectralAlge\n\nAI-supported spectroscopic plastic ageing determination during mechanical recycling\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][108]\n\n## Keep up with\n## the latest News.\n\n## Receive early access to new arrivals, sales, exclusive content, events and much more!\n\n## *By signing up, you will receive HAIP Solutions offers, promotions and other commercial messages.\n## You are also agreeing to HAIP Solutions's Privacy Policy. You may unsubscribe at any time.\n\n#### HAIP Solutions GmbH\n* [ +49 511 37352860 ][109]\n* [ info@haip-solutions.com ][110]\n* [ Escherstr. 23, 30159 Hannover ][111]\n\n#### Quicklinks\n* [ Products ][112]\n* [ Applications ][113]\n* [ Library ][114]\n* [ Support ][115]\n* [ Company ][116]\n* [ News ][117]\n\n#### Follow us\n* [ LinkedIn ][118]\n* [ Instagram ][119]\n* [ YouTube ][120]\n* 