            "url": "https://www.haip-solutions.com/company/research-projects/spectralaige/",
            "text": "[Zum Inhalt wechseln][1]\n[ [Logo_V2_HAIP-07_weiss] ][2]\n* [ PRODUCTS ][3] Schlie\u00dfe PRODUCTS \u00d6ffne PRODUCTS\n\n## [Cameras][4]\n\n[ [Camera_Overview_Header] ][5]\n* [ RGB ][6]\n* [ VNIR (500 - 1000 nm) ][7]\n* [ NIR (700 - 1050 nm) ][8]\n* [ SWIR (900 - 1730 nm) ][9]\n\n## [Illumination][10]\n\n[ [HAIP Solutions Illumination Overview] ][11]\n* [ BlackBright VNIR LED Area ][12]\n* [ BlackBright VNIR LED Bar ][13]\n* [ BlackBright FMWIR Bar ][14]\n\n## [Software][15]\n\n[ [Software_Overview_Header] ][16]\n* [ BlackStudio ][17]\n* [ BlackIndustry On-Camera Classifier ][18]\n\n## [Accessories][19]\n\n[ [BlackIndustry_Station_Vorne_Hinten_thumbnail_header] ][20]\n* [ BlackIndustry Station ][21]\n* [ APPLICATIONS ][22] Schlie\u00dfe APPLICATIONS \u00d6ffne APPLICATIONS\n* [ VEGETATION ][23]\n* [ RECYCLING ][24]\n* [ FOOD INDUSTRY ][25]\n* [ GEOLOGY ][26]\n* [ ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING ][27]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Vegetation] ][28]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Recycling] ][29]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Food Industry] ][30]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Geology] ][31]\n[ [Hyperspectral Imaging Application Environmental Monitoring] ][32]\n* [ LIBRARY ][33] Schlie\u00dfe LIBRARY \u00d6ffne LIBRARY\n* [ KNOWLEDGE BASE ][34]\n* [ APPLICATION NOTES ][35]\n* [ WHITE PAPERS ][36]\n* [ RESEARCH PUBLICATIONS ][37]\n* [ PRESS ][38]\n* [ NEWS ][39]\n* [ SUPPORT ][40]\n* [ COMPANY ][41] Schlie\u00dfe COMPANY \u00d6ffne COMPANY\n* [ TEAM ][42]\n* [ JOBS ][43]\n* [ SALES ][44]\n* [ RESEARCH PROJECTS ][45]\n* [PRODUCTS][46]\n* [CAMERAS][47]\n* [ILLUMINATION][48]\n* [SOFTWARE][49]\n* [ACCESSORIES][50]\n* [APPLICATIONS][51]\n* [VEGETATION][52]\n* [RECYCLING][53]\n* [FOOD INDUSTRY][54]\n* [GEOLOGY][55]\n* [ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING][56]\n* [LIBRARY][57]\n* [KNOWLEDGE][58]\n* [APPLICATION NOTES][59]\n* [WHITE PAPERS][60]\n* [RESEARCH PUBLICATIONS][61]\n* [PRESS][62]\n* [SUPPORT][63]\n* [NEWS][64]\n* [COMPANY][65]\n* [TEAM][66]\n* [JOBS][67]\n* [SALES][68]\n* [RESEARCH PROJECTS][69]\n* [PRODUCTS][70]\n* [CAMERAS][71]\n* [ILLUMINATION][72]\n* [SOFTWARE][73]\n* [ACCESSORIES][74]\n* [APPLICATIONS][75]\n* [VEGETATION][76]\n* [RECYCLING][77]\n* [FOOD INDUSTRY][78]\n* [GEOLOGY][79]\n* [ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING][80]\n* [LIBRARY][81]\n* [KNOWLEDGE][82]\n* [APPLICATION NOTES][83]\n* [WHITE PAPERS][84]\n* [RESEARCH PUBLICATIONS][85]\n* [PRESS][86]\n* [SUPPORT][87]\n* [NEWS][88]\n* [COMPANY][89]\n* [TEAM][90]\n* [JOBS][91]\n* [SALES][92]\n* [RESEARCH PROJECTS][93]\n[ Contact ][94]\n\n# Research Projects\n\nHyperspectral Imaging\n\n## SpectralAIge\n\n## KI gest\u00fctzte, spektroskopische Ermittlung der Alterung von Kunststoffen beim mechanischen\n## Recycling\n\n## AI-supported, spectroscopic determination of the ageing of plastics during mechanical recycling\n\nThe increasing use of plastics requires a sustainable circular economy, i.e. the cyclical reuse of\nplastics after the end-of-life of products.\n\nThe associated challenges in waste management require innovative solutions. The SpectralAIge joint\nproject aims to develop the world\u2019s first spectroscopic measurement systems that can assess the\nprocess-related material ageing of plastics quickly and precisely. With the support of artificial\nintelligence (AI), the best possible decisions are to be made for the processing and use of\nsecondary plastics in order to recognize and sort plastic material that has aged to varying degrees\nand to feed it into the optimal recycling path.\n\nThe knowledge gained from the project should make it possible to identify degraded materials in the\nclosed PET deposit bottle cycle and in plastic sorting systems. This offers the option of making the\nbest possible decisions for the processing and use of secondary plastics. Sorting out excessively\ndegraded materials at an early stage ensures a higher quality of recyclate. This is essential, for\nexample in the production of food packaging such as returnable bottles.\n\n[HAIP Solutions Joint research project SpectralAIge]\n\n**Challenges due to material ageing**\n\nPlastics are repeatedly exposed to high temperatures and mechanical stresses during the recycling\nprocess, usually in the extrusion and injection molding process. This can lead to ageing or\ndegradation of the materials. If the concentration of heavily aged material in the manufacturing\nprocess is too high, the quality of the product could deteriorate. This can lead to the product no\nlonger being allowed to be placed on the market due to quality defects. Although additives can\ncompensate for these ageing processes to a certain extent, the only option for heavily aged material\nis downcycling or chemical recycling. However, there is currently a lack of industrial processes for\nquickly and reliably analyzing and evaluating the ageing of plastic waste.\n\n**Research project pursues two possible approaches**\nIn the first project approach, hyperspectral camera systems (HSI), which are already established in\nplastics sorting, will be expanded to include LED-based light sources for fluorescence excitation.\nIn addition to the classic absorption spectra, excited fluorescence spectra can also be recorded.\nThe analysis of this spectral data using AI enables the precise determination of the material ageing\nof plastic waste.\n\nThe second approach focuses on the development of AI-supported, inexpensive inverted spectrometers.\nTo this end, relevant wavelengths are extracted from broadband measurement results from HSI\nmeasurements and an inverse spectrometer is built using this data. This should allow conclusions to\nbe drawn about the process-related ageing of plastic materials. In contrast to a spectrometer, which\ncovers a complete wavelength range, an inverse spectrometer only covers specific individual\nwavelength bands. This allows production costs to be reduced and a wide range of industrial\napplications to be achieved.\n\n**Great economic potential**\n\u201cThe knowledge gained from the research project can be used to promote a wide range of economic\napplications and enable SMEs to move towards a circular economy through the optimal use of secondary\nplastics,\u201d says Frank St\u00fcpmann, Managing Director of Silicann Systems GmbH.\n\n\u201cWe hope that the packaging sector, among others, will benefit greatly from the developments in the\nproject. This generates the largest proportion of post-consumer (PC) plastic waste and there are\nshort product life cycles and consequently frequent processing,\u201d adds Dr. Linda Mittelberg, Head of\nQuality and Life Cycle at SKZ. \u201cThe results can be used in PET deposit bottle cycles and plastic\nsorting plants in particular.\u201d\n\n## Key Facts\n* **Project duration**: 10/2024 \u2013 09/2027\n* **Funding measure**: KMU innovativ \u2013 Production research in the program \u201cFuture of Value Creation\u201d\nby the Federal Ministry of Education and Research (BMBF)\n* **Project partners**: Silicann Systems GmbH, HAIP Solutions GmbH, SKZ \u2013 KFE GmbH,\nFraunhofer-Institut f\u00fcr Fabrikbetrieb und -automatisierung IFF\n\n[ Learn more ][95]\n\n## Involved HAIP Products\n\n[[Hyperspectral camera called BlackIndustry SWIR 1.7 manufactured by HAIP Solutions]][96]\n\n### [BlackIndustry SWIR 1.7 Max][97]\n\n900 - 1730 nm wavelength range\n5 \u00b5m slit option\n\n[ Read More ][98]\n[[Hyperspectral imaging software called BlackStudio by HAIP Solutions]][99]\n\n### [BlackStudio][100]\n\nHyperspectral imaging software\n\n[ Read More ][101]\n\n## Project Partners\n\n[ [Silicann systems GmbH und HAIP Solutions] ][102]\n[ [SKZ und HAIP Solutions] ][103]\n[ [Fraunhofer und HAIP Solutions] ][104]\n\n## Funded by\n\n[ [BMBF und HAIP Solutions] ][105] Funding number: 13N17200\n\n## Start with HSI Today!\n\n[ Contact Us ][106]\n\n## Other Research Projects\n\n[Research project Emsig by HAIP Solutions]\n\n### EMSig\n\nDevelopment of a hyperspectral measurement platform for pest symptom detection\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][107]\n[HAIP Solutions Research Project Mikroplastikanalyse IKK]\n\n### Mikroplastikanalyse (IKK)\n\nZIM feasibility study: Use of hyperspectral imaging for microplastic analysis\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][108]\n[HAIP Solutions Joint research project PWGram]\n\n### PWGram\n\nExperimental research on the development of a multi-sensor measuring system with market maturity for\nthe non-contact determination of water supply status using short-range photogrammetry\n\n[ VIEW MORE ][109]\n\n## Keep up with\n## the latest News.\n\n## Receive early access to new arrivals, sales, exclusive content, events and much more!\n\n## *By signing up, you will receive HAIP Solutions offers, promotions and other commercial messages.\n## You are also agreeing to HAIP Solutions's Privacy Policy. You may unsubscribe at any time.\n\n#### HAIP Solutions GmbH\n* [ +49 511 37352860 ][110]\n* [ info@haip-solutions.com ][111]\n* [ Escherstr. 23, 30159 Hannover ][112]\n\n#### Quicklinks\n* [ Products ][113]\n* [ Applications ][114]\n* [ Library ][115]\n* [ Support ][116]\n* [ Company ][117]\n* [ News ][118]\n\n#### Follow us\n* [ LinkedIn ][119]\n* [ Instagram ][120]\n* [ YouTube ][121]\n* [ Facebook ][122]\n\n[Privacy Policy][123]\n\n[Imprint][124]\n\n[Cookie Settings][125]\n\n## Get in touch with us!\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://www.haip-solutions.com\n[3]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/\n[4]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#cameras\n[5]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#cameras\n[6]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#rgb\n[7]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#vnir\n[8]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#nir\n[9]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#swir\n[10]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#illumination\n[11]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#illumination\n[12]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackbright-area/\n[13]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackbright-bar/\n[14]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackbright-fast-medium-wave-ir/\n[15]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#software\n[16]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#software\n[17]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/hyperspectral-imaging-software/\n[18]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/on-camera-classifier/\n[19]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/#accessories\n[20]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/products/#accessories\n[21]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/blackindustry-station/\n[22]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/\n[23]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/vegetation/\n[24]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/recycling/\n[25]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/food-industry/\n[26]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/geology/\n[27]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/environmental-monitoring/\n[28]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/vegetation/\n[29]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/recycling/\n[30]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/food-industry/\n[31]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/geology/\n[32]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-imaging-applications/environmental-monitoring/\n[33]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/library-applications/\n[34]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/library/knowledge-base/\n[35]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/library-applications/application-notes/\n[36]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/library-applications/white-papers/\n[37]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/library-applications/research-publications/\n[38]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/library/press/\n[39]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/news/\n[40]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/support/\n[41]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/company/\n[42]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/company/team/\n[43]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/company/jobs/\n[44]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/company/sales-and-distribution-partners/\n[45]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/company/research-projects/\n[46]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hyperspectral-cameras/\n[47]: https://www.haip-solutions.com/hy"
