        "crawl_text": "Hypergram Inc. Accredited as a small and medium enterprise in Korea Korean venture business certification Certificate of small and medium enterprise verification Hyperspectral imaging Machine vision AI Cutting-edge technology Expert team from KAIST Focus on automation and precision T306, KAIST Truth Hall, 193, Munji-ro, Yuseong-gu, Daejeon, South Korea South Korea Foundation of Hypergram Inc. as a KAIST faculty startup in May 2023. Secured seed funding and venture business certification in 2023. Revolutionizing automated machinery manufacturing with hyperspectral imaging technology. Emerging leader in hyperspectral imaging for automated machinery inspection. Technological advancements in imaging and AI Increasing demand for automation in manufacturing top of page\n][1]\n* [Company][2]\n* [Greetings][3]\n* [About Us][4]\n* [CI][5]\n* [History][6]\n* [Technology][7]\n* [About HSI][8]\n* [Spectral range][9]\n* [Hypergram HSI][10]\n* [Applications][11]\n* [Semiconductor][12]\n* [Display][13]\n* [Electronics][14]\n* [Battery][15]\n* [Cosmetics][16]\n* [Pharmaceutics][17]\n* [Recycling][18]\n* [Food Quality][19]\n* [Agriculture][20]\n* [Careers][21]\n* [About our team][22]\n* [Join our team][23]\n* [News][24]\n* [Contact][25]\n[company_head.jpg]\n\n## COMPANY\n\n## Introducing Company\n\n[ci_logo.png]\n\n## Beyond Human Visibility\n\n## in Automation Machinery Manufacturing\n\nAbout Hypergram Inc.\n\nHypergram Inc. aims to revolutionize the automated machinery manufacturing industry with\ncutting-edge hyperspectral imaging technology capable of detecting defects invisible to the human\neye and conventional machine vision cameras. Founded in 2023 by Dr. Min H. Kim [[link][26]] as a\nKAIST faculty startup in Korea, Hypergram is dedicated to building autonomous inspection systems\nthat surpass human visual capabilities, particularly in the field of automated machinery\nmanufacturing.\n\nOur team comprises leading experts in computational imaging, physics, photography, machine learning,\nartificial intelligence, and computer science, including professors and Ph.D. graduates from KAIST.\nLeveraging this diverse expertise, Hypergram is pioneering the future of machine vision inspection\ntechnology \u2014 faster, more reliable, more precise, and more efficient \u2014 by overcoming the inherent\nlimitations of human vision and conventional camera systems.\n\nWith over 15 years of accumulated experience, knowledge, and passion in advanced imaging\ntechnologies, Hypergram is committed to leading technological advancements in the machine vision\nindustry. Our vision is to capture the highest-precision hyperspectral images at the fastest\npossible speeds without compromising between speed and accuracy. Step by step, we are bringing\ncutting-edge hyperspectral imaging solutions to life.\n\nHypergram provides state-of-the-art hyperspectral cameras and machine vision AI software solutions\ntailored for the automated machinery manufacturing sector.\n\nThank you.\n\nMin H. Kim\n\n[ceo_500_580.jpg]\n\n###### CEO\n\n### Dr. Min H. Kim\n\n## Hyperspectral Camera & AI Software Solution\n\n## HYPERGRAM\n\nHypergram Inc. provides a combined solution that consists of industry-level hyperspectral video\ncamera hardware and advanced spectral image analysis software. The name of our company is derived\nfrom combining these two words: hyper- from hyperspectral camera and -gram from machine vision AI\nprogram. Our unified solution can speed up the existing hyperspectral imaging solution and make it\nwork more accurately in detecting and classifying target objects through the automation machinery\nmanufacturing pipeline. Our machine vision solution will improve non-destructive and automated\ninspection in the manufacturing, food, recycling, and biomedical industries. Our team is dedicated\nto revolutionizing the way businesses conduct quality control and inspection processes. With\ncutting-edge technology and a passion for innovation, we aim to set new standards in the machine\nvision industry.\n\n## CI Concept\n\n[ci_symbol.png]\n\nOur company\u2019s logo symbolizes the energy of light refracted through a prism, depicting the\ntransition from short to long wavelengths. The fusion of two prisms, spiraling together, represents\nthe integration of innovative technologies: hyperspectral imaging and AI software solution in the\nautomation machinery manufactoring while also forming the initial \"H\" of Hypergram. This logo\nembodies our vision of \"Beyond Human Visibility,\" presenting new possibilities that go beyond the\nlimits of human sight in industrial machine vision applications.\n\n## History\n\n##### 2026\n\n###### 05\n\nPre-Series A Funding Secured\n\n##### 2025\n\n###### 09\n\nTIPS Startup Commercialization Program, selected\n\n###### 04\n\nHypergram Research Institute is accredited\n\n##### 2024\n\n###### 12\n\nSeed Extension Funding Secured\n\n###### 11\n\nDeepTech TIPS R&D funding, selected\n\n###### 09\n\nKorean venture business certification\n\n###### 08\n\nSeed Funding Secured\n\n###### 05\n\nCertificate of small and medium enterprise verification\n\n##### 2023\n\n###### 05\n\nFoundation of Hypergram Inc.\nas a KAIST faculty startup company\n\nT306, KAIST Truth Hall\n193, Munji-ro, Yuseong-gu, Daejeon\nSouth Korea\n\n[+82.42.867.3990][27]\n\n[info@hypergraminc.com][28]\n* [[LinkedIn]][29]\n\n\u00a9[2023 - 2025][30] by Hypergram Inc.\n\nbottom of page\n\n[1]: https://www.hypergraminc.com\n[2]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/company\n[3]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/company\n[4]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/company\n[5]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/company\n[6]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/company\n[7]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/technology\n[8]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/technology\n[9]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/technology\n[10]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/technology\n[11]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/applications\n[12]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/applications\n[13]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/applications\n[14]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/applications\n[15]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/applications\n[16]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/applications\n[17]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/applications\n[18]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/applications\n[19]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/applications\n[20]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/applications\n[21]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/careers\n[22]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/careers\n[23]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/careers\n[24]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/news\n[25]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/contact\n[26]: https://vclab.kaist.ac.kr/minhkim/\n[27]: tel:+82.42.867.3990\n[28]: mailto:info@hypergraminc.com\n[29]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/hypergram-inc\n[30]: tel:2023 - 2025 top of page\n][1]\n* [\n\nCompany\n\n][2]\n* [Greetings][3]\n* [About Us][4]\n* [CI][5]\n* [History][6]\n* [\n\nTechnology\n\n][7]\n* [About HSI][8]\n* [Spectral range][9]\n* [Hypergram HSI][10]\n* [\n\nApplications\n\n][11]\n* [Semiconductor][12]\n* [Display][13]\n* [Electronics][14]\n* [Battery][15]\n* [Cosmetics][16]\n* [Pharmaceutics][17]\n* [Recycling][18]\n* [Food Quality][19]\n* [Agriculture][20]\n* [\n\nCareers\n\n][21]\n* [About our team][22]\n* [Join our team][23]\n* [\n\nNews\n\n][24]\n* [\n\nContact\n\n][25]\n* More\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\n[company_head.jpg]\n\n## COMPANY\n\n## Introducing Company\n\n[ci_logo.png]\n\n## Beyond Human Visibility\n\n## in Automation Machinery Manufacturing\n\n[ceo_500_580.jpg]\n\n###### CEO\n\n### Dr. Min H. Kim\n\nAbout Hypergram Inc.\n\nHypergram Inc. aims to revolutionize the automated machinery manufacturing industry with\ncutting-edge hyperspectral imaging technology capable of detecting defects invisible to the human\neye and conventional machine vision cameras. Founded in 2023 by Dr. Min H. Kim [[link][26]] as a\nKAIST faculty startup in Korea, Hypergram is dedicated to building autonomous inspection systems\nthat surpass human visual capabilities, particularly in the field of automated machinery\nmanufacturing.\n\nOur team comprises leading experts in computational imaging, physics, photography, machine learning,\nartificial intelligence, and computer science, including professors and Ph.D. graduates from KAIST.\nLeveraging this diverse expertise, Hypergram is pioneering the future of machine vision inspection\ntechnology \u2014 faster, more reliable, more precise, and more efficient \u2014 by overcoming the inherent\nlimitations of human vision and conventional camera systems.\n\nWith over 15 years of accumulated experience, knowledge, and passion in advanced imaging\ntechnologies, Hypergram is committed to leading technological advancements in the machine vision\nindustry. Our vision is to capture the highest-precision hyperspectral images at the fastest\npossible speeds without compromising between speed and accuracy. Step by step, we are bringing\ncutting-edge hyperspectral imaging solutions to life.\n\nHypergram provides state-of-the-art hyperspectral cameras and machine vision AI software solutions\ntailored for the automated machinery manufacturing sector.\n\nThank you.\n\nMin H. Kim\n\n## Hyperspectral Camera & AI Software Solution\n\n## HYPERGRAM\n\nHypergram Inc. provides a combined solution that consists of industry-level hyperspectral video\ncamera hardware and advanced spectral image analysis software. The name of our company is derived\nfrom combining these two words: hyper- from hyperspectral camera and -gram from machine vision AI\nprogram. Our unified solution can speed up the existing hyperspectral imaging solution and make it\nwork more accurately in detecting and classifying target objects through the automation machinery\nmanufacturing pipeline. Our machine vision solution will improve non-destructive and automated\ninspection in the manufacturing, food, recycling, and biomedical industries. Our team is dedicated\nto revolutionizing the way businesses conduct quality control and inspection processes. With\ncutting-edge technology and a passion for innovation, we aim to set new standards in the machine\nvision industry.\n\n## CI Concept\n\n[ci_symbol.png]\n\nOur company\u2019s logo symbolizes the energy of light refracted through a prism, depicting the\ntransition from short to long wavelengths. The fusion of two prisms, spiraling together, represents\nthe integration of innovative technologies: hyperspectral imaging and AI software solution in the\nautomation machinery manufactoring while also forming the initial \"H\" of Hypergram. This logo\nembodies our vision of \"Beyond Human Visibility,\" presenting new possibilities that go beyond the\nlimits of human sight in industrial machine vision applications.\n\n## History\n\n##### 2026\n\n###### 05\n\nPre-Series A Funding Secured\n\n##### 2025\n\n###### 09\n\nTIPS Startup Commercialization Program, selected\n\n###### 04\n\nHypergram Research Institute is accredited\n\n##### 2024\n\n###### 12\n\nSeed Extension Funding Secured\n\n###### 11\n\nDeepTech TIPS R&D funding, selected\n\n###### 09\n\nKorean venture business certification\n\n###### 08\n\nSeed Funding Secured\n\n##### 2023\n\n###### 05\n\nCertificate of small and medium enterprise verification\n\n###### 05\n\nFoundation of Hypergram Inc.\nas a KAIST faculty startup company\n\nT306, KAIST Truth Hall\n193, Munji-ro, Yuseong-gu, Daejeon\nSouth Korea\n\n+82.42.867.3990\n\n[info@hypergraminc.com][27]\n* [[LinkedIn]][28]\n\n\u00a92023 - 2025 by Hypergram Inc.\n\nbottom of page\n\n[1]: https://www.hypergraminc.com\n[2]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/company\n[3]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/company\n[4]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/company\n[5]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/company\n[6]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/company\n[7]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/technology\n[8]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/technology\n[9]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/technology\n[10]: https://www.hypergraminc.com/technology\n[11]: https://www.hypergrami