            "url": "https://runlaminar.com",
            "text": "Laminar | Spectral Sensors for Faster and Smarter Factories\n\nLaminar has been named 2026 World Economic Forum (WEF) Technology Pioneer \u2192\n\nTry our free CIP Savings Finder today. Skip the consultant wait. \u2192\n\nCompany\n\nAbout\nCareers\nCompany News\n\nSolutions\n\nClean-in-Place\nProduct Changeover\nBatch &amp; Line Optimization\nReal-time Quality Analysis\n\nIndustries\n\nFood &amp; Beverage\nFlavor &amp; Fragrance\nBrewing\nHealth &amp; Beauty\nConsumer Packaged Goods\n\nTechnology\n\nKey Specs\nHow it Works\n\nResources\n\nCIP Analysis Tool\nCase Studies\nResource Center\nBlog Book a Demo\n\nSave Time, Water, and Chemicals\n\nDitch fixed timers. Unlock hidden capacity. Join the global brands switching to dynamic clean-in-place and product changeover.\nsee how it works\n\nThe CIP Standard for Top 10 Global F&amp;B &amp; CPG Brands\nThe #1 scaled CIP solution globally, installing on a new line every week. Trusted by Coca-Cola, Danone, AB InBev, Unilever, and more.\n\nClosed-loop automation driven by sub-second inline chemistry \u2014 not set points.\n\nTry Our Free CIP Savings Finder\n\nTry the #1 CIP Savings Finder helping Top 10 F&amp;B brands capture $10,000+ in savings with zero commitment.\nFIND CIP SAVINGS FAST\n\nReady to see how much production time you can save?\n\nBefore Laminar\n\nOverwashing &amp; Underwashing\n\nHigh Chemical &amp; Opex Waste\n\nTimer-Based Recipes\n\nAfter Laminar\n\nExact Clean\n\nResource Savings\n\nDynamic-Based Recipes\n\nsee How Much Your Line Can Save\n\nThink you&#x27;re operating to the gold standard? Our ML models can still unlock more production time.\n\nView all industries\n\n15%+ Faster CIP\nAccelerate every step and every cycle of your CIP. Your standards \u2014 just faster, more efficient, and without underwashes. Our CIP models use 20% less water, chemicals, and energy, enabling lines to run more sustainably.\n\n20% Faster Changeovers\nEvery static changeover means flushing good products down the drain and losing precious time instead of filling bottles and cans. Our models precisely switch between SKUs and cleaning to save time and fillable product in every changeover cycle.\n\n20% Water Savings\nFor many manufacturers, water is mission critical to your operations. We use real-time conditions to monitor CIP, startups, and changeovers to inform sub-second control to start the next step in your process and reduce water use across your recipes.\n\n20% Chemical Savings\nChemical costs are a significant driver of OPEX drain \u2014 even modest chemical savings add up. We optimize both raw chemical usage and the lifecycle of recirculated chemicals to address rising costs and environmental concerns. Reduce chemical use and prevent downtime by correcting real-time chemical overdose and tracking chemical degradation.\n\nWhy Laminar?\n\n1 / 3\n\nInstall In-Line\nPilot in weeks, not months. Our sensors are easy to install in any pipe and network with no major retrofit \u2014 adapting seamlessly to your plant. Designed for use cases like Clean-in-Place (CIP) applications and product changeovers, our always-on models track batch consistency, raw materials, and process efficiency to ensure uninterrupted production.\n\nSee The Results\nOur sensors detect each liquid in your pipes and capture its unique spectral fingerprint. We tailor ML models to your production line, driving sub-second PLC decisions for closed-loop automation. The result? Fully optimized CIP and changeover cycles that reclaim uptime, reduce product loss, and cut waste.\n\nScale Across Factories\nSee fast, measurable, and scalable results with every install through faster CIP, shorter changeovers, and reduced downtime. Our commercialized technology delivers unprecedented insights and undeniable results, transforming innovation projects into enterprise standards ready for global rollout.\n\nWhere Clean-in-Place is going autonomous\n\nFood &amp; Beverage\n\nHealth &amp; Beauty\n\nConsumer-Packaged Goods (CPG)\n\nBreweries\n\nData Centers\n\nPharmaceuticals\n\nROI in under a year with over 15% time, water, chemical and energy savings.\nLearn how Laminar transformed Unilever\u2019s CIP to run a better, more sustainable version of their factory.\n\nRead the case study\nView all case studies\n\nLaminar News &amp; Insights\n\nFebruary 5, 2026\n\nClean in Place (CIP): The Complete Guide\n\nRead More\n\nFebruary 26, 2026\n\nOn the Line Ep. 1: Peak Sauce &amp; CIP Bottlenecks\n\nRead More\n\nDecember 11, 2025\n\nCoca-Cola System Promotes Sustainability Activities through Co-creation with Startups\n\nRead More\n\nThere&#x27;s no technology out there like Laminar.\nAs a company that&#x27;s always pushing for innovation, Monin sees this as the kind of AI-driven solution that gives manufacturers a real edge. The fact that Laminar delivers on both sustainability and profitability makes it an easy decision to pilot and scale.\nAngel Pagan | VP of Manufacturing | Monin\n\nWe&#x27;ve been making quality food products for over a century, and one thing that&#x27;s kept us ahead is a willingness to invest in technology that actually moves the needle. Laminar is a unique application of technology, it lets us optimize our cleaning processes in ways we couldn&#x27;t before. We&#x27;re piloting ML models and sensors now and already planning to scale, because the technology checks both boxes that matter most to us: sustainability and profitability.\nPaul Liedtke | Sr. Director of Manufacturing Technology | The Marzetti Company\n\nWinland Foods is committed to exceeding consumer expectations with a high-quality food experience from the field to the table. Innovation is a critical pillar of our mission to provide superior value, and we&#x27;ve partnered with Laminar to enhance production flexibility with insights previously invisible to the naked eye. Leveraging their machine learning technology, we expect to enhance our production agility, reduce waste, and gain greater capacity so we can continue to deliver more world-class quality and value to our customers.\nDas Menon | Winland Foods, Sr. Director | Continuous Improvement\n\nOur partnership [with Laminar] has allowed for an 18% reduction in downtime during cleaning, which increases productivity and lowers costs in the supply chain. We have also saved 40% of a cleaning cycle&#x27;s water consumption by using the technology.\nSupply Chain Director | Unilever\n\nLaminar has industrialized exceptional technology that delivers results not found anywhere else in the market. The ability to generate real-time spectral fingerprints for each fluid and determine the liquid signature enhances our efforts to develop the best products and meet market demands. Their team is a true partner in our shared goal to identify productivity opportunities and use cases that are distinctive to their technology. We&#x27;re excited to leverage Laminar in creative ways that support our innovation goals, which give us our advantage in the marketplace.\nProcess Engineering Director | Market-Leading Snack Food Company\n\nAt its core, INX is a chemistry company\u2014where precision, performance, and science converge. Laminar\u2019s mastery of chemical intelligence, paired with its ability to transform real\u2011time chemical data into actionable insight, immediately set them apart. Their technology represents a new frontier in protecting the formulation integrity and product excellence that define who we are. As we push the boundaries of Industry 4.0 and reimagine what\u2019s possible in modern manufacturing, Laminar stands out as a truly differentiated solution. We haven\u2019t seen anything else in the market that delivers this level of chemical insight and control. We\u2019re energized by where Laminar\u2019s technology enables us to go\u2014today and as we shape the future of intelligent, data\u2011driven chemistry.\nChris Rodgers | Vice President of Operational Excellence | INX\n\nSee Your Factory in a New Light\n\nQuick Links Home CIP Savings Finder About Blog News Deployment FAQ Careers\n\nLocation\n444 Somerville Ave.\nSomerville, MA 02143\nUnited States\n\nContact hello@runlaminar.com (617) 741-7384\n\nBook a Consultation\n\nFirst Name *\n[Placeholder text - Hubspot will create the error message]\nLast Name *\n[Placeholder text - Hubspot will create the error message]\n\nEmail *\n[Placeholder text - Hubspot will create the error message]\nCompany *\n[Placeholder text - Hubspot will create the error message]\n\nQuestions or Comments *\n[Placeholder text - Hubspot will create the error message]\n\nBy clicking submit below, you agree to the processing of your personal information.\n\nSubmit\n\nThanks for submitting the form.\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Laminar All rights reserved.\nPrivacy policy\n| Terms &amp; Conditions\n\nFormerly"
