          },
          {
            "url": "https://runlaminar.com/solutions/real-time-quality-analysis",
            "text": "Laminar has been named 2026 World Economic Forum (WEF) Technology Pioneer \u2192\nTry our free CIP Savings Finder today. Skip the consultant wait. \u2192\n][1]\nCompany\nAbout\n][2][\nCareers\n][3][\nCompany News\n][4]\nSolutions\nClean-in-Place\n][5][\nProduct Changeover\n][6][\nBatch & Line Optimization\n][7][\nReal-time Quality Analysis\n][8]\nIndustries\nFood & Beverage\n][9][\nFlavor & Fragrance\n][10][\nBrewing\n][11][\nHealth & Beauty\n][12][\nConsumer Packaged Goods\n][13]\nTechnology\nKey Specs\n][14][\nHow it Works\n][15]\nResources\nCIP Analysis Tool\n][16][\nCase Studies\n][17][\nResource Center\n][18][\nBlog\n][19]\n[**Book a Demo**][20]\n\n# Inline Quality Monitoring\n\n[Food and beverage products moving down a factory conveyor with Laminar\u2019s spectral sensor data\noverlay, ensuring every unit meets quality standards.]\n\n## Stop Reactive Quality Control\n\n### **Mistakes That Keep Happening**\n\nMissing ingredients, stuck valves, incorrect dosing, insufficient operator training, shift-to-shift\nvariability\u2026 These don\u2019t all happen at the same time, but they do keep happening, and it's\nfrustrating to whack-a-mole from a quality standpoint.\n\n### **Sampling Heavy Quality Control**\n\nSampling is essential for ensuring quality, but it often slows down production\u2014particularly when\nunderlying root causes remain unresolved. Excessive process and input variability lead to an\noverreliance on inspection rather than prevention\u2014a cycle that operations find tough to break.\n\n### **Variability in Process and Inputs**\n\nEven manufacturers with a limited number of \u201chero\u201d SKUs face significant challenges from process and\ninput variability. For operations managing an expanding SKU portfolio, new suppliers, and evolving\nformulations, the complexity\u2014and the struggle to maintain consistency\u2014erodes margins and\nproductivity.\n[Laminar Gateway device mounted in a factory setting, linking inline spectral sensors on production\nlines to Laminar\u2019s AI platform for real-time process optimization.][Laminar spectral sensor in\nproduction pipeline]\n\n## Closed-Loop Inline Quality Inspection and Control\n\n1/3\n\n## **Prevent Mistakes Proactively**\n\nOur AI-powered sensors capture the spectral fingerprint of every product in your production line ,\nensuring constant QA coverage at every stage of the manufacturing process . Capture and maintain\ndetailed batch records, including full documentation of defect detections and product loss during\nchangeovers, for cost accounting and regulatory compliance and audits.\n\n# **Less Sampling, More Efficient InLine Quality Control**\n\nLaminar gives your QA team real-time visibility into what\u2019s flowing through your pipes. With\nprecise, human-readable insights, they can sample less, trust the data more, and focus on driving\nprocess innovation \u2014 all while ensuring every batch meets the highest quality inspection standards.\n\n# **Drive Down Variability, Get More Out of Production**\n\nLaminar\u2019s inline quality control sensors track every parameter \u2014 from color and viscosity to\nchemical traces \u2014 and our inline inspection model acts in sub-seconds to correct deviations and\nquality issues. Give your quality team the superpower to run smarter, faster, and more reliable\nprograms.\n\n## Transform your Quality Assurance Program. Get Proactive, not Reactive.\n\nEvery Laminar sensor gives you a clear view inside every pipe, continuously analysing liquid\nchemistry in real time.\n\nPaired with Agentic AI and edge ML models, they provide sub-second decisions that maintain quality\nacross every stage of production.\n[Laminar's patented sensor.]\n\n## Catch Defects Before They Become Recalls\n\nReal-time monitoring ensures every product meets specifications, protecting the brand's reputation,\nsafeguarding consumers and customer satisfaction, and keeping quality products in the market and out\nof the waste stream.\n\nImprove product consistency, traceability, and compliance with detailed batch records.\nCaustic Soda\nOil\nMayo\nWater\n[Laminar inline spectral sensor attached to a stainless steel production pipe, built with sanitary\nfittings for food and beverage environments and enabling AI-driven process optimization.]\n\n## Maintaining Quality at Scale\n\nA leading fine chemicals manufacturer struggled with inconsistent product quality grading due to\nreliance on grab sampling. Learn how they saved $80,000 per year on a single line with our in-line\nquality monitoring models.\nRead the case study\n][21][\nView all case studies\n][22]\n\n## Consistent Quality Starts Here\n\nReady to stop relying on manual spot checks? Talk to our team to learn how Laminar can transform QA\ninto a continuous inline safeguard.\nStart the Conversation\n][23]\n[AI-driven SKU changeover automation]\n\nThere's no technology out there like Laminar.\n\nAs a company that's always pushing for innovation, Monin sees this as the kind of AI-driven solution\nthat gives manufacturers a real edge. The fact that Laminar delivers on both sustainability and\nprofitability makes it an easy decision to pilot and scale.\n\nAngel Pagan | VP of Manufacturing | Monin\n\nWe've been making quality food products for over a century, and one thing that's kept us ahead is a\nwillingness to invest in technology that actually moves the needle. Laminar is a unique application\nof technology, it lets us optimize our cleaning processes in ways we couldn't before. We're piloting\nML models and sensors now and already planning to scale, because the technology checks both boxes\nthat matter most to us: sustainability and profitability.\n\nPaul Liedtke | Sr. Director of Manufacturing Technology | The Marzetti Company\n\nWinland Foods is committed to exceeding consumer expectations with a high-quality food experience\nfrom the field to the table. Innovation is a critical pillar of our mission to provide superior\nvalue, and we've partnered with Laminar to enhance production flexibility with insights previously\ninvisible to the naked eye.\n\nLeveraging their machine learning technology, we expect to enhance our production agility, reduce\nwaste, and gain greater capacity so we can continue to deliver more world-class quality and value to\nour customers.\n\nDas Menon | Winland Foods, Sr. Director | Continuous Improvement\n\nOur partnership [with Laminar] has allowed for an 18% reduction in downtime during cleaning, which\nincreases productivity and lowers costs in the supply chain. We have also saved 40% of a cleaning\ncycle's water consumption by using the technology.\n\nSupply Chain Director | Unilever\n\nLaminar has industrialized exceptional technology that delivers results not found anywhere else in\nthe market. The ability to generate real-time spectral fingerprints for each fluid and determine the\nliquid signature enhances our efforts to develop the best products and meet market demands.\n\nTheir team is a true partner in our shared goal to identify productivity opportunities and use cases\nthat are distinctive to their technology. We're excited to leverage Laminar in creative ways that\nsupport our innovation goals, which give us our advantage in the marketplace.\n\nProcess Engineering Director | Market-Leading Snack Food Company\n\nAt its core, INX is a chemistry company\u2014where precision, performance, and science converge.\nLaminar\u2019s mastery of chemical intelligence, paired with its ability to transform real\u2011time chemical\ndata into actionable insight, immediately set them apart. Their technology represents a new frontier\nin protecting the formulation integrity and product excellence that define who we are. As we push\nthe boundaries of Industry 4.0 and reimagine what\u2019s possible in modern manufacturing, Laminar stands\nout as a truly differentiated solution. We haven\u2019t seen anything else in the market that delivers\nthis level of chemical insight and control. We\u2019re energized by where Laminar\u2019s technology enables us\nto go\u2014today and as we shape the future of intelligent, data\u2011driven chemistry.\n\nChris Rodgers | Vice President of Operational Excellence | INX\nSee Your Factory in a New Light\nQuick Links\n[Home][24][CIP Savings\nFinder][25][About][26][Blog][27][News][28][Deployment][29][FAQ][30][Careers][31]\nLocation\n444 Somerville Ave.\nSomerville, MA 02143\nUnited States\nContact\n[hello@runlaminar.com][32][(617) 741-7384][33]\n**Book a Consultation**\nFirst Name*\n[Placeholder text - Hubspot will create the error message]\nLast Name*\n[Placeholder text - Hubspot will create the error message]\nEmail*\n[Placeholder text - Hubspot will create the error message]\nCompany*\n[Placeholder text - Hubspot will create the error message]\nQuestions or Comments*\n[Placeholder text - Hubspot will create the error message]\n\nBy clicking submit below, you agree to the processing of your personal information.\n\nSubmit\nThanks for submitting the form.\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Laminar\nAll rights reserved.\n[Privacy policy][34]\n[Terms & Conditions][35]\n**Formerly**\n\n[1]: https://runlaminar.com/press/laminar-named-a-2026-world-economic-forum-technology-pioneer\n[2]: /about\n[3]: /careers\n[4]: /in-the-news\n[5]: /solutions/clean-in-place\n[6]: /solutions/product-changeover-optimization\n[7]: /solutions/batch-optimization\n[8]: /solutions/real-time-quality-analysis\n[9]: /industries/food-beverage\n[10]: /industries/flavor-fragrance\n[11]: /industries/breweries\n[12]: /industries/health-beauty\n[13]: /industries/consumer-packaged-goods-cpg\n[14]: /key-specs\n[15]: /how-it-works\n[16]: https://na2.hubs.ly/H02wNqt0\n[17]: /case-studies\n[18]: /resource-center\n[19]: /blog\n[20]: /contact\n[21]: https://runlaminar.com/case-studies/fine-chemicals-company-saves-80-000-per-year\n[22]: /case-studies\n[23]: /contact\n[24]: /\n[25]: https://app.runlaminar.com/\n[26]: /about\n[27]: /blog\n[28]: /in-the-news\n[29]: /tech/deployment\n[30]: /frequently-asked-questions\n[31]: /careers\n[32]: mailto:hello@runlaminar.com\n[33]: tel:6177417384\n[34]: /legal/privacy-policy\n[35]: /legal/terms-conditions"
