        "crawl_text": "Wyvern Inc. Suite 466, 11007 Jasper Avenue NW, Edmonton, AB T5K 0K6, Canada Canada Instructions\nTo make this component work follow these steps:\n1. Remove the delete-this-class class from the navbar14_component div. This will change the\npositioning of the navbar to fixed.\n2. Add the navbar-on-page class to the page-wrapper class. This will ensure that the navbar is\ncentered on the page.\n3. Add the max-width-full class to the main-wrapper class. This will ensure all sections inside of\nthe main wrapper are full-wdith.\n[Products][1]\n[Hyperspectral imagery][2][\nArchive\n][3][\nOpen Data\n][4]\n[Technology][5]\n[Industries][6]\n[Agriculture][7][Peace and security][8][Forestry and ESG][9][Energy][10][Mining][11]\nCompany\n[About us][12][Join us][13]\nResources\n[Resource library][14][Knowledge centre][15][\nKnowledge Centre\n][16][\nProduct Guide\n][17][\nOpen Data\n][18][Product guide][19][Open data][20]\n[Partners][21]\nContact Us\n][22][\nOrder imagery\n][23]\nOur Mission\n\n# Better access.\n# A better earth.\n\nHigh-resolution hyperspectral imagery gives organizations the clarity they need to make smarter,\nmore sustainable decisions\u2014and the power to approach pressing environmental problems in completely\nnew ways.\n\nWe\u2019re creating a better Earth by making exceptional hyperspectral data widely accessible and easy to\nuse.\n\nOur story\n\n## A sustainable future for all\n\nOur founders believed deeply in the potential of hyperspectral imagery to drive positive change.\n\nSince launching our first satellites in 2023, we\u2019re proving what\u2019s possible: better wildfire\nmitigation, higher crop yields with fewer pesticides, faster wellsite reclamation, and other\nadvances that serve the planet.\n\nWith more than ten times the precision and detail of other remote sensors, our high-resolution\nhyperspectral sensors reveal critical hidden information about the planet, monitor environmental\nchanges in near-real time, and transform the way organizations respond.\n\nThat\u2019s why we\u2019re focused on making the highest-quality data available to as many people as possible.\nWhen we increase access to this powerful tool, we empower widespread stewardship of our home.\n\nOur impact\n\n## Expanding our view\n\nWyvern\u2019s hyperspectral imaging identifies materials and detect subtle environmental shifts with\nincredible accuracy.\n\nOur growing, 5-satellite constellation delivers a steady stream of insight-rich data\n\n4.9M\n\nWe\u2019ve imaged 4.9M square kilometres of Earth, and counting, through global tasking\n\n100+\n\nThe number of free hyperspectral images in our Open Data program increases each month\n\nOur team\n\n## meet the team behind the mission\n\nChristopher Robson\nCEO & Co-Founder\nLinkedin\n][24]\nKristen Cote\nCTO & Co-Founder\nLinkedin\n][25]\nKurtis Broda\nCOO & Co-Founder\nLinkedin\n][26]\nCallie Lissinna\nVP Strategic Relations & Co-Founder\nLinkedin\n][27]\nStephanie Wright\nCFO\nLinkedin\n][28]\nRoss Blakeney\nVP Engineering Programs\nLinkedin\n][29]\nWendy Segelken\nDirector of Software\nLinkedin\n][30]\nEllie Jones\nDirector of Analytics and Geospatial AI\nLinkedin\n][31]\nVince Sauer\nDirector of Research Projects\nLinkedin\n][32]\nChad Bryant\nPrincipal Scientist\nLinkedin\n][33]\n\n## Our advisors\n\nLisa Costa\nformer SpaceForce\nStephane Germain\nGHGSat\nChris Lewicki\nXPRIZE\nDoug Sinclair\nSinclair Interplanetary\n\n## Help us build a better earth from space\n\nWe\u2019re looking for passionate, dedicated individuals to join us on our mission.\n\n[explore careers][34]\nProducts\n[Hyperspectral imagery][35][Archive][36][Open Data][37]\nIndustries\n[Agriculture][38][Peace and security][39][Forestry and ESG][40][Energy][41][Mining][42]\nCompany\n[Our technology][43][Our partners][44][About us][45][Join us][46][Contact us][47]\nSubscribe\nJoin our newsletter to stay up to date on all things Wyvern.\nFirst name\nLast name\nEmail\nBy subscribing you agree to with our [Privacy Policy][48] and provide consent to receive updates\nfrom our company.\nThank you! You are now subscribed!\nOops! Something went wrong while submitting the form.\n\u00a9 2026 Wyvern Inc. All rights reserved.\n[Privacy Policy][49]\n][50][\n][51][\n][52][\n][53][\n][54]\nWe use cookies to enhance your experience.\nLearn more\n][55][Accept][56]\n][57]\n\n[1]: /product\n[2]: /product\n[3]: https://archive.wyvern.space/\n[4]: https://opendata.wyvern.space/#/?.language=en\n[5]: /technology\n[6]: /industries\n[7]: /industries/agriculture\n[8]: /industries/peace-and-security\n[9]: /industries/forestry\n[10]: /industries/energy\n[11]: /industries/mining\n[12]: /company/about-us\n[13]: /company/join-us\n[14]: /blog\n[15]: https://knowledge.wyvern.space/\n[16]: https://knowledge.wyvern.space/\n[17]: https://guide.wyvern.space/\n[18]: https://opendata.wyvern.space/#/?.language=en\n[19]: https://guide.wyvern.space/\n[20]: https://opendata.wyvern.space/#/?.language=en\n[21]: /partners\n[22]: /contact\n[23]: mailto:orders@wyvern.space?body=Hello,%0D%0A%0D%0AI'm interested in tasking imagery with the f\nollowing parameters:%0D%0A%0D%0AArea of interest (location and size):%0D%0ATime of interest (date ra\nnge):%0D%0ASingle capture or multiple collections:%0D%0ABudget:\n[24]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/christopherrjrobson/?originalSubdomain=ca#\n[25]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/kristencote/?originalSubdomain=ca\n[26]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/kurtisbroda/?originalSubdomain=ca\n[27]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/callielissinna/?originalSubdomain=ca\n[28]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/stephanie-wright-54b11837/?originalSubdomain=ca\n[29]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/rossb-01/\n[30]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/wendy-segelken/\n[31]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/elliejonesyyc/\n[32]: https://www.linkedin.com/in/vincent-sauer/\n[33]: https://ca.linkedin.com/in/chadbryantphd\n[34]: /company/join-us\n[35]: /product\n[36]: https://archive.wyvern.space/\n[37]: https://opendata.wyvern.space/#/?.language=en\n[38]: /industries/agriculture\n[39]: /industries/peace-and-security\n[40]: /industries/forestry\n[41]: /industries/energy\n[42]: /industries/mining\n[43]: /technology\n[44]: /partners\n[45]: /company/about-us\n[46]: /company/join-us\n[47]: /contact\n[48]: #\n[49]: /privacy-policy\n[50]: #\n[51]: #\n[52]: #\n[53]: https://www.linkedin.com/company/wyvern-space/?originalSubdomain=ca\n[54]: #\n[55]: /privacy-policy\n[56]: #\n[57]: # Instructions\nTo make this component work follow these steps:\n1. Remove the delete-this-class class from the navbar14_component div. This will change the\npositioning of the navbar to fixed.\n2. Add the navbar-on-page class to the page-wrapper class. This will ensure that the navbar is\ncentered on the page.\n3. Add the max-width-full class to the main-wrapper class. This will ensure all sections inside of\nthe main wrapper are full-wdith.\n[Products][1]\n[Hyperspectral imagery][2][\nArchive\n][3][\nOpen Data\n][4]\n[Technology][5]\n[Industries][6]\n[Agriculture][7][Peace and security][8][Forestry and ESG][9][Energy][10][Mining][11]\nCompany\n[About us][12][Join us][13]\nResources\n[Resource library][14][Knowledge centre][15][\nKnowledge Centre\n][16][\nProduct Guide\n][17][\nOpen Data\n][18][Product guide][19][Open data][20]\n[Partners][21]\nContact Us\n][22][\nOrder imagery\n][23]\n\n## Join us on our mission\n\nOur team is re-inventing the satellite to deliver the highest-resolution hyperspectral data in the\nsolar system. We seek creative, dedicated individuals to help us build a sustainable future for\nhumanity.\n\n## Our constellation is growing fast\n\nWe\u2019re a rapidly growing hyperspectral imaging company in Western Canada, powered by humans who are\npassionate about space and committed to excellence. If you\u2019re excited about increasing the\ncapability of space-based cameras, creating products that will revolutionize model-based\npredictions, or just collaborating to build amazing things\u2014we want you on our team.\n\n## Mission perks\n\nJoining our crew has its benefits:\n\nUnlimited vacation (seriously)\n\nAn employee stock option plan\n\nStellar health and dental benefits (including fertility coverage, 100% prescription coverage, and\nlots more)\n\nAll the best aspects of startup culture, like whole-team support when and where you need it\n\nAmple opportunities for professional development\n\nA strong sense of ownership over your work\n\nOn-sites with team-building activities\n\nFlexible working hours\n\nHybrid work opportunities\n\nWorking on space stuff!\n\nOur values\n\n## How we work\n\nOur team is caring and supportive. We learn, grow, and progress together\u2014personally and\nprofessionally.\n\n### We think outside the cube[sat]\n\nWe drive innovation by thinking beyond what\u2019s expected or even currently possible\n\n### We\u2019re committed to a better future\n\nOur technology serves a broader goal: a sustainable future for everyone\n\n### We communicate openly and honestly\n\nWe succeed when we\u2019re true to ourselves and our collective mission\n\n### We are reflective, receptive & responsive\n\nWe thoughtfully examine our actions, welcome feedback, and embrace change\n\n### We encourage originality\n\nWe foster a workplace where everyone\u2019s comfortable bringing their whole self\n\n### We take initiative and persevere\n\nWe have a bias to action and approach problems with tenacity and resilience\n\nDiversity, equity, and inclusion\n\n## everyone is\n## welcome here\n\nStarting with our gender-diverse leadership team, Wyvern is built on belonging, mutual respect, and\nkindness.\n\nWe share the responsibility of ensuring everyone feels heard and valued\u2014and we believe that\nwelcoming employees of all backgrounds, experiences, and lifestyles only expands what\u2019s possible.\n\nWhen we empower our true selves and embrace our uniqueness, we rise together.\n\nIf you require accommodations to participate in our hiring process, please reach out at\n[hiring@wyvern.space][24].\n\nOpen positions\n\n## Find your dream job\n\nSpace Operations Intern\nDepartment\nApply now\n][25]\n\n**We\u2019re looking for a DevOps specialist to work with the Software team. ** You'll be building and\nmaintaining the infrastructure that processes and analyzes those images and gets them to our\ncustomers in a timely manner. This is an excellent opportunity for someone eager to start their\ncareer in the space industry and offers room to grow as Wyvern expands its constellation and its\ndata offerings.\n\nRemote \u2022 Edmonton, AB\nContract Type\nApply now\n][26]\n\nDon\u2019t see the role you\u2019re looking for? We may be posting it soon. Feel free to [submit your\nresume][27] and cover letter in the meantime. Our hiring team will reach out if an appropriate\nposition becomes available.\n\nOpen positions\n\n## Find your dream job\n\nWe don\u2019t have any open roles at the moment, but we\u2019re always growing. Please check back soon for new\nopportunities.\n\nProducts\n[Hyperspectral imagery][28][Archive][29][Open Data][30]\nIndustries\n[Agriculture][31][Peace and security][32][Forestry and ESG][33][Energy][34][Mining][35]\nCompany\n[Our technology][36][Our partners][37][About us][38][Join us][39][Contact us][40]\nSubscribe\nJoin our newsletter to stay up to date on all things Wyvern.\nFirst name\nLast name\nEmail\nBy subscribing you agree to with our [Privacy Policy][41] and provide consent to receive updates\nfrom our company.\nThank you! You are now subscribed!\nOops! Something went wrong while submitting the form.\n\u00a9 2026 Wyvern Inc. All rights reserved.\n[Privacy Policy][42]\n][43][\n][44][\n][45][\n][46][\n][47]\nWe use cookies to enhance your experience.\nLearn more\n][48][Accept][49]\n][50]\n\n[1]: /product\n[2]: /product\n[3]: https://archive.wyvern.space/\n[4]: https://opendata.wyvern.space/#/?.language=en\n[5]: /technology\n[6]: /industries\n[7]: /industries/agriculture\n[8]: /industries/peace-and-security\n[9]: /industries/forestry\n[10]: /industries/energy\n[11]: /industries/mining\n[12]: /company/about-us\n[13]: /company/join-us\n[14]: /blog\n[15]: https://knowledge.wyvern.space/\n[16]: https://knowledge.wyvern.space/\n[17]: https://guide.wyvern.space/\n[18]: https://opendata.wyvern.space/#/?.language=en\n[19]: https://guide.wyvern.space/\n[20]: https://opendata.wyvern.space/#/?.language=en\n[21]: /partners\n[22]: /contact\n[23]: mailto:orders@wyvern.space?body=Hello,%0D%0A%0D%0AI'm interested in tasking imagery with the f\nollowing parameters:%0D%0A%0D%0AArea of int"
