ith Arduino. Easy to wire up and code.\n6. [Avatar of Dev Bhat][Avatar of Dev Bhat]\nRated **5** out of 5\n\n**Dev Bhat ** *(verified owner)* \u2013 January 20, 2024\n\nExcellent sensitivity and range on this LM35 Temperature Sensors. Works better than I expected.\n7. [Avatar of Vivek Rao][Avatar of Vivek Rao]\nRated **5** out of 5\n\n**Vivek Rao ** *(verified owner)* \u2013 February 11, 2024\n\nPerfect LM35 Temperature Sensors for my automation project. Integrates seamlessly with my\nmicrocontroller.\n8. [Avatar of Milan Ghosh][Avatar of Milan Ghosh]\nRated **5** out of 5\n\n**Milan Ghosh ** *(verified owner)* \u2013 April 14, 2024\n\nThis LM35 Temperature Sensors is excellent for the price. My data logging project is working\nperfectly now.\n9. [Avatar of Meera Khanna][Avatar of Meera Khanna]\nRated **5** out of 5\n\n**Meera Khanna ** *(verified owner)* \u2013 June 14, 2024\n\nVery satisfied with this LM35 Temperature Sensors. Library support is good and it\u2019s easy to\ninterface.\n10. [Avatar of Himanshu Patel][Avatar of Himanshu Patel]\nRated **5** out of 5\n\n**Himanshu Patel ** *(verified owner)* \u2013 June 25, 2024\n\nGreat quality LM35 Temperature Sensors. Calibrated it easily and the accuracy is impressive.\n11. [Avatar of Om Panchal][Avatar of Om Panchal]\nRated **5** out of 5\n\n**Om Panchal ** \u2013 December 13, 2024\n\nThis LM35 T"
