breadboard for easy and quick prototyping, allowing\nyou to build circuits without the need for soldering.\n* **Sensors and Modules**: A variety of sensors and modules may be included, such as temperature and\nhumidity sensors, ultrasonic distance sensors, motion sensors, and light sensors, enabling you to\nmeasure different environmental factors.\n* **Actuators**: The kit often contains actuators like servo motors, DC motors, and stepper motors,\nessential for projects involving motion control, robotics, and automation.\n* **Displays**: Various display options, including LCDs, OLEDs, and seven-segment displays, are\ntypically included, allowing you to create visual interfaces and display information from your\nArduino projects.\n* **Input Devices**: To facilitate user interaction and control, the kit comes with input devices\nsuch as keypads, buttons, potentiometers, and rotary encoders.\n* **Communication Modules**: Communication modules like Bluetooth, Wi-Fi, RFID, and IR modules may\nalso be featured, providing capabilities for wireless communication and connectivity.\n\n### **Specification:**\n* All-in-one kit, a great starter kit for learning coding.\n* Great for Starting with Arduino Programming\n* A variety of components are included in this pack to try out different projects.\n* The kit comes with quality components assured.\n* UNO Specs:\n* Model Type: UNO Rev R3\n* Microcontroller Chip: ATmega328\n* Input Voltage (Recommended): 7-12V.\n* Input Voltage (limit): 6-20V.\n* Operating Voltage: 5\n* Analog I/O Pins: 6\n* Digital I/O Pins: 14 (of which 6 provide PWM output)\n* PWM Digital I/O Pins: 6\n* DC Current per I/O Pin: DC Current per I/O Pin: 40 mA; DC Current for 3.3V Pin: 50 mA\n* Clock Speed: 16 MHz\n* EEPROM: 1 KB (ATmega328)\n* Flash Memory: 32 KB (ATmega328) of which 0.5 KB used by bootloader.\n* PWM Output Pins: 6\n* SRAM: 2 KB (ATmega328)\n* Power Supply Option: DC Jack or USB\n* On-Board LEDs: Yes\n* Operating Temperature (\u00b0C): -40 to +90\n* Dimensions in mm (LxWxH): 75 x 54 x 12\n* Weight (gm): 26\n\n### **Package Include:**\n* 1x 9V Battery Box.\n* 1 x UNO R3.\n* 1 x High-Quality Retail Box.\n* 1x USB cable.\n* 1 x 65 Jumper Wires.\n* 1 x 830 Point BREADBOARD.\n* 15 x LED (Red, Green, Yellow).\n* 30 x Resistance (220R, 10K, 1K).\n* 1 x Potentiometer.\n* 1x Active Buzzer.\n* 1 x Passive Buzzer.\n* 3 x 5mm LDR.\n* 5 x Button Switch with Cap.\n* 1 x IR Remote Control.\n* 1 x One Digital Tube.\n* 1x Four Digital Tube.\n* 1 x 8*8 Dot Matrix Tube.\n* 1 x 74HC595N.\n* 1 x LM35DZ.\n* 1 x 9v Battery Snap Connector DC Jack.\n* 1 x Infrared Receiving Head.\n* 2 x Vibration Switch\n* 1 x 4 pin RGB Module\n* 5 x IR sensor\n\n## Uno R3 Beginners Kit for Arduino Uno- SECONDRY KIT Overview\n\nThe Uno R3 Beginners Kit for Arduino Uno \u2013 SECONDRY KIT is a complete learning pack centred on the\nArduino Uno R3 microcontroller board. It\u2019s designed for hobbyists and beginners looking to expand\ntheir electronics and coding skills with a diverse set of components for hands-on projects.\n\n## Key Features of Uno R3 Beginners Kit for Arduino Uno- SECONDRY KIT\n* **Arduino Uno R3 Board:** Based on the ATmega328P (SMD) chip with CH340G USB-serial interface.\n* **Operating Voltage:** 5V logic level, ideal for most educational and prototype projects.\n* **Wide Input Range:** Recommended 7\u201312V DC input, supports 5\u201320V for varied power options.\n* **Rich I/O:** 14 digital pins (6 PWM outputs) and 6 analog inputs for sensors, actuators, LEDs.\n* **Quality Components:** Includes a variety of jumpers, passive parts and modules to explore\ncircuits.\n* **Fast Shipping from Zbotic:** Dispatch within 24 hours across India with tracking.\n\n## Applications and Use Cases\n* Interactive LED projects and light patterns.\n* Sensor experiments like temperature or light sensing.\n* Basic robotics control with motors and servos.\n* Prototyping home automation switches or alarms.\n* Learning serial communication and data logging.\n\n## How to Use Uno R3 Beginners Kit for Arduino Uno- SECONDRY KIT\n\nStart by connecting the Uno R3 board to your computer via USB, install the Arduino IDE, then load\nexample sketches to test built-in features. Assemble components on a breadboard using included\njumper wires, upload code through the CH340G interface, and power external modules within the\nrecommended voltage range.\n\n## Why Buy from Zbotic?\n* **Genuine Products:** All items sourced from authorized distributors\n* **Fast Shipping:** Orders ship within 24 hours with tracking (non backordered products)\n* **Free Shipping:** Free delivery on qualifying orders\n* **COD Available:** Cash on Delivery, UPI, cards, net banking\n* **Technical Support:** Expert help for setup and troubleshooting\n* **Easy Returns:** Hassle-free replacement for defective products\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n### Does this kit include the Arduino Uno R3 board?\n\nYes, the SECONDRY KIT comes with an official Arduino Uno R3 board featuring the ATmega328P (SMD) and\nCH340G USB interface.\n\n### Can I program the board using the Arduino IDE?\n\nAbsolutely. Simply connect the Uno R3 via USB to your PC or Mac, select the correct board and port\nin the Arduino IDE, and upload your sketches.\n\n### What components are provided for circuit experiments?\n\nThe kit supplies a curated selection of jumpers, breadboard-friendly modules and passive\ncomponents\u2014such as resistors and LEDs\u2014so you can build and test a variety of circuits right away.\n\n**Tags:** [Arduino][90] [Buy Online India][91] [Zbotic][92]\n**Related Articles:**\n[ [Arduino RFID Tutorial: RC522 Module for Access Control][Arduino RFID Tutorial: RC522 Module for\nAccess Control]\n\nArduino RFID Tutorial: RC522 Module for Access Control\n\nRFID (Radio Frequency Identification) technology powers everything from office access badges to\nlibrary book tracking and contactless payment...\n\nRead More \u2192\n][93][ [Arduino Watchdog Timer: Auto-Reset Frozen Programs][Arduino Watchdog Timer: Auto-Reset\nFrozen Programs]\n\nArduino Watchdog Timer: Auto-Reset Frozen Programs\n\nTable of Contents What Is a Watchdog Timer? How the ATMega328P Watchdog Works Basic Watchdog\nImplementation Timeout Values...\n\nRead More \u2192\n][94][ [Arduino ADC Tutorial: analogRead(), Resolution & Accuracy][Arduino ADC Tutorial:\nanalogRead(), Resolution & Accuracy]\n\nArduino ADC Tutorial: analogRead(), Resolution & Accuracy\n\nThe ability to read real-world analogue signals \u2014 voltages from sensors, potentiometers,\nthermistors, light-dependent resistors \u2014 is one...\n\nRead More \u2192\n][95]\n\n### Technical Specifications\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nBrand \u2502Arduino\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSKU \u2502AI0060\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nWeight \u25020.72 kg\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nAvailability\u2502In Stock\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n### Applications & Use Cases\n\nThe Uno R3 Beginners Kit for Arduino Uno- SECONDRY KIT is a versatile kits for arduinos used across\na wide range of applications including electronics projects, DIY builds, prototyping, and\neducational experiments.\n\n**Common use cases:**\n* Integrating into a custom electronics project\n* Learning and experimenting with circuits\n* Replacing or upgrading components in existing setups\n\nThis product is ideal for electronics enthusiasts, engineers, and students.\n\n**Technical Tip:** Always verify voltage and current requirements before connecting to your