            "text": "* [Technology Vendors][1]\n* [Recent Research][2]\n* [Newsletter][3]\n* [Media Support][4]\n* [Login][5]\n[[CB Insights]][6]\n* Who We Serve\n* Function\n* [Corporate Strategy][7]\n* [Corporate Venture Capital][8]\n* [Venture Capital][9]\n* [IT][10]\n* [Corporate Innovation][11]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### How VCs Use CB Insights\n\n[Go to the video gallery \u2192][12]\n* Industries\n* [Consumer & Retail][13]\n* [Tech][14]\n* [Insurance][15]\n* [Healthcare][16]\n* [Industrials][17]\n* [Financial Services][18]\n* [Professional Services][19]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Professional Services\n\n[Learn More\u2192][20]\n* [Success Stories][21]\n* How We Help\n* [Understand Tech Markets][22]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][23]\n* [Determine Tech Strategy][24]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors & Partners][25]\n* [Turbocharge Digital Transformation][26]\n* What We Offer\n* Platform\n* [Overview][27]\n* [Technology Search Engine][28]\n* [Market Analytics and Visualizations][29]\n* [Team Management and Collaboration][30]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Platform Overview\n\n[Learn More\u2192][31]\n* [Data][32]\n* [Research][33]\n* [Personal Briefing][34]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][35]\n* [Public Equity Data][36]\n* [Buyer Interview Transcripts][37]\n* [Analyst Briefings][38]\n* [API & Data Feeds][39]\n* Integrations\n* [Overview][40]\n* [Chrome and Edge][41]\n* [Salesforce][42]\n* [Affinity][43]\n* [Microsoft Excel][44]\n* [Google Sheets][45]\n* [Microsoft Teams][46]\n* [Slack][47]\n* [Google Slides][48]\n* [App Partners][49]\n* [Browser Extension][50]\n* [Pricing][51]\n* About Us\n* [Overview][52]\n* Our teams\n* [Business Development][53]\n* [Engineering][54]\n* [Operations][55]\n* [Product][56]\n* [See all \u2192][57]\n* [Open Jobs][58]\n\nLoading...\n\n[Artspan company logo]\n\n# Artspan\n\nUnclaimed\n[artspan.com][59]\n* [Overview & Products][60]\n* [People][61]\n* [Alternatives & Competitors][62]\n\n## Revenue\n\n$0000 View\n\n## About Artspan\n\nArtspan is a platform that operates within the online art sales industry, enabling artist website\ncreation. The company provides original art and prints for sale, along with services for artists to\ncreate and manage their own websites with e-commerce capabilities. Artspan serves artists who sell\ntheir work and individuals who purchase original pieces and prints. It is based in Lambertville, New\nJersey.\n\n## Headquarters Location\n\n26 Bridge Street\n\nLambertville, New Jersey, 08530,\n\nUnited States\n\n609-397-0888\n\nLoading...\n\nLoading...\n\n## Expert Collections containing Artspan\n\nExpert Collections are analyst-curated lists that highlight the companies you need to know in the\nmost important technology spaces.\n\nArtspan is included in **1 Expert Collection,** including **E-Commerce**.\n\n# E-Commerce\n\n11,526 items\n\nCompanies that sell goods online (B2C), or enable the selling of goods online via tech solutions\n(B2B).\n\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n## Latest Artspan News\n\n[SWAIA Launches Global Native American Art Marketplace With Help From The Clark Hulings Fund &\nArtspan][63]\n\nJun 29, 2020\n\nSWAIA Launches Global Native American Art Marketplace With Help From The Clark Hulings Fund &\nArtspan SANTA FE, N.M. Jun 29, 2020 4:29 PM EDT SANTA FE, N.M., June 29, 2020 /PRNewswire/ -- The\nSouthwestern Association for Indian Art (SWAIA) is pleased to announce additional details about\ntheir partnership with the Clark Hulings Fund , which will launch the 2020 Virtual Indian Market on\nAug. 1, 2020, while providing business training and support to Native artists. A further\ncollaboration with Artspan.com is producing e-commerce websites and a global marketplace where\nvisitors can easily find, experience and acquire the world's best Native American art. The Clark\nHulings Fund (CHF) has arranged for SWAIA to work with a third partner, Artspan, to provide\nwebsites to SWAIA artists throughout the U.S. and Canada. The CHF will deliver hands-on training to\nthe artists, not only to help create top-notch e-commerce sites but also to teach digital sales and\nmarketing strategies and how to employ them effectively. Artspan is currently working with SWAIA\nand the Clark Hulings Fund to create websites for SWAIA artists throughout the U.S. and Canada.\nThese individual artist websites will be integrated into a central Native American Art Marketplace\nopening August 1. Artspan was the first website company to focus on artists, artisans and\nphotographers. It will provide Native American artists with individual websites. The artwork on the\nsites will provide the inventory for an Art Marketplace which will stand in for the Santa Fe Indian\nMarket. The cancellation of this year's physical Santa Fe Indian Market, the most important juried\nNative art market to both artists and collectors, will now be accessible virtually year-round at the\nArtspan SWAIA Marketplace. Buyers will be able to purchase artworks directly from an artist's\nwebsite and through the Native American Art Marketplace\u2014 and artists will have a robust set of tools\nand platforms with which to run their businesses online. Virtual Indian Market will be live at\nswaia.org from August 1 through August 31\u2014offering engaging programming and fan favorites like the\nNative American Clothing Contest, and a re-imagined awards program. Individual artist websites will\nbe live for one year, with the option for artists to renew the e-commerce sites to market and sell\nwork. \"SWAIA's goals are both immediate and long-term,\" says Executive Director Kim Peone (Colville\nConfederated Tribes / Eastern Band of Cherokee Indians). \"Our first objective is to launch a\nsolution-based platform to meet the economic needs of our artists. Longer-term goals will position\nSWAIA as a technology leader and innovator, able to offer increased services and support to Native\nartists. \" For virtual market updates, events and a growing list of participating artists, please\nvisit: www.swaia.org. MEDIA CONTACT: Audrey Rubinstein | 505-490-5029 audrey@themettaagency.com\nAbout SWAIA: The Southwestern Association for Indian Arts (SWAIA) is a non-profit organization\nsupporting Native American arts and culture. It creates economic and cultural opportunities for\nNative American artists by producing and promoting the Santa Fe Indian Market, the biggest and most\nprestigious Indian art event in the world since 1922. www.swaia.org Related Images Related Links\n\nJun 29, 2020\n[SWAIA Launches Global Native American Art Marketplace With Help From the Clark Hulings Fund &\nArtspan][64]\nMay 8, 2017\n[Zephyr Real Estate Partners with ArtSpan to Showcase Local Artists in 2018 Calendar][65]\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n### Artspan Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n* Where is Artspan's headquarters?\n\nArtspan's headquarters is located at 26 Bridge Street, Lambertville.\n* Who are Artspan's competitors?\n\nCompetitors of Artspan include Rise Art and 7 more.\n\nLoading...\n\n## Compare Artspan to Competitors\n\n[Artsy Logo]\n[Artsy][66]\n\nArtsy is a marketplace for discovering and purchasing fine art, operating within the art industry.\nThe company offers a platform that facilitates the buying process of art for collectors and connects\nthem with artists and artworks. Artsy's services cater to the art collecting community. Artsy was\nformerly known as Exhibytes. It was founded in 2009 and is based in New York, New York.\n\n[Rise Art Logo]\n[Rise Art][67]\n\nRise Art operates as an online platform that offers a selection of original and limited-edition\nartworks from emerging and established artists, along with art advisory services. The platform\nserves individual collectors and businesses. It was founded in 2009 and is based in London, United\nKingdom.\n\n[Artfinder Logo]\n[Artfinder][68]\n\nArtfinder is an online marketplace that operates within the art industry. The company offers a\nplatform for purchasing artwork directly from independent artists, including paintings, sculptures,\nand photography. Artfinder also provides options for commissioning art and supports production\npractices. It was founded in 2010 and is based in Oxfordshire, England.\n\n[Ugallery Logo]\n[Ugallery][69]\n\nUGallery is an online art gallery that sells original paintings and fine art. The company offers a\nselection of artworks including oil, acrylic, watercolor, and mixed media pieces, as well as custom\nart commissions. UGallery serves art collectors, interior designers, and individuals looking to\npurchase original art. It was founded in 2006 and is based in San Francisco, California.\n\n[ARTMO][70]\n\nARTMO is a social art platform that operates within the online art marketplace and social media\nsectors. The company provides a platform for buying and selling physical, digital, and NFT artworks,\nas well as offering masterclasses and gift cards related to art. ARTMO serves artists, art\nenthusiasts, galleries, and art universities. It was founded in 2017 and is based in Hamburg,\nGermany.\n\n[ARTERNAL][71]\n\nARTERNAL is a company that provides management solutions for the art gallery sector. Its platform\nincludes customer relationship management (CRM), inventory management, email marketing, online\nviewing rooms, and invoicing and payment processing. It was founded in 2015 and is based in New\nYork, New York.\n\nLoading...\n\n[CB Insights]\n498 Seventh Avenue 12th floor\nNew York, NY 10018[info@cbinsights.com][72]\n[212 292 3148][73]\n\nFollow Us On Social\n\n[[Twitter]][74][[Linkedin]][75][[Facebook]][76]\n\n### [About][77]\n* [About Us][78]\n* [Upcoming Webinars][79]\n* [Contact Us][80]\n\n### [How We Help][81]\n* [Understand Tech Markets][82]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][83]\n* [Create Tech Strategy][84]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors][85]\n* [Digital Transformation][86]\n\n### [What We Offer][87]\n* [Platform][88]\n* [Data][89]\n* [Research Overview][90]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][91]\n* [Pricing][92]\n\n### [Popular Research][93]\n* [AI 100][94]\n* [Fintech 100][95]\n* [Digital Health 50][96]\n* [Tech Trends 2024][97]\n* [Generative AI Predictions][98]\n* [Unicorn Tracker][99]\n* [VC Glossary][100]\n* [Company List Applications][101]\n* [CB Insights Website Terms of Use][102]\n* [Privacy Policy][103]\n* [Do Not Sell My Info][104]\n* [Partnership][105]\n\nCopyright 2026 CB Information Services, Inc. All rights reserved.\n\nCBI websites generally use certain cookies to enable better interactions with our sites and\nservices. Use of these cookies, which may be stored on your device, permits us to improve and\ncustomize your experience. You can read more about your cookie choices at [our privacy policy][106].\nBy continuing to use this site you are consenting to these choices.\n\nI ACCEPT\nI DO NOT ACCEPT\n\n[1]: https://www.cbinsights.com/what-we-offer/technology-vendors/\n[2]: https://www.cbinsights.com/research/\n[3]: https://www.cbinsights.com/newsletter/\n[4]: https://www.cbinsights.com/media-support/\n[5]: https://www.cbinsights.com/login\n[6]: https://www.cbinsights.com\n[7]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-strategy/\n[8]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-venture-capital/\n[9]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/venture-capital/\n[10]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/head-of-it/\n[11]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-innovation/\n[12]: https://www.cbinsights.com/how-vcs-use-cb-insights/\n[13]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/consumer/\n[14]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/tech/\n[15]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/insurance/\n[16]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/healthcare/\n[17]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/industrials/\n[18]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/financial-services/\n[19]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/professional-services/\n[20]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/professional-services/\n[21]: https://www.cbinsights.com/resources/case-studies/\n[22]: https://www.cbinsights.com/how-we-help/understand-tech-markets/\n[23]: https://www.cbinsights.com/how-we-help/competitor-strategy/\n[24]: https://www.cbinsights.com/how-we-help/create-tech-strategy/\n[25]: https://www.c"
