            "url": "https://www.cbinsights.com/company/basix-india",
            "text": "* [Technology Vendors][1]\n* [Recent Research][2]\n* [Newsletter][3]\n* [Media Support][4]\n* [Login][5]\n[[CB Insights]][6]\n* Who We Serve\n* Function\n* [Corporate Strategy][7]\n* [Corporate Venture Capital][8]\n* [Venture Capital][9]\n* [IT][10]\n* [Corporate Innovation][11]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### How VCs Use CB Insights\n\n[Go to the video gallery \u2192][12]\n* Industries\n* [Consumer & Retail][13]\n* [Tech][14]\n* [Insurance][15]\n* [Healthcare][16]\n* [Industrials][17]\n* [Financial Services][18]\n* [Professional Services][19]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Professional Services\n\n[Learn More\u2192][20]\n* [Success Stories][21]\n* How We Help\n* [Understand Tech Markets][22]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][23]\n* [Determine Tech Strategy][24]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors & Partners][25]\n* [Turbocharge Digital Transformation][26]\n* What We Offer\n* Platform\n* [Overview][27]\n* [Technology Search Engine][28]\n* [Market Analytics and Visualizations][29]\n* [Team Management and Collaboration][30]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Platform Overview\n\n[Learn More\u2192][31]\n* [Data][32]\n* [Research][33]\n* [Personal Briefing][34]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][35]\n* [Public Equity Data][36]\n* [Buyer Interview Transcripts][37]\n* [Analyst Briefings][38]\n* [API & Data Feeds][39]\n* Integrations\n* [Overview][40]\n* [Chrome and Edge][41]\n* [Salesforce][42]\n* [Affinity][43]\n* [Microsoft Excel][44]\n* [Google Sheets][45]\n* [Microsoft Teams][46]\n* [Slack][47]\n* [Google Slides][48]\n* [App Partners][49]\n* [Browser Extension][50]\n* [Pricing][51]\n* About Us\n* [Overview][52]\n* Our teams\n* [Business Development][53]\n* [Engineering][54]\n* [Operations][55]\n* [Product][56]\n* [See all \u2192][57]\n* [Open Jobs][58]\n\nLoading...\n\n[Basix India company logo]\n\n# Basix India\n\nUnclaimed\n[basixindia.com][59]\n* [Overview & Products][60]\n* [Financials][61]\n* [People][62]\n* [Alternatives & Competitors][63]\n\n## Founded Year\n\n1996\n\n## Stage\n\nUnattributed VC | Alive\n\n## Total Raised\n\n$38.37M\n\n## Last Raised\n\n$2M | 14 yrs ago\n\n## About Basix India\n\nBasix India is a livelihood promotion institution that operates in the financial services sector.\nThe company offers services, including financial services, agricultural and business development\nservices, and institutional development services for rural poor households. Basix India serves the\nrural poor and urban slum dwellers, offering financial and technical support to improve living\nconditions. It was founded in 1996 and is based in Hyderabad, India.\n\n## Headquarters Location\n\nSurabhi Arcade, 3rd Floor, Troop Bazar Bank Street, Koti\n\nHyderabad, 500 001,\n\nIndia\n\n+ 91- 040 - 3917 2500\n\nLoading...\n\nLoading...\n\n## Latest Basix India News\n\n[Mastercard, LEAF and BASIX digitally empower over one million smallholder farmers in India][64]\n\nJan 13, 2023\n\nNew Delhi, 13 January 2023: Mastercard today announced that it has reached the milestone of\nbenefiting over one million smallholder farmers in India through Farm Pass, its scalable rural and\nagriculture digitization solution. Leveraging Farm Pass, Mastercard processed agricultural produce\nsales worth nearly INR 180 crores in 2022. Working with Lawrencedale Agro Processing India (LEAF)\nand BASIX Social Enterprise Group, the payments technology firm has now set a target of covering 10\nmillion farmers by 2025. Since 2020, Mastercard, LEAF, and BASIX have partnered to improve digital\naccess and financial inclusion for farmers in four Indian states: Maharashtra, Karnataka, Andhra\nPradesh, and Tamil Nadu. With its rich experience and expertise in digital and payments technology\nas well as agritech, in 2023, Mastercard will extend its Farm Pass solution to five more states\nincluding Himachal Pradesh, Assam, Odisha, Telangana, and West Bengal. Mastercard\u2019s Farm Pass is a\ndigital ecosystem platform for rural areas that also works offline in remote unconnected areas and\nencourages stakeholders in the agriculture sector to come together and serve the farmer community.\nThe platform enables the digitization of agricultural marketplaces and farmer data to create a\ncommercially sustainable ecosystem, enabling farmers to be part of the formal economy. Mastercard\nand its ecosystem partners are committed to empowering farmers by directly connecting them to\nbuyers, enabling them to achieve greater value for their products, providing access to agronomic\nknowledge and services, and supporting Farmer Producer Organizations (FPOs). Farm Pass is part of\nCommunity Pass, a shared, interoperable digital infrastructure for rural populations. It facilitates\naccess to critical services and reduces the cost to serve them for all stakeholders, including\ngovernments, banks, agricultural entities, and NGOs. Tara Nathan, Executive Vice President, of\nHumanitarian & Development, Mastercard, said, \u201cCommunity Pass, which includes Farm Pass, is designed\nto help smallholder farmers get paid more and faster. Mastercard is proud to have supported one\nmillion farmers in India last year. In line with the Government of India\u2019s vision to ensure\nfinancial inclusion and double farmers\u2019 income, Community Pass addresses the barriers smallholder\nfarmers face when trying to access reliable markets and financial services.\u201d Palat\nVijayaraghavan, Founder & CEO, LEAF, said, \u201cLeveraging our deep expertise in agritech, this\npartnership with Mastercard has led to the development of several digital products and solutions\nthat have transformed the lives of smallholder farmers. Through comprehensive training and capacity\nbuilding programs, we will continue to further empower farmers and make them more resilient.\u201d D\nSattaiah, CEO, of BASIX, said, \u201cWe are proud to collaborate with Mastercard in our endeavour to\nempower Indian farmers. BASIX\u2019s Farmers Market (BFM) uses Mastercard\u2019s technology to ensure complete\ntransparency in agriculture transactions and enable greater price realization for farmers.\u201d Last\nyear, Mastercard announced plans to expand its Farm Pass program to more markets in Asia Pacific in\n2023. The company is also in the process of launching a unique agricultural invoice discounting\nplatform, a rural financial inclusion card, as well as additional solutions to digitize the rural\necosystem.\n\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n### Basix India Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n* When was Basix India founded?\n\nBasix India was founded in 1996.\n* Where is Basix India's headquarters?\n\nBasix India's headquarters is located at Surabhi Arcade, 3rd Floor, Troop Bazar, Hyderabad.\n* What is Basix India's latest funding round?\n\nBasix India's latest funding round is Unattributed VC.\n* How much did Basix India raise?\n\nBasix India raised a total of $38.37M.\n* Who are the investors of Basix India?\n\nInvestors of Basix India include Acumen, Lok Capital, Z47, Hivos International, SIDBI Venture and\n3 more.\n* Who are Basix India's competitors?\n\nCompetitors of Basix India include Rang De and 6 more.\n\nLoading...\n\n## Compare Basix India to Competitors\n\n[Sambandh Financial Services Logo]\n[Sambandh Financial Services][65]\n\nSambandh Financial Services is a company focused on providing financial services within the\nmicrofinance sector. The company offers financial products and services to support small and\nmarginal entrepreneurs, with a focus on women and their livelihoods. Sambandh Financial Services\nprimarily caters to the microfinance industry, aiming to foster entrepreneurship for its clients. It\nwas founded in 2006 and is based in Rourkela, India.\n\n[SATYA MicroCapital Logo]\n[SATYA MicroCapital][66]\n\nSatya Microcapital is a non-banking financial company (NBFC) that provides microfinance services to\nlow-income entrepreneurs in rural and urban areas. The company offers loans such as limited\nliability loans, water and sanitation loans, and MSME business loans to individuals and small\nbusinesses. Satya Microcapital serves sectors needing financial inclusion and support for\nentrepreneurship, utilizing technology to improve customer experience and operational efficiency. It\nwas founded in 2017 and is based in New Delhi, India.\n\n[Jagaran Microfin Logo]\n[Jagaran Microfin][67]\n\nJagaran Microfin Private Limited is a microfinance entity that provides financial services to\neconomically challenged sections of society. The company offers various financial products for women\nand small businesses in rural areas. Jagaran Microfin serves sectors that require microfinance\nsupport for small business development and financial inclusion. It was founded in 2010 and is based\nin Kolkata, India.\n\n[Aavishkaar Capital][68]\n\nAavishkaar Capital provides venture capital financing and impact investment across sectors. It\noffers entrepreneurs financial support and resources, focusing on social and environmental outcomes.\nIt serves sectors aligning with its mission of promoting sustainable business solutions. Aavishkaar\nCapital was formerly known as Aavishkaar Venture Management Services. It was founded in 2001 and is\nbased in Mumbai, India.\n\n[Rang De][69]\n\nRang De operates a peer-to-peer lending platform championing microcredit access for rural India. The\ncompany enables individuals to invest in first-time borrowers, with a focus on farmers,\nentrepreneurs, and students from low-income households. It was founded in 2008 and is based in\nBangalore, India.\n\n[Svatantra][70]\n\nSvatantra is a microfinance institution that provides financial services to rural entrepreneurs. The\ncompany offers microfinance and MSME loans to support business expansion, primarily targeting rural\nwomen. Svatantra uses technology to provide digital financial solutions, including cashless\ndisbursements and a customer-facing app, to improve the delivery of its services. It was founded in\n2012 and is based in Mumbai, India.\n\nLoading...\n\n[CB Insights]\n498 Seventh Avenue 12th floor\nNew York, NY 10018[info@cbinsights.com][71]\n[212 292 3148][72]\n\nFollow Us On Social\n\n[[Twitter]][73][[Linkedin]][74][[Facebook]][75]\n\n### [About][76]\n* [About Us][77]\n* [Upcoming Webinars][78]\n* [Contact Us][79]\n\n### [How We Help][80]\n* [Understand Tech Markets][81]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][82]\n* [Create Tech Strategy][83]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors][84]\n* [Digital Transformation][85]\n\n### [What We Offer][86]\n* [Platform][87]\n* [Data][88]\n* [Research Overview][89]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][90]\n* [Pricing][91]\n\n### [Popular Research][92]\n* [AI 100][93]\n* [Fintech 100][94]\n* [Digital Health 50][95]\n* [Tech Trends 2024][96]\n* [Generative AI Predictions][97]\n* [Unicorn Tracker][98]\n* [VC Glossary][99]\n* [Company List Applications][100]\n* [CB Insights Website Terms of Use][101]\n* [Privacy Policy][102]\n* [Do Not Sell My Info][103]\n* [Partnership][104]\n\nCopyright 2026 CB Information Services, Inc. All rights reserved.\n\nCBI websites generally use certain cookies to enable better interactions with our sites and\nservices. Use of these cookies, which may be stored on your device, permits us to improve and\ncustomize your experience. You can read more about your cookie choices at [our privacy policy][105].\nBy continuing to use this site you are consenting to these choices.\n\nI ACCEPT\nI DO NOT ACCEPT\n\n[1]: https://www.cbinsights.com/what-we-offer/technology-vendors/\n[2]: https://www.cbinsights.com/research/\n[3]: https://www.cbinsights.com/newsletter/\n[4]: https://www.cbinsights.com/media-support/\n[5]: https://www.cbinsights.com/login\n[6]: https://www.cbinsights.com\n[7]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-strategy/\n[8]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-venture-capital/\n[9]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/venture-capital/\n[10]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/head-of-it/\n[11]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-innovation/\n[12]: https://www.cbinsights.com/how-vcs-use-cb-insights/\n[13]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/consumer/\n[14]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/tech/\n[15]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/insurance/\n[16]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/healthcare/\n[17]: https://www.cb"
