            "url": "https://www.cbinsights.com/company/activewords",
            "text": "* [Technology Vendors][1]\n* [Recent Research][2]\n* [Newsletter][3]\n* [Media Support][4]\n* [Login][5]\n[[CB Insights]][6]\n* Who We Serve\n* Function\n* [Corporate Strategy][7]\n* [Corporate Venture Capital][8]\n* [Venture Capital][9]\n* [IT][10]\n* [Corporate Innovation][11]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### How VCs Use CB Insights\n\n[Go to the video gallery \u2192][12]\n* Industries\n* [Consumer & Retail][13]\n* [Tech][14]\n* [Insurance][15]\n* [Healthcare][16]\n* [Industrials][17]\n* [Financial Services][18]\n* [Professional Services][19]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Professional Services\n\n[Learn More\u2192][20]\n* [Success Stories][21]\n* How We Help\n* [Understand Tech Markets][22]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][23]\n* [Determine Tech Strategy][24]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors & Partners][25]\n* [Turbocharge Digital Transformation][26]\n* What We Offer\n* Platform\n* [Overview][27]\n* [Technology Search Engine][28]\n* [Market Analytics and Visualizations][29]\n* [Team Management and Collaboration][30]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Platform Overview\n\n[Learn More\u2192][31]\n* [Data][32]\n* [Research][33]\n* [Personal Briefing][34]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][35]\n* [Public Equity Data][36]\n* [Buyer Interview Transcripts][37]\n* [Analyst Briefings][38]\n* [API & Data Feeds][39]\n* Integrations\n* [Overview][40]\n* [Chrome and Edge][41]\n* [Salesforce][42]\n* [Affinity][43]\n* [Microsoft Excel][44]\n* [Google Sheets][45]\n* [Microsoft Teams][46]\n* [Slack][47]\n* [Google Slides][48]\n* [App Partners][49]\n* [Browser Extension][50]\n* [Pricing][51]\n* About Us\n* [Overview][52]\n* Our teams\n* [Business Development][53]\n* [Engineering][54]\n* [Operations][55]\n* [Product][56]\n* [See all \u2192][57]\n* [Open Jobs][58]\n\nLoading...\n\n[ActiveWords company logo]\n\n# ActiveWords\n\nUnclaimed\n[activewords.com][59]\n* [Overview & Products][60]\n* [Alternatives & Competitors][61]\n\n## Founded Year\n\n1999\n\n## About ActiveWords\n\nActiveWords focuses on productivity software for the Windows operating system. Its main offering\nincludes software that allows users to trigger actions by typing specific words. It was founded in\n1999 and is based in Winter Park, Florida.\n\n## Headquarters Location\n\nWinter Park, Florida, 32790,\n\nUnited States\n\nLoading...\n\nLoading...\n\n## Latest ActiveWords News\n\n[ActiveWords 2 improves your efficiency and productivity (review)][62]\n\nAug 8, 2012\n\nThere are some extremely useful tools in the enterprise that helps our productivity. One such tool\nthat saves you time, keystrokes, and in the end money is ActiveWords and it has just recently been\nupdated to Version 2. | Topic: Mobility I last wrote about ActiveWords back in 2006 when I was using\nit with my UMPC and Tablet PCs. They recently rolled out Version 2 and I wanted to share a few of my\nexperiences. ActiveWords is not an application with a flashy UI and simplistic functionality, but\none that tech enthusiasts can embrace and customize to their heart's desires. ActiveWords is\ndesigned to increase your efficiency and improve your productivity. For just $50 for use on all of\nyour Windows computers it is definitely an application you should consider. You can check out\nseveral screenshots of ActiveWords in my image gallery , but understand that much of what goes on\nwith ActiveWords is not easily captured in a screenshot. You can view the videos embedded below for\nmore on using ActiveWords. As you can see on the ActiveWords 2.0 new features page, the following\nare part of this latest update: Rich text substitutions HTML substitutions Floating/docking icon\nunifies the interface; text monitor, action reporting, ActionPad (and InkPad on tablet and touch\ncomputers ActionPad pre-fills as you type to quickly select the ActiveWord you want. Assign\nActiveWords to groups Assign up to three ActiveWords to a new item in the AddWizard Share individual\nor selected ActiveWords Personalize key combination to open ActionPad Faster performance and other\nfixes Spellcheck is common in some apps, but not every application does it flawlessly so this is\nwhere ActiveWords steps in and takes care of auto correction. I like the rich text substitution\ncapability that lets me insert my signature with a simple \"sig\" and double space rather than a\ncouple of mouse clicks. I have several ActiveWords for launching common applications and navigating\nto websites. These save mouse clicks and movements and menu navigation selections. After you install\nActiveWords on your Windows computer, you will see the ActiveWords icon with options to: View\nActiveWords Toggle the AW Monitor bar View Options Access help files You can also drag the\nActiveWords icon around and even resize it to your preferred size. I haven't noticed any kind of\nperformance lag or impact due to having ActiveWords running all the time on my 3 year old Dell\nLatitude. The scripting functionality is pretty powerful in ActiveWords, but it does take some time\nand effort to setup the scripts. You need to write down all the actions you perform, such as Alt or\nCtrl, shift, then N, etc., and then select these and enter them into the scripting dialog box. I\nwish there was a way to record your actions and have the script generated, but then again it is a\nbit rewarding to create scripts that work with some efforts. My engineering firm is gearing up to\ntest ActiveWords and I look forward to seeing what kind of intricate scripts the engineers develop.\nWe already create quite a few programs to run scripts so it is a natural fit for engineers to\ncustomize scripts in ActiveWords as well. You should also make sure to check out the add-in content\navailable for Agents, text substitutions, program controls, and Internet functionality. You really\nneed to at least try out the free version to discover how ActiveWords can work best for YOU.\nActiveWords is one of those applications you can install and then just use the default, pre-loaded\nfunctions, but is 1000 times better if you take a bit of time and really optimize it for your own\nneeds. By default, automatic monitoring is enabled to even help you create useful ActiveWords. There\nare three versions of ActiveWords; free, Plus, and Enterprise. You can check out a comparison table\nand see that the free version is designed to let you try out ActiveWords for 60 days with several\nlimitations. The Plus version is priced at a one time fee of $49.95 and can be used on all of your\ncomputers. The Enterprise version is $29.95 per seat per year and includes unlimited support. After\nyou install ActiveWords, then you will receive some targeted emails that are designed to help you\nlearn more about this extremely powerful program. Join Discussion\n\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n### ActiveWords Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n* When was ActiveWords founded?\n\nActiveWords was founded in 1999.\n* Where is ActiveWords's headquarters?\n\nActiveWords's headquarters is located at Winter Park.\n* Who are ActiveWords's competitors?\n\nCompetitors of ActiveWords include Superhuman and 7 more.\n\nLoading...\n\n## Compare ActiveWords to Competitors\n\n[Engram][63]\n\nEngram provides an artificial intelligence (AI) writing tool specialized in proofreading,\nparaphrasing, and language translation services. The company offers solutions to improve grammar,\nrephrase sentences for enhanced vocabulary and fluency, and translate text to English, focusing on\naiding non-native English speakers. Engram's AI technology is designed to understand and correct\nreal mistakes made by non-native speakers, providing natural-sounding and human-like text. Engram\nwas formerly known as Pcanpi. It was founded in 2018 and is based in Seoul, South Korea.\n\n[Keypoint Technologies][64]\n\nKeypoint Technologies specializes in innovative language technology and user interface solutions\nacross various platforms and devices. The company offers a range of products and services including\nAI-powered multilingual keyboards, conversational AI platforms, and localization platforms, as well\nas comprehensive IT services such as software and app development, website development, and data\nscience. Keypoint Technologies primarily serves sectors that require advanced language technology\nand IT solutions, such as mobile technology, ecommerce, and enterprise software industries. It was\nfounded in 2004 and is based in Glasgow, Scotland.\n\n[Bobble AI][65]\n\nBobble AI is a company that provides an AI-powered mobile keyboard platform. The company offers\nservices including branding and marketing solutions for businesses, consumer intelligence data, and\na subscription service for consumers that includes various AI features. Bobble AI's products are\nused in the mobile technology and digital marketing sectors. It was founded in 2015 and is based in\nGurugram, India.\n\n[Kika Tech Logo]\n[Kika Tech][66]\n\nKika Tech is a company that develops a mobile keyboard application. It incorporates artificial\nintelligence to predict user intentions, and includes features like emoji, emoticons, stickers,\nGIFs, and keyboard themes. Kika Tech serves the mobile application industry, providing tools for\nuser communication. It was founded in 2016 and is based in San Jose, California.\n\n[Text Blaze][67]\n\nText Blaze provides text expansion and workflow automation tools within the software industry. The\ncompany offers a Chrome Extension that allows users to create and use text snippets, templates, and\nmacros. Text Blaze's tools integrate with web applications. It was founded in 2019 and is based in\nSan Francisco, California.\n\n[Hemingway App][68]\n\nHemingway App operates within the software industry and focuses on writing by checking grammar,\nspelling, and readability, as well as providing suggestions for tone adjustments. The app serves\nindividuals and professionals who want to improve their writing. It is based in New York, New York.\n\nLoading...\n\n[CB Insights]\n498 Seventh Avenue 12th floor\nNew York, NY 10018[info@cbinsights.com][69]\n[212 292 3148][70]\n\nFollow Us On Social\n\n[[Twitter]][71][[Linkedin]][72][[Facebook]][73]\n\n### [About][74]\n* [About Us][75]\n* [Upcoming Webinars][76]\n* [Contact Us][77]\n\n### [How We Help][78]\n* [Understand Tech Markets][79]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][80]\n* [Create Tech Strategy][81]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors][82]\n* [Digital Transformation][83]\n\n### [What We Offer][84]\n* [Platform][85]\n* [Data][86]\n* [Research Overview][87]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][88]\n* [Pricing][89]\n\n### [Popular Research][90]\n* [AI 100][91]\n* [Fintech 100][92]\n* [Digital Health 50][93]\n* [Tech Trends 2024][94]\n* [Generative AI Predictions][95]\n* [Unicorn Tracker][96]\n* [VC Glossary][97]\n* [Company List Applications][98]\n* [CB Insights Website Terms of Use][99]\n* [Privacy Policy][100]\n* [Do Not Sell My Info][101]\n* [Partnership][102]\n\nCopyright 2026 CB Information Services, Inc. All rights reserved.\n\nCBI websites generally use certain cookies to enable better interactions with our sites and\nservices. Use of these cookies, which may be stored on your device, permits us to improve and\ncustomize your experience. You can read more about your cookie choices at [our privacy policy][103].\nBy continuing to use this site you are consenting to these choices.\n\nI ACCEPT\nI DO NOT ACCEPT\n\n[1]: https://www.cbinsights.com/what-we-offer/technology-vendors/\n[2]: https://www.cbinsights.com/research/\n[3]: https://www.cbinsights.com/newsletter/\n[4]: https://www.cbinsights.com/media-support/\n[5]: https://www.cbinsights.com/login\n[6]: https://www.cbinsights.com\n[7]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-strategy/\n[8]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-venture-capital/\n[9]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/venture-capital/\n[10]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/head-of-it/\n[11]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-innovation/\n[12]: https://www.cbinsights.com/how-vcs-use-cb-insights/\n[13]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/consumer/\n[14]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/tech/\n[15]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/industries/insurance/\n[16]: https://www.cbinsights.com"
