            "url": "https://www.cbinsights.com/company/tunecore",
            "text": "* [Technology Vendors][1]\n* [Recent Research][2]\n* [Newsletter][3]\n* [Media Support][4]\n* [Login][5]\n[[CB Insights]][6]\n* Who We Serve\n* Function\n* [Corporate Strategy][7]\n* [Corporate Venture Capital][8]\n* [Venture Capital][9]\n* [IT][10]\n* [Corporate Innovation][11]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### How VCs Use CB Insights\n\n[Go to the video gallery \u2192][12]\n* Industries\n* [Consumer & Retail][13]\n* [Tech][14]\n* [Insurance][15]\n* [Healthcare][16]\n* [Industrials][17]\n* [Financial Services][18]\n* [Professional Services][19]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Professional Services\n\n[Learn More\u2192][20]\n* [Success Stories][21]\n* How We Help\n* [Understand Tech Markets][22]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][23]\n* [Determine Tech Strategy][24]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors & Partners][25]\n* [Turbocharge Digital Transformation][26]\n* What We Offer\n* Platform\n* [Overview][27]\n* [Technology Search Engine][28]\n* [Market Analytics and Visualizations][29]\n* [Team Management and Collaboration][30]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Platform Overview\n\n[Learn More\u2192][31]\n* [Data][32]\n* [Research][33]\n* [Personal Briefing][34]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][35]\n* [Public Equity Data][36]\n* [Buyer Interview Transcripts][37]\n* [Analyst Briefings][38]\n* [API & Data Feeds][39]\n* Integrations\n* [Overview][40]\n* [Chrome and Edge][41]\n* [Salesforce][42]\n* [Affinity][43]\n* [Microsoft Excel][44]\n* [Google Sheets][45]\n* [Microsoft Teams][46]\n* [Slack][47]\n* [Google Slides][48]\n* [App Partners][49]\n* [Browser Extension][50]\n* [Pricing][51]\n* About Us\n* [Overview][52]\n* Our teams\n* [Business Development][53]\n* [Engineering][54]\n* [Operations][55]\n* [Product][56]\n* [See all \u2192][57]\n* [Open Jobs][58]\n\nLoading...\n\n[TuneCore company logo]\n\n# TuneCore\n\nUnclaimed\n[tunecore.com][59]\n* [Overview & Products][60]\n* [Financials][61]\n* [People][62]\n* [Alternatives & Competitors][63]\n\n## Founded Year\n\n2005\n\n## Stage\n\nAcquired | Acquired\n\n## Total Raised\n\n$7M\n\n## Revenue\n\n$0000 View\n\n## About TuneCore\n\nTuneCore is a provider of digital distribution, providing universal access to distribution for tens\nof millions of music creators, film producers, and artists. TuneCore Music Distribution services\nhelp artists, labels, and managers sell their music through iTunes, Apple Music, Spotify, Amazon\nMusic, Google Play, and other major download and streaming sites while retaining 100 percent of\ntheir sales revenue and rights for a low annual flat fee. TuneCore Music Publishing Administration\nassists songwriters by administering their compositions through licensing, registration, world-wide\nroyalty collections, and placement opportunities in film, TV, commercials, video games and more. The\nTuneCore Artist Services portal offers a suite of tools and services that enable artists to promote\ntheir craft, connect with fans, and get their music heard. TuneCore, part of Believe Digital\nServices, operates as an independent company and is headquartered in Brooklyn, NY.\n\n## Headquarters Location\n\n63 Pearl Street Box #256\n\nBrooklyn, New York, 11201,\n\nUnited States\n\nLoading...\n\nLoading...\n\n## TuneCore Patents\n\nTuneCore has filed 1 patent.\n\n[patents chart]\nView Patents Chart\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nApplic\u2502Gran\u2502Title \u2502Related Topics \u2502Stat\nation \u2502t \u2502 \u2502 \u2502us\nDate \u2502Date\u2502 \u2502 \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n2/1/20\u2502 \u2502[Location based media distribution\u2502Content delivery network, Online content \u2502Appl\n16 \u2502 \u2502and content delivery and discovery\u2502distribution, Video on demand services, Social \u2502icat\n\u2502 \u2502mechanism][64] \u2502networking services, File sharing \u2502ion\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nApplication\u25022/1/2016\nDate \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nGrant Date \u2502\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nTitle \u2502[Location based media distribution and content delivery and discovery mechanism][65]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nRelated \u2502Content delivery network, Online content distribution, Video on demand services, Social\nTopics \u2502networking services, File sharing\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStatus \u2502Application\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n## Latest TuneCore News\n\n[Basile Beaugendre and Cyrus Chen promoted to regional heads for Europe and APAC at TuneCore][66]\n\nMay 27, 2026\n\nIn that role, he helped transform TuneCore France into the company's second-largest business unit\nworldwide, according to the company. He also developed technical tools to facilitate the transition\nof top-performing TuneCore artists to Believe , and restructured the region's approach to artist and\nbrand marketing. \u201cAs Europe is a cornerstone of the industry, I'm thrilled to now amplify this\nmission on a European scale, and am ready to ensure TuneCore remains at the forefront of its\ncreative evolution.\u201d Basile Beaugendre, Tunecore As Regional Head of TuneCore , Europe, Beaugendre\nwill oversee teams spanning France Germany , the UK Italy , the Netherlands Scandinavia and Eastern\nEurope Beaugendre said: \u201cI have always believed in a music industry that prioritizes the artist, and\nI've dedicated my career to making that a reality. \u201cAs Europe is a cornerstone of the industry, I'm\nthrilled to now amplify this mission on a European scale, and am ready to ensure TuneCore remains at\nthe forefront of its creative evolution.\u201d Chen has served as Head of TuneCore , Southeast Asia,\nsince 2020. In that role, he launched community hubs throughout the region, bringing TuneCore \u2018s\nsupport to emerging music markets in non-capital cities that, according to the company, the broader\nindustry had overlooked. He also pioneered localized payment rollouts in Indonesia , the Philippines\n, and Vietnam , and has grown the number of active TuneCore artists in the region by more than four\ntimes in the past three years, according to the company. As Regional Head of TuneCore , APAC, Chen\nwill oversee local teams in India Indonesia Vietnam , the Philippines Singapore Malaysia Laos , and\nThailand , while also driving expansion into new APAC territories outside of Southeast Asia. \u201cThe\nopportunity ahead is immense, and I'm deeply motivated to lead TuneCore's efforts in ensuring that\nindependent artists across the region have the tools, support, and platform to be part of that\ngrowth.\u201d Cyrus Chen, Tunecore Chen said: \u201cWe've forecasted internally that Asia will become the\nworld's largest music market by \u201cThe opportunity ahead is immense, and I'm deeply motivated to lead\nTuneCore's efforts in ensuring that independent artists across the region have the tools, support,\nand platform to be part of that growth.\u201d The new appointments arrive amid a period of leadership\ntransition at TuneCore. Former CEO Andreea Gleeson exited her role in January , moving to a\nStrategic Advisor position at parent company Believe Miller was subsequently promoted from Chief\nRevenue Officer to Chief Business Officer in April to oversee all of TuneCore \u2018s global business. At\na group level, Believe, which was taken private last year by a consortium led by founder , backed by\nEQT and TCV, has been investing in its international footprint. In April, Believe and TuneCore\nunveiled a significant update to their Generative AI policy , automatically blocking the\ndistribution of AI-generated tracks produced on unlicensed platforms. TuneCore \u2013 which is\ncelebrating its 20th anniversary this year \u2013 reported in November that self-releasing artists have\nearned more than $5 billion via its platform since its founding in 2006. That milestone represented\na payout of approximately $1 billion in the months prior, or roughly $59 million per month. TuneCore\ndistributes music to more than streaming and download platforms worldwide and operates across five\ncontinents. Music Business Worldwide\n\nMay 27, 2026\n[TuneCore Strengthens International Leadership Team, Names Basile Beaugendre Regional Head of\nTuneCore, Europe, and Cyrus Chen Regional Head of TuneCore, APAC][67]\nMay 27, 2026\n[TuneCore Strengthens International Leadership Team, Names Basile Beaugendre Regional Head of\nTuneCore, Europe, and Cyrus Chen Regional Head of TuneCore, APAC][68]\nMay 25, 2026\n[Udio's licensed AI music app will be called Starstruck, with four creation modes for fans\n(Report)][69]\nMay 15, 2026\n[Russ honored with NMPA Gold & Platinum Recognition celebrating 26 certified songs][70]\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n### TuneCore Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n* When was TuneCore founded?\n\nTuneCore was founded in 2005.\n* Where is TuneCore's headquarters?\n\nTuneCore's headquarters is located at 63 Pearl Street, Brooklyn.\n* What is TuneCore's latest funding round?\n\nTuneCore's latest funding round is Acquired.\n* How much did TuneCore raise?\n\nTuneCore raised a total of $7M.\n* Who are the investors of TuneCore?\n\nInvestors of TuneCore include Believe Music, Opus Capital and Greycroft.\n* Who are TuneCore's competitors?\n\nCompetitors of TuneCore include Stem, Noted Media Group, DistroKid, Believe Music, AWAL and 7\nmore.\n\nLoading...\n\n## Compare TuneCore to Competitors\n\n[DistroKid Logo]\n[DistroKid][71]\n\nDistroKid provides a suite of music tools for digital music distribution. It helps customers collect\nroyalties from their music, automatically split earnings among collaborators, publish credits and\nlyrics online, backup music files, procure cover song licenses, and get their music into major\nonline music stores and services worldwide. The company was founded in 2013 and is based in New\nYork, New York.\n\n[LANDR Audio Logo]\n[LANDR Audio][72]\n\nLANDR Audio operates in the audio technology industry. The company provides a platform that includes\naudio mastering, music distribution to streaming services, and a range of tools including plugins,\nsamples, and online music courses. LANDR Audio serves musicians, producers, and audio engineers\nseeking music production options. LANDR Audio was formerly known as MixGenius. It was founded in\n2013 and is based in Montreal, Quebec.\n\n[Last.fm Logo]\n[Last.fm][73]\n\nLast.fm is an online music service that tracks music listening habits and provides music\nrecommendations. It offers a platform for discovering and sharing music, with features like tracking\nhistory and recommending new music and events, as well as an encyclopedia of artists and tracks. It\nintegrates with music streaming services. It was founded in 2002 and is based in London, United\nKingdom.\n\n[Revelator Logo]\n[Revelator][74]\n\nRevelator provides business solutions for the music industry, operating within the sectors of music\ndistribution, rights management, and financial services. The company offers services including\ncatalog management, distribution and delivery, income tracking, royalty accounting, global payments,\nand analytics. Revelator serves independent record labels, distributors, and music tech companies.\nIt was founded in 2012 and is based in Los Angeles, California.\n\n[BMAT Music Innovators Logo]\n[BMAT Music Innovators][75]\n\nBMAT Music Innovators focuses on indexing music usage and ownership data within the music industry.\nThe company provides services to music industry stakeholders, such as CMOs, publishers, record\nlabels, and broadcasters, for managing copyright and tracking music usage. BMAT's platform includes\ntools for reporting, rights administration, and analytics, addressing the needs of artists, venues,\nand digital service providers. It was founded in 2005 and is based in Barcelona, Spain.\n\n[Sonicswap][76]\n\nSonicswap offers a personalized music recommendation service that inte"
