            "url": "https://www.cbinsights.com/company/doostang",
            "text": "* [Technology Vendors][1]\n* [Recent Research][2]\n* [Newsletter][3]\n* [Media Support][4]\n* [Login][5]\n[[CB Insights]][6]\n* Who We Serve\n* Function\n* [Corporate Strategy][7]\n* [Corporate Venture Capital][8]\n* [Venture Capital][9]\n* [IT][10]\n* [Corporate Innovation][11]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### How VCs Use CB Insights\n\n[Go to the video gallery \u2192][12]\n* Industries\n* [Consumer & Retail][13]\n* [Tech][14]\n* [Insurance][15]\n* [Healthcare][16]\n* [Industrials][17]\n* [Financial Services][18]\n* [Professional Services][19]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Professional Services\n\n[Learn More\u2192][20]\n* [Success Stories][21]\n* How We Help\n* [Understand Tech Markets][22]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][23]\n* [Determine Tech Strategy][24]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors & Partners][25]\n* [Turbocharge Digital Transformation][26]\n* What We Offer\n* Platform\n* [Overview][27]\n* [Technology Search Engine][28]\n* [Market Analytics and Visualizations][29]\n* [Team Management and Collaboration][30]\n* [Featured Item]\n\n### Platform Overview\n\n[Learn More\u2192][31]\n* [Data][32]\n* [Research][33]\n* [Personal Briefing][34]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][35]\n* [Public Equity Data][36]\n* [Buyer Interview Transcripts][37]\n* [Analyst Briefings][38]\n* [API & Data Feeds][39]\n* Integrations\n* [Overview][40]\n* [Chrome and Edge][41]\n* [Salesforce][42]\n* [Affinity][43]\n* [Microsoft Excel][44]\n* [Google Sheets][45]\n* [Microsoft Teams][46]\n* [Slack][47]\n* [Google Slides][48]\n* [App Partners][49]\n* [Browser Extension][50]\n* [Pricing][51]\n* About Us\n* [Overview][52]\n* Our teams\n* [Business Development][53]\n* [Engineering][54]\n* [Operations][55]\n* [Product][56]\n* [See all \u2192][57]\n* [Open Jobs][58]\n\nLoading...\n\n[Doostang company logo]\n\n# Doostang\n\nUnclaimed\n[doostang.com][59]\n* [Overview & Products][60]\n* [Financials][61]\n* [People][62]\n\n## Founded Year\n\n2004\n\n## Stage\n\nAcquired | Acquired\n\n## Total Raised\n\n$5.05M\n\n## About Doostang\n\nDoostang is a free invitation-only professional network that connects people through personal\nrelationships and affiliations. Its members commonly use Doostang to interact with one another,\nshare relevant career opportunities, and expand their network. People invited to Doostang are\nallowed immediate access to people and postings most relevant to them.\n\n## Headquarters Location\n\n410 Cambridge Avenue 2nd Floor\n\nPalo Alto, California, 94306,\n\nUnited States\n\nLoading...\n\nLoading...\n\n## Expert Collections containing Doostang\n\nExpert Collections are analyst-curated lists that highlight the companies you need to know in the\nmost important technology spaces.\n\nDoostang is included in **1 Expert Collection,** including **HR Tech**.\n\n# HR Tech\n\n6,137 items\n\nThe HR tech collection includes software vendors that enable companies to develop, hire, manage, and\npay their workforces. Focus areas include benefits, compensation, engagement, EORs & PEOs, HRIS &\nHRMS, learning & development, payroll, talent acquisition, and talent management.\n\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n## Latest Doostang News\n\n[Universum Buys Doostang][63]\n\nJul 12, 2011\n\nUniversum Buys Doostang July 12, 2011 Universum Development has acquired career networking platform\nDoostang, the company announced Tuesday. Doostang, based in Palo Alto, Calif., had raised venture\nfunding from Shasta Ventures and Tugboat Ventures and individual investors. Formed in 2005, the\ncompany targets young business professionals and has about 900,000 members, it says. Terms of the\ndeal were not released. PRESS RELEASE PALO ALTO, Calif., July 12, 2011 /PRNewswire/ \u2014 Universum\nDevelopment, mother company to Universum Group, the global leader in Employer Branding, announced\ntoday the acquisition of Doostang, the leading global career networking platform for young\nprofessionals. Founded in 2005, Doostang is one of the largest career networking platforms for young\nbusiness professionals in the world, with over 900,000 members. Members join Doostang to get\nexclusive access to over 15,000 hand-picked positions with thousands of prestigious employers across\nfinance and investment, consulting, media, and technology industries specifically targeting\nhigh-achieving students and graduates of leading academic institutions. \u201cWe have been monitoring\nDoostang closely for a long time and now look forward to be able to contribute to their continued\ngrowth,\u201d said Lars-Henrik Friis Molin, Founder and Chairman at Universum Development. \u201cUniversum\u2019s\nwell established contacts and know-how within the space will be of great use to Doostang,\u201d said\nPetter Nylander, CEO of Universum Group. In addition to the transaction, Jeff Berger will join\nDoostang as their new CEO. Previously, Berger was the CEO and Founder of KODA, an Internet\nrecruiting company based in San Francisco. \u201cI\u2019m excited about the opportunity to lead Doostang as it\ncontinues to grow as a leading professional destination online,\u201d said Berger. \u201cDoostang will provide\nan innovative social media solution to Universum\u2019s 1000+ clients across the globe.\u201d Doostang members\ncan access the Doostang community and their personal Facebook friend network to identify and\nleverage inside connections at the employers they want to work for. Unlike LinkedIn, Doostang does\nnot charge employers to post jobs, allows its members to contact any other member for free, and\nautomatically highlights any shared affiliation between individuals such as a common undergraduate\nuniversity or former employer. These social connections have proven invaluable to thousands of\nmembers who have successfully advanced their career on Doostang. Chuck Taylor had been the CEO of\nDoostang since 2008 and will continue to work with Universum and its digital strategy. \u201cThe\nacquisition of Doostang is a great opportunity for the group to help further develop a strong online\npresence,\u201d said Taylor. Doostang is partnered with career centers at leading undergraduate and\ngraduate business schools across the globe, as well as leading professional associations such as 85\nBroads, a globally recognized network of trailblazing, career-minded, multigenerational women\ngraduates and students of the world\u2019s leading colleges, universities, and graduate schools. Doostang\nhad raised capital from Shasta Ventures, a leading venture capital firm in Silicon Valley. About\nUniversum Group: Universum AB, founded in 1988, is the global world leader in Employer Branding\nresearch, consulting, and media productions. They have offices in 10 countries and conducts research\nin over 40, in close collaboration with the top universities of the world. www.universumglobal.com\nAbout Doostang: Doostang is an exclusive online career network that connects elite professionals\nwith the most prestigious jobs. Nearly a million young professionals from top universities and\nbusiness schools are members of Doostang. Companies using Doostang to recruit talent include\ntop-tier employers Goldman Sachs, Bain & Company, Kohlberg Kravis & Roberts, Summit Partners,\nGoogle, Time Warner and Facebook. \u00a9 2015 Buyouts Insider / Argosy Group LLC\n\nLearn more by requesting a demo\n\n### Doostang Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n* When was Doostang founded?\n\nDoostang was founded in 2004.\n* Where is Doostang's headquarters?\n\nDoostang's headquarters is located at 410 Cambridge Avenue, Palo Alto.\n* What is Doostang's latest funding round?\n\nDoostang's latest funding round is Acquired.\n* How much did Doostang raise?\n\nDoostang raised a total of $5.05M.\n* Who are the investors of Doostang?\n\nInvestors of Doostang include Universum, Shasta Ventures and Tugboat Ventures.\n\nLoading...\n\nLoading...\n\n[CB Insights]\n498 Seventh Avenue 12th floor\nNew York, NY 10018[info@cbinsights.com][64]\n[212 292 3148][65]\n\nFollow Us On Social\n\n[[Twitter]][66][[Linkedin]][67][[Facebook]][68]\n\n### [About][69]\n* [About Us][70]\n* [Upcoming Webinars][71]\n* [Contact Us][72]\n\n### [How We Help][73]\n* [Understand Tech Markets][74]\n* [Anticipate Competitor Strategy][75]\n* [Create Tech Strategy][76]\n* [Connect with Tech Vendors][77]\n* [Digital Transformation][78]\n\n### [What We Offer][79]\n* [Platform][80]\n* [Data][81]\n* [Research Overview][82]\n* [GenAI Instant Insights][83]\n* [Pricing][84]\n\n### [Popular Research][85]\n* [AI 100][86]\n* [Fintech 100][87]\n* [Digital Health 50][88]\n* [Tech Trends 2024][89]\n* [Generative AI Predictions][90]\n* [Unicorn Tracker][91]\n* [VC Glossary][92]\n* [Company List Applications][93]\n* [CB Insights Website Terms of Use][94]\n* [Privacy Policy][95]\n* [Do Not Sell My Info][96]\n* [Partnership][97]\n\nCopyright 2026 CB Information Services, Inc. All rights reserved.\n\nCBI websites generally use certain cookies to enable better interactions with our sites and\nservices. Use of these cookies, which may be stored on your device, permits us to improve and\ncustomize your experience. You can read more about your cookie choices at [our privacy policy][98].\nBy continuing to use this site you are consenting to these choices.\n\nI ACCEPT\nI DO NOT ACCEPT\n\n[1]: https://www.cbinsights.com/what-we-offer/technology-vendors/\n[2]: https://www.cbinsights.com/research/\n[3]: https://www.cbinsights.com/newsletter/\n[4]: https://www.cbinsights.com/media-support/\n[5]: https://www.cbinsights.com/login\n[6]: https://www.cbinsights.com\n[7]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-strategy/\n[8]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-venture-capital/\n[9]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/venture-capital/\n[10]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/head-of-it/\n[11]: https://www.cbinsights.com/who-we-serve/function/corporate-innovation/\n[12]: https://www.cbinsights.com/how-vcs-use-cb-insights/\n[13]: https://www.cbins