        "partnerships": "",
        "crawl_text": "Geospatial Media & Communications Media and Consulting Global Technology Media Company of the Year 2019 Tech Innovation Impact Award in Communications & Networking 2019 Global Geospatial Industry Ambassador Award to Sanjay Kumar by UN-GGIM Leadership Award for promoting advancement in Information Technology to Sanjay Kumar Rising Star award to Annu Negi by Foundation for Millennium Sustainable Development Goals Not specified Global Geospatial World: Advancing Knowledge for Sustainability\n\nGW CONSULTING\n\nGW EVENTS\n\nABOUT US\n\nVision\n\nMaking a Difference through Geospatial Knowledge and Space Infrastructure in World Economy and Society.\n\nOur Mission\n\nAdvancing Knowledge for Sustainability\n\nApproach\n\nEvangelism, Advocacy, Facilitation, and Amplification of adoption of space and geospatial technology across mainstream industries, and thereby improving Productivity, Efficiency, Transparency, and Compliance, and contributing to \u2018Sustainability of Everything\u2019 at national, regional, and global levels\n\nVision\n\nMaking a Difference through Space Infrastructure and Geospatial Knowledge in World Economy and Society\n\nOur Mission\n\nAdvancing Knowledge for Sustainability\u200b\n\nApproach\n\nEvangelism, Advocacy, Facilitation, and Amplification of adoption of space and geospatial technology across mainstream industries, and thereby improving Productivity, Efficiency, Transparency, and Compliance, and contributing to \u2018Sustainability of Everything\u2019 at national, regional, and global levels.\n\n100+\n\nTrusted Professionals\n\n50+\n\nIndustry Reports\n\n27+\n\nYears of Expertise\n\n10+\n\nAnnual Events\n\nOur Divisions\n\nEVENTS\n\nA thought leadership platform offering market directions, collaborative opportunities, business development interface amongst policy makers, users, technology providers, and mainstream leadership.\n\nProducts &amp; Services\n\nFlagship Events : Geospatial World Forum, GeoSmart India\n\nBusiness : GeoBuiz Summit\n\nPolicy : GeoGov Summit, Geospatial Artha Summit\n\nThematic : Indo-Pacific GeoIntelligence, AEC Forum\n\nDISCOVER OUR EVENTS\n\nCONSULTING\n\nA knowledge platform enhancing policies, processes, and practices of geospatial and space technologies through undertaking market research, socio-economic analysis, and consulting services.\n\nProducts &amp; Services\n\nSyndicate Reports\n\nGeospatial Resource Platform\n\nConsulting Services\n\nPolicy and Strategy Advocacy\n\nDISCOVER KNOWLEDGE HUB\n\nCOMMUNICATIONS\n\nA pre-eminent source of quality information, insights and analysis of contemporary global geospatial technology trends and business directions.\n\nProducts &amp; Services\n\nGW Prime Live\n\nGW Media Website\n\nEXPLORE GW PRIME\n\nEVENTS\n\nA thought leadership platform offering market directions, collaborative opportunities, business development interface amongst policy makers, users, technology providers, and mainstream leadership.\n\nProducts &amp; Services\n\nFlagship Events : Geospatial World Forum, GeoSmart India\n\nBusiness : GeoBuiz Summit\n\nPolicy : GeoGov Summit, Geospatial Artha Summit\n\nThematic : Indo-Pacific GeoIntelligence, AEC Forum\n\nDISCOVER OUR EVENTS\n\nCONSULTING\n\nA knowledge platform enhancing policies, processes, and practices of geospatial and space technologies through undertaking market research, socio-economic analysis, and consulting services.\n\nProducts &amp; Services\n\nSyndicate Reports\n\nGeospatial Resource Platform\n\nConsulting Services\n\nPolicy and Strategy Advocacy\n\nDISCOVER KNOWLEDGE HUB\n\nOur Partners\n\nIndustry Focus\n\nGeospatial Knowledge Infrastructure\n\nGeospatial Knowledge Infrastructure provides a blueprint to integrate digital economies, societies and citizens with geospatial approaches, data and technologies and in doing so, deliver the location-based knowledge, services and automation expected in the 4IR age.\n\nArchitecture Engineering and Construction (AEC)\n\nThe integration of geospatial and engineering solutions, including Building Information Modelling (BIM), offers a comprehensive context for the AEC industry. At Geospatial World, our team of consultants, which includes architects, engineers, and urban planners, advise leading AEC firms with market intelligence on technology maturity, digital transformation and the adoption of data-driven models. Through strategic guidance and innovative solutions, we empower the AEC industry to enhance efficiency, precision, and overall project outcomes with the use of technology.\n\nLocation and Business Intelligence\n\nLocation forms a major component of all data collected today, and with increased investment in geolocation infrastructure, it is set to be the cornerstone of Business Intelligence. Today, advanced analytics reveal rich insights that were previously unattainable in sectors such as banking, financial services and insurance, real estate, supply chain and logistics, etc. At Geospatial World, we harness our expertise with location systems and industry relationships, along with rigorous data analysis, to bring actionable intelligence to our partners. Through consulting services and events, we provide the necessary insights to help organizations leverage location data for improved decision-making and strategic planning.\n\nAutonomy and Robotics\n\nGeospatial World is at the forefront of communicating the value of the digital revolution by integrating geospatial elements into all aspects of data generation. Through our consulting services and thought leadership events, we provide insights into how vast amounts of big data, leveraged by Machine Learning algorithms, can deliver intelligent, smart solutions. These advancements drive innovation across various sectors, including mobility, targeted marketing, traffic management, and agriculture.\n\nEnvironmental, Social and Governance (ESG)\n\nESG frameworks have become essential at local, regional, national, and global levels covering a broad spectrum of issues, including environmental conservation, social equity, climate change mitigation, ethical business practices, and sustainable development. Geospatial technologies play a vital role in the ESG landscape by providing location intelligence, enhancing the accuracy and effectiveness of sustainability and social impact initiatives. Through our ESG unit, Geospatial World offers consulting services and hosts events to guide organizations in integrating geospatial solutions into their ESG strategies. We empower the development community and other stakeholders to make informed, data-driven decisions for a more sustainable and equitable future.\n\nGeospatial Knowledge Infrastructure\n\nArchitecture, Engineering and Construction\n\nLocation and Business Intelligence\n\nAutonomy and Robotics\n\nEnvironmental, Social and Governance\n\nGeospatial Knowledge Infrastructure\n\nGeospatial Knowledge Infrastructure\nGeospatial Knowledge Infrastructure provides a blueprint\nto integrate digital economies, societies and citizens\nwith geospatial approaches, data and technologies\nand in doing so, deliver the location-based knowledge,\nservices and automation expected in the 4IR age.\n\nArchitecture, Engineering and Construction\n\nArchitecture Engineering and Construction (AEC)\nThe integration of geospatial and engineering solutions, including Building Information Modelling (BIM), offers a comprehensive context for the AEC industry. At Geospatial World, our team of consultants, which includes architects, engineers, and urban planners, advise leading AEC firms with market intelligence on technology maturity, digital transformation and the adoption of data-driven models. Through strategic guidance and innovative solutions, we empower the AEC industry to enhance efficiency, precision, and overall project outcomes with the use of technology.\n\nLocation and Business Intelligence\n\nLocation and Business Intelligence\nLocation forms a major component of all data collected today, and with increased investment in geolocation infrastructure, it is set to be the cornerstone of Business Intelligence. Today, advanced analytics reveal rich insights that were previously unattainable in sectors such as banking, financial services and insurance, real estate, supply chain and logistics, etc. At Geospatial World, we harness our expertise with location systems and industry relationships, along with rigorous data analysis, to bring actionable intelligence to our partners. Through consulting services and events, we provide the necessary insights to help organizations leverage location data for improved decision-making and strategic plannin # ABOUT US\n\n## Advocacy\n\n## EVANGELISM\n\n## Engagement\n\nGW CONSULTING // GW EVENTS // GW MEDIA\n**\"Making a Difference through Geospatial Knowledge in the World Economy and Society\"**\n\nSustainability remains to be the essence of life on Earth. For a better future, we must adapt to\nbuild sustainable societies, economies and the environment, making decisions based on knowledge. It\nis everyone\u2019s responsibility and our passion.\n\nThe \u2018Geospatial Way\u2019 brings knowledge efficiently and effectively by integrating people,\norganizations, information and technology to understand and overcome the complex challenges we face\ntoday. Geospatial World approaches this by drawing upon the value of collaborative geospatial\nknowledge infrastructures.\n\nFor almost a quarter of a century, Geospatial World has been instrumental in strengthening\ngeospatial ecosystems at business, national, regional and global levels. Pursuing our vision of\n\u201cMaking a Difference through Geospatial Knowledge in the World Economy and Society\u201d, we will\ncontinue to advance global sustainability through our Consulting, Events and Media divisions.\n\n## 1997\n\nPrint Magazine Launched\n\n## 1998\n\nFirst National Conference Organized\n\n## 2000\n\nDedicated News and Resource Website Launched\n\n## 2002\n\nFirst Regional Conference Organized\n\n## 2007\n\nFirst Global Conference Organized\n\n## 2011\n\nGIS Development Renamed Geospatial Media & Communications\n\n## 2014\n\nDedicated Research Unit Established\n\n## 2017\n\nFirst GeoBuiz Report Published\n\n## 2021\n\nOrganization Rebranded as Geospatial World\n\n## INDUSTRIES WE SERVE\n\n### GEOSPATIAL INFRASTRUCTURE\n\n#### GIS, GNSS, Remote Sensing and more\n\nGeospatial industry and the use of geospatial data and information in traditional economic sectors\nstands at the threshold of a giant leap. There is an increasing need in the market to develop a\nbroad understanding of technology mandates, trends, and business models of Government and Public\nAdministration, and National Geospatial Organizations (inclusive of National Mapping Agencies, Space\nAgencies, Geological Agencies), Thematic Mapping Organizations and other sectors to understand the\nchallenges faced by them, and to facilitate collaborative mechanisms. Our consultants draw expertise\nfrom our 20+ years of experience and engagement in the geospatial industry and technology solutions\nto develop and implement solutions that deliver the best results.\n\n### ARCHITECTURE, ENGINEERING & CONSTRUCTION\n\n#### AI Modeling, BIM Solutions and more\n\nIntegration of geospatial and engineering solutions, i.e., Building Information Modelling (BIM)\nsolutions provides a broader context to the AEC industry. Integration of spatial information and\ncontextualizing it with in-built data helps the AEC industry digitally engineer and transform the\nconstruction project lifecycle \u2013 across surveying and monitoring, planning, designing and\nengineering, and construction processes. Our team of consultants - including architects, engineers,\nand urban planners - advise leading AEC firms to transform digitally and adopt data-driven models.\n\n[Know More][1]\n\n### LOCATION & BUSINESS INTELLIGENCE\n\n#### Big Data Analysis, Machine Learning and more\n\nLocation forms a major component of all data collected today, and with increased investment in\ngeolocation infrastructure, is set to be the cornerstone of Business Intelligence. Advanced\nanalytics reveal rich insights that have been unattainable until the coming of the new digital age.\n\nWe harness our expertise with location systems and relationships in the industry along with rigorou"
