        "crawl_text": "Nonprofit Charitable organization exempt under Internal Revenue Code Section 501(c)(3) Not specified Global MTEC has received $1.5B in federal funding and $1.2B in follow-on funding, indicating strong financial backing for medical technology development. MTEC has awarded 384 projects and has 150 products in the pipeline, showcasing its active role in advancing medical technologies. MTEC is actively seeking funding opportunities for various medical technology projects, including ventilation and autonomous closed-loop control mechanical ventilation. MTEC focuses on fostering military-civilian partnerships and collaboration within an extensive ecosystem of businesses and academic institutions. MTEC's flexible Other Transaction Agreement (OTA) allows for rapid deployment of funding and innovative solutions in medical technology. MTEC positions itself as a leader in advancing medical technology for military and civilian health. Increased federal funding for medical technology development and a growing network of innovators and service providers. Medical Technology Enterprise Consortium | MTEC\n\nMTEC\nFocus Areas\n\nWho we serve Solicitations Patents\n\nAbout Us Explore\n\nJoin MTEC\nLog In\n\nMEDICAL TECHNOLOGY ENTERPRISE CONSORTIUM\nAdvancing Medical Innovation\nWe advance the rapid deployment of innovative medical technologies that improve the health of the military and civilians.\nJOIN MTEC\n\nMTEC for\nFederal Agencies\nFind the most innovative solutions to your agency&#x27;s most pressing medical issues through the MTEC OTA Learn More\n\nMTEC for\nInnovators and Service Providers\nGet access to the funding, expertise, and resources you need to develop and deliver your technologies to market Learn More\n\nMTEC for\nHealthcare Investors\nExplore growth stage medical technology companies at the forefront of innovation Learn More\n\nFiDollarSign\n1.5B\nFederal funding\n\nGrGroup\n750+\nMTEC Members\n\nFiDollarSign\n1.2B\nFollow-on Funding\n\nFiFileText\n384\nProjects Awarded\n\nGiHoneycomb\n150\nProducts in Pipeline\n\nMTEC NEWS\nThe Newsroom\n\nView all News\n\n04 June 2026\n\nAn Upcoming Funding Opportunity: Ventilation\nView\n\n28 May 2026\n\nAn Upcoming Funding Opportunity: PROMPT\nView\n\n10 December 2025\n\nAn Upcoming Funding Opportunity and Two National Events: MTEC Prepares for a Big Start to 2026\nView\n\n24 October 2025\n\nMTEC to Co-Host Platelet &amp; Platelet-like Products State of Technology Meeting\nView\n\n05 August 2025\n\nMajor Momentum in MedTech: MTEC Launches Academic Advisory Council to Supercharge Academia&#x27;s Role in Military Medical Innovation\nView\n\n25 July 2025\n\nUnlikely Alliances: Building Funding Partnerships That Bridge Interests\nView\n\n1 / 6\n\nProjects\nTechnology Showcase See All Projects\n\nSafi Biotherapeutics\nNext-Generation Manufactured Red Blood Cells for Extended Battlefield Blood Supply: Safi Biotherapeutics\nSafi Biotherapeutics is developing manufactured red blood cells (mRBCs) with extended shelf life to improve battlefield transfusion readiness and emergency trauma care.\nView\n\nNon-Invasive Glymphatic (GF) Monitoring and Recovery Optimization for Warfighter Cognitive Readiness\nApplied Cognition is developing non-invasive glymphatic monitoring and recovery technologies to enhance warfighter cognitive readiness, resilience, and sleep recovery.\nView\n\nMoberg Analytics\nMoberg Analytics \u2013 Advanced Brain Monitoring &amp; Critical Care Informatic\nMoberg\u2019s platform unifies brain monitoring data for faster, precise treatment of severe brain injuries in military and civilian care.\nView\n\nUniversity of California San Francisco\nTemPredict: AI-Driven Wearable Monitoring for Early Illness Detection and Warfighter Readiness\nTemPredict: AI wearables detect early illness and health risks to support warfighter readiness.\nView\n\nActive Solicitations\nFunding Opportunities\n\nDepartment of the Air Force\nFunding Opportunity: Autonomous Closed Loop Control Mechanical Ventilation (ACLCMV)\nDue Date: July 15, 2026\nView\n\nDefense Threat Reduction Agency (DTRA)\nFunding Opportunity: PRimer and prObe Manufacturing PlaTform (PROMPT)\nDue Date: July 24, 2026\nView\n\nDHA and National Guard\nPre-Announcement: &quot;Multi-Topic Request for Proposals: Military Medical Prototype Advancement\u201d\nView\n\nMTEC\nFunding Opportunity: MTEC Prototype Acceleration Bridge Loans\nView\n\nJoin MTEC\nMaking an Impact\nWe drive military-civilian partnerships and foster collaboration within an extensive ecosystem of small and large businesses, federal agencies, academic institutions, and more. Our collaborative approach - enabled by a flexible Other Transaction Agreement (OTA) - expedites the development of cutting-edge medical technologies essential to improving military and civilian health.\nJoin MTEC\n\nFunding\nEfficient access to government funding opportunities through MTEC\u2019s OTA\u2014designed to reduce administrative burden and speed time-to-award.\n\nCollaboration\nPartnering &amp; teaming opportunities on groundbreaking research and prototype efforts having commercial potential.\n\nGuidance\nStep-by-step guidance throughout the required government vetting, certification, and contracting process.\n\nAccess\nAn active voice in the future direction of military and civilian medical technology development.\nThe MTEC community\nOver 700 Members Strong\n\nbridging the gap between groundbreaking research and real-world application\nbridging the gap between groundbreaking research and real-world application Browse All MTEC Members\nMembers that are currently seeking investment\nThese MTEC innovators are actively seeking funding to advance groundbreaking medical technologies. Your investment can help accelerate cutting-edge research, drive innovation, and bring life-saving solutions to market. Explore the members currently raising capital and be part of the future of medical innovation.\n\nShow more\n\nMTEC EVENTS\nDrive Operational Excellence\n\nView all Events\n\nThis event has ended\n\nconference\n10th Annual MTEC Membership Meeting\nWe\u2019re excited to invite you to register for a milestone event\u2014the 10th Annual MTEC Membership Meeting! This year celebrates a decade of collaboration, innovation, and partnership with our Government partners and the broader MTEC community.\n\nOver two dynamic days, attendees will engage in networking, knowledge sharing, and strategic discussions that advance military medical innovation. This is your opportunity to connect directly with industry peers, government stakeholders, and academic leaders shaping the future of medical technology.\n\nPlease note: Registration is open to MTEC members only. Membership is required to attend this event and participate fully in consortium programs.\n\nJune 16, 2026\n\nThis event has ended\n\nconference\nAIM 2026\nDr. Chuck Hutti will be presenting on MTEC at 1:30 PM Tuesday, May 19th.\nMay 19, 2026\n\nThis event has ended\n\nconference\nPlatelet &amp; Platelet-like Products State of the Technology Meeting\n\nPlatelet and Platelet-like Products State of Technology Meeting, hosted by the Administration for Strategic Preparedness and Response\u2019s Biomedical Advanced Research and Development Authority (BARDA), Radiological and Nuclear Medical Countermeasures Program, in collaboration with the Defense Health Agency, Research and Engineering, Combat Casualty Care Portfolio and the Medical Technology Enterprise Consortium (MTEC).\n\nFebruary 17, 2026\n\nJOIN OUR MAILING LIST\nStay Connected with MTEC\nKeep up with active and upcoming solicitations, MTEC news and other valuable information.\n\nMTEC\nFor federal agencies\nFocus Areas Technology Showcase Member Directory Events For innovators and service providers\nMember Directory Submitting Proposals Active Solicitations How to Join For healthcare investors\nTechnology Showcase How to Join About MTEC\nWho We Are Capabilities Events Resources Contact Us\n\nThe Internal Revenue Service has recognized MTEC as a charitable organization which is exempt under Internal Revenue Code Section 501(c)(3).\n\n\u00a9 Copyright 2025 Linkedin Privacy Policy Terms of Use Consent Preferences\n\nPowered by Berkeley FIT [[MTEC Logo]MTEC][1]\n[Focus Areas][2]\n\n## Who we serve\n\n[Solicitations][3][Patents][4]\n\n## About Us\n\n[ Explore][5]\n[Join MTEC][6]\n[Log In][7]\n\n# Advancing Medical Innovation\n\nAt MTEC, we advance the rapid deployment of innovative medical technologies that improve the health\nof the military and civilians.\n\n[Advancing Medical Innovation]\n\n## Who Are We?\n\nMTEC is a nonprofit that funds medical technology development. We operate under a government-awarded\nOther Transaction Agreement (OTA)\u2014a flexible contracting vehicle that allows us to move faster,\ncollaborate more freely, and engage a broader range of innovators.\n\nWe drive military-civilian partnerships and foster collaboration within an extensive ecosystem of\nsmall and large businesses, federal agencies, academic institutions, and more. We rapidly deploy\nfunding and drive innovative medical technologies that improve military and civilian health\nglobally.\n\n[Check out our Focus Areas][8]\n\n## MTEC by the Numbers\n\nFiDollarSign\n\n1.5B\n\nFederal funding\n\nGrGroup\n\n750+\n\nMTEC Members\n\nFiDollarSign\n\n1.2B\n\nFollow-on Funding\n\nFiFileText\n\n384\n\nProjects Awarded\n\nGiHoneycomb\n\n150\n\nProducts in Pipeline\n\n## MTEC Members\n\nSpanning over 20 countries, our membership base includes small and large corporations, investors,\nacademic institutions, and nonprofits.\n\nOur corporate members also include a team of trusted service providers. These subject matter experts\nhelp you navigate the complexities of the healthcare ecosystem and increase the likelihood of your\ncommercial success.\n\n[Explore Our Member Directory][9]\n[MTEC Members]\n\n## Our Global Presence\n\n[Our Global Presence]\n\n## MTEC Leadership\n\n[Shawn-Headshot.jpg]\n\n### Dr. Shawn J. Green\n\nPresident\n\n[Shawn.Green@mtec-sc.org][10]\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][11]\n[Lauren Palestrini HS 2025.jpg]\n\n### Dr. Lauren Palestrini\n\nChief Science Officer\n\n[Lauren.Palestrini@mtec-sc.org][12]\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][13]\n[TOM Headshot.png]\n\n### Tom Shemanski\n\nChief Financial Officer & Treasurer\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][14]\n[Christopher-Steele-Headshot.png]\n\n### Dr. Chris Steele\n\nChief Business Development\n\n[Chris.Steele@mtec-sc.org][15]\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][16]\n[Elaine HS for website formatted.png]\n\n### Elaine Sumera\n\nChief Operating Officer\n\n[Elaine.Sumera@mtec-sc.org][17]\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][18]\n\n## MTEC Team\n\n[mb hs.png]\n\n### Madison Bell\n\nMarketing & Communications\n\n[madison.bell@mtec-sc.org][19]\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][20]\n[Chuck Hutti Headshot.png]\n\n### Dr. Chuck Hutti\n\nSenior Technical Program Manager\n\n[chuck.hutti@mtec-sc.org][21]\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][22]\n[criag Headshots for Website 245x341.png]\n\n### Craig Lebo\n\nDirector of Contracting and Compliance\n\n[Kim Olsen HS 2025.jpg]\n\n### Kim Olsen\n\nMember Relations Manager\n\n[Kim.Olsen@mtec-sc.org][23]\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][24]\n[Richard-Satcher.jpg]\n\n### Rick Satcher\n\nEducational\n\n[Rick.Satcher@mtec-sc.org][25]\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][26]\n\n## MTEC Strategic Advisors\n\n[Donna-Boston (1).jpg]\n\n### Donna Boston\n\nSenior Advisor\n\n[Bill Howell HS 2025.jpg]\n\n### Bill Howell\n\nPresident Emeritus\n\n[MTEC-George-Ludwig (1).png]\n\n### Dr. George V. Ludwig\n\nSenior Advisor\n\n[Ron HS 2025.jpg]\n\n### Dr. Ron Poropatich\n\nSenior Advisor\n\n[mei Headshots for Website 245x341.png]\n\n### Mei Sun, PhD, MBA\n\nDirector, Research Operations\n\n[Mei.Sun@mtec-sc.org][27]\n\n[Stuart-Tyner-Headshot (1).png]\n\n### Dr. Stuart Tyner\n\nSenior Advisor\n\n## MTEC Academic Advisory Council (MAAC)\n\n[Dr. Erin Rothwell headshot for website.png]\n\n### Dr. Erin Rothwell\n\nChair\n\nUniversity of Utah\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][28]\n[Dr. Sofia Matta for website.png]\n\n### Dr. Sofia Matta\n\nVice Chair\n\nMGB / Home Base\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][29]\n[Dr. Vik Bebarta for website.png]\n\n### Dr. Vik Bebarta\n\nUniversity of Colorado\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][30]\n[7c6e52cff03aa8ee12eb353280bf83bd6108cb22-246x341.jpg]\n\n### Dr. Ron Poropatich\n\nUniversity of Pittsburgh\n\n[AiFillLinkedin][31]\n\n## MTEC Board of Directors\n\n[Ellen-Embrey.jpg]\n\n### Ellen Embrey\n\nChair\n\nStratitia\n\n[Mike-Black.jpg]\n\n### Mike Black\n\nAccelerMED\n\nAt Large Board Representative\n\n[Michael-Brown.jpg]\n\n### Michael Brown\n\nGE Healt"
