ogram][107]\n    * [Exploring NEON-Derived Data Products Workshop Series][108]\n  * [Partnerships][109]\n  * [Community Engagement][110]\n  * [Work Opportunities][111]\n  \n  ### Get Involved\n* [My Account][112]\n* [Search][113]\n* Search\n\n### Search\n\nSearch\n\n### NEON data inform the nation's safety, security and well-being.\n\nThe National Ecological Observatory Network provides comprehensive ecological data from across the\nU.S.\u00a0\n\n[Niwot Ridge (NIWO) tower in the autumn]\n\n**Data Access and Licensing Changes Coming Soon:** Starting June 30, 2026, NEON will require users\nto sign in with a NEON account or use an API token when downloading data products and sample data.\nAdditionally, all data products will be released under a Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY 4.0)\nlicense. The pending updates support more reliable data access, clearer attribution, and improved\nunderstanding of how NEON data and samples are used. Review [this data notification][114] to learn\nmore and sign up for data notification email alerts in [your user account][115].\n\n### Explore 180+ data products from across the continent\n\n[Data Portal ][116]\n\n### Get access to over 700,000 samples and specimens\n\n[Biorepository Sample Portal ][117]\n[Soil Samples]\n\n### Learn how data and samples are collected\n\n[Data Collection Methods ][118]\n[Fall fish sampling in ND]\n\n### Start your journey with data and resources\n\n[Get Started ][119]\n[Photo boulder flatirons]\n\n### By ecologists. For everyone.\n\nNEON is a network of field research sites, designed by ecologists to provide open data for all.\nDiscover how we learn and grow.\n\n[What we do ][120]\n[Field technician doing aquatic observational sampling ]\n\n### 81 field sites across the U.S.\n\nTo uniquely support 30+ years of site-level and continental-scale research, NEON locates sites\nacross the U.S. to capture variability in ecological and climatological conditions.\n\n[Explore Field Sites ][121]\n[homepage image]\n\n### The Latest from NEON\n\n## Observatory Updates\n\n### [Observatory Status ][122]\n\nJune 23, 2026\n\n[We're committed thumb]\n\n### [What\u2019s the Big Deal About Continuous Discharge? ][123]\n\nJune 16, 2026\n\n[LECO field site in Domain 07 (TN)]\n\n### [From Instrument to Insight: How NEON Builds Confidence in Ecological Data ][124]\n\nMay 29, 2026\n\n[Sensor to measure aspirated air temperature]\n\n### [Data in Action: What Keeps Stream Critters in Sync (or Not)? ][125]\n\nMay 18, 2026\n\n[Dragonfly larvae on sand]\n[Read more from our Blog ][126]\n\n## Upcoming Events\n\nJul 26\n\n### [ESA 2026: Ecology in an Era of Uncertainty ][127]\n\nJul 26 -31, 2026\n\nConference/Meeting\n\nAug 4\n\n### [Ecological Forecasting Initiative 2026 Conference ][128]\n\nAug 4 -7, 2026\n\nConference/Meeting\n\nAug 12\n\n### [2026 Hacking Limnology Workshop Series: Day 3 NEON Workshop ][129]\n\nAug 12, 2026\n\nWorkshop\n\nSep 9\n\n### [2026 AmeriFlux Annual Meeting ][130]\n\nSep 9 -11, 2026\n\nConference/Meeting\n\nSep 21\n\n### [2026 TDWG Annual Conference ][131]\n\nSep 21 -25, 2026\n\nConference/Meeting\n\n[Find More Events ][132]\n\n## Data Notifications\n\n### [Next Week: Required Logins and Data Licensing Updates ][133]\n\nJune 23, 2026\n\n### [Nitrate in surface water (DP1.20033.001) algorithm updates ][134]\n\nJune 12, 2026\n\n### [New resources for site management and event reporting data ][135]\n\nJune 2, 2026\n\n### [New visualization tool for surface-atmosphere exchange data ][136]\n\nMay 7, 2026\n\n### [New summary table available for terrestrial sampling location changes ][137]\n\nApril 23, 2026\n\n[More Data Notifications ][138]\n\n## [Resources][139]\n\n### Put NEON data to work\n\nMake the most of NEON, whether you\u2019re a scientist \u00a0looking for tools and research opportunities, a\nstudent just getting started, or ecology-curious.\n\n### For Researchers\n\nExplore the wide range of\u00a0resources that we offer to enhance your research program, including\nresearch support, code for data analyses, tutorials,\u00a0and workshops.\n\n[Explore Resources ][140]\n\n### Get Started with NEON Data\n\nNEON offers over 180 free, open\u00a0data products collected using a variety of methods including\nautomated instruments, observational sampling, and airborne remote sensing.\u00a0\n\n[Explore the Learning Hub ][141]\n\n## [Get Involved][142]\n\n### Build with us\n\nNEON does not operate alone. We\u2019re here to work with scientists, educators, and partners to improve\nour science, tools, and processes.\n\n### [Events][143]\n\nSign up for a workshop and see what community events NEON is participating in.\n\n\u00a0\n\n\u00a0\n\n[The NEON Board of Directors visit the Smithsonian Institute of Conservation Biology ]\n\n### [Engagement][144]\n\nLearn what we're doing to ensure that NEON is a valuable community resource.\n\n\u00a0\n\n[Thumbs up from a field scientist at KONA]\n\n### [Feedback][145]\n\nYour feedback improves our products and services. Let us know how we can help!\n\n[Stock photo of people looking at a map]\n[NSF NEON, Operated by Battelle]\n\n#### Follow Us:\n\n#### Join Our Newsletter\n\nGet updates on events, opportunities, and how NEON is being used today.\n\n[Subscribe Now ][146]\n\n## Footer\n* [About Us][147]\n* [Contact Us][148]\n* [Terms & Conditions][149]\n* [Careers][150]\n* [Code of Conduct][151]\n\nCopyright \u00a9 Battelle, 2026\n\nThe National Ecological Observatory Network is a major facility fully funded by the U.S. National\nScience Foundation.\n\nAny opinions, findings and conclusions or recommendations expressed in this material do not\nnecessarily reflect the views of the U.S. National Science Foundation.\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: https://www.neonscience.org\n[3]: https://www.neonscience.org/about\n[4]: https://www.neonscience.org/about/overview\n[5]: https://www.neonscience.org/about/visionandmanagement\n[6]: https://www.neonscience.org/about/overview/design\n[7]: https://www.neonscience.org/about/overview/history\n[8]: https://www.neonscience.org/about-neon-biorepository\n[9]: https://www.neonscience.org/asu-neon-biorepository-staff\n[10]: https://www.neonscience.org/about/contact-neon-biorepository\n[11]: https://www.neonscience.org/impact/observatory-blog\n[12]: https://www.neonscience.org/newsletter-archive\n[13]: https://www.neonscience.org/about/staff\n[14]: https://www.neonscience.org/about/faq\n[15]: https://www.neonscience.org/about/user-accounts\n[16]: https://www.neonscience.org/about/contact-us\n[17]: https://www.neonscience.org/data\n[18]: https://data.neonscience.org/data-products/explore\n[19]: https://data.neonscience.org/visualizations/data-availability\n[20]: https://data.neonscience.org/data-api\n[21]: https://data.neonscience.org/prototype-search\n[22]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-samples/data-management/externally-hosted-data\n[23]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-collection-methods\n[24]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-collection/airborne-remote-sensing\n[25]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-collection/automated-instruments\n[26]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-collection/instrumented-collection-types\n[27]: https://www.neonscience.org/aquatic-instrument-system-ais\n[28]: https://www.neonscience.org/terrestrial-instrument-system-tis\n[29]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-collection/observational-sampling\n[30]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-collection/observation-types\n[31]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-samples/data-collection/observational-sampling/site-level-sam\npling-design\n[32]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-collection/sampling-schedules\n[33]: https://data.neonscience.org/taxonomic-lists\n[34]: https://www.neonscience.org/optimizing-observational-sampling-designs\n[35]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-collection/protocols-standardized-methods\n[36]: https://www.neonscience.org/resources/getting-started-neon-data-resources\n[37]: https://www.neonscience.org/neonutilities-r-python\n[38]: https://www.neonscience.org/resources/learning-hub\n[39]: https://www.neonscience.org/resources/code-hub\n[40]: https://www.neonscience.org/data/using-data\n[41]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-samples/data-management/data-formats-conventions\n[42]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-samples/data-management/data-revisions-releases\n[43]: https://www.neonscience.org/data-samples/data-management/data-product-bundles\n[44]: https://www.neonscience.org/usage-policies\n[45]: https://www.neonscience.org/data"
