        "crawl_text": "[Skip to main content][1]\n[[Cornell University]][2]\n[Learn about arXiv becoming an independent nonprofit.][3]\nWe gratefully acknowledge support from the Simons Foundation, [member institutions][4], and all\ncontributors. [Donate][5]\n\n# [arxiv logo]\n\nStatus\n[Login][6]\n\n[Help][7] | [Advanced Search][8]\n\nAll fields Title Author Abstract Comments Journal reference ACM classification MSC classification\nReport number arXiv identifier DOI ORCID arXiv author ID Help pages Full text\nSearch\n[[arXiv logo]][9]\n[ [Cornell University Logo] ][10]\nGO\n\n## quick links\n* [Login][11]\n* [Help Pages][12]\n* [About][13]\n\narXiv is a free distribution service and an open-access archive for nearly 2.4 million scholarly\narticles in the fields of physics, mathematics, computer science, quantitative biology, quantitative\nfinance, statistics, electrical engineering and systems science, and economics. Materials on this\nsite are not peer-reviewed by arXiv.\n\nSubject search and browse:\nPhysics Mathematics Quantitative Biology Computer Science Quantitative Finance Statistics Electrical\nEngineering and Systems Science Economics\n\n## Physics\n* [Astrophysics][14] (**astro-ph** [new][15], [recent][16], [search][17]) [Astrophysics of\n  Galaxies][18]; [Cosmology and Nongalactic Astrophysics][19]; [Earth and Planetary\n  Astrophysics][20]; [High Energy Astrophysical Phenomena][21]; [Instrumentation and Methods for\n  Astrophysics][22]; [Solar and Stellar Astrophysics][23]\n* [Condensed Matter][24] (**cond-mat** [new][25], [recent][26], [search][27]) [Disordered Systems\n  and Neural Networks][28]; [Materials Science][29]; [Mesoscale and Nanoscale Physics][30]; [Other\n  Condensed Matter][31]; [Quantum Gases][32]; [Soft Condensed Matter][33]; [Statistical\n  Mechanics][34]; [Strongly Correlated Electrons][35]; [Superconductivity][36]\n* [General Relativity and Quantum Cosmology][37] (**gr-qc** [new][38], [recent][39], [search][40])\n* [High Energy Physics - Experiment][41] (**hep-ex** [new][42], [recent][43], [search][44])\n* [High Energy Physics - Lattice][45] (**hep-lat** [new][46], [recent][47], [search][48])\n* [High Energy Physics - Phenomenology][49] (**hep-ph** [new][50], [recent][51], [search][52])\n* [High Energy Physics - Theory][53] (**hep-th** [new][54], [recent][55], [search][56])\n* [Mathematical Physics][57] (**math-ph** [new][58], [recent][59], [search][60])\n* [Nonlinear Sciences][61] (**nlin** [new][62], [recent][63], [search][64])\n  includes: [Adaptation and Self-Organizing Systems][65]; [Cellular Automata and Lattice Gases][66];\n  [Chaotic Dynamics][67]; [Exactly Solvable and Integrable Systems][68]; [Pattern Formation and\n  Solitons][69]\n* [Nuclear Experiment][70] (**nucl-ex** [new][71], [recent][72], [search][73])\n* [Nuclear Theory][74] (**nucl-th** [new][75], [recent][76], [search][77])\n* [Physics][78] (**physics** [new][79], [recent][80], [search][81])\n  includes: [Accelerator Physics][82]; [Applied Physics][83]; [Atmospheric and Oceanic Physics][84];\n  [Atomic and Molecular Clusters][85]; [Atomic Physics][86]; [Biological Physics][87]; [Chemical\n  Physics][88]; [Classical Physics][89]; [Computational Physics][90]; [Data Analysis, Statistics and\n  Probability][91]; [Fluid Dynamics][92]; [General Physics][93]; [Geophysics][94]; [History and\n  Philosophy of Physics][95]; [Instrumentation and Detectors][96]; [Medical Physics][97];\n  [Optics][98]; [Physics and Society][99]; [Physics Education][100]; [Plasma Physics][101]; [Popular\n  Physics][102]; [Space Physics][103]\n* [Quantum Physics][104] (**quant-ph** [new][105], [recent][106], [search][107])\n\n## Mathematics\n* [Mathematics][108] (**math** [new][109], [recent][110], [search][111])\n  includes: (see [detailed description][112]): [Algebraic Geometry][113]; [Algebraic Topology][114];\n  [Analysis of PDEs][115]; [Category Theory][116]; [Classical Analysis and ODEs][117];\n  [Combinatorics][118]; [Commutative Algebra][119]; [Com