        "crawl_text": "[[Resonon - Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions]Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions][1]\n[[Resonon - Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions]Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions][2]\nBack\nHyperspectral Cameras\n[Pika UV (330-800nm)][3]\n[Pika L (400-1000nm)][4]\n[Pika L-F (420-980nm)][5]\n[Pika XC2 (400-1000nm)][6]\n[Pika IR (900-1700nm)][7]\n[Pika IR+ (900-1700nm)][8]\n[Pika IR-L (925-1700nm)][9]\n[Pika IR-L+ (925-1700nm)][10]\n[Pika SWIR (1000-2500nm)][11]\n[See All Cameras][12]\nHyperspectral Systems\n[Airborne Remote Sensing][13]\n[Fully-Integrated Airborne][14]\n[Outdoor][15]\n[SpectralSight\u2122][16]\n[Benchtop - Reflectance][17]\n[Benchtop - Reflectance/Transmission ][18]\n[Benchtop - Large Samples][19]\n[Bio-LIF\u2122][20]\n[See All Systems][21]\n[Machine Vision][22]\nSoftware\n[Spectronon\u2122][23]\n[RVS Machine Vision][24]\n[Airborne][25]\n[SDK][26]\n[Compatible Software][27]\n[See All Software][28]\nProducts\nBack\n[Precision Agriculture][29]\n[Environmental Monitoring][30]\n[Biotechnology][31]\n[Remote Sensing][32]\n[Food Production][33]\n[Industrial Applications][34]\n[See All Applications][35]\n[Applications][36]\nBack\n[Blog][37]\n[Research Publications][38]\n[Manuals & Tutorials][39]\n[Tutorial Videos][40]\n[Data Sheets][41]\n[Downloads][42]\n[See More][43]\n[Library][44]\nBack\n[Customer Support][45]\n[Sales and Support Team][46]\n[Training][47]\n[International Distributors][48]\n[Warranty and Repair][49]\n[Imager Service Plan][50]\n[Policies, Terms & Conditions][51]\n[See More][52]\n[Support][53]\nBack\n[About Us][54]\n[What Our Clients Say][55]\n[Why Choose Resonon][56]\n[Careers][57]\n[See More][58]\n[Company][59]\nBack\n[Contact Resonon][60]\n[International Distributors][61]\n[See More][62]\n[Contact Us][63]\nSearch Google\n[Resonon airborne hyperspectral imaging system]\n\n# Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions\n\n[Hyperspectral Imaging Applications][64]\n[Learn About Hyperspectral Imaging][65]\n\n## Hyperspectral Imaging Systems\n\nResonon has been designing and building hyperspectral imaging systems for over 20 years.\u00a0Our\nhyperspectral imagers are used around the world in factories, laboratories, underwater, on the\nground, in the air, and in Low Earth orbit.\n\nOur integrated hardware and software systems produce high-quality data to stimulate new insights and\nsolve challenging problems.\u00a0\n\nContact us to determine the best system for your application.\n[View Complete Systems][66]\n[View Hyperspectral Cameras][67]\n[\n\nRead Our Latest Blog Post\n\n][68]\n**By combining our AI model with Resonon's hyperspectral imaging system, we can distinguish plastic\nobjects to recognize and classify waste. ** We are able to detect objects that we were once unable\nto when using just RGB cameras. I am very satisfied with the purchase of the Resonon camera.\nMyeong-hun Lim\nManager\n[SuperBin][69]\n\ue022\n\ue023\n**Airborne Remote Sensing System**\nComplete systems providing georegistered hyperspectral data from drones and piloted aircraft.\n[See More][70]\n**Fully-Integrated Airborne**\nFully-integrated, ready-to-fly hyperspectral airborne system.\n[See More][71]\n**Outdoor**\nPortable, tripod-based, hyperspectral system for outdoor measurements.\n[See More][72]\n**SpectralSight\u2122**\nSystem for rapid automated hyperspectral data collection and optical sorting.\n[See More][73]\n**Benchtop - Reflectance**\nLaboratory system for measuring hyperspectral reflectance data.\n[See More][74]\n**Benchtop - Reflectance/Transmission **\nLaboratory system for measuring both reflectance and transmission hyperspectral data.\n[See More][75]\n**Benchtop - Large Samples**\nLaboratory hyperspectral systems for scanning large objects.\n[See More][76]\n**Bio-LIF\u2122**\nLaser-Induced Fluorescence and Hyperspectral Imaging combined to yield unparalleled insight into\nbiological samples emission data.\n[See More][77]\n**Machine Vision Systems**\nHyperspectral machine vision systems for automated optical inspection, sorting, and quality control.\n[See More][78]\n**Spectronon\u2122 Software**\nPowerful analysis and visualization tools make Spectronon popular for all types of hyperspectral\ndata.\n[See More][79]\nPika UV (330-800nm)\n[See More][80]\nPika L (400-1000nm)\n[See More][81]\nPika L-F (420-980nm)\n[See More][82]\nPika XC2 (400-1000nm)\n[See More][83]\nPika IR (900-1700nm)\n[See More][84]\nPika IR+ (900-1700nm)\n[See More][85]\nPika IR-L (925-1700nm)\n[See More][86]\nPika IR-L+ (925-1700nm)\n[See More][87]\nPika SWIR (1000-2500nm)\n[See More][88]\n\n> Complete Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions\n\n### \n### Technical Excellence\n\nHigh-precision data.\n\n### \n### Rugged and Reliable\n\nBuilt for harsh environments.\n\n### \n### Superior Results\n\nProviding the answers you need.\n\n### Application Example: Hyperspectral Imaging at Night Boosts Plant Stress Detection\n\nA [Pika L][89] hyperspectral imager was used with a halogen light to image plants inside a dark room\nat noon and midnight over several days.\n\nNighttime imaging significantly improved detection of spider mite infestations, increasing\nclassification accuracy by 29-31%.\n\nPublished in: [C. Nansen et al,. Plant Methods (2024)][90]\n[More Information][91]\n[View All Applications][92] [[Resonon - Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions]Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions][1]\n[[Resonon - Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions]Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions][2]\nBack\nHyperspectral Cameras\n[Pika UV (330-800nm)][3]\n[Pika L (400-1000nm)][4]\n[Pika L-F (420-980nm)][5]\n[Pika XC2 (400-1000nm)][6]\n[Pika IR (900-1700nm)][7]\n[Pika IR+ (900-1700nm)][8]\n[Pika IR-L (925-1700nm)][9]\n[Pika IR-L+ (925-1700nm)][10]\n[Pika SWIR (1000-2500nm)][11]\n[See All Cameras][12]\nHyperspectral Systems\n[Airborne Remote Sensing][13]\n[Fully-Integrated Airborne][14]\n[Outdoor][15]\n[SpectralSight\u2122][16]\n[Benchtop - Reflectance][17]\n[Benchtop - Reflectance/Transmission ][18]\n[Benchtop - Large Samples][19]\n[Bio-LIF\u2122][20]\n[See All Systems][21]\n[Machine Vision][22]\nSoftware\n[Spectronon\u2122][23]\n[RVS Machine Vision][24]\n[Airborne][25]\n[SDK][26]\n[Compatible Software][27]\n[See All Software][28]\nProducts\nBack\n[Precision Agriculture][29]\n[Environmental Monitoring][30]\n[Biotechnology][31]\n[Remote Sensing][32]\n[Food Production][33]\n[Industrial Applications][34]\n[See All Applications][35]\n[Applications][36]\nBack\n[Blog][37]\n[Research Publications][38]\n[Manuals & Tutorials][39]\n[Tutorial Videos][40]\n[Data Sheets][41]\n[Downloads][42]\n[See More][43]\n[Library][44]\nBack\n[Customer Support][45]\n[Sales and Support Team][46]\n[Training][47]\n[International Distributors][48]\n[Warranty and Repair][49]\n[Imager Service Plan][50]\n[Policies, Terms & Conditions][51]\n[See More][52]\n[Support][53]\nBack\n[About Us][54]\n[What Our Clients Say][55]\n[Why Choose Resonon][56]\n[Careers][57]\n[See More][58]\n[Company][59]\nBack\n[Contact Resonon][60]\n[International Distributors][61]\n[See More][62]\n[Contact Us][63]\nSearch Google\n[Resonon airborne hyperspectral imaging system]\n\n# Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions\n\n[Hyperspectral Imaging Applications][64]\n[Learn About Hyperspectral Imaging][65]\n\n## Hyperspectral Imaging Systems\n\nResonon has been designing and building hyperspectral imaging systems for over 20 years.\u00a0Our\nhyperspectral imagers are used around the world in factories, laboratories, underwater, on the\nground, in the air, and in Low Earth orbit.\n\nOur integrated hardware and software systems produce high-quality data to stimulate new insights and\nsolve challenging problems.\u00a0\n\nContact us to determine the best system for your application.\n[View Complete Systems][66]\n[View Hyperspectral Cameras][67]\n[\n\nRead Our Latest Blog Post\n\n][68]\n**By combining our AI model with Resonon's hyperspectral imaging system, we can distinguish plastic\nobjects to recognize and classify waste. ** We are able to detect objects that we were once unable\nto when using just RGB cameras. I am very satisfied with the purchase of the Resonon camera.\nMyeong-hun Lim\nManager\n[SuperBin][69]\n\ue022\n\ue023\n**Airborne Remote Sensing System**\nComplete systems providing georegistered hyperspectral data from drones and piloted aircraft.\n[See More][70]\n**Fully-Integrated Airborne**\nFully-integrated, ready-to-fly hyperspectral airborne system.\n[See More][71]\n**Outdoor**\nPortable, tripod-based, hyperspectral system for outdoor measurements.\n[See More][72]\n**SpectralSight\u2122**\nSystem for rapid automated hyperspectral data collection and optical sorting.\n[See More][73]\n**Benchtop - Reflectance**\nLaboratory system for measuring hyperspectral reflectance data.\n[See More][74]\n**Benchtop - Reflectance/Transmission **\nLaboratory system for measuring both reflectance and transmission hyperspectral data.\n[See More][75]\n**Benchtop - Large Samples**\nLaboratory hyperspectral systems for scanning large objects.\n[See More][76]\n**Bio-LIF\u2122**\nLaser-Induced Fluorescence and Hyperspectral Imaging combined to yield unparalleled insight into\nbiological samples emission data.\n[See More][77]\n**Machine Vision Systems**\nHyperspectral machine vision systems for automated optical inspection, sorting, and quality control.\n[See More][78]\n**Spectronon\u2122 Software**\nPowerful analysis and visualization tools make Spectronon popular for all types of hyperspectral\ndata.\n[See More][79]\nPika UV (330-800nm)\n[See More][80]\nPika L (400-1000nm)\n[See More][81]\nPika L-F (420-980nm)\n[See More][82]\nPika XC2 (400-1000nm)\n[See More][83]\nPika IR (900-1700nm)\n[See More][84]\nPika IR+ (900-1700nm)\n[See More][85]\nPika IR-L (925-1700nm)\n[See More][86]\nPika IR-L+ (925-1700nm)\n[See More][87]\nPika SWIR (1000-2500nm)\n[See More][88]\n\n> Complete Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions\n\n### \n### Technical Excellence\n\nHigh-precision data.\n\n### \n### Rugged and Reliable\n\nBuilt for harsh environments.\n\n### \n### Superior Results\n\nProviding the answers you need.\n\n### Application Example: Hyperspectral Imaging at Night Boosts Plant Stress Detection\n\nA [Pika L][89] hyperspectral imager was used with a halogen light to image plants inside a dark room\nat noon and midnight over several days.\n\nNighttime imaging significantly improved detection of spider mite infestations, increasing\nclassification accuracy by 29-31%.\n\nPublished in: [C. Nansen et al,. Plant Methods (2024)][90]\n[More Information][91]\n[View All Applications][92]\nHyperspectral imaging with an active light source inside dark room (a). Soybean plants at 1 \u00d7 1 (b)\nand 9 \u00d7 9 (c) spatial binning. Coleus plants at 1 \u00d7 1 (d) and 9 \u00d7 9 (e) spatial binning.\nHyperspectral imaging with an active light source inside dark room (a). Soybean plants at 1 \u00d7 1 (b)\nand 9 \u00d7 9 (c) spatial binning. Coleus plants at 1 \u00d7 1 (d) and 9 \u00d7 9 (e) spatial binning.\n\ue017Prev\nNext\ue000\n\n## Newsletter Signup\n\nGet notifications about our latest products, blog posts, videos, and company news.\nName\nEmail\nSubscribe\nBy clicking subscribe, you are consenting to receive emails from Resonon (~6 per year).\u00a0\nYou can unsubscribe at any time.\n\n## Contact Us\n\nClick below and our hyperspectral experts will contact you soon.\n[Learn More][93]\n\n> Complete Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions\n\n### Discover\n\n[Home][94]\n[Hyperspectral Cameras][95]\n[Systems][96]\n[Machine Vision][97]\n[Objective Lenses][98]\n[Software][99]\n[Applications][100]\n\n### Resources\n\n[Library][101]\n[Support][102]\n[Research Publications][103]\n[Distributors][104]\n[Company][105]\n[Contact Us][106]\n[Downloads][107]\n[Privacy Policy][108]\n\n### Contact\n\n**Resonon Inc.**\n123 Commercial Drive\nBozeman, MT 59715 USA\nPhone:+1.406.586.3356[+1.406.586.3356][109]\nEmail:[Contact Us][110]\n\n### Follow\n\n[\ue005][111][\ue006][112]\n[[Resonon - Hyperspectral Imaging Solutions]][113]\n[Website design by JTech Communications][114]\n\u00a9 2026 Resonon 