        "crawl_text": "[Skip to content][1]\n[[Cubert Logo]][2]\n[Search]\n* [Products[Expand]][3]\n  * [Ultris X20]\n    \n    Ultris X20\n    \n    [Hyperspectral Camera Cubert Ultris X20 Plus]\n    \n    Ultris X20 Plus\n    \n    [Xmr And Lens 1]\n    \n    Ultris XMR\n    \n    [Hyperspectral Camera Cubert Ultris S5]\n    \n    Ultris 5\n    \n    [Ultris Swir1 Hyperspektalkamera]\n    \n    Ultris SWIR1\n    \n    [Cubert Cuvis Packaging]\n    \n    Software\n* [Applications[Expand]][4]\n  * [Machine Vision][5]\n  * [Remote Sensing][6]\n  * [Medical][7]\n  * [Defense][8]\n* [Knowledge[Expand]][9]\n  * [Blog][10]\n  * [Technology][11]\n  * [Literature][12]\n* [News][13]\n* [Company[Expand]][14]\n  * [Career][15]\n  * [Our distributors][16]\n  * [Events][17]\n* [Support][18]\n* [Contact][19]\n* [[German]][20]\n[[Cubert Logo]][21]\n\n* [ [German]][22]\n\n[Toggle Menu]\n\n# Real-Time Spectral Imaging\n\nHyperspectral snapshot cameras for real-time analysis of materials, tissue, and surfaces.\n\n[Products][23] [Contact][24]\n[Hyperspectral Camera Ultris X20 Cubert]\n\n## Experience Innovation:\n## How Hyperspectral Imaging Works\n\n## Hello World,\n## we are Cubert!\n\nSince its founding in 2012, Cubert has been a leader in the development of [hyperspectral imaging\ntechnology][25], with a particular focus on snapshot technology that enables real-time data capture.\nUnlike conventional hyperspectral camera systems, such as [push-broom sensors][26], our cameras\ncapture the entire scene instantly, allowing for live data acquisition at video rates.\n\nWe recognize the vast potential of our technology, along with the untapped markets and applications\nit can unlock. Our goal is to explore these opportunities together with our customers. Thanks to our\ninnovative approach, we cover a wide range of applications\u2014from research and development to\nindustrial inspections.\n\n[Learn more about Cubert][27] [Watch our image video][28]\n[Team Foto Cubert]\n\n## What\u2019s new at Cubert?\n\n[Newsroom][29]\n* [Banner LinkedIn inVISION Days 2025 Cubert Emtek]\n  \n  ### inVISION Days 2025 \u2013 Cubert on Stage!\n  \n  26. November 2025\n  \n  [Read more][30]\n* ### Cubert to Join chii2026 as Gold Sponsor\n  \n  14. November 2025\n  \n  [Read more][31]\n* [XMR PrismAward]\n  \n  ### Cubert Named Finalist for the 2026 SPIE Prism Awards\n  \n  11. November 2025\n  \n  [Read more][32]\n\n## Our Technology\n\nCubert is revolutionizing [hyperspectral imaging][33] with cutting-edge [snapshot technology][34]\nthat enables real-time spectral data capture. Our cameras capture the entire scene in a single\nmoment, offering a unique combination of speed, flexibility, and precision. With our solutions, you\ncan analyze spectral information live and at video rates\u2014ideal for applications in research,\nindustry, and beyond.\n\nOur hyperspectral imaging technology extends imaging far beyond the visible spectrum. Using [light\nfield technology][35], both the intensity and direction of light are recorded, allowing for advanced\npost-processing such as refocusing. This provides comprehensive spectral data for each pixel,\nelevating your applications to a new level. We are committed to true [video spectroscopy][36],\nseamlessly integrating spectral and spatial data in real-time, opening entirely new possibilities in\nimaging.\n\n### Snapshot\n\n[Learn more][37]\n\n### Hyperspectral\n\n[Learn more][38]\n\n### Light Field\n\n[Learn more][39]\n\n## Our Products\n\nDiscover our advanced hyperspectral cameras and software solutions \u2013 for precise imaging and\nefficient data analysis.\n\n[Hyperspectral Camera Ultris X20 Cubert]\n\n### Ultris X20\n* 410x410px\n* 350-1000nm\n* 164 bands\n\n[Learn more][40]\n[Hyperspectral Camera Cubert Ultris X20 Plus]\n\n### Ultris X20 Plus\n* 1886x1886px\n* 350-1000nm\n* 164 bands\n\n[Learn more][41]\n[Cubert Ultris XMR Hyperspektralkamera und Objektiv]\n\n### Ultris XMR\n* 1000x1000px\n* 430-910nm\n* 61 bands\n\n[Learn more][42]\n[Hyperspectral Camera Cubert Ultris S5]\n\n### Ultris 5\n* 290x275px\n* 450-850nm\n* 51 bands\n\n[Learn more][43]\n[Ultris Swir1 Hyperspektalkamera]\n\n### Ultris SWIR 1\n* 200x200px\n* 980-1650nm\n* 38 bands\n\n[Learn more][44]\n[Cubert Cuvis Packaging]\n\n### Cuvis\n* Cubert Software Suite\n* Full SDK\n* Platform-independent\n\n[Learn more][45]\n[Person in moderner Schutzkleidung vor blauem Hintergrund mit Hyperspektralkamera von Cubert.]\n\n## The technology of tomorrow\n\nHyperspectral snapshot cameras based on innovative light field technology \u2013 ready for immediate use\nin demanding applications.\n\n**Solutions for the highest demands.**\n* Powerful spectral imaging software for easy and fast data capture and analysis in real-time.\n* Comprehensive Software Development Kit (SDK) for full flexibility and customizations by system\n  developers.\n* Customization services for specific application requirements.\n* Support for application development and system integration to unlock the full potential of\n  hyperspectral imaging \u2013 in research and industry.\n\n## Good To Know\n\n[More guides][46]\n* [Graphic1]\n  \n  ### Material-specific detection in industrial applications\n  \n  [Read more][47]\n* [Bild5]\n  \n  ### Cr [Skip to content][1]\n[[Cubert Logo]][2]\n[Search]\n* [Products[Expand]][3]\n  * [Ultris X20]\n    \n    Ultris X20\n    \n    [Hyperspectral Camera Cubert Ultris X20 Plus]\n    \n    Ultris X20 Plus\n    \n    [Xmr And Lens 1]\n    \n    Ultris XMR\n    \n    [Hyperspectral Camera Cubert Ultris S5]\n    \n    Ultris 5\n    \n    [Ultris Swir1 Hyperspektalkamera]\n    \n    Ultris SWIR1\n    \n    [Cubert Cuvis Packaging]\n    \n    Software\n* [Applications[Expand]][4]\n  * [Machine Vision][5]\n  * [Remote Sensing][6]\n  * [Medical][7]\n  * [Defense][8]\n* [Knowledge[Expand]][9]\n  * [Blog][10]\n  * [Technology][11]\n  * [Literature][12]\n* [News][13]\n* [Company[Expand]][14]\n  * [Career][15]\n  * [Our distributors][16]\n  * [Events][17]\n* [Support][18]\n* [Contact][19]\n* [[German]][20]\n[[Cubert Logo]][21]\n\n* [ [German]][22]\n\n[Toggle Menu]\n\n# Real-Time Spectral Imaging\n\nHyperspectral snapshot cameras for real-time analysis of materials, tissue, and surfaces.\n\n[Products][23] [Contact][24]\n[Hyperspectral Camera Ultris X20 Cubert]\n\n## Experience Innovation:\n## How Hyperspectral Imaging Works\n\n## Hello World,\n## we are Cubert!\n\nSince its founding in 2012, Cubert has been a leader in the development of [hyperspectral imaging\ntechnology][25], with a particular focus on snapshot technology that enables real-time data capture.\nUnlike conventional hyperspectral camera systems, such as [push-broom sensors][26], our cameras\ncapture the entire scene instantly, allowing for live data acquisition at video rates.\n\nWe recognize the vast potential of our technology, along with the untapped markets and applications\nit can unlock. Our goal is to explore these opportunities together with our customers. Thanks to our\ninnovative approach, we cover a wide range of applications\u2014from research and development to\nindustrial inspections.\n\n[Learn more about Cubert][27] [Watch our image video][28]\n[Team Foto Cubert]\n\n## What\u2019s new at Cubert?\n\n[Newsroom][29]\n* [Banner LinkedIn inVISION Days 2025 Cubert Emtek]\n  \n  ### inVISION Days 2025 \u2013 Cubert on Stage!\n  \n  26. November 2025\n  \n  [Read more][30]\n* ### Cubert to Join chii2026 as Gold Sponsor\n  \n  14. November 2025\n  \n  [Read more][31]\n* [XMR PrismAward]\n  \n  ### Cubert Named Finalist for the 2026 SPIE Prism Awards\n  \n  11. November 2025\n  \n  [Read more][32]\n\n## Our Technology\n\nCubert is revolutionizing [hyperspectral imaging][33] with cutting-edge [snapshot technology][34]\nthat enables real-time spectral data capture. Our cameras capture the entire scene in a single\nmoment, offering a unique combination of speed, flexibility, and precision. With our solutions, you\ncan analyze spectral information live and at video rates\u2014ideal for applications in research,\nindustry, and beyond.\n\nOur hyperspectral imaging technology extends imaging far beyond the visible spectrum. Using [light\nfield technology][35], both the intensity and direction of light are recorded, allowing for advanced\npost-processing such as refocusing. This provides comprehensive spectral data for each pixel,\nelevating your applications to a new level. We are committed to true [video spectroscopy][36],\nseamlessly integrating spectral and spatial data in real-time, opening entirely new possibilities in\nimaging.\n\n### Snapshot\n\n[Learn more][37]\n\n### Hyperspectral\n\n[Learn more][38]\n\n### Light Field\n\n[Learn more][39]\n\n## Our Products\n\nDiscover our advanced hyperspectral cameras and software solutions \u2013 for precise imaging and\nefficient data analysis.\n\n[Hyperspectral Camera Ultris X20 Cubert]\n\n### Ultris X20\n* 410x410px\n* 350-1000nm\n* 164 bands\n\n[Learn more][40]\n[Hyperspectral Camera Cubert Ultris X20 Plus]\n\n### Ultris X20 Plus\n* 1886x1886px\n* 350-1000nm\n* 164 bands\n\n[Learn more][41]\n[Cubert Ultris XMR Hyperspektralkamera und Objektiv]\n\n### Ultris XMR\n* 1000x1000px\n* 430-910nm\n* 61 bands\n\n[Learn more][42]\n[Hyperspectral Camera Cubert Ultris S5]\n\n### Ultris 5\n* 290x275px\n* 450-850nm\n* 51 bands\n\n[Learn more][43]\n[Ultris Swir1 Hyperspektalkamera]\n\n### Ultris SWIR 1\n* 200x200px\n* 980-1650nm\n* 38 bands\n\n[Learn more][44]\n[Cubert Cuvis Packaging]\n\n### Cuvis\n* Cubert Software Suite\n* Full SDK\n* Platform-independent\n\n[Learn more][45]\n[Person in moderner Schutzkleidung vor blauem Hintergrund mit Hyperspektralkamera von Cubert.]\n\n## The technology of tomorrow\n\nHyperspectral snapshot cameras based on innovative light field technology \u2013 ready for immediate use\nin demanding applications.\n\n**Solutions for the highest demands.**\n* Powerful spectral imaging software for easy and fast data capture and analysis in real-time.\n* Comprehensive Software Development Kit (SDK) for full flexibility and customizations by system\n  developers.\n* Customization services for specific application requirements.\n* Support for application development and system integration to unlock the full potential of\n  hyperspectral imaging \u2013 in research and industry.\n\n## Good To Know\n\n[More guides][46]\n* [Graphic1]\n  \n  ### Material-specific detection in industrial applications\n  \n  [Read more][47]\n* [Bild5]\n  \n  ### Crawly Food Future: Revolutionizing the Food and Feed Industry with Insects\n  \n  [Read more][48]\n* [Opthalmologische untersuchung]\n  \n  ### Early Detection of Alzheimer\u2019s Using Hyperspectral Technology\n  \n  [Read more][49]\n\nCurious to see it in action?\nJoin us for a short live demo\nand discover how our technology simplifies your workflow.\n\n## Get in Touch\n\n**Dr. Matthias Locherer**\nDirector Global Market Development\n* [+49 731 708156 \u2013 70][50]\n* [sales@cubert-gmbh.de][51]\n\nHave a question about your Cubert system? Find help and solutions in our **[Help Center][52]**.\n\n[Get Support][53]\n[Matthias Locherer Cubert Freistehend]\n\n\"*\" indicates required fields\n\nFacebook\nThis field is for validation purposes and should be left unchanged.\nFirst Name*\nLast Name*\nCompany*\nApplication\nRemote SensingMedicalIndustrial / Machine VisionDefenseOther\nEmail*\nPhone\n*\nCountry * Afghanistan\u00c5land IslandsAlbaniaAlgeriaAmerican SamoaAndorraAngolaAnguillaAntarcticaAntigua\nand\nBarbudaArgentinaArmeniaArubaAustraliaAustriaAzerbaijanBahamasBahrainBangladeshBarbadosBelarusBelgium\nBelizeBeninBermudaBhutanBoliviaBonaire, Sint Eustatius and SabaBosnia and HerzegovinaBotswanaBouvet\nIslandBrazilBritish Indian Ocean TerritoryBrunei DarussalamBulgariaBurkina FasoBurundiCabo\nVerdeCambodiaCameroonCanadaCayman IslandsCentral African RepublicChadChileChinaChristmas IslandCocos\nIslandsColombiaComorosCongoCongo, Democratic Republic of theCook IslandsCosta RicaC\u00f4te\nd'IvoireCroatiaCubaCura\u00e7aoCyprusCzechiaDenmarkDjiboutiDominicaDominican RepublicEcuadorEgyptEl\nSalvadorEquatorial GuineaEritreaEstoniaEswatiniEthiopiaFalkland IslandsFaroe\nIslandsFijiFinlandFranceFrench GuianaFrench PolynesiaFrench Southern\nTerritoriesGabonGambiaGeorgiaGermanyGhanaGibraltarGreeceGreenlandGrenadaGuadeloupeGuamGuatemalaGuern\nseyGuineaGuinea-BissauGuyanaHaitiHeard Island and McDonald IslandsHoly SeeHondurasHong\nKongHungaryIcelandIndiaIndonesiaIranIraqIrelandIsle of\nManIsraelItalyJamaicaJapanJerseyJordanKazakhstanKenyaKiribatiKorea, Dem"
