        "crawl_text": "[[imec logo]][1]\n[Expertise][2]\n[What we offer][3]\n[Applications][4]\n[Your career][5]\n[About imec][6]\n[Contact][7]\n[CMOS: advanced and beyond][8]\nDiscover why imec is the premier R&D center for advanced logic & memory devices.\n[Integrated photonics][9]\nTake a look at technologies for optical transceivers, sensors and more.\n[Health technologies][10]\nSee how imec brings the power of chip technology to the world of healthcare.\n[Sensing and actuation][11]\nExplore imec\u2019s CMOS- and photonics-based sensing and actuation systems.\n[Connectivity technology][12]\nLook into our reliable, high-performance, low-power network technologies.\n[More expertises][13]\nDiscover all our expertises.\n[Research][14]\nBe the first to reap the benefits of imec\u2019s research by joining one of our programs or starting an\nexclusive bilateral collaboration.\n[Manufacturing][15]\nGo from idea to scalable and reliable semiconductor manufacturing with IC-Link.\n[Venturing][16]\nWe create and co-create new ventures, and we invest in and accelerate existing ventures.\n[Education and workforce development][17]\nImec supports formal and on-the-job training for a range of careers in semiconductors.\n[NanoIC pilot line][18]\nAligned with the EU Chips Act, access to the pilot line will accelerate beyond-2nm innovation.\n[Semiconductor technology][19]\n[Life sciences and health solutions][20]\n[Data and telecommunication][21]\n[Automotive technologies][22]\n[Robotics technology for Industry 4.0][23]\n[More applications][24]\n[Article Monolithic ASIC vs Chiplet]\n[AI Protein engineering]\n[PR 2D materials TSMC ASML]\n\n## When to move from a monolithic ASIC to a chiplet-based design?\n\n[Click to explore ][25]\n\n## Transforming AI\u2011driven lab-in-the-loop protein engineering\n\n[Read the story ][26]\n\n## ASML, TSMC and imec bring 2D-material transistors closer to industrial readiness\n\nWith breakthrough 300mm integration\n\n[Read the full press release ][27]\nWhen to move from a monolithic ASIC to a chiplet-based design?\nTransforming AI\u2011driven lab-in-the-loop protein engineering\nASML, TSMC and imec bring 2D-material transistors closer to industrial readiness\n\nImec is the world's leading independent nanoelectronics R&D hub. The combination of our\n[talent][28], [infrastructure][29], and partner network enables breakthroughs towards\n[microchips][30] that are smaller, faster, more affordable, and more sustainable. We combine that\nnanotech expertise with data and AI to create and support [applications][31] for a smarter, better\nfuture.\n\n[[Expertise]][32]\n\n##### Expertise\n\nWith firm roots in nanoelectronics, our portfolio covers a range of hardware and software\ntechnologies.\n\n[Dive into our expertise][33]\n\n[[Research]][34]\n\n##### Research\n\nIn our 12,000 m\u00b2 cleanrooms and state-of-the-art labs, we\u2019re taking nano- and digital technology to\nthe next level.\n\n[Join our research][35]\n\n[[Development]][36]\n\n##### Manufacturing\n\nGo from idea to scalable and reliable semiconductor manufacturing with IC-Link.\n\n[Go from concept to production][37]\n\n[[PR NanoIC]][38]\n\n##### NanoIC pilot line\n\nA pivotal initiative of the EU Chips Act to reinforce Europe\u2019s leadership in semiconductor\ninnovation.\n\n[Learn how you can benefit][39]\n\n[[Venturing]][40]\n\n##### Venturing & start-ups\n\nOur venturing ecosystem supports tech entrepreneurs by providing them with funds and knowhow.\n\n[Boost your start- or scale-up][41]\n\n\u00a0\n\n[[Applications]][42]\n\n##### Applications\n\nGet inspired by an overview of the ways in which imec\u2019s technologies can transform your industry.\n\n[Get inspired by our applications][43]\n\n[[Green IC industry white paper]][44]\n\n##### Sustainability\n\nTake a look at how the goal of a sustainable future guides our research and our internal\norganization.\n\n[Discover our\u00a0Sustainable Development Goals][45]\n\n[\n\n## Stories\n\n][46]\n[[AI Protein engineering]][47]\n\n#### [\n#### AI\u2011driven lab-in-the-loop protein engineering\n#### ][48]\n\nA new approach through next\u2011generation chip technologies.\n[[Article Monolithic ASIC vs Chiplet]\n\nLongread\n\n][49]\n\n#### [\n#### When does it make sense to move from a monolithic ASIC to a chiplet-based design?\n#### ][50]\n\nThe benefits, trade-offs and technical implications of moving to chiplets.\n[[PR FeFET FeCAP]\n\nPress release\n\n17 June 2026\n\n][51]\n\n#### [\n#### Breakthroughs in ferroelectric memory research\n#### ][52]\n\nFor solutions that meet AI-era data needs.\n[[PR imec Sony]\n\nPress release\n\n16 June 2026\n\n][53]\n\n#### [\n#### Sony and imec unveil high-density backside connectivity module\n#### ][54]\n\nEnabling next-generation 3D chip integration.\n[[PR 2D materials TSMC ASML]\n\nPress release\n\n15 June 2026\n\n][55]\n\n#### [\n#### 2D-material transistors closer to industrial readiness\n#### ][56]\n\nWith breakthrough 300mm integration.\n[[PR RF Interposer]\n\nPress release\n\n11 June 2026\n\n][57]\n\n#### [\n#### Imec unlocks system-level III-V chiplet integration on Si-CMOS\n#### ][58]\n\nBy advancing its 300mm RF silicon interposer platform.\n[[Collaboration signing IMEC and TUe]][59]\n\n#### [\n#### Imec and TU/e formalize a [[imec logo]][1]\n[Expertise][2]\n[What we offer][3]\n[Applications][4]\n[Your career][5]\n[About imec][6]\n[Contact][7]\n[CMOS: advanced and beyond][8]\nDiscover why imec is the premier R&D center for advanced logic & memory devices.\n[Integrated photonics][9]\nTake a look at technologies for optical transceivers, sensors and more.\n[Health technologies][10]\nSee how imec brings the power of chip technology to the world of healthcare.\n[Sensing and actuation][11]\nExplore imec\u2019s CMOS- and photonics-based sensing and actuation systems.\n[Connectivity technology][12]\nLook into our reliable, high-performance, low-power network technologies.\n[More expertises][13]\nDiscover all our expertises.\n[Research][14]\nBe the first to reap the benefits of imec\u2019s research by joining one of our programs or starting an\nexclusive bilateral collaboration.\n[Manufacturing][15]\nGo from idea to scalable and reliable semiconductor manufacturing with IC-Link.\n[Venturing][16]\nWe create and co-create new ventures, and we invest in and accelerate existing ventures.\n[Education and workforce development][17]\nImec supports formal and on-the-job training for a range of careers in semiconductors.\n[NanoIC pilot line][18]\nAligned with the EU Chips Act, access to the pilot line will accelerate beyond-2nm innovation.\n[Semiconductor technology][19]\n[Life sciences and health solutions][20]\n[Data and telecommunication][21]\n[Automotive technologies][22]\n[Robotics technology for Industry 4.0][23]\n[More applications][24]\n[Article Monolithic ASIC vs Chiplet]\n[AI Protein engineering]\n[PR 2D materials TSMC ASML]\n\n## When to move from a monolithic ASIC to a chiplet-based design?\n\n[Click to explore ][25]\n\n## Transforming AI\u2011driven lab-in-the-loop protein engineering\n\n[Read the story ][26]\n\n## ASML, TSMC and imec bring 2D-material transistors closer to industrial readiness\n\nWith breakthrough 300mm integration\n\n[Read the full press release ][27]\nWhen to move from a monolithic ASIC to a chiplet-based design?\nTransforming AI\u2011driven lab-in-the-loop protein engineering\nASML, TSMC and imec bring 2D-material transistors closer to industrial readiness\n\nImec is the world's leading independent nanoelectronics R&D hub. The combination of our\n[talent][28], [infrastructure][29], and partner network enables breakthroughs towards\n[microchips][30] that are smaller, faster, more affordable, and more sustainable. We combine that\nnanotech expertise with data and AI to create and support [applications][31] for a smarter, better\nfuture.\n\n[[Expertise]][32]\n\n##### Expertise\n\nWith firm roots in nanoelectronics, our portfolio covers a range of hardware and software\ntechnologies.\n\n[Dive into our expertise][33]\n\n[[Research]][34]\n\n##### Research\n\nIn our 12,000 m\u00b2 cleanrooms and state-of-the-art labs, we\u2019re taking nano- and digital technology to\nthe next level.\n\n[Join our research][35]\n\n[[Development]][36]\n\n##### Manufacturing\n\nGo from idea to scalable and reliable semiconductor manufacturing with IC-Link.\n\n[Go from concept to production][37]\n\n[[PR NanoIC]][38]\n\n##### NanoIC pilot line\n\nA pivotal initiative of the EU Chips Act to reinforce Europe\u2019s leadership in semiconductor\ninnovation.\n\n[Learn how you can benefit][39]\n\n[[Venturing]][40]\n\n##### Venturing & start-ups\n\nOur venturing ecosystem supports tech entrepreneurs by providing them with funds and knowhow.\n\n[Boost your start- or scale-up][41]\n\n\u00a0\n\n[[Applications]][42]\n\n##### Applications\n\nGet inspired by an overview of the ways in which imec\u2019s technologies can transform your industry.\n\n[Get inspired by our applications][43]\n\n[[Green IC industry white paper]][44]\n\n##### Sustainability\n\nTake a look at how the goal of a sustainable future guides our research and our internal\norganization.\n\n[Discover our\u00a0Sustainable Development Goals][45]\n\n[\n\n## Stories\n\n][46]\n[[AI Protein engineering]][47]\n\n#### [\n#### AI\u2011driven lab-in-the-loop protein engineering\n#### ][48]\n\nA new approach through next\u2011generation chip technologies.\n[[Article Monolithic ASIC vs Chiplet]\n\nLongread\n\n][49]\n\n#### [\n#### When does it make sense to move from a monolithic ASIC to a chiplet-based design?\n#### ][50]\n\nThe benefits, trade-offs and technical implications of moving to chiplets.\n[[PR FeFET FeCAP]\n\nPress release\n\n17 June 2026\n\n][51]\n\n#### [\n#### Breakthroughs in ferroelectric memory research\n#### ][52]\n\nFor solutions that meet AI-era data needs.\n[[PR imec Sony]\n\nPress release\n\n16 June 2026\n\n][53]\n\n#### [\n#### Sony and imec unveil high-density backside connectivity module\n#### ][54]\n\nEnabling next-generation 3D chip integration.\n[[PR 2D materials TSMC ASML]\n\nPress release\n\n15 June 2026\n\n][55]\n\n#### [\n#### 2D-material transistors closer to industrial readiness\n#### ][56]\n\nWith breakthrough 300mm integration.\n[[PR RF Interposer]\n\nPress release\n\n11 June 2026\n\n][57]\n\n#### [\n#### Imec unlocks system-level III-V chiplet integration on Si-CMOS\n#### ][58]\n\nBy advancing its 300mm RF silicon interposer platform.\n[[Collaboration signing IMEC and TUe]][59]\n\n#### [\n#### Imec and TU/e formalize a shared vision for semiconductor innovation\n#### ][60]\n\nReinforcing Eindhoven's position as as a semiconductor innovation hub.\n[[PR UWB]\n\nPress release\n\n9 June 2026\n\n][61]\n\n#### [\n#### Imec unlocks fourfold UWB range extension\n#### ][62]\n\nUsing narrowband receiver chip compliant with IEEE 802.15.4ab standard.\n[[PR Hybrid Bonding]\n\nPress release\n\n28 May 2026\n\n][63]\n\n#### [\n#### W2W hybrid bonding with 200nm interconnect pitch\n#### ][64]\n\nAdvancing overlay performance required for advanced logic-to-logic and memory-to-logic tier\nstacking.\n[[ACP architecture]\n\nVision\n\n][65]\n\n#### [\n#### From horsepower to high-performance compute\n#### ][66]\n\nAutomotive chiplets take the leap towards autonomous edge computing.\n[[PR HNA Qubits]\n\nPress release\n\n19 May 2026\n\n][67]\n\n#### [\n#### World first: quantum dot qubit device using High NA EUV\n#### ][68]\n\nMost advanced litho will be key for scaling up quantum technology.\n[[PR Venturing]\n\nPress release\n\n18 May 2026\n\n][69]\n\n#### [\n#### Imec expands global footprint of imec.ventures with dedicated US presence\n#### ][70]\n\nSupporting the creation and scaling of semiconductor deep-tech ventures worldwide.\n[[PR 3D CCD]\n\nPress release\n\n12 May 2026\n\n][71]\n\n#### [\n#### Imec demonstrates first 3D implementation of a CCD for AI memory applications\n#### ][72]\n\nPaving the way for a solution to address the memory wall for AI-specific workloads.\n[\n\n#### Discover more\n\n][73]\n\n## Publications\n\nExplore the scientific achievements of imec\u2019s researchers, including those at affiliated university\nresearch groups.\n\n[Visit the publication repository][74]\n\n[\n\n## Upcoming events\n\n][75]\n[\n\nMay 24 - June 28, 2026\n\n#### Compound Semiconductor Week (CSW) 2026\n\nKumamoto, Japan\n\n][76][\n\nJune 28 - July 02, 2026\n\n#### OECC 2026\n\nBusan, South-Korea\n\n][77][\n\nJune 28 - July 02, 2026\n\n#### 2D Transmission Metal Dichalcogenides (2D TMDs) Conference 2026\n\nUTown, NUS, Singapore\n\n][78][\n\nJuly 13 - 17, 2026\n\n#### Spin Qubit\n\nDelft, Netherlands\n\n][79][\n\nJuly 20 - 24, 2026\n\n####"
      }
