        "crawl_text": "[[MTEC Logo]MTEC][1]\n[Focus Areas][2]\n\n## Who we serve\n\n[Solicitations][3][Patents][4]\n\n## About Us\n\n[ Explore][5]\n[Join MTEC][6]\n[Log In][7]\n\nMEDICAL TECHNOLOGY ENTERPRISE CONSORTIUM\n\n# Advancing Medical Innovation\n\nWe advance the rapid deployment of innovative medical technologies that improve the health of the\nmilitary and civilians.\n\n[JOIN MTEC][8]\n[\n\nMTEC for\n\n## Federal Agencies\n\nFind the most innovative solutions to your agency's most pressing medical issues through the MTEC\nOTA\n\nLearn More\n][9][\n\nMTEC for\n\n## Innovators and Service Providers\n\nGet access to the funding, expertise, and resources you need to develop and deliver your\ntechnologies to market\n\nLearn More\n][10][\n\nMTEC for\n\n## Healthcare Investors\n\nExplore growth stage medical technology companies at the forefront of innovation\n\nLearn More\n][11]\nFiDollarSign\n\n1.5B\n\nFederal funding\n\nGrGroup\n\n750+\n\nMTEC Members\n\nFiDollarSign\n\n1.2B\n\nFollow-on Funding\n\nFiFileText\n\n384\n\nProjects Awarded\n\nGiHoneycomb\n\n150\n\nProducts in Pipeline\n\nMTEC NEWS\n\n## The Newsroom\n\n\n[View all News][12]\n[An Upcoming Funding Opportunity: Ventilation]\n\n04 June 2026\n\n### An Upcoming Funding Opportunity: Ventilation\n\n[View][13]\n[An Upcoming Funding Opportunity: PROMPT]\n\n28 May 2026\n\n### An Upcoming Funding Opportunity: PROMPT\n\n[View][14]\n[An Upcoming Funding Opportunity and Two National Events: MTEC Prepares for a Big Start to 2026]\n\n10 December 2025\n\n### An Upcoming Funding Opportunity and Two National Events: MTEC Prepares for a Big Start to 2026\n\n[View][15]\n[MTEC to Co-Host Platelet & Platelet-like Products State of Technology Meeting]\n\n24 October 2025\n\n### MTEC to Co-Host Platelet & Platelet-like Products State of Technology Meeting\n\n[View][16]\n[Major Momentum in MedTech: MTEC Launches Academic Advisory Council to Supercharge Academia's Role\nin Military Medical Innovation]\n\n05 August 2025\n\n### Major Momentum in MedTech: MTEC Launches Academic Advisory Council to Supercharge Academia's\n### Role in Military Medical Innovation\n\n[View][17]\n[Unlikely Alliances: Building Funding Partnerships That Bridge Interests]\n\n25 July 2025\n\n### Unlikely Alliances: Building Funding Partnerships That Bridge Interests\n\n[View][18]\n\n1/6\n\n[Home page banner]\n\nProjects\n\n## Technology Showcase\n\n[See All Projects][19]\n\nSafi Biotherapeutics\n\n### Next-Generation Manufactured Red Blood Cells for Extended Battlefield Blood Supply: Safi\n### Biotherapeutics\n\nSafi Biotherapeutics is developing manufactured red blood cells (mRBCs) with extended shelf life to\nimprove battlefield transfusion readiness and emergency trauma care.\n\n[View][20]\n\n### Non-Invasive Glymphatic (GF) Monitoring and Recovery Optimization for Warfighter Cognitive\n### Readiness\n\nApplied Cognition is developing non-invasive glymphatic monitoring and recovery technologies to\nenhance warfighter cognitive readiness, resilience, and sleep recovery.\n\n[View][21]\n\nMoberg Analytics\n\n### Moberg Analytics \u2013 Advanced Brain Monitoring & Critical Care Informatic\n\nMoberg\u2019s platform unifies brain monitoring data for faster, precise treatment of severe brain\ninjuries in military and civilian care.\n\n[View][22]\n\nUniversity of California San Francisco\n\n### TemPredict: AI-Driven Wearable Monitoring for Early Illness Detection and Warfighter Readiness\n\nTemPredict: AI wearables detect early illness and health risks to support warfighter readiness.\n\n[View][23]\n\nActive Solicitations\n\n## Funding Opportunities\n\nDepartment of the Air Force\n\n### [Funding Opportunity: Autonomous Closed Loop Control Mechanical Ventilation (ACLCMV)][24]\n\nDue Date: July 15, 2026\n\n[View][25]\n\nDefense Threat Reduction Agency (DTRA)\n\n### [Funding Opportunity: PRimer and prObe Manufacturing PlaTform (PROMPT)][26]\n\nDue Date: July 24, 2026\n\n[View][27]\n\nDHA and National Guard\n\n### [Pre-Announcement: \"Multi-Topic Request for Proposals: Military Medical Prototype\n### Advancement\u201d][28]\n\n[View][29]\n\nMTEC\n\n### [Funding Opportunity: MTEC Prototype Acceleration Bridge Loans][30]\n\n[View][31]\n\nJoin MTEC\n\n## Making an Impact\n\nWe drive military-civilian partnerships and foster collaboration within an extensive ecosystem of\nsmall and large businesses, federal agencies, academic institutions, and more. Our collaborative\napproach - enabled by a flexible Other Transaction Agreement (OTA) - expedites the development of\ncutting-edge medical technologies essential to improving military and civilian health.\n\n[Join MTEC][32]\n\n### Funding\n\nEfficient access to government funding opportunities through MTEC\u2019s OTA\u2014designed to reduce\nadministrative burden and speed time-to-award.\n\n### Collaboration\n\nPartnering & teaming opportunities on groundbreaking research and prototype efforts having\ncommercial potential.\n\n### Guidance\n\nStep-by-step guidance throughout the required government vetting, certification, and contracting\nprocess.\n\n### Access\n\nAn active voice in the future direction of military and civilian medical technology development.\n\nThe MTEC community\n\n## Over 700 Members Strong\n\n[\n[Altrazeal Life Sciences Inc.]\n][33][ [[MTEC Logo]MTEC][1]\n[Focus Areas][2]\n\n## Who we serve\n\n[Solicitations][3][Patents][4]\n\n## About Us\n\n[ Explore][5]\n[Join MTEC][6]\n[Log In][7]\n\nMEDICAL TECHNOLOGY ENTERPRISE CONSORTIUM\n\n# Advancing Medical Innovation\n\nWe advance the rapid deployment of innovative medical technologies that improve the health of the\nmilitary and civilians.\n\n[JOIN MTEC][8]\n[\n\nMTEC for\n\n## Federal Agencies\n\nFind the most innovative solutions to your agency's most pressing medical issues through the MTEC\nOTA\n\nLearn More\n][9][\n\nMTEC for\n\n## Innovators and Service Providers\n\nGet access to the funding, expertise, and resources you need to develop and deliver your\ntechnologies to market\n\nLearn More\n][10][\n\nMTEC for\n\n## Healthcare Investors\n\nExplore growth stage medical technology companies at the forefront of innovation\n\nLearn More\n][11]\nFiDollarSign\n\n1.5B\n\nFederal funding\n\nGrGroup\n\n750+\n\nMTEC Members\n\nFiDollarSign\n\n1.2B\n\nFollow-on Funding\n\nFiFileText\n\n384\n\nProjects Awarded\n\nGiHoneycomb\n\n150\n\nProducts in Pipeline\n\nMTEC NEWS\n\n## The Newsroom\n\n\n[View all News][12]\n[An Upcoming Funding Opportunity: Ventilation]\n\n04 June 2026\n\n### An Upcoming Funding Opportunity: Ventilation\n\n[View][13]\n[An Upcoming Funding Opportunity: PROMPT]\n\n28 May 2026\n\n### An Upcoming Funding Opportunity: PROMPT\n\n[View][14]\n[An Upcoming Funding Opportunity and Two National Events: MTEC Prepares for a Big Start to 2026]\n\n10 December 2025\n\n### An Upcoming Funding Opportunity and Two National Events: MTEC Prepares for a Big Start to 2026\n\n[View][15]\n[MTEC to Co-Host Platelet & Platelet-like Products State of Technology Meeting]\n\n24 October 2025\n\n### MTEC to Co-Host Platelet & Platelet-like Products State of Technology Meeting\n\n[View][16]\n[Major Momentum in MedTech: MTEC Launches Academic Advisory Council to Supercharge Academia's Role\nin Military Medical Innovation]\n\n05 August 2025\n\n### Major Momentum in MedTech: MTEC Launches Academic Advisory Council to Supercharge Academia's\n### Role in Military Medical Innovation\n\n[View][17]\n[Unlikely Alliances: Building Funding Partnerships That Bridge Interests]\n\n25 July 2025\n\n### Unlikely Alliances: Building Funding Partnerships That Bridge Interests\n\n[View][18]\n\n1/6\n\n[Home page banner]\n\nProjects\n\n## Technology Showcase\n\n[See All Projects][19]\n\nSafi Biotherapeutics\n\n### Next-Generation Manufactured Red Blood Cells for Extended Battlefield Blood Supply: Safi\n### Biotherapeutics\n\nSafi Biotherapeutics is developing manufactured red blood cells (mRBCs) with extended shelf life to\nimprove battlefield transfusion readiness and emergency trauma care.\n\n[View][20]\n\n### Non-Invasive Glymphatic (GF) Monitoring and Recovery Optimization for Warfighter Cognitive\n### Readiness\n\nApplied Cognition is developing non-invasive glymphatic monitoring and recovery technologies to\nenhance warfighter cognitive readiness, resilience, and sleep recovery.\n\n[View][21]\n\nMoberg Analytics\n\n### Moberg Analytics \u2013 Advanced Brain Monitoring & Critical Care Informatic\n\nMoberg\u2019s platform unifies brain monitoring data for faster, precise treatment of severe brain\ninjuries in military and civilian care.\n\n[View][22]\n\nUniversity of California San Francisco\n\n### TemPredict: AI-Driven Wearable Monitoring for Early Illness Detection and Warfighter Readiness\n\nTemPredict: AI wearables detect early illness and health risks to support warfighter readiness.\n\n[View][23]\n\nActive Solicitations\n\n## Funding Opportunities\n\nDepartment of the Air Force\n\n### [Funding Opportunity: Autonomous Closed Loop Control Mechanical Ventilation (ACLCMV)][24]\n\nDue Date: July 15, 2026\n\n[View][25]\n\nDefense Threat Reduction Agency (DTRA)\n\n### [Funding Opportunity: PRimer and prObe Manufacturing PlaTform (PROMPT)][26]\n\nDue Date: July 24, 2026\n\n[View][27]\n\nDHA and National Guard\n\n### [Pre-Announcement: \"Multi-Topic Request for Proposals: Military Medical Prototype\n### Advancement\u201d][28]\n\n[View][29]\n\nMTEC\n\n### [Funding Opportunity: MTEC Prototype Acceleration Bridge Loans][30]\n\n[View][31]\n\nJoin MTEC\n\n## Making an Impact\n\nWe drive military-civilian partnerships and foster collaboration within an extensive ecosystem of\nsmall and large businesses, federal agencies, academic institutions, and more. Our collaborative\napproach - enabled by a flexible Other Transaction Agreement (OTA) - expedites the development of\ncutting-edge medical technologies essential to improving military and civilian health.\n\n[Join MTEC][32]\n\n### Funding\n\nEfficient access to government funding opportunities through MTEC\u2019s OTA\u2014designed to reduce\nadministrative burden and speed time-to-award.\n\n### Collaboration\n\nPartnering & teaming opportunities on groundbreaking research and prototype efforts having\ncommercial potential.\n\n### Guidance\n\nStep-by-step guidance throughout the required government vetting, certification, and contracting\nprocess.\n\n### Access\n\nAn active voice in the future direction of military and civilian medical technology development.\n\nThe MTEC community\n\n## Over 700 Members Strong\n\n[\n[Altrazeal Life Sciences Inc.]\n][33][\n[Booz Allen Hamilton]\n][34][\n[The University of Texas System]\n][35][\n[SurgiBox Inc.]\n][36][\n[Prytime Medical Devices, Inc.]\n][37][\n[SanaHeal]\n][38]\n[\n[Metis Foundation]\n][39][\n[Mayo Clinic]\n][40][\n[University of Pittsburgh]\n][41][\n[Sibel Health]\n][42]\n\nbridging the gap between groundbreaking research and real-world application\n\nbridging the gap between groundbreaking research and real-world application\n\n[Browse All MTEC Members][43]\n\n### Members that are currently seeking investment\n\nThese MTEC innovators are actively seeking funding to advance groundbreaking medical technologies.\nYour investment can help accelerate cutting-edge research, drive innovation, and bring life-saving\nsolutions to market. Explore the members currently raising capital and be part of the future of\nmedical innovation.\n\n[\n[Moberg Analytics]\n][44]\n[\n[RxMP Therapeutics]\n][45]\n[\n[MyndBlue]\n][46]\n[\n[OBVIUS Robotics]\n][47]\n[\n[PyrAmes Inc.]\n][48]\n[Show more][49]\n\nMTEC EVENTS\n\n## Drive Operational Excellence\n\n[View all Events][50]\n[\nThis event has ended\n\nconference\n\n### 10th Annual MTEC Membership Meeting\n\nWe\u2019re excited to invite you to register for a milestone event\u2014the 10th Annual MTEC Membership\nMeeting! This year celebrates a decade of collaboration, innovation, and partnership with our\nGovernment partners and the broader MTEC community. Over two dynamic days, attendees will engage in\nnetworking, knowledge sharing, and strategic discussions that advance military medical innovation.\nThis is your opportunity to connect directly with industry peers, government stakeholders, and\nacademic leaders shaping the future of medical technology. Please note: Registration is open to MTEC\nmembers only. Membership is required to attend this event and participate fully in consortium\nprograms.\n\nJune 16, 2026\n\n][51][\nThis event has ended\n\nconference\n\n### AIM 2026\n\nDr. Chuck Hutti will be presenting on MTEC at 1:30 PM Tuesday, May 19th.\n\nMay 19, 2026\n\n][52][\nThis event has ended\n\nconference\n\n### Platelet & Platele"
      }
