        "crawl_text": "* [PhotonDelta][1]\n  * Back\n  * [AboutWho We Are][2]\n  * [Mission & VisionOur Values][3]\n  * [Team & GovernanceMeet the Team][4]\n  * [Insights, Achievements, and Impact from the Past Year\n    Annual Report 2025][5]\n* [Ecosystem][6]\n  * Back\n  * [Ecosystem PartnersA Growing Network of Integrated Photonics Innovators][7]\n  * [Ecosystem OverviewConnecting Innovators Across the Value Chain][8]\n  * [Join Our EcosystemConnect, Collaborate, and Grow with the Ecosystem][9]\n  * [Value ChainFrom Design to Real-World Impact][10]\n  * [\n    PhotonFirst and Curtiss-Wright Announce Collaboration to Bring Integrated Fibre Optic Sensing to\n    Flight Test Instrumentation][11]\n* [Photonic Chips][12]\n  * Back\n  * [Automotive & Mobility][13]\n  * [Data & Telecom][14]\n  * [Food & Agriculture][15]\n  * [Medical & Healthcare][16]\n  * [\n    Building InP-Based Photonic Integrated Circuits with SMART Photonics][17]\n* [Innovation][18]\n  * Back\n  * [ProjectsAccelerating Integrated Photonic Innovation Through Innovation Programmes][19]\n  * [\n    From Foundation to Scale: Progress, Pressure, and the Next Phase for Photonics][20]\n* [Activities][21]\n  * Back\n  * [InternationalisationConnecting the Ecosystem to Global Markets and Opportunities][22]\n  * [Human CapitalDeveloping, Attracting, and Connecting Photonics Talent][23]\n  * [FundingSupporting Early-Stage Integrated Photonics Startups with Growth Capital][24]\n  * [PIC Summit EuropeEurope\u2019s Leading Integrated Photonics Event][25]\n  * [PhotonJobsConnecting Talent to Ppportunities in the Dutch Photonic Chip Industry.][26]\n  * [PhotonStudioTransforming Opportunities into Startups][27]\n  * [Global Photonics Engineering ContestDesign the Next Generation Application with Integrated\n    Photonics][28]\n* [News & Insights][29]\n  * Back\n  * [NewsDiscover the latest industry and ecosystem updates.][30]\n  * [Downloads/ReportsInsights, Reports, and Industry Resources][31]\n  * [Events CalendarBrowse Upcoming Events and Networking Opportunities][32]\n  * [CareersJoin the Team][33]\n  * [Scaling Integrated Photonics for Global Impact\n    PIC Summit Europe 2026][34]\n* [Contact][35]\nClear\nPopular searches[Ecosystem][36][Supply Chain][37][Prototyping][38][Photonic Integrated Chips\n(PICs)][39]\n\n# Next generation microchips,\n# powered by light.\n\n## Key Enabling Technology\n\nPhotonic Chip technology enables emerging high-end solutions in communication, computing and sensing\nand will be a key component for the worldwide semiconductor technology to contribute to Sustainable\nDevelopment Goals. A flourishing Photonic Chip industry will contribute to Europe\u2019s ambition towards\ntechnology leadership in key enabling technologies and strategic autonomy.\n\n[Photonic Chips][40]\n\n## Our focus\n\n[ Innovation\n\nAccelerating Photonic Chip application and industrialisation, PhotonDelta distributes subsidies for\ngroundbreaking innovation projects.\n\n][41] [ Internationalisation\n\nFacilitating international collaboration to support the growth, development and industrialisation of\nPhotonic Chip technology.\n\n][42] [ Funding\n\nFunding startups in the phase where their risk profile is high.\n\n][43] [ Talent\n\nBridging the gap between today\u2019s and tomorrow\u2019s talent and the needs of the Photonic Chip industry.\n\n][44]\n01234567890\n01234567890\n\nPartners in our ecosystem (2024)\n\n01234567890\n^{k}\n\nFTE by 2028\n\n01234567890\n01234567890\n01234567890\n^{M}\n\nFunding deployed\n\n## Application markets\n\n[\n\n### Automotive & Mobility\n\nCompact and cost-saving sensor technology for safer autonomous driving.\n\n][45]\n[\n\n### Data & Telecom\n\nFaster, energy-efficient digital infrastructure \u2013 such as 5G and 6G.\n\n][46]\n[\n\n### Food & Agriculture\n\nSustainable and safer food production through advanced sensors.\n\n][47]\n[\n\n### Medical & Healthcare\n\nAdvanced and affordable early detection and diagnostics.\n\n][48]\n[Applications][49]\n\n## Stay in the loop\n\n[\nnews\n\n### Silicon Nitride Photonic Integrated Circuits: Foundry Insights from New Origin\n\nA discussion with New Origin CEO Twan Korthorst on why SiN is gaining popularity as an integrated\nphotonics platform and how dedicated foundries can take PICs from prototype to production, creating\nnew opportunities for startups and Global Photonics Engineering Contest 2026 participants.\n\n][50]\n[\nevent\n\n### Tomorrow starts today- PIC Summit Europe Pavillion\n\nWhere cutting-edge technology leads to real-world impact.\n\n][51]\n[\nnews\n\n### PhotonFirst and Curtiss-Wright Announce Collaboration to Bring Integrated Fibre Optic Sensing to\n### Flight Test Instrumentation (FTI)\n\nPhotonFirst, a leading innovator in Fiber Bragg Grating (FBG) sensing technology and integrated\nphotonics, and Curtiss-Wright, a global market leader in Flight Test Instrumentation (FTI)\nsolutions, today announced a collaboration to accelerate the adoption of fibre optic sensing\ntechnology within the aerospace flight test domain.\n\n][52]\n[\nnews\n\n### What Investors Look for in Photonic Startups? Perspectives from PhotonVentures, a Photonics VC\n### Fund\n\nPhotonVentures explains h * [PhotonDelta][1]\n  * Back\n  * [AboutWho We Are][2]\n  * [Mission & VisionOur Values][3]\n  * [Team & GovernanceMeet the Team][4]\n  * [Insights, Achievements, and Impact from the Past Year\n    Annual Report 2025][5]\n* [Ecosystem][6]\n  * Back\n  * [Ecosystem PartnersA Growing Network of Integrated Photonics Innovators][7]\n  * [Ecosystem OverviewConnecting Innovators Across the Value Chain][8]\n  * [Join Our EcosystemConnect, Collaborate, and Grow with the Ecosystem][9]\n  * [Value ChainFrom Design to Real-World Impact][10]\n  * [\n    PhotonFirst and Curtiss-Wright Announce Collaboration to Bring Integrated Fibre Optic Sensing to\n    Flight Test Instrumentation][11]\n* [Photonic Chips][12]\n  * Back\n  * [Automotive & Mobility][13]\n  * [Data & Telecom][14]\n  * [Food & Agriculture][15]\n  * [Medical & Healthcare][16]\n  * [\n    Building InP-Based Photonic Integrated Circuits with SMART Photonics][17]\n* [Innovation][18]\n  * Back\n  * [ProjectsAccelerating Integrated Photonic Innovation Through Innovation Programmes][19]\n  * [\n    From Foundation to Scale: Progress, Pressure, and the Next Phase for Photonics][20]\n* [Activities][21]\n  * Back\n  * [InternationalisationConnecting the Ecosystem to Global Markets and Opportunities][22]\n  * [Human CapitalDeveloping, Attracting, and Connecting Photonics Talent][23]\n  * [FundingSupporting Early-Stage Integrated Photonics Startups with Growth Capital][24]\n  * [PIC Summit EuropeEurope\u2019s Leading Integrated Photonics Event][25]\n  * [PhotonJobsConnecting Talent to Ppportunities in the Dutch Photonic Chip Industry.][26]\n  * [PhotonStudioTransforming Opportunities into Startups][27]\n  * [Global Photonics Engineering ContestDesign the Next Generation Application with Integrated\n    Photonics][28]\n* [News & Insights][29]\n  * Back\n  * [NewsDiscover the latest industry and ecosystem updates.][30]\n  * [Downloads/ReportsInsights, Reports, and Industry Resources][31]\n  * [Events CalendarBrowse Upcoming Events and Networking Opportunities][32]\n  * [CareersJoin the Team][33]\n  * [Scaling Integrated Photonics for Global Impact\n    PIC Summit Europe 2026][34]\n* [Contact][35]\nClear\nPopular searches[Ecosystem][36][Supply Chain][37][Prototyping][38][Photonic Integrated Chips\n(PICs)][39]\n\n# Next generation microchips,\n# powered by light.\n\n## Key Enabling Technology\n\nPhotonic Chip technology enables emerging high-end solutions in communication, computing and sensing\nand will be a key component for the worldwide semiconductor technology to contribute to Sustainable\nDevelopment Goals. A flourishing Photonic Chip industry will contribute to Europe\u2019s ambition towards\ntechnology leadership in key enabling technologies and strategic autonomy.\n\n[Photonic Chips][40]\n\n## Our focus\n\n[ Innovation\n\nAccelerating Photonic Chip application and industrialisation, PhotonDelta distributes subsidies for\ngroundbreaking innovation projects.\n\n][41] [ Internationalisation\n\nFacilitating international collaboration to support the growth, development and industrialisation of\nPhotonic Chip technology.\n\n][42] [ Funding\n\nFunding startups in the phase where their risk profile is high.\n\n][43] [ Talent\n\nBridging the gap between today\u2019s and tomorrow\u2019s talent and the needs of the Photonic Chip industry.\n\n][44]\n01234567890\n01234567890\n\nPartners in our ecosystem (2024)\n\n01234567890\n^{k}\n\nFTE by 2028\n\n01234567890\n01234567890\n01234567890\n^{M}\n\nFunding deployed\n\n## Application markets\n\n[\n\n### Automotive & Mobility\n\nCompact and cost-saving sensor technology for safer autonomous driving.\n\n][45]\n[\n\n### Data & Telecom\n\nFaster, energy-efficient digital infrastructure \u2013 such as 5G and 6G.\n\n][46]\n[\n\n### Food & Agriculture\n\nSustainable and safer food production through advanced sensors.\n\n][47]\n[\n\n### Medical & Healthcare\n\nAdvanced and affordable early detection and diagnostics.\n\n][48]\n[Applications][49]\n\n## Stay in the loop\n\n[\nnews\n\n### Silicon Nitride Photonic Integrated Circuits: Foundry Insights from New Origin\n\nA discussion with New Origin CEO Twan Korthorst on why SiN is gaining popularity as an integrated\nphotonics platform and how dedicated foundries can take PICs from prototype to production, creating\nnew opportunities for startups and Global Photonics Engineering Contest 2026 participants.\n\n][50]\n[\nevent\n\n### Tomorrow starts today- PIC Summit Europe Pavillion\n\nWhere cutting-edge technology leads to real-world impact.\n\n][51]\n[\nnews\n\n### PhotonFirst and Curtiss-Wright Announce Collaboration to Bring Integrated Fibre Optic Sensing to\n### Flight Test Instrumentation (FTI)\n\nPhotonFirst, a leading innovator in Fiber Bragg Grating (FBG) sensing technology and integrated\nphotonics, and Curtiss-Wright, a global market leader in Flight Test Instrumentation (FTI)\nsolutions, today announced a collaboration to accelerate the adoption of fibre optic sensing\ntechnology within the aerospace flight test domain.\n\n][52]\n[\nnews\n\n### What Investors Look for in Photonic Startups? Perspectives from PhotonVentures, a Photonics VC\n### Fund\n\nPhotonVentures explains how venture capital investors assess photonic chip startups, focusing on\nscalability, ecosystem alignment, and market readiness. They highlight key signals of investment\nreadiness and the role of early validation opportunities like the Global Photonics Engineering\nContest.\n\n][53]\n[\nnews\n\n### Building InP-Based Photonic Integrated Circuits with SMART Photonics\n\nIndium phosphide (InP) enables fully integrated photonic chips with high performance and efficiency.\nAs an InP foundry, SMART Photonics supports the transition from design to scalable production\nthrough mature platforms and proven design flows.\n\n][54]\n[\nevent\n\n### DE\u2013NL Online Integrated Photonics Symposium 2026\n\nThe DE\u2013NL Online Integrated Photonics Symposium 2026 brings together industry leaders, researchers,\nand ecosystem partners from Germany and the Netherlands for a focused afternoon of discussion on the\nfuture of photonic integrated circuits.\n\n][55]\n[\nevent\n\n### Integrated Photonics Mission to SEMICON Taiwan 2026\n\nPhotonDelta, in collaboration with the Netherlands Office Taipei (NLOT, Innovation Network), is\npreparing an\u00a0Integrated Photonics Mission to SEMICON Taiwan 2026, bringing together Dutch companies\nand ecosystem partners active in integrated photonics, semiconductors, advanced packaging and\nrelated deep-tech fields.\n\n][56]\n[\nevent\n\n### PIC Summit Europe 2026\n\nPIC Summit Europe 2026 focuses on scaling integrated photonics for global impact. As PICs move into\ncommercial deployment and high-volume manufacturing, the programme explores the industrialisation\nchallenges and opportunities shaping the future of the industry.\n\n][57]\n[\nnews\n\n### Building a Talent Ecosystem for Integrated Photonics\n\nWhy attracting talent isn\u2019t enough and how building a connected community will enable the integrated\nphotonics sector to recruit and retain the right people, according to Evi Somers, PhotonDelta\u2019s\nHuman Capital Programme Director.\n\n][58]\n[\nevent\n\n### Integrated Photonics for Health & Bio Applications Webinar\n\nO"
      }
