        "crawl_text": "[ Skip to main content ][1]\n[ [Home] ][2]\n* [Products][3]\n* [Functions][4]\n* [Applications][5]\n* [About][6]\n* [Support][7]\n* [Quote][8]\n\n## Follow\n* [facebook][9]\n* [twitter][10]\n* [linkedin][11]\n\n[ [Home] ][12]\nSearch\n[ [Home] ][13]\n* [Products][14]\n* [Functions][15]\n* [Applications][16]\n* [About][17]\n* [Support][18]\n* [Quote][19]\n* [PV is spectral. Measure accordingly]\n  \n  # Advanced solar and atmospheric sensors\n  \n  accurate \u00b7 affordable \u00b7 reliable\n* [A new standard in solar measurement]\n  \n  # A new standard in solar measurement\n  \n  accurate \u00b7 affordable \u00b7 reliable\n* [PV is spectral. Measure accordingly]\n  \n  # PV is spectral. Measure accordingly\n  \n  accurate \u00b7 affordable \u00b7 reliable\n* [Advanced solar and atmospheric sensors]\n  \n  # Unlock the power of spectral data\n  \n  accurate \u00b7 affordable \u00b7 reliable\n\n### The world's most advanced solar irradiance sensors\n\ndesigned to supersede traditional spectroradiometers,\npyranometers, sun photometers and more...\n\n## our products\n* #### [SolarBand-C3US][20]\n  \n  Three component measurement with no external moving parts.\n  \n  [[SolarBand-C3US] ][21]\n* #### [SolarBand-C3][22]\n  \n  Three component measurement with no external moving parts.\n  \n  [[SolarBand-C3] ][23]\n* #### [SolarSIM-ALB][24]\n  \n  Our spectral albedometer, for measuring spectral albedo and PV rearside irradiance.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-ALB] ][25]\n* #### [SolarSIM-E][26]\n  \n  The world's most advanced shadow band. All-in-one measurement from a single sensor.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-E] ][27]\n* #### [SolarSIM-GUV][28]\n  \n  The SolarSIM ideal for measuring UVA/B/T/ and even PAR.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-GUV] ][29]\n* #### [ST-5 Sun Tracker][30]\n  \n  Our sun tracker for accurate, affordable direct or plane-of-array irradiance measurement.\n  \n  [[ST-5 Sun Tracker] ][31]\n* #### [SolarSIM-GPV][32]\n  \n  Our spectral pyranometer for measuring GHI and PV spectral correction factors.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-GPV] ][33]\n* #### [SolarSIM-D2][34]\n  \n  The original SolarSIM, for measuring spectral and broadband DNI and atmospheric parameters.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-D2] ][35]\n* #### [SolarSIM-G][36]\n  \n  Our spectral sensor for measuring spectral and broadband global irradiance.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-G] ][37]\n* #### [Recalibration][38]\n  \n  Periodic recalibration ensures optimal performance of your SolarSIMs.\n  \n  [[Recalibration] ][39]\n* #### [Systems][40]\n  \n  Turn-key or custom. Whatever capabilities you need, we can put it all together for you.\n  \n  [[Spectral measurement system] ][41]\n\n## applications\n* [Solar]\n  \n  ##### [solar][42]\n  \n  The SolarSIM sensors represent the state-of-the-art in solar resource measurement for PV\n  applications. They are the only Class A sensors capable of resolving both broadband irradiance and\n  the spectral uncertainty inherent in all PV technologies.\n  \n  [Explore][43]\n* [meteorological]\n  \n  ##### [meteorological][44]\n  \n  Spectrafy's ability to combine multiple, previously expensive and difficult measurement\n  capabilities into a single compact, robust sensor makes advanced meteorological measurements\n  practical and affordable.\n  \n  [Explore][45]\n* [Agriculture]\n  \n  ##### [agriculture][46]\n  \n  Spectrafy's multi-spectral measurement approach enables highly accurate measurements of UV, PAR\n  and global irradiance in a single sensor. Ideal for agricultural research and irradiance networks.\n  \n  [Explore][47]\n\n## our technology\n\nAt Spectrafy we embrace the spectral nature of sunlight. Our sensors combine multi-spectral\nmeasurement with proprietary radiative transfer algorithms to accurately resolve the full-range\nsolar spectrum.\n\nThis powerful approach enables our sensors to unlock the wealth of information embedded within\nspectral data and creates measurement capabilities that are unmatched in terms of functionality and\naccuracy.\n\n[Learn more][48]\n\n## latest news\n* 15 Oct\n  [Spectrafy attends the IPC-XIV in Davos, Switzerland][49]\n  [Read More][50]\n* 01 May\n  [Spectrafy welcomes Ammonit Measurement to the team!][51]\n  [Read More][52]\n* 24 Mar\n  [Spectrafy launches the SolarBand-C3][53]\n  [Read More][54]\n\n## upcoming events\n* 07 May\n  [Intersolar Europe][55]\n  Munich, Germany\n  [Read More][56]\n* 08 Jun\n  [2025 IEEE PVSC 53][57]\n  Montreal, QC\n  [Read More][58]\n\n## our customers\n\n[ [Clearway] ][59]\n[ [DEWA] ][60]\n[ [EDF] ][61]\n[ [Fraunhofer] ][62]\n[ [McMaster] ][63]\n[ [AZUR Space] ][64]\n[ [T\u00dcV Rheinland] ][65]\n[ [University Nottingham] ][66]\n[ [ONREL] ][67]\n[ [ines] ][68]\n[ [RSE] ][69]\n[ [UNSW] ][70]\n[ [Morgan Solar] ][71]\n[ [First Solar] ][72]\n[ [Natural Resources Canada] ][73]\n\n## contact us\n\nContact us at [info@spectrafy.com][74] or subscribe to our newsletter to stay up to date with the\nour latest products, news and events.\n* [facebook-square][75]\n* [twitter-square][76]\n* [linkedin][77]\n\n[[Home]][78]\n\n## Footer menu\n* [Home][79]\n* [Privacy Statement][80]\n* [Terms of use][81]\n* [Contact][82]\n\n\u00a9 2025 Spectrafy Inc. All rights reserved.\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: /\n[3]: /products\n[4]: /functions\n[5]: /applications\n[6]: /ab [ Skip to main content ][1]\n[ [Home] ][2]\n* [Products][3]\n* [Functions][4]\n* [Applications][5]\n* [About][6]\n* [Support][7]\n* [Quote][8]\n\n## Follow\n* [facebook][9]\n* [twitter][10]\n* [linkedin][11]\n\n[ [Home] ][12]\nSearch\n[ [Home] ][13]\n* [Products][14]\n* [Functions][15]\n* [Applications][16]\n* [About][17]\n* [Support][18]\n* [Quote][19]\n* [PV is spectral. Measure accordingly]\n  \n  # Advanced solar and atmospheric sensors\n  \n  accurate \u00b7 affordable \u00b7 reliable\n* [A new standard in solar measurement]\n  \n  # A new standard in solar measurement\n  \n  accurate \u00b7 affordable \u00b7 reliable\n* [PV is spectral. Measure accordingly]\n  \n  # PV is spectral. Measure accordingly\n  \n  accurate \u00b7 affordable \u00b7 reliable\n* [Advanced solar and atmospheric sensors]\n  \n  # Unlock the power of spectral data\n  \n  accurate \u00b7 affordable \u00b7 reliable\n\n### The world's most advanced solar irradiance sensors\n\ndesigned to supersede traditional spectroradiometers,\npyranometers, sun photometers and more...\n\n## our products\n* #### [SolarBand-C3US][20]\n  \n  Three component measurement with no external moving parts.\n  \n  [[SolarBand-C3US] ][21]\n* #### [SolarBand-C3][22]\n  \n  Three component measurement with no external moving parts.\n  \n  [[SolarBand-C3] ][23]\n* #### [SolarSIM-ALB][24]\n  \n  Our spectral albedometer, for measuring spectral albedo and PV rearside irradiance.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-ALB] ][25]\n* #### [SolarSIM-E][26]\n  \n  The world's most advanced shadow band. All-in-one measurement from a single sensor.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-E] ][27]\n* #### [SolarSIM-GUV][28]\n  \n  The SolarSIM ideal for measuring UVA/B/T/ and even PAR.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-GUV] ][29]\n* #### [ST-5 Sun Tracker][30]\n  \n  Our sun tracker for accurate, affordable direct or plane-of-array irradiance measurement.\n  \n  [[ST-5 Sun Tracker] ][31]\n* #### [SolarSIM-GPV][32]\n  \n  Our spectral pyranometer for measuring GHI and PV spectral correction factors.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-GPV] ][33]\n* #### [SolarSIM-D2][34]\n  \n  The original SolarSIM, for measuring spectral and broadband DNI and atmospheric parameters.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-D2] ][35]\n* #### [SolarSIM-G][36]\n  \n  Our spectral sensor for measuring spectral and broadband global irradiance.\n  \n  [[SolarSIM-G] ][37]\n* #### [Recalibration][38]\n  \n  Periodic recalibration ensures optimal performance of your SolarSIMs.\n  \n  [[Recalibration] ][39]\n* #### [Systems][40]\n  \n  Turn-key or custom. Whatever capabilities you need, we can put it all together for you.\n  \n  [[Spectral measurement system] ][41]\n\n## applications\n* [Solar]\n  \n  ##### [solar][42]\n  \n  The SolarSIM sensors represent the state-of-the-art in solar resource measurement for PV\n  applications. They are the only Class A sensors capable of resolving both broadband irradiance and\n  the spectral uncertainty inherent in all PV technologies.\n  \n  [Explore][43]\n* [meteorological]\n  \n  ##### [meteorological][44]\n  \n  Spectrafy's ability to combine multiple, previously expensive and difficult measurement\n  capabilities into a single compact, robust sensor makes advanced meteorological measurements\n  practical and affordable.\n  \n  [Explore][45]\n* [Agriculture]\n  \n  ##### [agriculture][46]\n  \n  Spectrafy's multi-spectral measurement approach enables highly accurate measurements of UV, PAR\n  and global irradiance in a single sensor. Ideal for agricultural research and irradiance networks.\n  \n  [Explore][47]\n\n## our technology\n\nAt Spectrafy we embrace the spectral nature of sunlight. Our sensors combine multi-spectral\nmeasurement with proprietary radiative transfer algorithms to accurately resolve the full-range\nsolar spectrum.\n\nThis powerful approach enables our sensors to unlock the wealth of information embedded within\nspectral data and creates measurement capabilities that are unmatched in terms of functionality and\naccuracy.\n\n[Learn more][48]\n\n## latest news\n* 15 Oct\n  [Spectrafy attends the IPC-XIV in Davos, Switzerland][49]\n  [Read More][50]\n* 01 May\n  [Spectrafy welcomes Ammonit Measurement to the team!][51]\n  [Read More][52]\n* 24 Mar\n  [Spectrafy launches the SolarBand-C3][53]\n  [Read More][54]\n\n## upcoming events\n* 07 May\n  [Intersolar Europe][55]\n  Munich, Germany\n  [Read More][56]\n* 08 Jun\n  [2025 IEEE PVSC 53][57]\n  Montreal, QC\n  [Read More][58]\n\n## our customers\n\n[ [Clearway] ][59]\n[ [DEWA] ][60]\n[ [EDF] ][61]\n[ [Fraunhofer] ][62]\n[ [McMaster] ][63]\n[ [AZUR Space] ][64]\n[ [T\u00dcV Rheinland] ][65]\n[ [University Nottingham] ][66]\n[ [ONREL] ][67]\n[ [ines] ][68]\n[ [RSE] ][69]\n[ [UNSW] ][70]\n[ [Morgan Solar] ][71]\n[ [First Solar] ][72]\n[ [Natural Resources Canada] ][73]\n\n## contact us\n\nContact us at [info@spectrafy.com][74] or subscribe to our newsletter to stay up to date with the\nour latest products, news and events.\n* [facebook-square][75]\n* [twitter-square][76]\n* [linkedin][77]\n\n[[Home]][78]\n\n## Footer menu\n* [Home][79]\n* [Privacy Statement][80]\n* [Terms of use][81]\n* [Contact][82]\n\n\u00a9 2025 Spectrafy Inc. All rights reserved.\n\n[1]: #main-content\n[2]: /\n[3]: /products\n[4]: /functions\n[5]: /applications\n[6]: /about-us\n[7]: /support\n[8]: /quotecart\n[9]: http://www.facebook.com/\n[10]: http://twitter.com/\n[11]: http://www.linkedin.com/\n[12]: /\n[13]: /\n[14]: /products\n[15]: /functions\n[16]: /applications\n[17]: /about-us\n[18]: /support\n[19]: /quotecart\n[20]: /products/solarband-c3us\n[21]: /products/solarband-c3us\n[22]: /products/solarband-c3\n[23]: /products/solarband-c3\n[24]: /products/solarsim-alb\n[25]: /products/solarsim-alb\n[26]: /products/solarsim-e\n[27]: /products/solarsim-e\n[28]: /products/solarsim-guv\n[29]: /products/solarsim-guv\n[30]: /products/st-5-sun-tracker\n[31]: /products/st-5-sun-tracker\n[32]: /products/solarsim-gpv\n[33]: /products/solarsim-gpv\n[34]: /products/solarsim-d2\n[35]: /products/solarsim-d2\n[36]: /products/solarsim-g\n[37]: /products/solarsim-g\n[38]: /products/recalibration\n[39]: /products/recalibration\n[40]: /products/systems\n[41]: /products/systems\n[42]: /applications/solar\n[43]: /applications/solar\n[44]: /applications/meteorological\n[45]: /applications/meteorological\n[46]: /applications/agriculture\n[47]: /applications/agriculture\n[48]: /support/publications\n[49]: /news\n[50]: /news\n[51]: /news\n[52]: /news\n[53]: /news\n[54]: /news\n[55]: /events\n[56]: /events\n[57]: /events\n[58]: /events\n[59]: https://www.clearwayenergygroup.com/\n[60]: http://www.dewa.gov.ae/en/\n[61]: https://www.edf-re.com/\n[62]: https://www.fraunhofer.org/\n[63]: https://www.mcmaster.ca/\n[64]: http://www.azurspace.com/index.php/en/\n[65]: https://www.tuv.com/world/en/\n[66]: https://www.nottingham.ac.uk/\n[67]: https://www.nrel.gov/\n[68]: https://www.ines-solaire.org/\n[69]: http://www.rse-web.it/home.page\n[70]: https://www.engineering.unsw.edu.au/energy-engineering/\n[71]: https://www.morgansolar.com\n[72]: https://www.firstsolar.com\n[73]: https://www.nrcan.gc.ca/energy/energy-offices-and-labs/canmetenergy/5715\n[74]: mailto:info@spectrafy.com\n[75]: https://www.facebook.com/spectrafy/\n[76]: https://twitter.com/Spectrafy\n[77]: https://ca.linkedin.com/company/spectrafy\n[78]: /\n[79]: /\n[80]: /priva"
